sh liquidity, hotel holds, food/nutrition, exercise, entertainment/comps, job-search obligations, and eventual Mexico relocation.\n\n[L21] ### Major pivots\n[L22] The conversation moved from ordinary day-to-day planning into a more rigorous reconciliation of **MGM promotional stays and liquidity**. Don identified ambiguity around modified Cosmopolitan/Vdara reservations, FREEPLAY, resort credit, and the 72-hour promotional-trip rule. MGM terms visible in a reservation email supplied the grounding evidence.\n\n[L24] A second pivot consolidated the scattered personal planning into a **portable Personal Operations handoff ZIP**, so future chats would not have to reconstruct lodging, money, nutrition, exercise, travel, and job context from conversation history.\n\n[L26] The final append added **Daphne Magna / Build a Life Abroad** as a live Playa relocation contact introduced by Jason Baibokas.\n\n[L28] ### Final scope\n[L29] This ended as a **Personal Operations reconciliation/handoff lane**, not a GCE Framework redesign. It contains current personal planning truth and supporting reference material across:\n\n[L31] **Vegas → liquidity → MGM offers → nutrition → exercise → job week → Mexico/Playa relocation.**\n\n---\n\n[L35] # 3. ACCOMPLISHMENTS BY DATE\n\n[L37] ## DATE: 2026-09-07\n\n[L39] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:** Personal Operations material was consolidated into a structured handoff package rather than remaining distributed across chat context.\n\n[L41] **DECISION / RESULT:** A living-project structure was established with explicit supersession rules: newer Don corrections and fresh evidence outrank stale planning arithmetic.\n\n[L43] **WHO / WHICH SEAT OWNED IT:** Don authority; Coda organization/reconciliation.\n\n[L45] **STATUS:** implemented\n\n[L47] A ZIP was generated containing project instructions, current state, lodging/calendar, budget/cash flow, nutrition, exercise, entertainment/comps, job week, Mexico travel, MGM rules, source index, bootstrap prompt, manifest, and workout document.\n\n---\n\n[L51] ## DATE: 2026-09-23 — MGM OFFER RECONCILIATION\n\n[L53] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:** Don reconciled apparently duplicated MGM promotional benefits against the actual promotional terms visible in the updated Vdara reservation.\n\n[L55] **DECISION / RESULT:** The visible MGM terms established that:\n\n[L57] - FREEPLAY loads on the **first trip booked under the promotion**.\n[L58] - It may only be redeemed on that first trip.\n[L59] - It is available **once per offer across Las Vegas MGM Rewards destinations**.\n[L60] - The offer covers a **single room on a single trip**.\n[L61] - Promotional components can vary by resort.\n[L62] - Promotional trips require **72 hours between them**.\n\n[L64] This eliminated the unsafe assumption that every confirmation displaying $270 FREEPLAY represented an independently collectible $270 award.\n\n[L66] **WHO / WHICH SEAT OWNED IT:** Don interpreted his MGM booking history; Coda reconciled the evidence.\n\n[L68] **STATUS:** accepted\n\n---\n\n[L72] ## DATE: 2026-09-23 — COSMOPOLITAN → VDARA MODIFICATION\n\n[L74] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:** The difference between an original promotional booking confirmation and a later room-change notification was identified.\n\n[L76] **DECISION / RESULT:** Absence of FREEPLAY/resort-credit language from a modified-room confirmation was **not treated as proof that the underlying promotional components disappeared**.\n\n[L78] The remaining source-of-truth action became confirmation with MGM VIP/Casino Services/Cosmo rather than guessing from the modification email.\n\n[L80] **WHO / WHICH SEAT OWNED IT:** Don.\n\n[L82] **STATUS:** accepted\n\n---\n\n[L86] ## DATE: 2026-09-23 — PROMOTIONAL PLANNING BASELINE\n\n[L88] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:** Don tested a newly received Excalibur offer against the booking system and observed that the promotional inventory/offer would not simply produce another equivalent promotional booking while an offer was already allocated.\n\n[L90] **DECISION / RESULT:** Budgeting was grounded conservatively: do **not** count multiple $270 FREEPLAY awards. Resort-credit treatment remained subject to the particular offer/resort and MGM confirmation.\n\n[L92] **WHO / WHICH SEAT OWNED IT:** Don.\n\n[L94] **STATUS:** accepted\n\n---\n\n[L98] ## DATE: 2026-09-23 — NUTRITION SHOPPING\n\n[L100] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:** Multiple low-cost nutrition/supplement candidates were examined, including greens powders, mushroom blends, vitamin products, sea-vegetable powder, and MCT oil.\n\n[L102] **DECISION / RESULT:** The working objective remained filling actual nutritional gaps cheaply rather than buying supplements because of marketing claims. Greens/whole-food powders and sea vegetables were considered more aligned with the identified nutritional objective than mushroom-only blends or MCT oil.\n\n[L104] **WHO / WHICH SEAT OWNED IT:** Don decision-making with Coda analysis.\n\n[L106] **STATUS:** proposed/supporting; no universal supplement protocol was canonized.\n\n---\n\n[L110] ## DATE: 2026-09-23 — PLAYA RELOCATION APPEND\n\n[L112] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:** The Jason Baibokas → Daphne Magna introduction thread was ingested into the Personal Operations context.\n\n[L114] **DECISION / RESULT:** Daphne became a live supporting relocation contact for neighborhood selection, apartment search, and relocation logistics. Gladys' involvement in apartment selection was explicitly recognized.\n\n[L116] **WHO / WHICH SEAT OWNED IT:** Don.\n\n[L118] **STATUS:** accepted/supporting\n\n---\n\n[L122] # 4. FINAL ACCEPTED DECISIONS\n\n[L124] ### DECISION: Personal Operations uses living-state supersession\n[L125] **DATE ACCEPTED:** 2026-09-07  \n[L126] **AUTHORITY:** Don  \n[L127] **SCOPE:** Personal Operations project  \n[L128] **STATUS:** PROJECT-CANONICAL\n\n[L130] Latest explicit Don correction and fresh evidence outrank older planning assumptions.\n\n[L132] ### DECISION: Hotel holds are locked liquidity\n[L133] **DATE ACCEPTED:** 2026-09-07  \n[L134] **AUTHORITY:** Don  \n[L135] **SCOPE:** Personal cash-flow planning  \n[L136] **STATUS:** PROJECT-CANONICAL\n\n[L138] They are not available spending cash.\n\n[L140] ### DECISION: Promotional FREEPLAY is not baseline cash\n[L141] **DATE ACCEPTED:** 2026-09-07; reinforced 2026-09-23  \n[L142] **AUTHORITY:** Don  \n[L143] **SCOPE:** Vegas personal budgeting  \n[L144] **STATUS:** PROJECT-CANONICAL\n\n[L146] Do not budget FREEPLAY as cash until actually available, played/converted, and realized.\n\n[L148] ### DECISION: Do not multiply MGM FREEPLAY from duplicate-looking confirmations\n[L149] **DATE ACCEPTED:** 2026-09-23  \n[L150] **AUTHORITY:** Don  \n[L151] **SCOPE:** MGM Vegas promotional planning  \n[L152] **STATUS:** PROJECT-CANONICAL\n\n[L154] Visible MGM terms establish once-per-offer treatment.\n\n[L156] ### DECISION: MGM promotional trips require 72-hour separation\n[L157] **DATE ACCEPTED:** 2026-09-23  \n[L158] **AUTHORITY:** MGM terms accepted by Don as source evidence  \n[L159] **SCOPE:** MGM promotional-trip planning  \n[L160] **STATUS:** PROJECT-CANONICAL\n\n[L162] ### DECISION: Modified reservation email does not independently establish loss of promotional components\n[L163] **DATE ACCEPTED:** 2026-09-23  \n[L164] **AUTHORITY:** Don  \n[L165] **SCOPE:** Cosmo/Vdara booking  \n[L166] **STATUS:** PROVISIONAL\n\n[L168] Final entitlement requires MGM confirmation.\n\n[L170] ### DECISION: Daphne Magna is an active Playa relocation resource\n[L171] **DATE ACCEPTED:** 2026-09-23  \n[L172] **AUTHORITY:** Don  \n[L173] **SCOPE:** Playa relocation  \n[L174] **STATUS:** PROJECT-CANONICAL as contact/status; her recommendations themselves are not canonical.\n\n---\n\n[L178] # 5. CANON / AUTHORITY CLASSIFICATION\n\n[L180] ## A. FRAMEWORK CANON\n\n[L182] **NONE created in this chat.**\n\n[L184] The chat applied evidence discipline and supersession concepts compatible with GCE doctrine, but did not modify GCE Framework authority, seats, routing, architecture, or lifecycle.\n\n---\n\n[L188] ## B. PROJECT CANON\n\n[L190] **Personal Operations living-state rules.** They govern this personal project because Don explicitly wanted a portable organized operating picture.\n\n[L192] **Cash classification:** cash, hotel holds, expected refunds, resort credit, FREEPLAY, and restricted balances remain distinct.\n\n[L194] **MGM promotional baseline:** once-per-offer FREEPLAY and 72-hour promotional-trip separation are the operative planning rules supported by the visible MGM terms.\n\n[L196] **Daphne relocation-contact status:** belongs to Playa relocation execution, not Framework.\n\n---\n\n[L200] ## C. SUPPORTING / REFERENCE\n\n[L202] The hotel screenshots, MGM emails/terms, supplement screenshots, nutrition comparisons, market observations, Daphne email thread, and existing Google Drive living-plan documents are supporting evidence.\n\n[L204] They inform decisions but do not independently establish GCE canon.\n\n---\n\n[L208] ## D. EXPERIMENTAL\n\n[L210] Supplement selection and AG1-like low-cost nutrition-stack exploration remained exploratory.\n\n[L212] The proposed manipulation of hotel/property sequence to reduce incidental holds was scenario planning, not durable authority.\n\n---\n\n[L216] ## E. SUPERSEDED / DEAD\n\n[L218] The assumption that three confirmations displaying similar FREEPLAY/resort-credit language necessarily mean three independent FREEPLAY awards is **dead**.\n\n[L220] Any earlier arithmetic counting all prospective FREEPLAY as available liquidity is **dead**.\n\n[L222] The idea that omission of promotional language on the Vdara modification automatically proves promotional benefits were removed is **dead**.\n\n---\n\n[L226] ## F. HISTORICAL PROVENANCE\n\n[L228] Earlier Vegas hotel sequences, older hold amounts, temporary Airbnb bridging, and prior promotional assumptions remain useful history but must not automatically overwrite newer Vegas operating state.\n\n[L230] The 2026-09-07 Per