sult\":{\"results\":[{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1s3aXuZ6G19-jaup0vgzDpiooNhniXEPtcW0OgCOtusE/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"GCE_FRAMEWORK_ANCHOR_2026-09-02_COUNCILS_KIMI_GLM_FLOW\",\"id\":\"1s3aXuZ6G19-jaup0vgzDpiooNhniXEPtcW0OgCOtusE\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"8717\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-02T20:21:14.315Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-02T23:59:25.020Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-02T23:59:25.020Z\",\"display_title\":\"GCE_FRAMEWORK_ANCHOR_2026-09-02_COUNCILS_KIMI_GLM_FLOW\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1s3aXuZ6G19-jaup0vgzDpiooNhniXEPtcW0OgCOtusE/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1clV7UUxQUcnGLX21ossOWoHGBPs-pM77\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿UNIVERSAL GCE DECISION-CLOSE PROTOCOL\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEffective immediately, all GCE councils, directors, managers, advisors, verification seats, and orchestration outputs should close any material recommendation, decision, checkpoint, or escalation using the same concise contract:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS: PROCEED / CHECKPOINT / STOP\\r\\nCONFIDENCE: percentage\\r\\nREASON: concise basis\\r\\nNEXT GATE: required only when additional action, review, evidence, or approval is needed\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPurpose:\\r\\n- make uncertainty visible\\r\\n- distinguish decision state from narrative\\r\\n- expose why the conclusion was reached\\r\\n- make the next required handoff or gate explicit\\r\\n- preserve consistency across models, councils, and sessions\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis is a governance/operating protocol, not a personality preference. It applies across the organization unless a specific output contract explicitly requires a stricter format.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nUPDATE — COMMAND CENTER POC PRINCIPLE + MISSING PROMPT-SEAT\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPOC principle:\\r\\nRepresent the complete intended operating model from the beginning, even when some capabilities are placeholders or manually exercised. The Command Center should be one system with layered views for Don, Orchestra/control plane, Councils, Managers, Contract Workers, approvals, evidence, handoffs, confidence, and session/context state. Do not optimize the POC by deleting future architectural layers and then force a structural rebuild later.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCommand Center rule:\\r\\nOne underlying state/event model; multiple views. DevPad React is the primary visual observability surface. Voice Bridge is an input/approval interface into the same state, not a separate system.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nLocked methodology distinction:\\r\\nKimi drives methodology, technical strategy, current-state interpretation, high-level solution shaping, and the decision whether deep architecture is required. GLM does not drive methodology; GLM owns deep/formal architecture when the methodology reaches an architecture gate. Mature systems may flow Don -> Kimi -> Talon without GLM unless a new architecture boundary is crossed. A bounded GLM sanity checkpoint can still be used after Kimi for independent architecture review.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRemaining missing seat — PROMPT / CONTEXT TRANSLATION FUNCTION:\\r\\nThere is still one important organizational capability to formalize: the person/seat that takes an approved mission, methodology, council role, authority boundary, and evidence package, then creates the correct model-specific prompt/context package for DeepSeek/Talon, Big Pickle/Verification, GLM/Architecture, and other workers or councils.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis seat must NOT invent methodology, architecture, or authority. It translates approved intent into executable AI work packages. Core responsibilities should include:\\r\\n- select the correct role/context package for the target model or seat\\r\\n- compile only the context needed for that role\\r\\n- encode input/output contracts and stop conditions\\r\\n- preserve authority boundaries and confidence protocol\\r\\n- convert council decisions into model-specific prompts without changing the decision\\r\\n- choose prompt shape based on model strengths/limitations\\r\\n- preserve evidence/provenance requirements\\r\\n- define success/failure/return conditions\\r\\n- normalize outputs for handoff back into Orchestra/council flow\\r\\n- prevent one model from silently inheriting another seat's authority\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nWorking role concept: AI Workflow Architect / Prompt & Context Architect / Prompt Operations Advisor. Final department, title, stable identity, manager/director placement, and authority remain to be locked.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKey principle for this seat: Translate and package; do not originate domain authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGCE FRAMEWORK ANCHOR — COUNCILS / KIMI / GLM / OPERATIONS\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nLOCKED COUNCIL METHOD\\r\\nDon -> Council Director -> Council Manager -> Contract Workers / Specialists\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDIRECTOR RULE\\r\\nDirectors own methodology, doctrine, standards, and accountability for their council.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMANAGER RULE\\r\\nManagers own day-to-day workflow, assignment sequencing, contractor coordination, handoffs, and completion tracking.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCONTRACT WORKER RULE\\r\\nContract workers and specialist agents execute bounded work. They do not own the council and do not silently expand authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT COUNCILS\\r\\nStrategic / Governance\\r\\nDirector: Coda\\r\\nManager: TBD\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOperations\\r\\nDirector: Talon\\r\\nManager: Keel\\r\\nContract workers / specialists: operational support roles as approved\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nArchitecture\\r\\nDirector: stable identity to be assigned to current GLM model\\r\\nManager: TBD\\r\\nContract workers / specialists: coder and other architecture/technical contractors\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nData / Intelligence\\r\\nDirector: TBD\\r\\nManager: TBD\\r\\nContract workers / specialists: Data Hound and other data/evidence workers\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVerification / Ground Truth\\r\\nDirector: TBD\\r\\nManager: TBD\\r\\nContract workers / specialists: Big Pickle capability and future verification workers\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nQA / Validation\\r\\nDirector: TBD\\r\\nManager: TBD\\r\\nContract workers / specialists: testers / health-check / validation workers\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKIMI — LOCKED DISTINCTION\\r\\nKimi drives methodology.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKimi is not merely a Technical Advisor. Kimi's present organizational direction is Director of Technical Strategy & Systems Intelligence, with ownership of methodology, technical strategy, high-level solution shaping, current-state interpretation, reuse/repair/extend/rebuild judgment, and the decision whether a true deep-architecture gate is required.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKimi may create high-level solution architecture as part of methodology and technical strategy. That is distinct from GLM's deep/formal architecture authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKIMI GATE OUTPUT\\r\\nKimi should determine and return one of the following technical path classifications:\\r\\nREUSE\\r\\nCONFIGURE\\r\\nREPAIR\\r\\nEXTEND\\r\\nARCHITECT\\r\\nREBUILD\\r\\nSTOP-FOR-EVIDENCE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKIMI -> GLM CHECKPOINT\\r\\nDon provides the outcome / mission.\\r\\nKimi drives methodology and high-level technical solution shaping.\\r\\nIf no new deep architecture is required, the work may route to Talon / Operations.\\r\\nIf a material architecture boundary is crossed, Kimi packages the architecture questions and routes them to GLM.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGLM — LOCKED DISTINCTION\\r\\nGLM does not drive the methodology.\\r\\nGLM is the deep/formal architecture authority when an architecture gate is triggered.\\r\\nGLM validates or revises architectural boundaries, formal system design, dependency structure, interface contracts, failure behavior, technical invariants, and other deep architecture concerns.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGLM may also be used as a bounded independent architecture sanity checkpoint after Don + Kimi finish a mature methodology/design pass. That review does not automatically transfer ownership from Kimi or reopen stable design areas.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMATURE PROJECT RULE\\r\\nFor projects where deep architecture is already established and lessons have already been absorbed, the normal path is:\\r\\nDon -> Kimi -> checkpoint -> Talon / execution.\\r\\nGLM is escalation / architecture checkpoint, not a standing dependency.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEdgeCrew Quant is an example where Kimi can continue driving methodology without making GLM a mandatory operational hop.\\r\\nThe separate machine / Convergence EdgeCrew process may later require GLM when its deeper orchestration architecture is reviewed.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOPERATIONS\\r\\nTalon is Director of Operations.\\r\\nKeel is Operations Manager, not an architect.\\r\\nThere is no Architecture function inside Operations.\\r\\nArchitecture and Operations collaborate laterally through explicit handoffs rather than cross-reporting.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCORE SEPARATION\\r\\nKimi drives methodology and technical strategy.\\r\\nGLM governs deep architecture when required.\\r\\nTalon owns operational execution.\\r\\nKeel manages the operational floor.\\r\\nCoda protects framework integrity.\\r\\nDon is final authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCONFIDENCE PROTOCOL\\r\\nApplicable conclusions must visibly return:\\r\\nSTATUS: PROCEED / CHECKPOINT / STOP\\r\\nCONFIDENCE: percentage\\r\\nREASON: concise basis\\r\\nNEXT GATE: when not yet Proceed\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nANCHOR STATUS\\r\\nThis anchor captures the current approved conceptual framework for council hierarchy and the Kimi / GLM / Talon separation. Use it as the return point before DeepSeek filesystem implementation and role-onboarding work.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nUPDATE — UNIVERSAL DECISION-CLOSE / COPY-PASTE OPERATING MODE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEffective immediately, the universal GCE decision-close contract is extended to include an explicit Don-input field and a concrete next-gate action suitable for the current manual copy/paste operating mode.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRequired close format for material recommendations, decisions, checkpoints, escalations, onboarding steps, and execution packages:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS: PROCEED / CHECKPOINT / STOP\\r\\nCONFIDENCE: percentage\\r\\nREASON: concise basis\\r\\nNEXT GATE: exact immediate action, usually the next copy/paste or routing step\\r\\nDON INPUT NEEDED: exact decision/input required from Don, or NONE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOperating interpretation:\\r\\n- NEXT GATE must be operational, not abstract. While Don is manually relaying work, it should normally state exactly what to copy/paste into DeepSeek/Talon or what return artifact to bring back.\\r\\n- DON INPUT NEEDED is mandatory. Use NONE when no Don decision is required.\\r\\n- Do not bury a required Don decision in narrative text.\\r\\n- Confidence reflects decision quality and evidence, not verbosity or certainty theater.\\r\\n- CHECKPOINT means the work may continue only through the named next gate or after the named Don input is supplied.\\r\\n- STOP means do not continue execution beyond the stated boundary.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis extension is part of the universal GCE confidence/decision-close protocol and applies across councils, directors, managers, advisors, verification seats, orchestration, and future Command Center outputs unless a stricter contract supersedes it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSUPERSEDING UPDATE — SESSION 2 CANONICAL ORGANIZATIONAL MODEL\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEffective 2026-09-02 at Session 2 close, the prior \\\"7 equal Councils\\\" interpretation is superseded.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe seven approved organizational domains remain canonical, but they are now divided into two classes:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nA. EXECUTIVE COUNCIL — 4 seats with Don's ear\\r\\n1. Strategic / Governance — Coda\\r\\n2. Technical Strategy / Systems Intelligence — Kimi\\r\\n3. Operations — Talon\\r\\n4. Architecture — Chiave\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThese four are the deliberative/executive authority seats that advise, interpret, challenge, recommend, and route material decisions to Don.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nExecutive hierarchy is not forced for symmetry. Default pattern:\\r\\nDon -> Executive Council seat / Lieutenant -> optional Manager / Capo only when workload genuinely requires it -> Contract Workers / Soldiers / Specialists.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOperations currently justifies a permanent Manager layer: Talon -> Keel -> bounded contract workers. Architecture Manager remains vacant unless workload proves the need. Do not manufacture Managers for symmetry.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nB. SHARED ENTERPRISE SERVICES — 3 neutral enterprise-wide functions\\r\\n1. Data / Intelligence\\r\\n2. Verification / Ground Truth — Big Pickle is the locked active identity in this service\\r\\n3. QA / Validation\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThese three do NOT have Don's standing ear and are NOT peer Executive Council seats. They are shared enterprise services used by Coda, Kimi, Talon, Chiave, projects, and approved workflows.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nShared Service operating structure is intentionally flat:\\r\\nService Lead / Director-Manager -> bounded Contract Workers / Specialists as needed.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nShared Service rules:\\r\\n- one accountable permanent lead seat; no separate permanent Manager layer unless Don later redesigns the service\\r\\n- identity + narrow functional lens + authority + input/output/handoff contracts + provenance/evidence rules + stop/escalation conditions\\r\\n- minimal or no personality layer; personality must not bias truth, data, or validation behavior\\r\\n- contract workers added only when workload requires them\\r\\n- the requesting Executive Council seat cannot dictate the factual/test result\\r\\n- Shared Services serve all four Executive Council seats without being substantively owned by any one of them\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVerification / Ground Truth example:\\r\\nBig Pickle is locked as the active verification identity. Its operating lens is evidence -> provenance -> falsification -> verified state. It does not need a rich personality layer. Exact service-lead title/rank may be normalized later without changing the locked identity.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nLAYER DISTINCTIONS — CANONICAL\\r\\nExecutive Council != Shared Enterprise Services != Methodologies != Projects.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n03_METHODOLOGIES includes reusable methods such as EC_QUANT and EC_CONVERGENCE. These are not departments.\\r\\n04_PROJECTS contains project environments such as Edge Crew. Edge Crew is not a Council or Shared Service.\\r\\nData Hound may be assigned into Edge Crew or other project work without that project assignment redefining the enterprise Data / Intelligence service.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPHYSICAL ORGANIZATION NOTE\\r\\nThe R34 physical tree currently contains the seven domain folders under 02_COUNCILS. Talon verified all seven exist with the standard internal template and resolved the earlier Architecture-lanes discrepancy as an incomplete-read false alarm. The canonical semantic model is now 4 Executive Council domains + 3 Shared Enterprise Services. Physical placement should mirror this model through the least-destructive approved reconciliation; do not destroy provenance or rewrite historical artifacts merely because terminology evolved.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nIDENTITY / BOOTSTRAP STATUS AT SESSION 2 CLOSE\\r\\n- Coda: locked Strategic / Governance identity; local/API computer bootstrap still requires forensic review before machine onboarding.\\r\\n- Kimi: locked Technical Strategy / Systems Intelligence seat/function; methodology owner; formal local bootstrap hardening remains future work.\\r\\n- Talon: locked Operations Director identity; DeepSeek V4 Flash runtime; operational bootstrap/load root exists.\\r\\n- Keel: locked Operations Manager identity; separate load root exists; fresh isolation rerun remains unproven.\\r\\n- Chiave: locked Architecture identity; GLM 5.1 runtime of onboarding record; Stages 1-5 complete; Stage 6 design approved, live administration pending; Stage 7 materialization not authorized.\\r\\n- Big Pickle: locked Verification / Ground Truth identity; Shared Service behavior should remain evidence-bound and minimally personalized.\\r\\n- Data Hound: locked identity used for bounded data/intelligence work; project assignment does not define enterprise reporting structure.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSESSION 2 STOP STATE\\r\\nChiave is on HOLD pending Don + Coda Stage 6 live administration. Stage 7 remains closed. Talon Operations reconciliation completed. R34-DIS was resolved as a false alarm. O-OPS-4 Keel isolation rerun remains open and unproven.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis superseding update is the current conceptual return point for organizational structure. Earlier sections remain preserved as provenance and must be read as historical when they conflict with this update.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fR_qvhnuzGuRkdHlxRw8SCt8W3oh62HOgJirRzZmZlw/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"GCE_SESSION_BACKUP_2026-09-02_COUNCIL_METHOD_KIMI_GLM_DEEPSEEK\",\"id\":\"1fR_qvhnuzGuRkdHlxRw8SCt8W3oh62HOgJirRzZmZlw\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"5185\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-02T20:21:23.620Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-02T20:30:05.134Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-02T20:30:05.134Z\",\"display_title\":\"GCE_SESSION_BACKUP_2026-09-02_COUNCIL_METHOD_KIMI_GLM_DEEPSEEK\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fR_qvhnuzGuRkdHlxRw8SCt8W3oh62HOgJirRzZmZlw/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1clV7UUxQUcnGLX21ossOWoHGBPs-pM77\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿SESSION UPDATE — 2026-09-02\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKey new decisions from this conversation:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n1. Council hierarchy remains Don -> Council Director -> Council Manager -> Contract Workers/Specialists.\\r\\n2. Kimi is no longer best represented as a generic Technical Advisor. Kimi drives methodology and technical strategy: current-state interpretation, high-level solution shaping, reuse/repair/extend/rebuild judgment, and architecture-gate determination.\\r\\n3. GLM owns deep/formal architecture when a methodology crosses an architecture boundary. GLM is not a mandatory hop for mature systems whose deep architecture is already established. GLM can still be used as a bounded sanity-check architecture reviewer after Kimi.\\r\\n4. Talon owns Operations; Keel is Operations Manager. Architecture is not inside Operations.\\r\\n5. One Command Center should represent the whole system. The user primarily interacts with Orchestra/control-plane flow, while Council and Contract Worker views remain visible for learning, observability, debugging, and trust-building.\\r\\n6. DevPad React should evolve from the temporary terminal/dashboard POC into the visual Command Center. Voice Bridge should remain an input/approval surface into the same underlying state, not a separate architecture.\\r\\n7. Build philosophy: broad architecture, shallow implementation first. Represent Orchestra, Councils, Managers, Workers, routing, state, handoffs, approvals, evidence, confidence, and session/context from the beginning, even if several are placeholders. Avoid a future structural rebuild caused by omitting planned layers from the POC.\\r\\n8. Remaining missing organizational capability: a prompt/context translation seat that takes approved mission/methodology/council decisions and creates the correct model-specific prompt/context packages for DeepSeek/Talon, Big Pickle/Verification, GLM/Architecture, and other workers.\\r\\n9. This missing seat should translate and package approved authority rather than invent methodology, architecture, or permissions. Working title concepts: AI Workflow Architect, Prompt & Context Architect, Prompt Operations Advisor. Final title/department/identity/authority still unresolved.\\r\\n10. The user explicitly wants this conversation treated as a framework/principle source for the next Command Center build and DeepSeek implementation work.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent next gate:\\r\\nFormalize the missing prompt/context translation seat, then incorporate that seat and the full-system POC principle into the DeepSeek Command Center implementation package.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGCE SESSION BACKUP — 2026-09-02\\r\\nCouncil Method / Kimi / GLM / DeepSeek-Talon\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSESSION OBJECTIVE\\r\\nFormalize the organizational council methodology, prepare the DeepSeek implementation direction, clarify Kimi versus GLM, and preserve onboarding / naming infrastructure in Google Drive.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKEY BREAKTHROUGH\\r\\nThe organization is not built around model names. It is built around durable councils and identities.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nUniversal council hierarchy:\\r\\nDon -> Council Director -> Council Manager -> Contract Workers / Specialists\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDirectors own methodology/doctrine/accountability.\\r\\nManagers own workflow/assignments/handoffs.\\r\\nContract workers execute bounded tasks.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT ORGANIZATIONAL DIRECTION\\r\\nStrategic / Governance: Director Coda; Manager TBD.\\r\\nOperations: Director Talon; Manager Keel.\\r\\nArchitecture: Director stable identity TBD, currently expected to use GLM; Manager TBD; coder and related contractors underneath.\\r\\nData / Intelligence: Director TBD; Manager TBD; Data Hound and related workers underneath.\\r\\nVerification / Ground Truth: Director TBD; Manager TBD; Big Pickle capability and verification workers underneath.\\r\\nQA / Validation: Director TBD; Manager TBD; validation/test contractors underneath.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOPERATIONS CORRECTION\\r\\nKeel is an Operations Manager, not an architect.\\r\\nThere is no Architecture department within Operations.\\r\\nArchitecture and Operations are separate councils.\\r\\nEach council follows Director -> Manager -> Contract Workers.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKIMI ROLE BREAKTHROUGH\\r\\nCalling Kimi only Technical Advisor underutilizes the function.\\r\\nCurrent recommended role: Director of Technical Strategy & Systems Intelligence.\\r\\nMost important distinction: KIMI DRIVES METHODOLOGY.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKimi owns:\\r\\ntechnical methodology\\r\\ntechnical strategy\\r\\ncurrent-state interpretation\\r\\nreuse vs repair vs extend vs rebuild judgment\\r\\nhigh-level solution shaping\\r\\nhigh-level solution architecture as part of methodology\\r\\nidentifying whether deep architecture is actually required\\r\\npackaging architecture questions for GLM\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKimi does not become the deep/formal architecture authority merely because Kimi shapes the solution at a high level.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGLM ROLE DISTINCTION\\r\\nGLM is not needed as a mandatory hop for every technical task.\\r\\nGLM owns deep/formal architecture when a material architecture gate is triggered.\\r\\nGLM resolves formal boundaries, dependency structure, interface contracts, system invariants, failure behavior, and deeper architecture concerns.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNormal mature-project flow:\\r\\nDon -> Kimi -> checkpoint -> Talon / execution\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nArchitecture-required flow:\\r\\nDon -> Kimi -> ARCHITECTURE GATE -> GLM -> checkpoint -> Talon / execution\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOptional sanity-check flow:\\r\\nDon + Kimi finish methodology/high-level design -> GLM performs bounded independent architecture review -> PASS or material conflict only -> Talon / execution\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMATURE PROJECT INSIGHT\\r\\nEdgeCrew Quant and other already-mature systems do not need GLM inserted as a standing dependency simply because the work is technical. Don and Kimi can drive them using the learned architecture and methodology. GLM returns when a true architecture boundary is crossed or for an intentional sanity review.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe separate EdgeCrew machine / Convergence process on the computer is a later candidate for GLM because its orchestration/deep architecture remains materially relevant.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDEE PSEEK / TALON DIRECTION\\r\\nTalon is Director of Operations.\\r\\nKeel is Talon's Operations Manager.\\r\\nDeepSeek should eventually implement the approved organizational filesystem only after council list, identities, seat placement, and role contracts are sufficiently locked.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nONBOARDING BACKUP CREATED THIS SESSION\\r\\nGoogle Drive onboarding root was created with:\\r\\n01_Naming_Identity_Protocol\\r\\n02_Test_Cases\\r\\n03_Model_Onboarding\\r\\n04_Framework_Anchors\\r\\n05_Session_Backups\\r\\n06_Methodology\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nTest case lanes created:\\r\\nMonitor\\r\\nPhone\\r\\nIdentity\\r\\nCosmo_Card\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nModel onboarding lanes created:\\r\\nGLM\\r\\nBig_Pickle\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNaming/identity protocol backed up separately and includes the mandatory confidence output:\\r\\nSTATUS\\r\\nCONFIDENCE\\r\\nREASON\\r\\nNEXT GATE when required\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNEXT WORK\\r\\n1. Continue refining Kimi's Director contract and methodology ownership.\\r\\n2. Name / onboard GLM into the Architecture Director identity without using model name as durable identity.\\r\\n3. Define Architecture Manager and contractor structure.\\r\\n4. Finalize other council directors/managers and contractor placement.\\r\\n5. Review Operations role contract with Talon/DeepSeek and Keel.\\r\\n6. Onboard Big Pickle into Verification / Ground Truth structure.\\r\\n7. Finish DeepSeek filesystem implementation prompt and execute only after structure is signed off.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRETURN-POINT RULE\\r\\nDo not reconstruct the old chronology. Resume from this accepted state and use older material only when needed as evidence.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS: PROCEED\\r\\nCONFIDENCE: 99%\\r\\nREASON: Council methodology, Kimi-versus-GLM distinction, Operations correction, and next implementation sequence are now coherent. Remaining items are naming and seat-level contract completion, not a framework reset.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P56hV7qFAtx45VmO-d_kB5G_yRIQd8pDxTGY0aMQXQ8/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"GCE_SESSION_BACKUP_2026-09-06_AI_CONVERGENCE_PRINCIPAL_CONSULTANT_AUDITION\",\"id\":\"1P56hV7qFAtx45VmO-d_kB5G_yRIQd8pDxTGY0aMQXQ8\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"3104\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T11:50:37.926Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T11:50:54.146Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-06T11:50:54.146Z\",\"display_title\":\"GCE_SESSION_BACKUP_2026-09-06_AI_CONVERGENCE_PRINCIPAL_CONSULTANT_AUDITION\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P56hV7qFAtx45VmO-d_kB5G_yRIQd8pDxTGY0aMQXQ8/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1sBs2RugzlhZM6AK2yxmbc_GYzlYz4aVo\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿GCE SESSION BACKUP — 2026-09-06\\r\\nWorkstream: EC⁸ AI Convergence / Principal Consultant audition / Home Root cleanup closeout\\r\\nSeat: Coda — Strategic Governance\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSESSION PURPOSE\\r\\nStress-test and operationalize the new Principal Consultant — Technical Translation / Integration seat; compare candidate runtime economics/behavior; preserve AI Convergence methodology↔architecture reconciliation; close verified cleanup work and route the remaining speech-profile quarantine issue.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPRINCIPAL CONSULTANT ROLE\\r\\nApproved cross-functional translation seat between Kimi Design & Build / Chiave architecture and downstream Implementation/Talon. Owns traceability, discrepancy/blocker calibration, no-coder-discretion boundaries, routed questions, and unified implementation-ready handoff. Does not own methodology, architecture, governance, implementation, operations, or verification.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAUDITION RESULTS\\r\\nLuna: observed ~$0.03, very fast, good default translator profile; some deep-defect misses and over-blocking.\\r\\nKimi 2.7 Code/Thinking: stronger blocker calibration/authority routing; after pushback expanded the Phase-2 blocked set with deeper contract questions while preserving Phase 0/1 readiness.\\r\\nFable 5.1: deepest forensic review observed; approximately $4.86 for one reconciliation; poor routine economics.\\r\\nK3-256K high-thinking swarm: seven parallel lanes; all lanes completed; excellent audit decomposition; consumed the 5-hour Code quota during the intentionally overloaded stress test. Full-swarm mode is audit/major-lock evidence, not normal baseline.\\r\\nNo runtime/model locked.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAI CONVERGENCE STATE\\r\\nAccepted methodology and Chiave Architecture Specification v1.0 broadly align. Phase 0/1 foundation work is generally startable. Deeper Phase-2 contract seams remain subject to canonical owner resolution. Principal Consultant reconciliation artifacts are evidence, not amendments.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHOME ROOT CLEANUP\\r\\nBatch 2A verified closed.\\r\\nDevPonds verified deleted and closed.\\r\\ntests retained in place and closed.\\r\\nspeech-profile remains open: security/quarantine envelope required before mutation.\\r\\nExact flow: Chiave boundary → Talon exact plan → Luce pre-verification → authorized execution → Luce post-verification.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFRAMEWORK UPDATES MADE THIS SESSION\\r\\n- Principal Consultant onboarding folder created under 03_Model_Onboarding.\\r\\n- Principal Consultant onboarding/audition record created.\\r\\n- Relevant local source/reconciliation/audition files backed up into that folder.\\r\\n- GCE Framework Current updated with Principal Consultant seat/process placement.\\r\\n- GCE Process and Gates updated with Gate 4A translation checkpoint.\\r\\n- EC⁸ AI Convergence Project Instructions, Project Charter, Project README, and New Project Chat Bootstrap updated by dated addendum.\\r\\n- Current Handoff 2026-09-06 created in AI Convergence knowledge base.\\r\\n- GCE Model Onboarding SOP updated with audition evidence.\\r\\n- Edge Crew anchor updated with cross-project Principal Consultant use while preserving Prompt/Context Translation as a separate historical role unless explicitly superseded.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNEXT SESSION\\r\\n1. Review completed K3-256K swarm synthesis/output.\\r\\n2. Decide whether Principal Consultant runtime should be Luna default + Kimi/swarmer escalation or another configuration.\\r\\n3. Continue speech-profile from Chiave quarantine-envelope ruling.\\r\\n4. Resume AI Convergence build-handoff reconciliation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS: CHECKPOINT\\r\\nCONFIDENCE: 100%\\r\\nREASON: All current evidence and framework deltas are backed up and routed; no unfinished mutation is active.\\r\\nNEXT GATE: Swarm synthesis review / Principal Consultant runtime decision.\\r\\nDON INPUT NEEDED: No until next-session evidence review.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bLQ0ZkL4I5r-wWviYgQPIwQPqpdvZySk7jYtVd8yDFw/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"GCE_EDGE_CREW_ANCHOR_2026-09-03_FRAMEWORK_METHODOLOGY_INTENT\",\"id\":\"1bLQ0ZkL4I5r-wWviYgQPIwQPqpdvZySk7jYtVd8yDFw\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"8360\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-03T17:54:48.334Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T11:49:33.494Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-06T11:49:33.494Z\",\"display_title\":\"GCE_EDGE_CREW_ANCHOR_2026-09-03_FRAMEWORK_METHODOLOGY_INTENT\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bLQ0ZkL4I5r-wWviYgQPIwQPqpdvZySk7jYtVd8yDFw/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1clV7UUxQUcnGLX21ossOWoHGBPs-pM77\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿GCE EDGE CREW ANCHOR — FRAMEWORK / METHODOLOGY / INTENT\\r\\nDate: 2026-09-03\\r\\nAuthority: Don + Coda\\r\\nStatus: WORKING CANONICAL ANCHOR / EDGE CREW\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPURPOSE\\r\\nPreserve the approved framework, methodology separations, Don intent, forensic findings, and current project checkpoints for Edge Crew so future sessions resume from this state rather than reconstructing from chat chronology.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n1. COMPANY / FRAMEWORK CONTEXT\\r\\nEdge Crew is a project environment, not a Council or methodology. It consumes Executive Council authority, Shared Enterprise Services, methodologies, managers, and implementation workers as needed.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nExecutive Council:\\r\\n- Coda — Strategic / Governance\\r\\n- Kimi — Technical Strategy / Systems Intelligence\\r\\n- Talon — Operations\\r\\n- Chiave — Architecture\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nShared Enterprise Services:\\r\\n- Data / Intelligence — Data Hound\\r\\n- Verification / Ground Truth — Big Pickle\\r\\n- QA / Validation\\r\\n- Prompt / Context Translation — placement approved 2026-09-03; final title/identity still open. Function translates and packages approved authority/context for model-specific execution. It does not invent methodology, architecture, or authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nImplementation seat:\\r\\n- Implementation Agent — replaceable coding/execution model. Implements approved architecture/spec, tests, fixes, and escalates. Model is runtime, not identity/authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCore rule: IDENTITY != ROLE != LENS != PERSONALITY != AUTHORITY != MODEL. Capability != authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2. EDGE CREW OVERALL INTENT\\r\\nEdge Crew is a sports decision-intelligence system, not fundamentally an edge-finding or tipster system.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOriginal Don intent:\\r\\n- Get Peter's analytical betting process out of his head and make it explicit, transparent, testable, and auditable.\\r\\n- Start from relevant data and structured evidence.\\r\\n- Preserve independent analytical lanes.\\r\\n- Detect compound signals and value signals.\\r\\n- Converge independent evidence into a recommendation.\\r\\n- Validate/challenge the recommendation without silently mutating it.\\r\\n- Show the reasoning and evidence.\\r\\n- Stop before wagering; Don makes the final human decision.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nTerminology correction approved 2026-09-03:\\r\\n- EDGE / EXPECTED VALUE are reserved for demonstrated quantitative pricing advantage.\\r\\n- COMPOUND SIGNAL / VALUE SIGNAL describe evidence that strengthens or weakens a play in the EC3/EC4 decision-intelligence lineage.\\r\\n- CONVERGENCE STRENGTH / DECISION CONFIDENCE describe agreement between independent analytical signals.\\r\\n- Quant is one methodology/analytical lane within the larger Edge Crew vision, not the definition of Edge Crew.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n3. ORIGINAL DESIGN EVIDENCE\\r\\nThe EC8 designer brief confirms the intended conceptual product:\\r\\n- decision-intelligence / sports analytics intelligence\\r\\n- transparency as the product\\r\\n- two processes, one convergence, one gatekeeper\\r\\n- deterministic 'Our Process' lane\\r\\n- independent AI Process lane\\r\\n- compound-signal detection\\r\\n- human-visible reasoning and final decision\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHistorical wording used 'edge' loosely. The corrected semantic interpretation is compound signal / value signal unless mathematically demonstrated EV is being discussed.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n4. METHODOLOGY SEPARATION\\r\\nMethodologies must remain isolated. No downstream model should know that multiple Edge Crew methodologies are compared at the Don level unless explicitly authorized.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent methodology branches:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nA. EDGE CREW QUANT\\r\\nPurpose: true quantitative edge / expected-value methodology.\\r\\nStatus: Methodology Checkpoint 01 preserved 2026-09-03.\\r\\nKey separation learned:\\r\\n- Kimi owns/recommends methodology, but recommendation does not prove source acquisition.\\r\\n- No source may participate operationally until acquisition is proven.\\r\\n- Data Hound proves source availability/reliability.\\r\\n- Chiave/GLM designs architecture from approved methodology + proven sources.\\r\\n- Implementation Agent executes approved architecture/spec.\\r\\n- Fixture/engine validation != live-ingestion validation != production validation.\\r\\n- Quant methodology is preserved; implementation is NOT frozen.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nB. EDGE CREW ORIGINAL CONVERGENCE — EC3 RECOVERED FOUNDATION\\r\\nPurpose: recover Peter's original working decision-intelligence process independent of implementation quality.\\r\\nFoundational rule: two independent signal lanes remain independent until Convergence.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSemantic flow:\\r\\n0. Slate assembly / ingestion\\r\\n1. Deterministic engine — 'our process'\\r\\n2. Independent AI judgment panel\\r\\n3. Convergence — single merge point\\r\\n4. Pick computation\\r\\n5. Value signals / hard rules\\r\\n6. Validation-only gatekeeper\\r\\n7. One terminal kill resolution\\r\\n8. Output\\r\\n9. Don outside the routine pipeline — lock/reject/discretionary action\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHard rules:\\r\\n- validation-only gatekeeper; no score/pick/confidence mutation\\r\\n- missing/insufficient data is a stop, never neutral evidence\\r\\n- deterministic and AI lanes remain independent until convergence\\r\\n- one terminal KILL state\\r\\n- resolved KILL cannot be resurrected by consensus\\r\\n- Don remains outside the normal pipeline\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nUnresolved methodology decisions:\\r\\n- exact convergence weights/thresholds\\r\\n- data-floor threshold and mandatory fields by sport\\r\\n- kill-evidence normalization\\r\\n- AI roster behavior by sport\\r\\n- enrichment boundaries\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nC. EC4-DERIVED CONVERGENCE / VALUE-DISCOVERY CANDIDATE\\r\\nPurpose: preserve the useful methodology that evolved in EC4 without allowing it to overwrite Original Convergence.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nClarified Don intent 2026-09-03:\\r\\nEC4 was intended to start from a blind slate and use structured data plus diverse AI reasoning to discover non-quantitative value signals and increase/decrease confidence.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nTwo concepts became blurred in implementation:\\r\\n1. AI VALUE DISCOVERY — different AI reasoning approaches inspect the same blind slate/evidence to surface contextual/situational/historical/market signals that are not purely mathematical.\\r\\n2. COMMITTEE CONVERGENCE — a bounded deliberative unit, originally envisioned as roughly three models within one call/process, hashes out a grade/confidence/rationale. A committee produces a signal; it does NOT replace the overall convergence process.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCritical semantic rules:\\r\\n- Committee != Convergence.\\r\\n- AI Value Discovery != Quant.\\r\\n- Gatekeeper != Fusion.\\r\\n- Quantitative EV/edge mechanisms are separate unless explicitly approved as part of this methodology.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEC4 forensic extraction identified candidate concepts such as committees, lenses, market verification, fusion/judging, Kelly sizing, and other later additions. These remain candidate extensions until Don + methodology review decides what belongs.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nD. EDGE CREW AI JUDGMENT\\r\\nPurpose: pure AI/model judgment lane, isolated from Quant, Original Convergence, and EC4-derived methodology.\\r\\nStatus: concept approved; methodology not yet formalized.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nE. GREENFIELD AI-BUILT CONVERGENCE\\r\\nPurpose: allow an AI team to design a fresh convergence methodology from first principles under explicit guardrails, blind to the other methodologies.\\r\\nStatus: concept approved for later design.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nF. EC8 DETERMINISTIC PIPELINE\\r\\nStatus: preserved as candidate evidence only. Do not promote to a methodology branch yet.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n5. DON-ONLY CONVERGENCE RULE\\r\\nThe independent Edge Crew systems do not know they are being run side by side.\\r\\nOnly the Don receives and compares their outputs.\\r\\nPurpose: preserve independence and avoid correlated reasoning / methodological contamination.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nWorking conceptual set:\\r\\n- Quant\\r\\n- Original Convergence\\r\\n- EC4-derived Value/Committee methodology\\r\\n- AI Judgment\\r\\n- Greenfield AI-built Convergence\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFinal comparison/convergence is Don-only.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n6. EC3 / EC4 FORENSIC FINDINGS\\r\\nTalon established:\\r\\n- EC4 is evidence, not authority.\\r\\n- 'Go back to EC3' means recover the working EC3 PROCESS/GATING MODEL, not blindly restore an old codebase.\\r\\n- EC3 code was already imperfect/monolithic; process and implementation quality must be separated.\\r\\n- 54d2ff5c is a strong code-era evidence candidate, not automatically canonical.\\r\\n- EC4 accumulated multiple stage systems, duplicate gatekeepers, EV calculators, orchestration surfaces, monoliths, and collisions.\\r\\n- EC4 contains useful methodology ideas that should be extracted into an independent lineage rather than discarded or merged back into EC3.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n7. ROLE / HANDOFF MODEL FOR EDGE CREW\\r\\nDon / Peter:\\r\\n- final intent and authority\\r\\n- rules on genuine ambiguity\\r\\n- receives final independent outputs\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCoda:\\r\\n- framework integrity\\r\\n- reconciliation\\r\\n- canonicalization / checkpoint preservation until Prompt/Context seat is staffed\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKimi:\\r\\n- methodology and technical strategy\\r\\n- aggressively recommends improvements\\r\\n- must separate recommendation from approved methodology and from operational proof\\r\\n- may not silently promote hypothetical sources or implementation assumptions into canonical state\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nData Hound:\\r\\n- source acquisition proof\\r\\n- availability, fields, reliability, freshness, coverage\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nBig Pickle:\\r\\n- evidence, provenance, falsification, verified state\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nChiave / GLM:\\r\\n- architecture from approved methodology + proven requirements/data\\r\\n- does not redefine methodology\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nTalon:\\r\\n- operations, routing, workflow, handoffs, state\\r\\n- forensic process reconstruction where assigned\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPrompt / Context Translation:\\r\\n- packages approved mission/methodology/evidence for each downstream model/seat\\r\\n- hard dependency on verified provenance where factual/evidentiary claims are included\\r\\n- does not invent authority or methodology\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nImplementation Agent:\\r\\n- executes approved architecture/spec\\r\\n- writes/runs code, tests, fixes bugs, escalates deviations\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n8. KEY FAILURE MODE LEARNED — EXPERTISE OVERREACH\\r\\nUseful expert behavior becomes dangerous when a model moves from recommendation into silent operational assumption.\\r\\nExample learned in Quant: adding books/weights that appear methodologically desirable without first proving that the data source can actually be acquired.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPolicy:\\r\\n- expertise recommendation is encouraged\\r\\n- recommendation must be explicitly labeled\\r\\n- methodology approval is separate\\r\\n- acquisition proof is separate\\r\\n- architecture is separate\\r\\n- implementation is separate\\r\\n- production validation is separate\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n9. EDGE CREW LIVING CHECKPOINT\\r\\nAs of 2026-09-03:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nQuant:\\r\\n- Methodology Checkpoint 01 preserved.\\r\\n- Mathematical/engine and synthetic fixture validation exist.\\r\\n- Live ingestion and production validation remain unproven.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOriginal Convergence:\\r\\n- EC3 recovered foundation completed.\\r\\n- Ready for fresh Kimi methodology formalization with Don.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEC4-derived methodology:\\r\\n- forensic candidate extracted.\\r\\n- Don intent clarified: AI value discovery + committee signal generation, not Quant edge hunting.\\r\\n- Ready for separate Kimi formalization; do not expose Original Convergence/Quant unless specifically authorized.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAI Judgment:\\r\\n- concept approved; not formalized.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGreenfield AI-built Convergence:\\r\\n- concept approved; later blind design exercise.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCasa Companion:\\r\\n- planned final cross-domain framework test before broad migration/development.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n10. DEVELOPMENT / VALIDATION STRATEGY\\r\\nUse projects as staged framework tests:\\r\\n1. Edge Crew Quant — methodology boundaries, source authority, validation-state separation.\\r\\n2. Edge Crew Convergence family — full-team orchestration, forensic recovery, isolated methodology formalization, handoff fidelity.\\r\\n3. Casa Companion — final generalization test outside sports analytics before broad migration/development.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDo not rush implementation. First prove that the framework preserves intent, role boundaries, provenance, methodology isolation, and handoffs.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n11. NEXT GATES\\r\\n- Preserve this Edge Crew anchor as the return point.\\r\\n- Formalize Original Convergence with a fresh Kimi project.\\r\\n- Formalize EC4-derived Value/Committee methodology in a separate fresh Kimi project.\\r\\n- Keep the two blind to one another and blind to Quant unless Don explicitly changes that rule.\\r\\n- Later perform cross-method capability-gap analysis at the framework level.\\r\\n- Kimi may identify conceptual gaps; GLM translates approved methodologies into architecture/capability requirements.\\r\\n- Do not add a new methodology merely because a feature is missing; first determine whether the gap belongs to Shared Services, architecture, data, verification, operations, or implementation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS: PROCEED\\r\\nCONFIDENCE: 99%\\r\\nREASON: Edge Crew intent, framework, historical recovery, methodology boundaries, and current checkpoints are aligned and explicitly separated.\\r\\nNEXT GATE: Fresh methodology formalization passes, starting with Original Convergence and EC4-derived Value/Committee lineage.\\r\\nDON INPUT NEEDED: Only genuine methodology decisions surfaced by those independent passes.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2026-09-06 ADDENDUM — PRINCIPAL CONSULTANT CROSS-PROJECT USE\\r\\nPrincipal Consultant — Technical Translation / Integration is now an approved GCE cross-functional seat available to Edge Crew and EC⁸ sibling branches. It is not an Edge Crew methodology and does not change Edge Crew branch boundaries.\\r\\nFor Edge Crew use, the seat may reconcile approved Kimi methodology / Design & Build with approved Chiave architecture and package the result for Implementation/Talon. It may identify gaps, record drift, and no-coder-discretion surfaces, but may not rewrite methodology, redefine architecture, create governance authority, execute, or certify.\\r\\nThe older Prompt / Context Translation candidate function remains a separate historical record unless Don explicitly consolidates or supersedes it. Do not silently merge the two roles.\\r\\nRuntime/model for Principal Consultant is not locked; 2026-09-06 audition evidence is filed separately in Model Onboarding.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1G9AmyEqDi1gGtSTptFjICKbFOH8I29nDgfrIe4_s1HI/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"08_PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS_FOR_CHATGPT\",\"id\":\"1G9AmyEqDi1gGtSTptFjICKbFOH8I29nDgfrIe4_s1HI\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"3171\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T03:24:17.730Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T11:49:13.682Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-06T11:49:13.682Z\",\"display_title\":\"08_PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS_FOR_CHATGPT\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1G9AmyEqDi1gGtSTptFjICKbFOH8I29nDgfrIe4_s1HI/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1-2XT7kaaOIIu8aqjcGFIPF_ktPF0N9vQ\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿ChatGPT Project Instructions — EC⁸ AI Convergence\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nYou are Coda operating as Strategic Advisor / Governance for the EC⁸ AI Convergence project.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPURPOSE\\r\\nBuild the AI Convergence branch of EC⁸ from scratch through the GCE process.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nBRAND / BRANCH MODEL\\r\\n- EC⁸ = parent intelligence platform\\r\\n- Edge Crew = quantitative / mathematical intelligence\\r\\n- AI Convergence = separate sibling branch; final branch name may be decided later\\r\\n- Do not use Edge Crew as the umbrella for non-quantitative methodologies\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFOUNDATIONAL GCE DOCTRINE\\r\\nIDENTITY != ROLE != LENS != PERSONALITY != AUTHORITY != MODEL.\\r\\nMODEL != SEAT.\\r\\nStable seat identity survives runtime substitution.\\r\\nContext breadth does not grant authority breadth.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT SEATS\\r\\n- Don — Vision / Final Authority / interim human orchestrator\\r\\n- Coda — Strategic Governance\\r\\n- Kimi — Technical Stack Methodology / Design & Build\\r\\n- Chiave — Architecture\\r\\n- Talon — Operations\\r\\n- Luce — Verification / Ground Truth\\r\\n- Data / Intelligence — shared service\\r\\n- QA / Validation — approved vacant shared service\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCODA OWNS\\r\\ngovernance; authority boundaries; framework integrity; canon/supersession control; cross-seat reconciliation; Don decision framing.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCODA MUST NOT ABSORB\\r\\nKimi methodology / Design & Build; Chiave architecture; Talon operations; Luce verification; implementation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPROCESS\\r\\nDon intent → Coda governance framing → Kimi methodology → Chiave architecture when materially required → Kimi Design & Build → implementation → Talon operations → Luce verification → Coda reconciliation → Don decision.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSOURCE DISCIPLINE\\r\\nEdge Crew Quant != AI Convergence.\\r\\nEC3 and EC4 are evidence, not automatic canon.\\r\\nNewer != canonical.\\r\\nDo not silently merge conflicting sources.\\r\\nDo not infer authority from filenames.\\r\\nHistorical records remain provenance.\\r\\nSupersessions are additive, not rewrites.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCLAIM DISCIPLINE\\r\\nDistinguish material claims as FACT / GIVEN, DERIVED, PROPOSED, UNKNOWN, VERIFIED, OUTSIDE AUTHORITY.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKIMI BOUNDARY\\r\\nKimi owns methodology of the technical stack and Design & Build direction. Kimi may recommend tools, components, prototypes, workflows, build packages, and technical test requirements. Kimi routes durable topology, interfaces, architecture boundaries, security architecture, and failure-domain rulings to Chiave. Kimi routes deployment and sustained operations to Talon. Kimi does not make governance decisions.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCHIAVE BOUNDARY\\r\\nChiave owns architecture when architecture is materially required. Do not turn Architecture into a choke point for ordinary technical choices.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nLUCE BOUNDARY\\r\\nLuce certifies evidence / execution. Verification does not itself create substantive decision authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT PROJECT STATE\\r\\nMethodology is not yet locked. DeepSeek/Talon EC4 methodology recovery has returned but must be reviewed as evidence before it is introduced to Kimi. Do not code before the methodology gate is accepted.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRESPONSE PROTOCOL FOR SUBSTANTIVE FRAMEWORK ANSWERS\\r\\nDATE: YYYY-MM-DD\\r\\nSESSION: <current>\\r\\nSEAT: Coda — Strategic Advisor / Governance\\r\\nCURRENT GATE: <gate>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n<body>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS: PROCEED / CHECKPOINT / STOP\\r\\nCONFIDENCE: X%\\r\\nREASON: ...\\r\\nNEXT GATE: ...\\r\\nDON INPUT NEEDED: Yes / No\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTYLE\\r\\nBe concise, exact, and direct. Do not jump gates. Do not invent organizational decisions. Own Coda governance/prompt mistakes directly.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2026-09-06 ADDENDUM — PRINCIPAL CONSULTANT\\r\\nAdd current seat: Principal Consultant — Technical Translation / Integration.\\r\\nOwns methodology↔architecture traceability, implementation-contract translation, discrepancy/blocker classification, no-coder-discretion boundaries, routed questions, and unified downstream handoff.\\r\\nDoes not own methodology, architecture, governance, implementation, operations, or verification.\\r\\nCurrent process: Don → Coda → Kimi methodology → Chiave architecture when required → Kimi Design & Build → Principal Consultant translation/reconciliation → Implementation → Talon → Luce → Coda → Don.\\r\\nCurrent project state: methodology and Architecture Specification v1.0 exist and are broadly aligned; Phase 0/1 are generally startable while named Phase-2 semantic/interface surfaces remain subject to reconciliation. Principal Consultant runtime is not locked; audition evidence must not be treated as seat authority.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fcXEa980Z2xzDtAVWieeNCdvbyk5ABTZERfHXuLmcHg/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"GCE_EDGE_CREW_CLEANUP_RESTRUCTURE_STATUS_2026-09-02.md\",\"id\":\"1fcXEa980Z2xzDtAVWieeNCdvbyk5ABTZERfHXuLmcHg\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"4790\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-02T19:12:03.021Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-02T19:12:05.286Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-02T19:12:05.286Z\",\"display_title\":\"GCE_EDGE_CREW_CLEANUP_RESTRUCTURE_STATUS_2026-09-02.md\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1fcXEa980Z2xzDtAVWieeNCdvbyk5ABTZERfHXuLmcHg/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1hVjoAIajSm8ULRTjQqYjrn5usENclr6D\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿# GCE EDGE CREW — CLEANUP, RESTRUCTURE & STATUS\\r\\n**Checkpoint / Bookmark:** 2026-09-02  \\r\\n**Owner:** Don  \\r\\n**Strategic Framework:** Coda  \\r\\n**Primary Project:** EdgeCrew\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 1. PURPOSE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis document is the working bookmark for the EdgeCrew project after the latest framework decisions.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nIt is intentionally focused on:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- current EdgeCrew status\\r\\n- ambiguity cleanup\\r\\n- naming / methodology separation\\r\\n- future filesystem cleanup and restructuring\\r\\n- what is decided now\\r\\n- what is explicitly NOT decided yet\\r\\n- the next forensic pass on the existing Desktop EdgeCrew material\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis is a **working authority / checkpoint document**, not final canon.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 2. PUBLIC BRAND VS INTERNAL METHODS\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n### Public brand\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**EdgeCrew**\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe public-facing brand remains EdgeCrew.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n### Internal reality\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThere are currently two materially different EdgeCrew methodologies.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThey must **not** be distinguished primarily by version numbers such as:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- EdgeCrew v4\\r\\n- EdgeCrew v8\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThat naming creates false chronology and implies that one methodology is simply a later release of the other.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThey are different operating models under the same public brand.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 3. INTERNAL METHOD FAMILY — APPROVED DIRECTION\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n### A. EdgeCrew Quant\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nWorking internal identifier:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n`EC_QUANT`\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent implementation / lane:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n`EC_QUANT_KIMI`\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCharacteristics:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- Kimi-led\\r\\n- math / edge-finding driven\\r\\n- isolated desktop workflow\\r\\n- single-project / single-chat method\\r\\n- no convergence requirement\\r\\n- analysis produces edges / picks\\r\\n- Kalshi market sanity-check layer is being added\\r\\n- gaps and weak reasoning are expected to be surfaced and corrected\\r\\n- this process should remain isolated from the broader machine-convergence architecture unless explicitly integrated later\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis is the Kimi EdgeCrew process currently being stabilized through live daily use.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n### B. EdgeCrew Convergence\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nWorking internal identifier:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n`EC_CONVERGENCE`\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCharacteristics:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- Don-led methodology\\r\\n- machine-based multi-AI workflow\\r\\n- uses multiple specialized seats / models\\r\\n- may include data retrieval, analysis, validation, adversarial verification, routing, retries, escalation, confidence adjustment, and convergence\\r\\n- orchestration architecture is still being formalized\\r\\n- not the same methodology as Kimi's Quant lane\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis is the broader GCE / machine EdgeCrew methodology.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 4. NAMING PRINCIPLE — LOCKED\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe EdgeCrew naming model is:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n`Brand != Methodology != Implementation != Version`\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMeaning:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Brand:** EdgeCrew\\r\\n- **Methodology:** Quant / Convergence\\r\\n- **Implementation or lane:** Kimi / Machine / future implementation\\r\\n- **Version:** revision inside that specific methodology\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVersion numbers must not be used as the primary identity of different methodologies.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n### Example\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nInstead of:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n`EdgeCrew v4`\\r\\n`EdgeCrew v8`\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nUse:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n`EdgeCrew Quant`\\r\\n`EdgeCrew Convergence`\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThen version within the method if needed:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n`EdgeCrew Quant — Q1`\\r\\n`EdgeCrew Quant — Q2`\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n`EdgeCrew Convergence — C1`\\r\\n`EdgeCrew Convergence — C2`\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nImplementation revisions may separately use conventional versioning such as:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n`1.0`\\r\\n`1.1`\\r\\n`2.0`\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOnly after the methodology is identified.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 5. KIMI EDGE CREW — CURRENT STATUS\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Kimi lane has been deliberately isolated.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent understanding:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- one desktop project\\r\\n- one active chat / context\\r\\n- math-first edge finding\\r\\n- no multi-agent convergence\\r\\n- market sanity checking is being incorporated\\r\\n- Kalshi is being introduced as an external market sanity-check layer\\r\\n- Data Hound can provide the structured data / market context needed by Kimi\\r\\n- Kimi remains responsible for the analytical edge-finding methodology\\r\\n- gaps from prior runs are useful evidence for process improvement, not proof of failure\\r\\n- Kimi has shown willingness to identify sloppy prior work and adjust the methodology\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe framework should **protect this process from being contaminated by the machine-convergence architecture** simply because both are called EdgeCrew.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 6. MACHINE EDGE CREW — CURRENT STATUS\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe machine-based EdgeCrew remains a separate methodology.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent desired operating pattern includes specialized functions such as:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- Don / orchestration authority\\r\\n- strategic framework / governance\\r\\n- operations\\r\\n- data acquisition\\r\\n- analytical reasoning\\r\\n- verification / Truth Teller\\r\\n- QA / testing\\r\\n- confidence / escalation\\r\\n- bounded execution\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe exact orchestration implementation is still evolving.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nImportant current insight:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nA subordinate may receive broad mission context while retaining narrow execution authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n`Context breadth != authority breadth`\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis has been demonstrated operationally by DeepSeek-based seats.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 7. EDGE CREW DATA / ANALYSIS LOOP — EMERGING PATTERN\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent useful pattern:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n`Data acquisition`\\r\\n→ `Kimi analysis`\\r\\n→ `Kalshi / market sanity check`\\r\\n→ `gap / disagreement detection`\\r\\n→ `confidence adjustment`\\r\\n→ `final recommendation / picks`\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis does **not** automatically make the Kimi lane a convergence system.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nIt remains an edge-finding methodology with explicit sanity checking.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe distinction is important.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 8. CLEANUP TARGET — EXISTING DESKTOP EDGE CREW MATERIAL\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nWhen Don has sufficient time and focus, the next dedicated cleanup exercise will target the existing **EdgeCrew 4 folder on the Desktop**.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThat exercise should use the same evidence-first method now being used successfully elsewhere.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe first task is **not** to rename it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe first task is to determine what it actually contains.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe forensic questions are:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n1. Which components are Quant?\\r\\n2. Which components are Convergence?\\r\\n3. Which components are shared infrastructure?\\r\\n4. Which components are historical?\\r\\n5. Which components are duplicated?\\r\\n6. Which components are mislabeled by old version-number naming?\\r\\n7. Which components are path-sensitive?\\r\\n8. Which components are actively referenced?\\r\\n9. Which components are safe to relocate later?\\r\\n10. Which components belong to a different project despite an EdgeCrew-like name?\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNo cleanup should occur until those questions are answered.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 9. FUTURE PHYSICAL STRUCTURE — CONCEPT ONLY\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nA possible future structure is:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n```text\\r\\nGCE_EdgeCrew/\\r\\n├── Quant/\\r\\n│   └── Kimi/\\r\\n├── Convergence/\\r\\n│   └── Machine/\\r\\n├── Shared/\\r\\n├── Evidence/\\r\\n└── Archive/\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis is **NOT approved as the final physical tree yet**.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nIt is only a conceptual target used to clarify method separation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe actual filesystem structure must be derived from the forensic inventory of the existing EdgeCrew folders and their dependencies.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 10. CLEANUP RULES\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFor the future EdgeCrew cleanup pass:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- inventory first\\r\\n- classify second\\r\\n- dependency-map third\\r\\n- rename / move only after evidence\\r\\n- do not rely on folder names as truth\\r\\n- do not assume newest = current\\r\\n- do not assume higher version = better / later methodology\\r\\n- do not merge Quant and Convergence merely because both are EdgeCrew\\r\\n- preserve historical evidence\\r\\n- isolate name traps\\r\\n- verify hard-coded paths before moves\\r\\n- preserve working systems until replacement paths are tested\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 11. WHAT IS DECIDED NOW\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n### Locked / Proceed\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- EdgeCrew remains the public brand.\\r\\n- Kimi's methodology is distinct from the machine-convergence methodology.\\r\\n- Version numbers will no longer serve as the primary identity separating these methodologies.\\r\\n- Internal semantic naming is preferred:\\r\\n  - `EC_QUANT`\\r\\n  - `EC_CONVERGENCE`\\r\\n- `EC_QUANT_KIMI` is a valid working identifier for the current Kimi implementation.\\r\\n- The current Kimi desktop workflow remains isolated.\\r\\n- The future Desktop EdgeCrew cleanup will be evidence-first.\\r\\n- The existing EdgeCrew 4 folder will be investigated before being renamed or reorganized.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 12. WHAT IS NOT DECIDED YET\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- final physical EdgeCrew folder tree\\r\\n- final canonical names\\r\\n- final revision / version syntax\\r\\n- whether Quant and Convergence share one physical parent or only a brand namespace\\r\\n- what from the existing EdgeCrew 4 folder belongs to each method\\r\\n- what can safely be archived\\r\\n- which shared components should be centralized\\r\\n- final orchestration implementation for Convergence\\r\\n- whether a dedicated Orchestrator seat exists or whether orchestration is primarily system logic\\r\\n- final machine handoff / fork / merge implementation\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 13. IMPORTANT RELATED FRAMEWORK DISTINCTIONS\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n### Data Hound vs Truth Teller\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Data Hound**\\r\\nasks:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n`What does the evidence / data say?`\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Truth Teller**\\r\\nasks:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n`Is the claim actually true, and what evidence would falsify it?`\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThese are separate functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n### Operations vs Strategic Advisor\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Operations / Talon**\\r\\n- recon\\r\\n- sequencing\\r\\n- execution\\r\\n- testing\\r\\n- stop boundaries\\r\\n- operational reconciliation\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Strategic Advisor / Coda**\\r\\n- framework integrity\\r\\n- role boundaries\\r\\n- governance\\r\\n- ambiguity resolution\\r\\n- cross-seat reconciliation\\r\\n- decision routing\\r\\n- Proceed / Checkpoint / Stop calls\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n### Fork semantics\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent conversational \\\"fork\\\" behavior is not yet a real technical fork.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDesired future meaning:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- `FORK` = create independent child workstream\\r\\n- `HOLD` = preserve state with no execution\\r\\n- `RESUME` = reactivate preserved lane\\r\\n- `MERGE` = return conclusions / artifacts to parent\\r\\n- `CLOSE` = terminate and archive lane state\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis remains an orchestration architecture item.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 14. CURRENT EDGE CREW CHECKPOINT\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n### Status\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Framework direction:** Proceed  \\r\\n**Physical restructure:** Not started  \\r\\n**Kimi Quant methodology:** Active and being refined  \\r\\n**Convergence methodology:** Active concept / implementation evolving  \\r\\n**Desktop EdgeCrew 4 cleanup:** Pending dedicated forensic pass\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n### Current working statement\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n> EdgeCrew is one public brand with multiple internal methodologies.  \\r\\n> Kimi's EdgeCrew is a Quant / edge-finding methodology.  \\r\\n> Don's machine EdgeCrew is a Convergence methodology.  \\r\\n> They must not be distinguished merely by version numbers.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 15. BOOKMARK — RETURN POINT\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nWhen this EdgeCrew thread is resumed, begin here:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n### Next major action\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Forensic inventory of the existing Desktop EdgeCrew 4 folder.**\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGoal:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDetermine the actual contents, dependencies, methodology ownership, duplicates, history, and name traps before any rename or move.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n### Required output from that future pass\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- current-state map\\r\\n- Quant components\\r\\n- Convergence components\\r\\n- Shared components\\r\\n- historical / provenance items\\r\\n- duplicate families\\r\\n- path-sensitive dependencies\\r\\n- name traps\\r\\n- safe cleanup candidates\\r\\n- review-required items\\r\\n- proposed future structure\\r\\n- confidence bucket\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNo filesystem cleanup until that report is reviewed.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 16. CHECKPOINT\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**CHECKPOINT / BOOKMARK CREATED**\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEdgeCrew naming ambiguity has been resolved at the framework level.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe next EdgeCrew filesystem action is intentionally deferred until a focused forensic pass of the existing Desktop EdgeCrew 4 folder.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Confidence: Proceed / Go / Capiche — 100% on the methodology distinction and checkpoint.**\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Confidence: Checkpoint / Review on the final physical restructure until the forensic inventory is complete.**\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1cVD0XgrN5tOIUzPmUW9ZrgsidWmr1R0_3nf_BwgnyPQ/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"09_NEW_PROJECT_CHAT_BOOTSTRAP\",\"id\":\"1cVD0XgrN5tOIUzPmUW9ZrgsidWmr1R0_3nf_BwgnyPQ\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"3787\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T03:24:38.471Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T15:55:39.037Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-06T15:55:39.037Z\",\"display_title\":\"09_NEW_PROJECT_CHAT_BOOTSTRAP\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1cVD0XgrN5tOIUzPmUW9ZrgsidWmr1R0_3nf_BwgnyPQ/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1-2XT7kaaOIIu8aqjcGFIPF_ktPF0N9vQ\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿New Project Chat Bootstrap — EC⁸ AI Convergence\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGround yourself in the attached EC⁸ AI Convergence knowledge base.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nWe are building the AI Convergence branch of EC⁸ from scratch through the GCE framework.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEC⁸ is the parent.\\r\\nEdge Crew is the quantitative / mathematical branch.\\r\\nAI Convergence is a separate sibling branch.\\r\\nEdge Crew Quant != AI Convergence.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent seats:\\r\\n- Don — Vision / Final Authority / interim human orchestrator\\r\\n- Coda — Strategic Governance\\r\\n- Kimi — Technical Stack Methodology / Design & Build\\r\\n- Chiave — Architecture\\r\\n- Talon — Operations\\r\\n- Luce — Verification / Ground Truth\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent sequence:\\r\\nDon intent → Coda governance → Kimi methodology → Chiave architecture when materially required → Kimi Design & Build → implementation → Talon operations → Luce verification → Coda reconciliation → Don decision.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDeepSeek/Talon has already returned an EC4 methodology recovery package. Treat it as evidence, not automatic canon.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nImmediate next gate:\\r\\nreview the DeepSeek recovery, isolate the clean AI Convergence methodology, preserve conflicts/unknowns, and prepare the methodology package for Kimi.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDo not import EC3 or Edge Crew Quant by default.\\r\\nDo not silently merge conflicting historical material.\\r\\nDo not start coding before methodology is accepted.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2026-09-06 BOOTSTRAP ADDENDUM\\r\\nAdd current seat: Principal Consultant — Technical Translation / Integration.\\r\\nCurrent sequence: Don → Coda → Kimi methodology → Chiave architecture when required → Kimi Design & Build → Principal Consultant translation/reconciliation → Implementation → Talon → Luce → Coda → Don.\\r\\nCurrent state supersedes the old immediate-next-gate language above: methodology and Architecture Specification v1.0 now exist; the project is post-architecture-gate, pre-implementation. Phase 0/1 are generally startable; named Phase-2 contract seams require reconciliation before coding those surfaces.\\r\\nPrincipal Consultant runtime/model is not locked. Ground future chats in the Principal Consultant onboarding/audition record before making runtime assumptions\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2026-09-06 BOOTSTRAP ADDENDUM — RUNTIME DESIGN / NEW-CHAT STATE\\r\\nCurrent verified technical state:\\r\\n- Corrected handoff package has K1–K9 physically applied and verified.\\r\\n- Chiave Architecture v1.1 exists.\\r\\n- The project is post-methodology/post-architecture and is now in runtime/design selection before implementation.\\r\\n- Phase 0/1 foundation work remains generally startable; semantic/runtime surfaces still require the final design/constraint pass before implementation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent working organizational refinement — PROPOSED, not yet final canon:\\r\\nDon → Coda governance → Kimi methodology → Chiave architecture when required → Principal Consultant specification/translation → Independent Design & Build [provisional] → Talon operational routing → Keel build/deploy/implementation test/evidence return → Luce independent verification → Coda reconciliation → Don.\\r\\nDo not silently convert this proposal into canon; preserve the prior combined Kimi Design & Build record until Don explicitly locks the new seat topology.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRuntime Design audition state:\\r\\n- Grok 4.6 produced EC8 Runtime Design v1.0 and a Value-Optimized Profile V. Strong live-environment interrogation; tested Nova current-path behavior; current value profile approximately $0.436 per 53-call slate under its token assumptions.\\r\\n- GLM 5.1 produced Independent Runtime / Model Design Pass v1.0. Recommended Balanced Profile B at approximately $0.397 per 53-call slate; Nova-heavy and Bedrock-native on paper; direct Nova executability is being tested now.\\r\\n- No runtime roster is approved. Treat all model IDs, availability, structured-output support, pricing, and token assumptions as PROPOSED/UNKNOWN until live verified where required.\\r\\n- Important comparison issue: GLM Profile B's stated L3 fallback uses Llama while Llama is also in its analyst pool; this appears to violate the outside-pool L3 constraint and must be corrected before adoption.\\r\\n- Nova is NOT permanently excluded. Prior Grok/Talon current-path failure is execution evidence, not a governance decision. GLM is now testing whether a viable Nova invocation path exists.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPrincipal Consultant audition state:\\r\\n- Luna remains leading routine/default candidate (~$0.03 observed).\\r\\n- Sol is being tested as a possible low-cost deeper second-pass tier (~$0.47 observed at current point).\\r\\n- Kimi/ChatGPT swarm remains a major-lock audit placeholder.\\r\\n- Astra has moved into premium-forensic economics (~$4.64+ observed during current audition); Fable remains the earlier premium forensic benchmark (~$4.86 observed).\\r\\n- Runtime stack remains PROPOSED; no Principal Consultant model is locked.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nImmediate next work for a new project chat:\\r\\n1. Ground in the new current handoff document and the corrected K1–K9 package + Architecture v1.1.\\r\\n2. Receive/inspect GLM's Nova test and any final tangent findings.\\r\\n3. Reconcile Grok Profile V vs GLM Profile B slot-by-slot on VALUE, not cheapest price.\\r\\n4. Verify live model IDs / Nova path / family constraints before any runtime canon decision.\\r\\n5. Continue Principal Consultant Sol/Astra audition comparison only as needed; extract reusable defect classes into the GCE review checklist.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNEW-CHAT GROUNDING ANCHOR\\r\\nPrimary current handoff: 10_CURRENT_HANDOFF_2026-09-06_RUNTIME_DESIGN\\r\\nDrive ID: 1SLU50Xz-ujenM6hGHdweEhNIJTvAkNFhjzJuI66MDOU\\r\\nStart there before interpreting older bootstrap text.\\r\\n.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1WEQjl0JlK-x-JPK-S2UUdJpoiXxvAfAY1ntZ-0d3wWM/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"00_PROJECT_README\",\"id\":\"1WEQjl0JlK-x-JPK-S2UUdJpoiXxvAfAY1ntZ-0d3wWM\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"2546\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T03:21:49.047Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T15:51:04.124Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-06T15:51:04.124Z\",\"display_title\":\"00_PROJECT_README\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1WEQjl0JlK-x-JPK-S2UUdJpoiXxvAfAY1ntZ-0d3wWM/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1-2XT7kaaOIIu8aqjcGFIPF_ktPF0N9vQ\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿EC⁸ — AI Convergence Project\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPurpose\\r\\nBuild the AI Convergence branch of EC⁸ from scratch through the GCE process.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEC⁸ is the parent intelligence platform.\\r\\nEdge Crew is the quantitative / mathematical intelligence branch.\\r\\nAI Convergence is a separate sibling branch and must not inherit Edge Crew Quant methodology by default.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent project state\\r\\n- Parent brand: EC⁸\\r\\n- Quantitative branch: Edge Crew\\r\\n- AI Convergence branch name: TBD\\r\\n- GCE framework: active\\r\\n- Kimi seat: validated for Technical Stack Methodology / Design & Build\\r\\n- DeepSeek/Talon EC4 methodology recovery: returned to Don, not yet incorporated into this package\\r\\n- Immediate next gate: review recovered EC4 methodology as evidence, then establish the clean methodology package for Kimi\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCore rule\\r\\nHistorical EC3/EC4 material is evidence, not automatic canon.\\r\\nEdge Crew Quant != AI Convergence.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2026-09-06 PROJECT INDEX UPDATE\\r\\nPrincipal Consultant — Technical Translation / Integration has been added as an approved cross-functional seat. Onboarding/audition evidence is filed under GCE onboarding → 03_Model_Onboarding → Principal_Consultant. The current AI Convergence process now includes a Principal Consultant translation/reconciliation checkpoint between Kimi Design & Build and downstream Implementation/Talon. Runtime/model assignment is not yet locked\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2026-09-06 RUNTIME DESIGN / DELIVERY-CHAIN UPDATE\\r\\nCurrent technical state: K1–K9 methodology corrections are physically applied and verified in the corrected handoff package; Chiave Architecture v1.1 exists. The project is now focused on concrete runtime/model assignment and implementation design, not methodology invention.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPROPOSED / PROVISIONAL authority refinement: Don identified a governance conflict in combining methodology authorship and concrete Design & Build selection under Kimi. Current working topology separates Kimi Technical Stack Methodology from an Independent Design & Build function. This separation is not yet recorded as final canon unless Don explicitly locks the seat; preserve the prior record as provenance.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent runtime-design evidence: Grok 4.6 produced Cost Profile A and Value Profile V; GLM 5.1 produced Cost/Balanced/Maximum-Quality profiles. Both independently converged near the ~$0.40–$0.44 per 53-call slate value band, but with different model populations. No runtime roster is canonical. Nova remains a design candidate with current-path executability under active testing; do not treat prior Nova failure as permanent exclusion.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPrincipal Consultant runtime remains unlocked. Current audition stack under evaluation: Luna as routine/default candidate; Sol/K2.7 as possible deeper single-pass tier; ChatGPT/Kimi swarm as major-lock audit placeholder; Astra/Fable as premium forensic candidates when justified.\\r\\n.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NDhIIIK1xL6YaLEjs4lgF0eP9fdjpJwMl2bvWTw2ko4/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"GCE_SESSION2_CLOSE_CANONICAL_ORG_2026-09-02\",\"id\":\"1NDhIIIK1xL6YaLEjs4lgF0eP9fdjpJwMl2bvWTw2ko4\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"12270\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-02T23:59:48.400Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-08T15:30:12.562Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-08T15:30:12.562Z\",\"display_title\":\"GCE_SESSION2_CLOSE_CANONICAL_ORG_2026-09-02\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NDhIIIK1xL6YaLEjs4lgF0eP9fdjpJwMl2bvWTw2ko4/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1clV7UUxQUcnGLX21ossOWoHGBPs-pM77\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿GCE SESSION 2 CLOSE — CANONICAL ORGANIZATIONAL MODEL\\r\\nDate: 2026-09-02\\r\\nAuthority: Don + Coda\\r\\nStatus: CANONICAL / SESSION CLOSE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPURPOSE\\r\\nPersist the refined organizational source of truth reached at Session 2 close and supersede the earlier interpretation of seven equal Councils.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCANONICAL ORGANIZATIONAL MODEL\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDON\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEXECUTIVE COUNCIL — 4 seats with Don's ear\\r\\n1. Coda — Strategic / Governance\\r\\n2. Kimi — Technical Strategy / Systems Intelligence\\r\\n3. Talon — Operations\\r\\n4. Chiave — Architecture\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThese four are the executive/advisory authority seats. They interpret, challenge, recommend, and route material decisions to Don.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nExecutive hierarchy:\\r\\nDon -> Executive Council seat / Lieutenant -> optional Manager / Capo only where workload creates a distinct management responsibility -> Contract Workers / Soldiers / Specialists.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nManagers are not manufactured for symmetry.\\r\\n- Operations currently justifies Talon -> Keel -> bounded contract workers.\\r\\n- Architecture Manager remains vacant unless workload proves the need.\\r\\n- Strategic/Governance and Technical Strategy do not require permanent Managers merely to satisfy a template.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSHARED ENTERPRISE SERVICES — 3\\r\\n1. Data / Intelligence\\r\\n2. Verification / Ground Truth — Big Pickle\\r\\n3. QA / Validation\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nShared Services are enterprise-wide neutral functions. They do not have Don's standing ear and are not peer Executive Council seats.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nShared Service structure:\\r\\nService Lead / Director-Manager -> bounded Contract Workers / Specialists as needed.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nShared Service rules:\\r\\n- one accountable permanent lead seat\\r\\n- no separate permanent Manager layer unless explicitly redesigned later\\r\\n- identity + narrow functional lens + explicit authority + contracts + provenance/evidence rules + stop/escalation conditions\\r\\n- minimal or no personality by default\\r\\n- personality must never bias data, verification, falsification, or QA outcomes\\r\\n- workers are added only when workload requires them\\r\\n- Shared Services serve all four Executive Council seats and approved projects/workflows\\r\\n- the requesting seat cannot dictate the service result\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVERIFICATION / GROUND TRUTH\\r\\nBig Pickle is a locked identity in the Verification / Ground Truth Shared Service.\\r\\nNarrow lens: evidence -> provenance -> falsification -> verified state.\\r\\nNo rich personality layer is required.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDATA / INTELLIGENCE\\r\\nData Hound is a locked bounded identity used for data/intelligence work. Project assignment does not imply enterprise leadership or redefine organizational reporting.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nLAYER DISTINCTIONS\\r\\nExecutive Council != Shared Enterprise Services != Methodologies != Projects.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMethodologies:\\r\\n- EC_QUANT\\r\\n- EC_CONVERGENCE\\r\\nThese are reusable methods, not departments.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nProjects:\\r\\n- Edge Crew and other project environments\\r\\nProjects consume Executive Council authority, Shared Services, methodologies, managers, and contract workers as needed. Edge Crew is not a Council.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPHYSICAL FILESYSTEM STATE\\r\\nAt Session 2 close, Talon verified seven domain folders existed under GCE_ORG\\\\02_COUNCILS with the standard internal template:\\r\\n- Strategic_Governance\\r\\n- Technical_Strategy_Systems_Intelligence\\r\\n- Operations\\r\\n- Architecture\\r\\n- Data_Intelligence\\r\\n- Verification_Ground_Truth\\r\\n- QA_Validation\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe earlier R34-DIS Architecture-lanes discrepancy was resolved as an incomplete-read false alarm. All seven domain folders exist.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSEMANTIC REFINEMENT\\r\\nThose seven domains are no longer interpreted as seven equal Councils. The current semantic source of truth is:\\r\\n4 Executive Council domains + 3 Shared Enterprise Services.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPhysical placement should be reconciled through the least-destructive approved change. Preserve provenance and historical references.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nIDENTITY / BOOTSTRAP STATE\\r\\n- Coda: locked Strategic / Governance identity; computer/API bootstrap still needs forensic review before local onboarding.\\r\\n- Kimi: locked Technical Strategy / Systems Intelligence seat/function; methodology and technical classification authority.\\r\\n- Talon: locked Operations identity; DeepSeek V4 Flash runtime; operational load root exists.\\r\\n- Keel: locked Operations Manager identity; separate load root exists; fresh isolation rerun remains unproven.\\r\\n- Chiave: locked Architecture identity; GLM 5.1 onboarding runtime of record; Stage 6 qualification administration pending; Stage 7 materialization not authorized.\\r\\n- Big Pickle: locked Verification / Ground Truth Shared Service identity; minimal/no personality by design.\\r\\n- Data Hound: locked bounded data/intelligence identity.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCHIAVE O1 STATE\\r\\nStage 1 COMPLETE\\r\\nStage 2 COMPLETE\\r\\nStage 3 COMPLETE\\r\\nStage 4 COMPLETE / PASS\\r\\nStage 5 COMPLETE / PASS WITH AMENDMENTS\\r\\nStage 6 DESIGN APPROVED / ADMINISTRATION PENDING — NOT STARTED\\r\\nStage 7 CLOSED / NOT AUTHORIZED\\r\\nChiave / GLM is on HOLD.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOPERATIONS CLOSE\\r\\nTalon final reconciliation completed.\\r\\nR34-DIS resolved as false alarm.\\r\\nO-OPS-4 Keel isolation rerun remains OPEN / NOT PROVEN.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSOURCE-OF-TRUTH RULE\\r\\nThis document is the Session 2 organizational close anchor. Where earlier Session 2 framework documents describe seven equal Councils, this document supersedes that interpretation while preserving the earlier material as provenance.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCORE PRINCIPLES PRESERVED\\r\\nIDENTITY != ROLE != LENS != PERSONALITY != AUTHORITY != MODEL.\\r\\nCapability != authority.\\r\\nContext breadth != authority breadth.\\r\\nOne owner per responsibility.\\r\\nOne context per role.\\r\\nMethodology remains separate from sessions and projects.\\r\\nEvidence before destructive change.\\r\\nExplicit handoffs and stop conditions.\\r\\nPersonality/lens never expand authority.\\r\\nRuntime is replaceable; stable seat survives.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS: HOLD\\r\\nCONFIDENCE: 100%\\r\\nREASON: Session 2 organizational model is now defined as 4 Executive Council seats plus 3 Shared Enterprise Services, with remaining validation gates explicitly open rather than implied complete.\\r\\nNEXT GATE: Resume from this anchor; do not reconstruct the organization from prior chat chronology.\\r\\nDON INPUT NEEDED: NONE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSUPERSEDING ORGANIZATIONAL BOARD UPDATE — 2026-09-06\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPRINCIPAL CONSULTANT — APPROVED VACANT SEAT\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe 4 Executive Council + 3 Shared Enterprise Services model remains intact. This update adds one cross-functional solution-definition / delivery-interface seat; it does not create a fifth Executive Council seat or fourth Shared Enterprise Service.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent delivery chain for complex builds:\\r\\nDon / Stakeholder\\r\\n-> relevant Executive Council outputs (Kimi methodology; Chiave architecture; Coda governance as required)\\r\\n-> Principal Consultant\\r\\n-> Talon / Operations\\r\\n-> Keel / build-deploy-test-evidence-return resources\\r\\n-> Luce / Verification-Ground Truth adjudication\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPrincipal Consultant owns one integrated middle-layer function with two internal capabilities:\\r\\n1. Specification / Solution Definition\\r\\n2. Translation / Alignment\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRole purpose: turn frozen upstream intent/methodology/architecture/governance into an implementation-ready specification and translation pack without contaminating or silently rewriting upstream authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOwned output: IMPLEMENTATION SPEC + TRANSLATION PACK.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAuthority boundary: may clarify requirements, expose gaps, define interfaces/schemas/outputs/acceptance criteria, recommend model/function assignments, and translate approved specification into bounded work packages/prompts. May not redefine methodology, architecture, governance, scope, Verification truth state, or execute builds/deployments.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSeat state: APPROVED VACANT / ONBOARDING-READY. Model/runtime/name/animal/personality remain TBD pending controlled audition and standard onboarding gates.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSource-of-truth rule: where the earlier organizational flow jumps directly from Council outputs to Operations for complex solution work, this 2026-09-06 update inserts Principal Consultant as the implementation-readiness interface. Operations authority and the 4+3 organizational model otherwise remain unchanged.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSUPERSEDING ORGANIZATIONAL HARDENING UPDATE — 2026-09-06\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAUTHORITY: Don + Coda\\r\\nSTATUS: CURRENT WORKING CANON — supersedes earlier 4 Executive Council + 3 Shared Enterprise Services interpretation where inconsistent. Historical text remains provenance.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCORE DOCTRINE\\r\\nIDENTITY != ROLE != LENS != PERSONALITY != AUTHORITY != MODEL\\r\\nMODEL != SEAT\\r\\nCLASS != OPERATIONAL ROUTING AUTHORITY\\r\\nOne owner per responsibility. Capability and personality do not expand authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEXECUTIVE COUNCIL — 4\\r\\n1. Coda — Strategic Governance. Current occupant/runtime: ChatGPT 5.6 Sol. Made-person: Coda. Animal: Volpe / Fox. Mafia rank: Consigliere.\\r\\n2. Kimi — Technical Stack Methodology. Current occupant/runtime: Kimi / Moonshot. Seat/function is locked. Made-person name and animal are intentionally NOT assigned yet; do not manufacture them.\\r\\n3. Chiave — Architecture. Current occupant/runtime: GLM / Z.AI. Current working model: GLM 5.3. Made-person: Chiave. Animal: Aquila / Eagle. Mafia rank: Counsel / Lieutenant. Deep/formal architecture remains Chiave.\\r\\n4. Talon — Operations. Current occupant/runtime: DeepSeek. Made-person: Talon. Animal: Tasso / Badger. Mafia rank: Counsel-Lieutenant / Head of Operations. Talon owns routing, sequencing, operational control, work assignment, and bounded low-level implementation directing; Talon does not absorb Chiave architecture.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCoda governs framework integrity across the entire stack and is not another delivery-chain step.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDELIVERY CHAIN — CURRENT\\r\\nDon / stakeholder intent\\r\\n-> Kimi methodology\\r\\n-> Chiave architecture\\r\\n-> Principal Consultant\\r\\n-> Calibro / Implementation Design & Engineer\\r\\n-> Talon / Operations\\r\\n-> Keel / Build-Deploy-Test-Evidence Return\\r\\n-> Coder / implementation workers / contract specialists\\r\\n-> Luce / Verification-Ground Truth\\r\\n-> QA / Validation\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPRINCIPAL CONSULTANT\\r\\nCurrent occupant: ChatGPT 5.6 Luna.\\r\\nState: functionally slotted for routine use; NOT currently being onboarded as a made-person.\\r\\nPurpose: reconciliation, specification, translation, implementation-readiness, blocker/gap exposure, acceptance conditions, and traceable handoff.\\r\\nOwned output remains implementation-ready specification / translation package.\\r\\nAuthority does not include methodology re-authoring, architecture redefinition, governance expansion, build execution, or Verification adjudication.\\r\\nCurrent hardening objective: improve the reusable Principal Consultant prompt for lower verbosity, stronger claim discipline, mechanical blocker routing, and Talon/Keel-ready outputs without invention.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCALIBRO\\r\\nMade-person: Calibro.\\r\\nAnimal: Picchio / Woodpecker.\\r\\nSeat: Implementation Design & Engineer.\\r\\nClass / mafia rank: Capo.\\r\\nCurrent occupant/model: Grok 4.6; occupant is not the seat.\\r\\nPurpose: take accepted methodology + architecture + Principal Consultant package and decide the bounded implementation design: runtime/provider/model assignment, family assignment, gateway/API choice, configuration/parameters, retry/timeout/fallback strategy, cost-quality-reliability tradeoffs, implementation manifests, and implementation-level sequencing.\\r\\nBoundary: Calibro does not rewrite Kimi methodology, amend Chiave architecture, override Coda governance, route Operations as Talon, execute as Keel/Coder, or verify as Luce.\\r\\nOperating identity: exact pins, evidence over brochure, slot-local change over system redesign, reversible PROPOSED choices when evidence is incomplete, and no silent CONFLICT repair.\\r\\nBootstrap state: identity locked; bootstrap substance authored by Calibro; materialization/fresh-session testing is the current gate.\\r\\nRouter doctrine: explicit active seat binding controls. Do not encode model-family = seat. Unknown/ambiguous mapping must STOP / ASK; never default to Luce and never assume every Grok runtime is Calibro.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOPERATIONS EXECUTION FAMILY\\r\\nTalon — Head of Operations / Counsel-Lieutenant.\\r\\nKeel — Operations Manager / Capo; build, deploy, test, evidence return. Keel authority does not include methodology or architecture redesign. Live execution vetting remains a current proof gate.\\r\\nCoder / Implementation Engineer — OPEN permanent seat; actual code production within approved package.\\r\\nBounded contract workers / specialists may execute under approved Operations routing.\\r\\nOperations soldiers remain bounded identities/functions including Falcon Data Hound, Pigeon Transport, Magpie Secretary/Register, and Raven Documentation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVERIFICATION AND QA\\r\\nLuce — made-person Verification / Ground Truth lead; current runtime Big Pickle; animal Lince / Lynx. Luce independently determines supportable truth from evidence and does not build or rewrite upstream design.\\r\\nQA / Validation is a VACANT downstream assurance function positioned AFTER delivery and Verification. It is no longer modeled as a peer Shared Enterprise Service in the current flow.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDATA / INTELLIGENCE RETIREMENT\\r\\nData / Intelligence is RETIRED as a standalone enterprise service. Its useful capabilities may be reallocated later to concrete seats/services when functionally justified.\\r\\nFalcon / Data Hound remains a bounded Operations soldier/function; this does not recreate an enterprise Data / Intelligence service.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSOURCE-OF-TRUTH RULE\\r\\nThis 2026-09-06 hardening block controls current org placement, delivery flow, Principal Consultant placement, Calibro identity/seat, QA placement, and retirement of Data / Intelligence where older sections differ. Preserve older text as provenance; do not silently rewrite history.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT OPEN GATES\\r\\n1. Finish Calibro bootstrap materialization.\\r\\n2. Fresh monitor and phone/session validation for Calibro.\\r\\n3. Vet Keel on a real Talon -> Keel build handoff.\\r\\n4. Audition permanent Coder / Implementation Engineer.\\r\\n5. QA / Validation remains vacant.\\r\\n6. Harden Luna Principal Consultant prompt using cross-project lessons from Luna/Fable/Astra/EdgeCrew/EC8 work.\\r\\n7. Continue bootstrap/router/session-header integrity work as a separate framework lane.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRUNTIME OCCUPANCY UPDATE — 2026-09-07\\r\\nK3 / Corrado — Technical Stack Methodology / Technical Advisor\\r\\nCurrent runtime: K3-256K Thinking, low effort\\r\\nBootstrap status: Corrado bootstrap successfully loaded\\r\\nDoctrine unchanged: MODEL != SEAT; runtime occupancy does not alter seat identity, role, lens, authority, or organizational boundaries.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFRAMEWORK CLOSEOUT UPDATE — 2026-09-08\\r\\nAUTHORITY: Don + Coda\\r\\nSTATUS: CURRENT WORKING STATE / MORNING HANDOFF\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSESSION ISOLATION / BUCKETING\\r\\n- Personal chronology, Vegas/Playa operations, job search, and GCE framework work are being separated into distinct chat/work buckets while preserving cross-reference through anchors and durable artifacts.\\r\\n- Framework work should not reopen personal chronology unless explicitly relevant.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT ORGANIZATIONAL / DELIVERY STATE\\r\\n- Core doctrine remains: IDENTITY != ROLE != LENS != PERSONALITY != AUTHORITY != MODEL; MODEL != SEAT; CLASS != OPERATIONAL ROUTING AUTHORITY.\\r\\n- Current complex-build route remains: Corrado methodology -> Coda governance as needed -> Chiave architecture -> Luce pre-PC certification -> Ragno packaging -> Calibro implementation design -> Talon routing -> Keel build/deploy/test/evidence -> Luce execution verification -> QA when staffed.\\r\\n- Coda governs framework integrity across the stack rather than acting as a sequential delivery hop.\\r\\n- Ragno/Principal Consultant is now actively demonstrated as a seat occupied by K3/Kimi Swarm for scraper packaging; MODEL != SEAT was preserved.\\r\\n- Calibro identity is locked as Implementation Design & Engineer / Picchio-Woodpecker / Capo; Grok 4.6 current occupant.\\r\\n- Talon remains Operations owner; Keel owns build/deploy/test/evidence return; Luce independently verifies and does not repair or redesign.\\r\\n- Falcon/Data Hound remains a bounded Operations soldier used for evidence hunts and reconciliation, not a restored enterprise Data/Intelligence service.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHANDOFF / MATERIALIZATION DOCTRINE — CONFIRMED\\r\\n- Singular live handoff bus is Operations\\\\06_HANDOFFS\\\\<RECEIVING_SEAT>\\\\.\\r\\n- Legacy GCE_DON\\\\03_HANDOFFS is frozen for new writes; no bulk migration.\\r\\n- Complete downstream handoff artifact must be materialized; terminal/session output alone is not a handoff.\\r\\n- Artifact ownership != transport routing: authoritative artifact stays with owner; transport copy goes to receiving seat lane.\\r\\n- New operational lesson confirmed overnight: DELIVERED != DISCOVERED != VERIFIED. Consumer-side reconciliation/adjudication state is required; a file existing in a receiving lane does not prove the receiving seat has consumed it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKIMI LOAD-SURFACE CLEANUP — CLOSED\\r\\n- Luce audit identified dead/contaminated Kimi load-surface residue including Notion MCP residue, stale plugin duplicates, secret-bearing backups, orphan kimi-chat-cleanup, fabricated SWARM/AgentSwarm behavior mappings, and emoji transcript contamination.\\r\\n- Don approved bounded D1-D4 cleanup; Keel executed and materialized the return.\\r\\n- Falcon later proved the execution/return artifact existed after a pickup visibility miss.\\r\\n- Luce independently re-verified on disk and returned PASS at 94% confidence.\\r\\n- Kimi cleanup is EXECUTED + VERIFIED + CLOSED.\\r\\n- D5 session history and D6 emoji transcripts remained untouched as ordered.\\r\\n- Moonshot credential rotation remains a separate OPEN Don/Operations credential item; deletion of exposed copies does not equal rotation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMAILROOM POC — CONDITIONAL PASS / DEFECT ROUTED\\r\\n- Luce independently reproduced Keel evidence and returned CONDITIONAL PASS at 84%.\\r\\n- 9/9 golden tests passed, but Luce found a real CLI send-path defect missed by the harness: send normalized don_input_needed and refs into representations rejected by controller ingest, causing CLI-sent items to dead-letter.\\r\\n- Defect owner: Keel. Required fix: align representations and add test_send_roundtrip. Do not operate CLI seat send path until fixed.\\r\\n- O1 dead_letter FK deviation remains a separate architecture/governance item for Coda.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCROSS-PROVIDER SCRAPER / INGESTION WAVE 1 — VERIFIED / ACCEPTANCE CLOSED\\r\\n- Keel completed Wave-1 build/test/evidence.\\r\\n- Luce independently reproduced fresh pytest execution: 35/35 PASS, exit 0.\\r\\n- 16/16 verification objectives passed; import-graph guard and secrets sweep passed; no blockers.\\r\\n- Core invariant preserved: RAW != NORMALIZED != CLASSIFIED != KNOWLEDGE != CANON != ARTIFACT.\\r\\n- G1-G6 governance preserved.\\r\\n- Kimi remains the only demonstrated live provider adapter; ChatGPT/Claude remain non-live/stub paths unless separately authorized.\\r\\n- C4 93-vs-106 count conflict and C6 live-daemon contract remain explicit holds and were not invented away.\\r\\n- Luce verdict: CONDITIONAL PASS 90% but Wave-1 POC VERIFIED / ACCEPTANCE CLOSED for manifest scope.\\r\\n- Low non-blocking O1-O3 findings route to Calibro for Wave 2; do not reopen Wave 1 design.\\r\\n- Next design discussion is operating model: when scraper runs, who triggers it, Keel execution role, Talon scheduling/routing, Luce selective health verification, and boundaries between ingestion/searchable context/knowledge/canon candidates.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nK3 / RAGNO LAUNCH-PATH DEFECT — PARALLEL FRAMEWORK ITEM\\r\\n- K3 subscription runtime was shown launching from user home rather than GCE_IDENTITY\\\\Ragno, forcing discovery by glob/ls instead of direct bootstrap load.\\r\\n- Luce confirmed this as a launch-path defect; owner Talon, execution Keel, verification Luce.\\r\\n- This does not invalidate the scraper package already produced by Ragno/K3; fix remains parallel framework hygiene.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOVERNIGHT-CREW DESIGN SIGNAL\\r\\n- Falcon hunt and Luce reconciliation demonstrated a real future overnight function: reconcile open handoffs, execution returns, missing materializations, undiscovered inbound work, stale queues, verifier state, and next-route readiness.\\r\\n- Overnight crew must remain mechanical/reconciliation-focused: discover, compare, surface, and route; no architecture redesign or silent closure.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT OPEN FRAMEWORK ITEMS\\r\\n1. Mailroom CLI send-path fix -> Keel -> Luce re-verify.\\r\\n2. Moonshot key rotation -> Don/Operations credential path.\\r\\n3. Recovered Luce mailbox W0/W1 items remain pending dedicated verification sessions; not silently closed.\\r\\n4. K3/Ragno launch-path repair -> Talon -> Keel -> Luce.\\r\\n5. Scraper C6 live daemon probe -> Talon -> Keel -> Luce.\\r\\n6. Scraper Wave-2 O1-O3 -> Calibro.\\r\\n7. C4 93-vs-106 ruling remains Coda -> Don when needed.\\r\\n8. QA/Validation permanent seat remains vacant.\\r\\n9. Permanent implementation coder seat remains open.\\r\\n10. Small Talon/Don review housekeeping and stale ADHOC/W2/O1/P4/P5 sweep are maintenance debt, not current blockers.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMORNING RULE\\r\\n- Do not reopen framework cleanup before the 10:00 interview / 11:00 checkout sequence unless a real blocker appears.\\r\\n- After relocation to Excalibur and stable work setup, resume from this state rather than reconstructing from terminal history.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS: PROCEED\\r\\nCONFIDENCE: 97%\\r\\nOUTCOME: Framework overnight loops reconciled; Kimi cleanup closed; scraper Wave-1 acceptance closed; Mailroom defect isolated and routed; handoff-consumption defect class identified.\\r\\nNEXT ROUTE: Morning interview/logistics first; framework resumes from explicit open items above.\\r\\nDON INPUT NEEDED: NONE before interview.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1SLU50Xz-ujenM6hGHdweEhNIJTvAkNFhjzJuI66MDOU/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"10_CURRENT_HANDOFF_2026-09-06_RUNTIME_DESIGN\",\"id\":\"1SLU50Xz-ujenM6hGHdweEhNIJTvAkNFhjzJuI66MDOU\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"9183\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T15:53:56.977Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T15:55:11.018Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-06T15:55:11.018Z\",\"display_title\":\"10_CURRENT_HANDOFF_2026-09-06_RUNTIME_DESIGN\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1SLU50Xz-ujenM6hGHdweEhNIJTvAkNFhjzJuI66MDOU/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1-2XT7kaaOIIu8aqjcGFIPF_ktPF0N9vQ\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿EC8 AI Convergence — Current Handoff\\r\\nDate: 2026-09-06\\r\\nSession focus: post-architecture runtime design, authority separation, Principal Consultant/runtime auditions\\r\\nSeat: Coda — Strategic Advisor / Governance\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n1. CURRENT PROJECT STATE\\r\\nEC8 AI Convergence is post-methodology, post-architecture, pre-implementation. Don approved the short canon decision establishing the current implementation baseline. Kimi's K1–K9 semantic corrections were ultimately physically applied and independently verified in the corrected handoff package. Chiave Architecture v1.1 exists. The immediate project question is no longer methodology invention; it is concrete runtime/model/provider design, live Bedrock executability, and the delivery-chain authority model that will carry the accepted spec into implementation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPhase posture:\\r\\n- Phase 0 Foundation: generally startable.\\r\\n- Phase 1 Provider/Ledger layer: generally startable.\\r\\n- Phase 2 semantic pipeline: do not treat as fully unblocked until the final runtime/contract checks and remaining architecture/operations constraints are closed.\\r\\n- Phase 3 pilot: not yet.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2. CANON / SOURCE STATE\\r\\nCurrent implementation baseline established by Don:\\r\\n- corrected handoff-zip methodology copy S1, content/hash controlled\\r\\n- Chiave architecture source, now supplemented by EC8_Architecture_v1.1.md\\r\\n- prompts 01–09, content controlled; K7–K9 prompt revisions applied\\r\\n- Reconciliation v0.2 + corrigendum remains the controlling reconciliation record until source corrections replace the need for its temporary interpretations; reconciliation is not methodology or architecture canon\\r\\n- older methodology copy is SUPERSEDED FOR IMPLEMENTATION / PROVENANCE-ONLY\\r\\n- ruling collisions bind by ruling substance/content + source hash until numbering is corrected\\r\\n- OnDemand excluded from pilot\\r\\n- one scheduled MLB game = one slate; multi-game days contain independent slates\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVerified Kimi correction state:\\r\\n- K1 Stage 4 deterministic behavior correction applied\\r\\n- K2 L1/L2 classification semantics applied\\r\\n- K3 machine-checkable G2 threshold/freshness behavior applied\\r\\n- K4 IF-3 gap-request contract applied\\r\\n- K5 cumulative request lifecycle applied\\r\\n- K6 sufficiency-score definitions applied\\r\\n- K7 baseline-lines vs restricted market evidence prompt boundary applied\\r\\n- K8 normalization-tier threshold authority clarified\\r\\n- K9 changed prompts version-bumped\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n3. AUTHORITY / ORGANIZATIONAL TOPOLOGY\\r\\nIMPORTANT: Don identified a governance conflict in the earlier combined Kimi “Technical Stack Methodology / Design & Build” ownership. The methodology author should not be the sole authority selecting the concrete implementation/runtime design that executes that methodology.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent working topology — PROPOSED / PROVISIONAL until Don explicitly locks the new seat:\\r\\nDON — Final Authority / Stakeholder / Decision Owner\\r\\nExecutive Council:\\r\\n- Coda — Strategic Governance: governance, authority, reconciliation, canon\\r\\n- Kimi — Technical Stack Methodology: methodology, technical process, design logic/requirements; not sole concrete runtime selector under the proposed refinement\\r\\n- Chiave — Architecture: system architecture, contracts, durable boundaries\\r\\n- Talon — Operations Authority: routing, operational control, execution flow\\r\\nShared Enterprise Services:\\r\\n- Data / Intelligence\\r\\n- Luce — Verification / Ground Truth\\r\\n- QA / Validation — vacant\\r\\nDelivery / Build Chain:\\r\\n- Principal Consultant — approved seat; Specification + Translation\\r\\n- Independent Design & Build — PROVISIONAL NEW SEAT; exact runtime/provider/model selection, implementation design, detailed build choices, cost/value optimization, runtime assignments\\r\\n- Talon — operational routing / deployment coordination\\r\\n- Keel — Build · Deploy · Implementation/Integration Test · Evidence Return\\r\\n- Soldiers / Contract Workers — bounded tasks (Falcon, Pigeon, Magpie, Raven, etc.)\\r\\n- Luce — independent verification / ground-truth certification\\r\\nReturn path: Luce → Coda reconciliation → Don decision\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMODEL != SEAT. Current Grok 4.6 audition is evidence for the provisional Independent Design & Build function, not a seat identity lock.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n4. PRINCIPAL CONSULTANT STATUS\\r\\nPrincipal Consultant role is APPROVED. Runtime/model is NOT locked.\\r\\nPurpose: consume accepted methodology + architecture + prompts + governing records and produce a downstream-safe Implementation Spec + Translation Pack without redesigning methodology/architecture or making governance decisions.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent audition evidence:\\r\\n- Luna / GPT-5.6 Luna: ~3-cent observed pass; extremely fast; strongest routine/default economics; good consolidation/handoff compression; weaker on deep cross-contract seam discovery and some blocker calibration.\\r\\n- Kimi 2.7 Code/Thinking: deeper bounded review; improved blocker calibration/authority routing after pushback; good escalation candidate.\\r\\n- K3-256K high-thinking swarm: seven-lane major-lock/adversarial audit; completed analysis lanes but consumed the 5-hour Code quota in stress configuration. Smaller/lower-thinking swarm remains a production option to test.\\r\\n- Claude Fable 5.1: strong forensic defect discovery; ~4.86-dollar observed pass; premium-forensic economics.\\r\\n- ChatGPT Astra: current audition spend exceeded ~4.64 dollars before completion; premium-forensic class; final unique-value comparison pending.\\r\\n- ChatGPT Sol: current audition approximately ~0.47 dollars at checkpoint; candidate for the missing middle tier if it catches a meaningful share of Luna's missed seams. Final return pending.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPROPOSED Principal Consultant runtime ladder, not canon:\\r\\n1. Routine/default — Luna\\r\\n2. Deeper single-pass escalation — Sol or Kimi 2.7, based on final evidence\\r\\n3. Major-lock / disputed-package audit — ChatGPT or Kimi swarm\\r\\n4. Premium forensic exception — Astra / Fable only when marginal value justifies cost\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOperating principle: extract premium-review findings into reusable GCE defect classes/checklists so future default-seat passes become cheaper and more reliable.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n5. INDEPENDENT DESIGN & BUILD / RUNTIME DESIGN AUDITIONS\\r\\nThe next concrete problem is to populate the 53-call MLB pilot with actual models/providers/runtime IDs without allowing the methodology author to select the implementation unchallenged.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nA. Grok 4.6 runtime design\\r\\nDrive artifact: EC8_Runtime_Design_Grok_v1.0\\r\\nProfile V addendum: EC8_Runtime_Design_Grok_ProfileV_Addendum_2026-09-06\\r\\nBehavioral strength: strong live-environment curiosity; it attempted Nova rather than only reasoning from documentation. It distinguished VERIFIED/PROPOSED/UNKNOWN reasonably well and re-optimized when Don changed the objective from CHEAPEST to VALUE.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGrok Profile V — current value proposal:\\r\\n- Framing P01: Qwen3 32B\\r\\n- Analyst A Situational: Qwen3 235B\\r\\n- Analyst B Form: Qwen3 235B\\r\\n- Analyst C Structural: DeepSeek V3.2\\r\\n- Analyst D Market: Kimi K2.5\\r\\n- Analyst E Micro: GLM 5\\r\\n- L2-A/B/D: DeepSeek V3.2\\r\\n- L2-C/E: Qwen3 235B\\r\\n- L3 primary: Mistral Large 3\\r\\n- L3 fallback: Claude Haiku 4.5\\r\\n- Normalization P09: Qwen3 32B\\r\\n- L1: deterministic code\\r\\nEstimated under its assumptions: ~0.217 dollars Morning, ~0.217 Pre-Game, ~0.436 per 53-call slate, ~6.54 dollars per 15-slate day, ~196 dollars / 30-day full-cadence month.\\r\\nOpen Grok question: Qwen/DeepSeek concentration may create correlated-reasoning risk despite formal family compliance. Several printed IDs remain to be live-pinned.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nB. GLM 5.1 runtime design\\r\\nDrive artifact: EC8_Runtime_Design_GLM5.1_v1.0\\r\\nGLM independently converged near the same value band but with a different model philosophy.\\r\\nRecommended Profile B — Balanced:\\r\\n- Framing: Amazon Nova Lite\\r\\n- Analyst A Situational: DeepSeek V3.2\\r\\n- Analyst B Form: Mistral Large 3\\r\\n- Analyst C Structural: Llama 3.3 70B\\r\\n- Analyst D Market: MiniMax M2.5\\r\\n- Analyst E Micro: Amazon Nova Pro\\r\\n- L2: mix of Llama / DeepSeek / Nova\\r\\n- L3 primary: Claude 3 Haiku\\r\\n- Normalization: Amazon Nova Lite\\r\\nEstimated: ~0.397 dollars per 53-call slate, ~5.95 dollars per 15-slate day, ~178 dollars/month at full 15-slate/day cadence.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nImportant GLM defect already identified by Coda: the stated Profile B L3 fallback is Llama 3.3 70B while Llama is also used as Analyst C. That appears to violate the architecture requirement that L3/fallback remain outside the analyst pool. Treat Profile B as a candidate, not approved.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGLM currently went on a useful tangent after Don explicitly asked it to test Nova. ACTIVE / NOT YET INGESTED: receive its live Nova invocation result and any corrected runtime observations before final comparison.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n6. NOVA / BEDROCK STATUS\\r\\nDo not confuse DESIGN FIT with CURRENT EXECUTABILITY.\\r\\n- Don specifically wants Amazon Bedrock partly to access Amazon models; Nova remains strategically relevant.\\r\\n- Grok/Talon current-path evidence indicated Nova was not callable through the tested Mantle/current configuration. Grok actually attempted the call; this is valuable execution evidence.\\r\\n- That failure is NOT a governance decision permanently excluding Nova.\\r\\n- GLM Profile B independently recommends Nova heavily on design/value grounds and is now explicitly testing whether it can obtain a live Nova path.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRequired next truth state for Nova:\\r\\nVERIFIED if an exact model + endpoint/API path + region + auth mode + model/inference-profile ID succeeds.\\r\\nPROPOSED if design-fit is strong but no live invocation is proven.\\r\\nUNAVAILABLE ON CURRENT PATH if a specific path fails. Never promote that wording to permanent architectural exclusion without broader evidence/Don decision.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n7. RUNTIME DESIGN DECISION CRITERION\\r\\nDon corrected an earlier Coda prompt bias: do NOT optimize for cheapest model.\\r\\nControlling design objective for comparisons:\\r\\nMAXIMIZE EXPECTED QUALITY + RELIABILITY + METHODOLOGICAL FIDELITY + INDEPENDENCE + COST EFFICIENCY PER DOLLAR.\\r\\nCost is a first-class design variable, not the sole objective and not a hard cap.\\r\\nA more expensive model is justified when it materially buys down a named failure mode. A cheaper model is preferred only when it is materially equivalent for the assigned stage.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nInteresting current convergence:\\r\\n- Grok Profile V ~0.436/slate\\r\\n- GLM Profile B ~0.397/slate\\r\\nThe few cents difference is not a meaningful decision driver. The real decision is stage fit, cognitive diversity, reliability, live availability, structured-output support, and failure/fallback legality.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHigh-interest disagreements for the next comparison:\\r\\n- Framing/Normalization: Qwen vs Nova\\r\\n- Situational: Qwen vs DeepSeek\\r\\n- Form: Qwen vs Mistral Large 3\\r\\n- Structural: DeepSeek vs Llama\\r\\n- Market: Kimi K2.5 vs MiniMax M2.5\\r\\n- Micro: GLM 5 vs Nova Pro\\r\\n- L2 concentration/topology\\r\\n- L3: Mistral Large 3 vs Claude Haiku\\r\\n- exact fallback legality\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n8. DATA-ACQUISITION NOTE\\r\\nDon already developed per-sport data-fetch work with Kimi through the Edge Crew Quant process. Do NOT import that wholesale into AI Convergence yet. Treat it as evidence/reusable-infrastructure candidate only. Later perform a bounded comparison: reusable shared acquisition infrastructure vs quant-specific methodology. Edge Crew Quant != AI Convergence remains controlling.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n9. VISUAL ARCHITECTURE\\r\\nA pipeline diagram was created during the session and materially improved Don's comprehension. It represents:\\r\\nexternal data/scraping → acquisition/store → Prompt 01 framing → five isolated Prompts 02–06 first pass → gap router/evidence acquisition → same-session Prompts 02–06 re-analysis → L1 deterministic + Prompt 07 L2 + Prompt 08 L3 → Prompt 09 normalization → nine-section SAP/artifact store, with provider abstraction/Bedrock, ledger, secrets, checkpoint/resume, observability underneath.\\r\\nTreat the diagram as explanatory, not canonical. Future version should populate the winning exact model/runtime assignments and stage costs after Don selects a roster.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n10. IMMEDIATE NEXT SESSION — DO THIS FIRST\\r\\n1. Ground in this handoff plus:\\r\\n   - corrected K1–K9 handoff package\\r\\n   - EC8 Architecture v1.1\\r\\n   - Reconciliation v0.2 + corrigendum\\r\\n   - EC8_Runtime_Design_Grok_v1.0\\r\\n   - EC8_Runtime_Design_Grok_ProfileV_Addendum_2026-09-06\\r\\n   - EC8_Runtime_Design_GLM5.1_v1.0\\r\\n   - Principal Consultant onboarding record\\r\\n2. Receive GLM 5.1's live Nova test/tangent output. Do not assume result before reading it.\\r\\n3. Receive Sol and Astra Principal Consultant audition outputs if completed. Score unique findings vs Luna/Fable/K2.7, not raw prestige.\\r\\n4. Reconcile Grok Profile V vs GLM Profile B slot-by-slot under VALUE criterion.\\r\\n5. Separate design recommendation from live runtime verification. Flag exact model IDs/support as VERIFIED/PROPOSED/UNKNOWN.\\r\\n6. Correct any L3/fallback family violations before a runtime can be considered compliant.\\r\\n7. Do not pick a canonical runtime roster until Don sees the side-by-side comparison and live Nova/model-ID evidence.\\r\\n8. If organizational topology is to be locked, Don must explicitly approve the provisional Independent Design & Build seat and the methodology/design separation. Until then preserve both the old combined-Kimi record and the proposed refinement as controlled provenance/conflict.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n11. ACTIVE OPEN QUESTIONS\\r\\n- Can GLM actually invoke Nova, and through what exact path?\\r\\n- Does Sol fill the Principal Consultant gap between Luna and premium forensic models?\\r\\n- Does Grok's Qwen/DeepSeek concentration reduce useful cognitive diversity despite formal EX-2 compliance?\\r\\n- Does GLM's Nova/Llama/MiniMax model mix survive live catalog and invocation tests?\\r\\n- Which runtime slots show enough value gain to justify premium spend?\\r\\n- Does Don canonize the Independent Design & Build seat, and if so what is the final seat name/authority language?\\r\\n- Principal Consultant runtime remains unlocked.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n12. SOURCE DISCIPLINE / HARD RULES\\r\\nEdge Crew Quant != AI Convergence.\\r\\nNewer != canonical.\\r\\nDo not silently merge conflicts.\\r\\nHistorical records remain provenance.\\r\\nSupersessions are additive.\\r\\nMODEL != SEAT.\\r\\nContext breadth does not grant authority breadth.\\r\\nImplementation may not invent missing methodology/architecture/governance.\\r\\nLive execution evidence is stronger than unsupported catalog assumptions, but a failed path is not automatically a permanent system-level prohibition.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS: PROCEED / CHECKPOINT\\r\\nReason: methodology and architecture corrections are mature enough to evaluate concrete runtime designs. Runtime roster, Nova path, Principal Consultant runtime tiering, and the proposed Independent Design & Build seat are not yet canonical.\\r\\nNext gate: ingest GLM Nova tangent + outstanding auditions → Coda side-by-side runtime reconciliation → Don decision framing.\\r\\nDon input needed: not until the comparison is ready, except explicit seat-topology canonization if Don chooses to lock it sooner.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ym-YfYi-O3AAtONDiE5CZW42bS3RIvjohNFf5Z2yUas/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"EC8_Runtime_Design_Grok_v1.0\",\"id\":\"1ym-YfYi-O3AAtONDiE5CZW42bS3RIvjohNFf5Z2yUas\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"11094\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T15:52:45.053Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T15:52:46.890Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-06T15:52:46.890Z\",\"display_title\":\"EC8_Runtime_Design_Grok_v1.0\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ym-YfYi-O3AAtONDiE5CZW42bS3RIvjohNFf5Z2yUas/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1-2XT7kaaOIIu8aqjcGFIPF_ktPF0N9vQ\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿# EC8 AI Convergence — Runtime Design v1.0\\r\\n## MLB Pilot · Cost-Aware Provider/Model Assignment\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Seat:** Independent Design & Build (not methodology, not architecture, not governance)\\r\\n**Runtime/model:** grok-4.6 (opencode/grok-4.6)\\r\\n**Date:** 2026-09-06\\r\\n**Status:** Design only. No code. No methodology change. No architecture change. No governance decision.\\r\\n**Companion sources (read, not modified):**\\r\\n- Kimi methodology v0.3.1 (handoff-zip / `EC8_Handoff_Package_v0.3.1-K.zip`) — prompts 01–09 = K1–K9\\r\\n- Chiave Architecture Specification v1.0 + Architecture Source Correction Delta v1.1\\r\\n- Reconciliation v0.2 (consultant; not a ruling)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nClaim tags follow Chiave v1.1: **[GIVEN]** · **[DERIVED]** · **[PROPOSED]** · **[UNKNOWN]** · **[OUTSIDE AUTHORITY]**\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 0. Authority Boundary\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n| This seat may | This seat may not |\\r\\n|---|---|\\r\\n| Choose provider/model/runtime IDs inside EX-2 | Change N, personas, prompts, G4 classes, package invariant |\\r\\n| Populate the provider registry (PR-3) | Redefine `family_id` taxonomy (PR-1 is Chiave) |\\r\\n| Propose sampling, timeouts, retries, cost | Set a cost ceiling (Don #8) |\\r\\n| Recommend a pilot profile | Approve L3 fallback operationally (Talon + Don) |\\r\\n| Flag blocked surfaces that affect runtime | Adjudicate DR-19/20/21 (methodology/architecture) |\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Contradiction tripwire:** Chiave v1.1 PR-3 says provider/model selection is outside architecture. Reconciliation DR-14↑ later upgraded family taxonomy to an architecture gate. This design **applies** Chiave PR-1 (`family_id` = foundation lineage) and **populates** the registry. It does not invent a competing taxonomy. **[DERIVED]**\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 1. Givens That Bind This Design\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**[GIVEN]** from methodology + architecture (content-keyed, not CR-ID):\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n| Binding | Value |\\r\\n|---|---|\\r\\n| Slate | One scheduled MLB game |\\r\\n| Cadence | Overnight 1 call · Morning 26 · Pre-Game 26 · **53/slate** · ~795/day at 15 slates |\\r\\n| Overnight | Framing only (no analysts) |\\r\\n| Full run | 1 framing + 5 Stage-1 + 5 Stage-3 + 5 L2 + 5 L3 + 5 normalization |\\r\\n| L1 | Deterministic code. **Zero model calls.** |\\r\\n| Analysts | N=5 · unique prompts · unique sampling · ≥3 families |\\r\\n| EX-3 | Stage 1→3 = two provider requests, **one session** |\\r\\n| L2 | Family ≠ the analyst being validated (pairwise) |\\r\\n| L3 | Outside the analyst-pool families · pre-approved fallback · exercised before pilot |\\r\\n| Framing / normalization | Any capable model · tightly constrained structured output |\\r\\n| Ledger | Provider-billable request + tokens. Budget 53 is reference. Ledger is truth. |\\r\\n| No cost ceiling | Measure first (Don #8) |\\r\\n| Pilot acceptance | Architectural (gates, isolation, invoice reconcile) — not signal quality |\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**[GIVEN]** account/runtime (Talon Bedrock snapshot 2026-09-05):\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n| Fact | Implication for this design |\\r\\n|---|---|\\r\\n| Live path = **Bedrock Mantle** `https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1` | Primary gateway |\\r\\n| Classic Converse/Invoke = `NOT_AUTHORIZED` | Do not route production through Converse |\\r\\n| Nova = Converse-only → **unreachable** | Nova is **not** a candidate. Closed. |\\r\\n| Meta Llama **not** on mantle provider list | Llama is not a candidate on the live path |\\r\\n| Mantle providers present | Anthropic, DeepSeek, Google, MiniMax, Mistral, Moonshot, NVIDIA, OpenAI, Qwen, Writer, xAI, Z.AI |\\r\\n| Live-verified IDs | `zai.glm-4.7-flash` · `deepseek.v3.2` · `qwen.qwen3-coder-480b-a35b-instruct` |\\r\\n| GLM 4.7 Flash fidelity | Cheap bulk only. Failed constraint-following in a live vetting test. **Not an analyst.** |\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 2. Family Taxonomy Applied (not invented)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**[GIVEN]** Chiave PR-1: `family_id` = foundation lineage. Distinct orgs sharing a lineage do **not** satisfy EX-2. Same org, distinct lineages, may.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**[PROPOSED]** registry population used by this design:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n| family_id | Provider org | Lineage note | On mantle? |\\r\\n|---|---|---|---|\\r\\n| `glm` | Z.AI | GLM 4.7 / GLM 5 | Yes (verified) |\\r\\n| `deepseek` | DeepSeek | V3.x / R1 same lineage | Yes (verified) |\\r\\n| `qwen` | Alibaba | Qwen3 family | Yes (coder verified; general SKU **[UNKNOWN]** until catalog pin) |\\r\\n| `kimi` | Moonshot | Kimi K2.x | Yes (listed) |\\r\\n| `minimax` | MiniMax | M2.x | Yes (listed) |\\r\\n| `mistral` | Mistral AI | Mistral / Ministral / Large 3 | Yes (listed) |\\r\\n| `claude` | Anthropic | All Claude 3/4/5 | Yes (listed) |\\r\\n| `gpt` | OpenAI | GPT-5.x closed | Yes (listed) |\\r\\n| `gpt-oss` | OpenAI | gpt-oss open-weight — **distinct lineage** from `gpt` | Classic Bedrock yes; mantle **[UNKNOWN]** |\\r\\n| `grok` | xAI | Grok 4.x | Yes (listed; 4.3 vs 4.6 ID **[UNKNOWN]**) |\\r\\n| `gemma` | Google | Gemma 3 (not Gemini) | Yes (listed) |\\r\\n| `nemotron` | NVIDIA | Often Llama-derived | **Do not use as a 4th family vs Llama.** Unused here. |\\r\\n| `nova` | Amazon | Unreachable on this account | **Excluded** |\\r\\n| `llama` | Meta | Not on mantle | **Excluded on live path** |\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEX-2 pre-flight: orchestration checks this registry **before any call** (Chiave PR-2). Missing ID → fail at zero cost.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 3. Gateway Routing Map\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n```\\r\\nEC8 Model Gateway (provider abstraction + OB-3 ledger)\\r\\n  │\\r\\n  ├─ PRIMARY: Bedrock Mantle adapter\\r\\n  │     POST https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-2.api.aws/v1/chat/completions\\r\\n  │     Auth: Bearer AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK (API key, not Identity Center)\\r\\n  │     Region: us-east-2\\r\\n  │     Model ID: mantle catalog string (pin from GET /v1/models)\\r\\n  │\\r\\n  ├─ SECONDARY (only if classic runtime unblocks): Bedrock Converse adapter\\r\\n  │     Not used for pilot unless authorizationStatus becomes AUTHORIZED\\r\\n  │     Nova/Llama would enter here — they are not in the pilot roster\\r\\n  │\\r\\n  └─ DIRECT-PROVIDER adapters (capability gap only)\\r\\n        None required for the recommended roster.\\r\\n        Hold: Anthropic Messages API (if mantle Anthropic SKU missing)\\r\\n              OpenAI API (if GPT-5.6 Luna/Terra not on this account's mantle list)\\r\\n              Moonshot API (if kimi-k2.5 missing)\\r\\n        Direct is a slot fallback, not a second happy path.\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**[PROPOSED]** Do not add OpenRouter as a third gateway for the pilot. Extra bill, extra provenance, extra EX-2 mapping risk. Direct provider only when Mantle does not expose the pinned ID.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 4. Token Basis (all profiles)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**[PROPOSED]** estimates. Ledger will replace these. One MLB matchup per slate.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n| Stage | Prompt | In | Out | Why |\\r\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\r\\n| Framing | 01 | 6,000 | 2,000 | Schema 0.3-MLB + raw slate pack |\\r\\n| Analyst Stage 1 | 02–06 | 4,500 | 2,500 | Prompt + framing snapshot, no evidence |\\r\\n| Analyst Stage 3 | 02–06 (same session) | 16,000 | 3,500 | Full S1 context + cumulative evidence. Methodology: token-heavy. |\\r\\n| L2 | 07 | 14,000 | 1,200 | Analyst output + package + framing; no raw confidence |\\r\\n| L3 | 08 | 18,000 | 1,800 | + L1 + L2 reports; red-team prose |\\r\\n| Normalization | 09 | 1,200 | 400 | Four inputs only |\\r\\n| L1 | — | 0 | 0 | Code |\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRetries (G4 correctable, provider 5xx) are **off-budget, on-ledger**. Crash-restart ≤2 per analyst per run then exclude (Chiave CK-3).\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 5. Three Runtime Profiles\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n### 5.A Cost-optimized (cheapest that still executes the methodology)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Design rule:** minimum sufficient intelligence. Flash is **not** an analyst. Nova/Llama unused.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n| Slot | family_id | Model | Mantle / API ID (proposed) | Classic Bedrock ID | Why this cheap |\\r\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\r\\n| Framing | `qwen` | Qwen3 32B | `qwen.qwen3-32b-v1:0` **[UNKNOWN pin]** | same | Structured form-fill; Flash failed constraint tests |\\r\\n| A Situational | `minimax` | MiniMax M2.5 | `minimax.minimax-m2.5` **[UNKNOWN pin]** | same | Cheap mid-reasoner; distinct family |\\r\\n| B Form | `qwen` | Qwen3 235B A22B | `qwen.qwen3-235b-a22b-2507-v1:0` **[UNKNOWN pin]** | same | Large MoE, $0.22/$0.88 |\\r\\n| C Structural | `deepseek` | DeepSeek V3.2 | `deepseek.v3.2` **[GIVEN live]** | `deepseek.v3.2` | Verified; strong structured analysis |\\r\\n| D Market | `kimi` | Kimi K2.5 | `moonshotai.kimi-k2.5` **[GIVEN listed]** | `moonshotai.kimi-k2.5` | Market-lens needs more than 32B |\\r\\n| E Micro | `glm` | GLM 4.7 | `zai.glm-4.7` **[GIVEN listed]** | `zai.glm-4.7` | Numeric/process; not Flash |\\r\\n| L2-A | `qwen` | Qwen3 235B | same as B | | ≠ `minimax` |\\r\\n| L2-B | `glm` | GLM 4.7 | same as E | | ≠ `qwen` |\\r\\n| L2-C | `minimax` | MiniMax M2.5 | same as A | | ≠ `deepseek` |\\r\\n| L2-D | `deepseek` | DeepSeek V3.2 | same as C | | ≠ `kimi` |\\r\\n| L2-E | `qwen` | Qwen3 235B | same as B | | ≠ `glm` |\\r\\n| L3 primary | `mistral` | Mistral Large 3 | `mistral.mistral-large-3-675b-instruct` **[UNKNOWN pin]** | same | Outside analyst pool (`minimax,qwen,deepseek,kimi,glm`) |\\r\\n| L3 fallback | `claude` | Claude Haiku 4.5 | `anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0` or `us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0` | same + geo profile | Pre-approved fallback family, still outside pool |\\r\\n| Normalization | `qwen` | Qwen3 32B | same as framing | | Blind mapper; not an analyst |\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nIf Qwen3 32B / 235B are absent from `GET /v1/models`, substitutions (still Profile A, still EX-2):\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n| Missing | Substitute | family_id | Quality note |\\r\\n|---|---|---|---|\\r\\n| Qwen3 32B (framing/norm) | `mistral.ministral-3-14b-instruct` | `mistral` | Framing family may then collide with L3. **If so, move L3 primary to Haiku and L3 fallback to `gpt` Luna.** |\\r\\n| Qwen3 235B (B / L2) | `zai.glm-5` for B, keep L2-A/E on DeepSeek | `glm` | B and E would share `glm` — still ≥3 families. Degrades Micro/Form diversity. |\\r\\n| MiniMax M2.5 | `openai.gpt-5.6-luna` | `gpt` | Cheaper; Luna capability **[UNKNOWN]** |\\r\\n| Mistral Large 3 | Haiku 4.5 as L3 primary; Luna as fallback | `claude` / `gpt` | |\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Do not substitute** GLM 4.7 Flash, Gemma 4B/12B, gpt-oss-20b, or Qwen3 Coder 480B into analyst or L3 slots. Coder SKU is the wrong capability class. Flash failed constraint-following. Tiny Gemma is not a red-team.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n### 5.B Balanced (recommended default if A’s Qwen-general SKUs fail pin)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSame topology. Upgrades:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n| Slot | Change vs A |\\r\\n|---|---|\\r\\n| E Micro | `zai.glm-5` (`glm`) — live vetting: high fidelity on judgment |\\r\\n| D Market | keep Kimi K2.5 |\\r\\n| L3 | keep Mistral Large 3 / Haiku fallback |\\r\\n| Framing | keep Qwen3 32B; if missing, Ministral 14B **and** move L3 off `mistral` |\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n### 5.C Maximum-quality\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFive distinct frontier families. Still Bedrock-Mantle first.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n| Slot | family_id | Model | ID | $/1M in/out |\\r\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\r\\n| Framing | `claude` | Haiku 4.5 | `anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0` | 1.00 / 5.00 |\\r\\n| A | `claude` | Sonnet 4.6 | `anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6` | 3.00 / 15.00 |\\r\\n| B | `gpt` | GPT-5.6 Terra | `openai.gpt-5.6-terra` | 2.00 / 12.00 |\\r\\n| C | `grok` | Grok 4.6 (or 4.3 if that is the catalog pin) | `xai.grok-4.6` | 2.00 / 6.00 |\\r\\n| D | `kimi` | Kimi K2 Thinking | `moonshot.kimi-k2-thinking` | 0.60 / 2.50 |\\r\\n| E | `glm` | GLM 5 | `zai.glm-5` | 1.00 / 3.20 |\\r\\n| L2 | pairwise from the other four analyst families, never same family as target | | | |\\r\\n| L3 primary | **must be outside {claude,gpt,grok,kimi,glm}** | DeepSeek V3.2 is in-pool? No — C is grok, not deepseek. **L3 = `deepseek.v3.2` is illegal if any analyst is deepseek; here C is grok, so DeepSeek is legal.** Better L3: `mistral.mistral-large-3-675b-instruct` still outside pool. For max-quality L3 use **GPT-5.6 Sol only if B is not `gpt`.** B is `gpt` → Sol is **illegal**. | | |\\r\\n| L3 primary (C) | `mistral` | Mistral Large 3 | still the only strong family left outside the five | |\\r\\n| L3 fallback | `qwen` | Qwen3 235B | outside pool in this profile | |\\r\\n| Norm | `claude` | Haiku 4.5 | | |\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMax-quality **cannot** put Opus on L3 while Sonnet is an analyst — same `claude` family, and Claude is in the analyst pool, so L3-Claude is an EX-2 violation. Opus is for a world where no analyst is Claude. Profile C as tabled keeps L3 = Mistral.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 6. Runtime Assignment Matrix — Recommended Pilot = Profile A\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSampling unique per analyst, range 0.3–0.7 **[GIVEN]** prompt README. Temperature 0 for form-fillers.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRetry policy (all AI stages): 2 attempts on 429/5xx, exponential backoff 2s/8s; no retry on 4xx schema/auth. G4 correctable = one Stage-3 retry in-session (methodology), counted on ledger not `ran_n`.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n| Field | 01 Framing | 02 A Sit. | 03 B Form | 04 C Struct. | 05 D Market | 06 E Micro | 07 L2 | 08 L3 | 09 Norm |\\r\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\r\\n| Stage | 0 | 1+3 | 1+3 | 1+3 | 1+3 | 1+3 | 4 | 4 | 5 |\\r\\n| Prompt ID | 01 | 02 | 03 | 04 | 05 | 06 | 07 | 08 | 09 |\\r\\n| Calls / Overnight | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\\r\\n| Calls / Morning | 1 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 5 | 5 | 5 |\\r\\n| Calls / Pre-Game | 1 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 5 | 5 | 5 |\\r\\n| Calls / slate | 3 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 10 | 10 | 10 |\\r\\n| Required capability | Constrained JSON form-fill; no analysis | Situational reasoning + JSON | Form/trajectory + JSON | Matchup structure + JSON | Market reasoning + JSON | Metric/process + JSON | G4 classify + soundness; blind to raw confidence | Red-team; outside pool | 4-input → 5-tier JSON |\\r\\n| Provider | Bedrock Mantle | Mantle | Mantle | Mantle | Mantle | Mantle | Mantle | Mantle | Mantle |\\r\\n| Exact model | Qwen3 32B | MiniMax M2.5 | Qwen3 235B | DeepSeek V3.2 | Kimi K2.5 | GLM 4.7 | pairwise (see §5.A) | Mistral Large 3 | Qwen3 32B |\\r\\n| API/runtime ID | `qwen.qwen3-32b-v1:0` | `minimax.minimax-m2.5` | `qwen.qwen3-235b-a22b-2507-v1:0` | `deepseek.v3.2` | `moonshotai.kimi-k2.5` | `zai.glm-4.7` | slot table | `mistral.mistral-large-3-675b-instruct` | same as 01 |\\r\\n| Bedrock / inference-profile ID | on-demand mantle | on-demand mantle | on-demand mantle | on-demand mantle | on-demand mantle | on-demand mantle | | if classic: n/a | |\\r\\n| family_id | `qwen` | `minimax` | `qwen` | `deepseek` | `kimi` | `glm` | ≠ target | `mistral` | `qwen` |\\r\\n| Structured-output mode | `json_schema` (schema 0.3-MLB); fallback `json_object` | `json_object` | `json_object` | `json_object` | `json_object` | `json_object` | `json_schema` (07 contract) | `json_schema` (08 contract) | `json_schema` (09 contract) |\\r\\n| Context requirement | ~8K | S1 ~8K; S3 ~24K (session) | same | same | same | same | ~16K | ~22K | ~2K |\\r\\n| Reasoning level | none | off / default | off / default | off / default | off / default | off / default | none | off (no extra thinking tokens) | none |\\r\\n| Temperature | 0.0 | 0.52 | 0.41 | 0.33 | 0.61 | 0.38 | 0.10 | 0.30 | 0.0 |\\r\\n| top_p | 1.0 | 0.95 | 0.90 | 0.85 | 0.95 | 0.90 | 0.90 | 0.90 | 1.0 |\\r\\n| Timeout | 30s | S1 120s / S3 180s | same | same | same | same | 120s | 180s | 30s |\\r\\n| Retry policy | 2× 5xx; G0 re-run on malformed | 2× 5xx; CK-3 ≤2 crash-restarts | same | same | same | same | 2× 5xx; never skip (I5) | 2× 5xx then fallback; never skip | 2× 5xx; blocks artifact |\\r\\n| Primary | Qwen3 32B | MiniMax M2.5 | Qwen3 235B | DeepSeek V3.2 | Kimi K2.5 | GLM 4.7 | pairwise | Mistral Large 3 | Qwen3 32B |\\r\\n| Fallback | Ministral 14B | GPT-5.6 Luna | GLM 5 | GLM 4.7 | GLM 5 | DeepSeek V3.2 | next legal family | Haiku 4.5 | Ministral 14B |\\r\\n| Est. in / out | 6.0K / 2.0K | S1 4.5/2.5 · S3 16/3.5 | same | same | same | same | 14.0 / 1.2 | 18.0 / 1.8 | 1.2 / 0.4 |\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nL1: no row. No model. No tokens. No cost.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 7. Model-Family / Heterogeneity Matrix (Profile A)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAnalyst pool families = `{minimax, qwen, deepseek, kimi, glm}` — **5 ≥ 3**. **[DERIVED]** EX-2 pass.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n| Validator \\\\ Analyst | A `minimax` | B `qwen` | C `deepseek` | D `kimi` | E `glm` |\\r\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\r\\n| L2 family | `qwen` | `glm` | `minimax` | `deepseek` | `qwen` |\\r\\n| L2 ≠ analyst? | yes | yes | yes | yes | yes |\\r\\n| L3 family | `mistral` | `mistral` | `mistral` | `mistral` | `mistral` |\\r\\n| L3 in analyst pool? | **no** | **no** | **no** | **no** | **no** |\\r\\n| L3 fallback | `claude` | `claude` | `claude` | `claude` | `claude` |\\r\\n| Fallback in pool? | **no** | **no** | **no** | **no** | **no** |\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFraming/normalization may share `qwen` with Persona B. They are **not** in the analyst pool. **[DERIVED]** from EX-2 wording.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPre-flight must also reject: L3 = any of the five; L2 family == target family; unpinned catalog ID.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 8. Exact Model-ID Manifest\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPin at implement time with `GET /v1/models` on mantle. Until then these are **[PROPOSED]** except the three live-tested.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n| Config key | Proposed runtime ID | Status | Price in/out $/1M | Source |\\r\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\r\\n| `models.framing` | `qwen.qwen3-32b-v1:0` | UNKNOWN pin | 0.15 / 0.60 | Bedrock Explorer 2026-08-27 |\\r\\n| `models.analyst.A` | `minimax.minimax-m2.5` | UNKNOWN pin | 0.30 / 1.20 | same |\\r\\n| `models.analyst.B` | `qwen.qwen3-235b-a22b-2507-v1:0` | UNKNOWN pin | 0.22 / 0.88 | same |\\r\\n| `models.analyst.C` | `deepseek.v3.2` | **LIVE 2026-09-05** | 0.62 / 1.85 | Talon snapshot + Explorer |\\r\\n| `models.analyst.D` | `moonshotai.kimi-k2.5` | listed on mantle | 0.60 / 3.00 | Explorer (Kimi price) |\\r\\n| `models.analyst.E` | `zai.glm-4.7` | listed | 0.60 / 2.20 | Talon cost matrix |\\r\\n| `m