n    D: {temperature: 0.61, top_p: 0.95}\\r\\n    E: {temperature: 0.38, top_p: 0.90}\\r\\n    framing: {temperature: 0.0, top_p: 1.0}\\r\\n    l2: {temperature: 0.10, top_p: 0.90}\\r\\n    l3: {temperature: 0.30, top_p: 0.90}\\r\\n    norm: {temperature: 0.0, top_p: 1.0}\\r\\n  timeouts_s: {framing: 30, s1: 120, s3: 180, l2: 120, l3: 180, norm: 30}\\r\\n  provider_retries: {max: 2, on: [429, 500, 502, 503, 529], backoff_s: [2, 8]}\\r\\n  assignments:  # see §6\\r\\n  l3_fallback:\\r\\n    primary_family: mistral\\r\\n    fallback_family: claude\\r\\n    granularity: whole_run\\r\\n    both_failed: block_entries\\r\\n  metering: execution_point   # OB-3, no retrofit\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 13. Risks / Unknowns\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n| ID | Class | Item | Impact |\\r\\n|---|---|---|---|\\r\\n| R1 | UNKNOWN | Exact mantle IDs for Qwen3 32B/235B, MiniMax M2.5, Mistral Large 3, Haiku | Blocks pin. Mitigate: catalog dump before spend; substitution table in §5.A |\\r\\n| R2 | UNKNOWN | Mantle `json_schema` vs `json_object` support per model | Framing/G0. Mitigate: validate JSON in code; G0 re-run |\\r\\n| R3 | UNKNOWN | Mantle session continuity (multi-turn) for MiniMax/Qwen/Kimi | EX-3. Mitigate: one-process message array; if provider drops session, CK-3 restart Stage 1 |\\r\\n| R4 | UNKNOWN | Mantle price = Explorer list price? | Ledger vs invoice. First-slate reconcile |\\r\\n| R5 | GIVEN | GLM Flash low fidelity | Already excluded from analyst/L3 |\\r\\n| R6 | GIVEN | Nova/Llama unreachable | Roster avoids them |\\r\\n| R7 | OUTSIDE | L3 fallback not yet Talon-approved | Seeded test (b) cannot run |\\r\\n| R8 | OUTSIDE | DR-19/21 validation wiring | Runtime can still assign L2/L3 models; G4 semantics remain methodology-blocked |\\r\\n| R9 | UNKNOWN | Kimi K2.5 sports-reasoning quality | Highest $ slot; swap path exists |\\r\\n| R10 | UNKNOWN | S3 evidence package size (5–40K) | Dominates cost variance |\\r\\n| R11 | UNKNOWN | NVIDIA Nemotron lineage vs Llama | Unused, correctly |\\r\\n| R12 | PROPOSED | Grok 4.3 vs 4.6 catalog name | Profile C only |\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 14. Recommended Pilot Runtime Profile\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Recommend Profile A (cost-optimized) for the MLB pilot.**\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nWhy, in methodology/architecture terms — not preference:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n1. Pilot acceptance is **architectural**, not signal quality (Chiave §11). Paying Sonnet/Opus rates does not fire G0–G6 better.\\r\\n2. Minimum sufficient intelligence: Flash is out; 32B+ form-fill; mid/large reasoners on A–E; 675B Mistral on L3.\\r\\n3. EX-2 is fully satisfied: 5 analyst families, pairwise L2, L3 + fallback both outside the pool.\\r\\n4. Live path is Mantle; roster is Mantle-native; Nova not required.\\r\\n5. Cost: **~$0.40/slate, ~$6/15-slate day, ~$180/month** at full cadence — measurable, not capped.\\r\\n6. Upgrade path is slot-local: E→GLM5 (Profile B) or D→stronger without touching isolation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Do not start on Profile C.** It spends 10–15× to buy signal the pilot is forbidden from judging.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 15. Final Answer\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Cheapest runtime that still faithfully executes accepted EC8 methodology + Chiave architecture:**\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nBedrock Mantle only. No Nova. No Llama. No Flash-as-analyst.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- **01 Framing / 09 Norm:** Qwen3 32B (`qwen`) @ $0.15/$0.60, temp 0\\r\\n- **02 A:** MiniMax M2.5 (`minimax`) temp 0.52\\r\\n- **03 B:** Qwen3 235B (`qwen`) temp 0.41\\r\\n- **04 C:** DeepSeek V3.2 (`deepseek`) temp 0.33 — live-verified\\r\\n- **05 D:** Kimi K2.5 (`kimi`) temp 0.61\\r\\n- **06 E:** GLM 4.7 (`glm`) temp 0.38\\r\\n- **07 L2:** pairwise different family (Qwen / GLM / MiniMax / DeepSeek / Qwen)\\r\\n- **08 L3:** Mistral Large 3 (`mistral`); fallback Haiku 4.5 (`claude`)\\r\\n- **L1:** code, $0\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**~$0.20 per Morning or Pre-Game run · ~$0.40 per 53-call slate · ~$6 per 15-slate day.**\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAnything cheaper (Flash analysts, Gemma L3, skip L3, share L3 family with the pool) stops being the methodology.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n*Design owner: Independent Design & Build · v1.0 · 2026-09-06*\\r\\n*Does not amend methodology v0.3.1, Architecture v1.0/v1.1, or Don guardrails.*\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/10LK7qH8X5iCGdDD00Wb2LjNfpi0R5q8OmL-x0My4NEw/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"07_CURRENT_HANDOFF_2026-09-06\",\"id\":\"10LK7qH8X5iCGdDD00Wb2LjNfpi0R5q8OmL-x0My4NEw\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"3217\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T11:50:06.081Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T15:55:23.287Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-06T15:55:23.287Z\",\"display_title\":\"07_CURRENT_HANDOFF_2026-09-06\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/10LK7qH8X5iCGdDD00Wb2LjNfpi0R5q8OmL-x0My4NEw/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1-2XT7kaaOIIu8aqjcGFIPF_ktPF0N9vQ\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿Current Handoff — 2026-09-06\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPROJECT STATE\\r\\nEC⁸ AI Convergence is post-architecture-gate, pre-implementation. Accepted methodology and Chiave Architecture Specification v1.0 are broadly aligned. Phase 0/1 foundation work is generally startable; named Phase-2 semantic/interface surfaces remain subject to owner reconciliation before coding those surfaces.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT SEATS\\r\\nDon — Vision / Final Authority / interim human orchestrator\\r\\nCoda — Strategic Governance\\r\\nKimi — Technical Stack Methodology / Design & Build\\r\\nChiave — Architecture\\r\\nPrincipal Consultant — Technical Translation / Integration\\r\\nTalon — Operations\\r\\nLuce — Verification / Ground Truth\\r\\nData / Intelligence — shared service\\r\\nQA / Validation — approved vacant shared service\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT PROCESS\\r\\nDon intent → Coda governance framing → Kimi methodology → Chiave architecture when materially required → Kimi Design & Build → Principal Consultant translation/reconciliation checkpoint → Implementation → Talon operations → Luce verification → Coda reconciliation → Don decision.\\r\\nPrincipal Consultant is a translation checkpoint, not a new approval authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPRINCIPAL CONSULTANT STATUS\\r\\nRole approved; runtime/model NOT locked.\\r\\nAudition evidence from 2026-09-06:\\r\\n- Luna: fastest/cheapest observed, strong routine/default fit, some deeper-defect misses/false blockers.\\r\\n- Kimi 2.7 Code/Thinking: stronger blocker calibration and authority routing; improved after pushback; good deep-review candidate.\\r\\n- Claude Fable 5.1: deepest forensic defect discovery but very high cost/latency; forensic-only profile if used.\\r\\n- K3-256K high-thinking swarm: seven parallel lanes, excellent deep-audit intake/decomposition, but consumed 5-hour Code quota in stress test; treat as audit-mode evidence.\\r\\nWorking hypothesis only: cheap/fast routine translation first, deeper Kimi/swarmer escalation when contested or at major locks.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPRINCIPAL CONSULTANT ARTIFACTS\\r\\nFiled under GCE onboarding → 03_Model_Onboarding → Principal_Consultant:\\r\\n- PRINCIPAL_CONSULTANT_ONBOARDING_2026-09-06\\r\\n- EC8_Handoff_Package_v0.3.1_FIXED.zip\\r\\n- EC8_Methodology_Architecture_Reconciliation_v0.1.md\\r\\n- EC8_Methodology_Architecture_Reconciliation_v0.2.md\\r\\n- EC8_Architecture_Specification_v1.0_Chiave_source.md\\r\\n- K3_256K_SWARM_AUDITION_OUTPUT_2026-09-06.txt\\r\\n- audition screenshots / quota evidence\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKNOWN RECONCILIATION POSTURE\\r\\nBroad alignment is established. Reconciliation evidence surfaced record/version/ruling drift plus deeper contract seams concentrated in Phase 2. Canonical remediation belongs to Kimi/Chiave/Coda according to ownership; reconciliation reports themselves are evidence, not canon.\\r\\nPhase 0/1 may proceed on unambiguous contracts. Do not let Implementation invent missing methodology/architecture decisions.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHOME ROOT CLEANUP CHECKPOINT\\r\\nBatch 2A = CLOSED / VERIFIED PASS.\\r\\nDevPonds = CLOSED / VERIFIED DELETE.\\r\\ntests = CLOSED / RETAIN IN PLACE.\\r\\nspeech-profile = OPEN / QUARANTINE-SECURITY HANDLING REQUIRED.\\r\\nNext speech-profile sequence: Chiave security/quarantine envelope → Talon exact plan → Luce pre-verification → authorized execution → Luce post-verification → close disposition.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNEXT SESSION\\r\\n1. Review completed K3-256K swarm synthesis/output.\\r\\n2. Compare downstream handoff quality against Luna/K2.7/Fable and decide runtime strategy only if evidence is sufficient.\\r\\n3. Continue speech-profile from Chiave quarantine ruling.\\r\\n4. Return to AI Convergence contract reconciliation / build handoff.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSOURCE DISCIPLINE\\r\\nNewer != automatically canonical. Historical records remain provenance. Do not silently merge conflicting sources. MODEL != SEAT\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2026-09-06 SUPERSESSION NOTE\\r\\nThis handoff remains provenance for the earlier 2026-09-06 state. The current continuation handoff is now:\\r\\n10_CURRENT_HANDOFF_2026-09-06_RUNTIME_DESIGN\\r\\nDrive ID: 1SLU50Xz-ujenM6hGHdweEhNIJTvAkNFhjzJuI66MDOU\\r\\nUse the newer handoff for runtime-design, provisional Independent Design & Build, Nova/Bedrock, and Principal Consultant audition state. Do not delete this earlier handoff.\\r\\n.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O9Lca5zqZ7tyf8XcYWGXwBtlGb9LnIhXn4tmSKZK75A/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"05_GCE_PROCESS_AND_GATES\",\"id\":\"1O9Lca5zqZ7tyf8XcYWGXwBtlGb9LnIhXn4tmSKZK75A\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"3225\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T03:23:24.205Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-08T20:44:36.993Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-08T20:44:36.993Z\",\"display_title\":\"05_GCE_PROCESS_AND_GATES\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O9Lca5zqZ7tyf8XcYWGXwBtlGb9LnIhXn4tmSKZK75A/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1-2XT7kaaOIIu8aqjcGFIPF_ktPF0N9vQ\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿EC⁸ AI Convergence — GCE Process and Gates\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGate 0 — Don Intent\\r\\nDefine problem, purpose, success criteria, exclusions, and Don sign-off boundaries.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGate 1 — Coda Governance Frame\\r\\nDefine authority, seat ownership, source-of-truth rules, canon/supersession rules, and routing boundaries.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGate 2 — Kimi Methodology\\r\\nDeliver convergence methodology, technical-stack methodology, independent-analysis method, reconciliation method, confidence method, stopping conditions, and methodology test plan. No implementation lock before methodology acceptance.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGate 3 — Chiave Architecture\\r\\nInvoke for material structural concerns: topology, interfaces, durable state, security architecture, runtime boundaries, failure domains, scaling/concurrency, canonical infrastructure.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGate 4 — Kimi Design & Build\\r\\nInput approved methodology + architecture where required. Deliver component plan, build sequence, implementation package, prototype sequence, assumption register, and technical tests.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGate 5 — Implementation\\r\\nBuild only approved scope and surface assumptions.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGate 6 — Talon Operations\\r\\nDeliver deployment sequence, runtime procedures, handoffs, observability, recovery, operational ownership.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGate 7 — Luce Verification\\r\\nVerify evidence lineage, claims, reproducibility, constraints, contradiction preservation, and execution.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGate 8 — Coda Governance Reconciliation\\r\\nConfirm authority compliance, canon state, unresolved Don decisions, and that no seat exceeded authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGate 9 — Don Decision\\r\\nAccept / reject / modify / return to prior gate.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRule\\r\\nCompetence does not replace authority separation. Do not skip gates because a model appears capable.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2026-09-06 ADDENDUM — TRANSLATION CHECKPOINT\\r\\nInsert between Gate 4 (Kimi Design & Build) and Gate 5 (Implementation):\\r\\nGate 4A — Principal Consultant Technical Translation / Integration\\r\\nInput: accepted methodology, accepted architecture where materially required, Kimi Design & Build package, governing source/canon state.\\r\\nOutput: methodology↔architecture traceability, discrepancy register, version/ruling crosswalk, implementation contract by component, no-coder-discretion register, routed questions, and component-level readiness verdict.\\r\\nRule: this is a translation checkpoint, not an approval gate. It may identify and route unresolved methodology/architecture/governance questions but may not resolve them by authority. Implementation proceeds only on surfaces whose contracts are unambiguous.\\r\\nOperational success test: Implementation/Talon can act from the handoff without inventing requirements or reinterpreting upstream methodology/architecture\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2026-09-06 PROPOSED PROCESS REVISION — TRANSLATION BEFORE INDEPENDENT DESIGN\\r\\nDon clarified that methodology authorship and concrete Design & Build selection should be separated. The earlier Gate 4 / Gate 4A ordering is therefore under controlled revision. Do not erase the earlier gate record; preserve it as provenance until Don canonizes the replacement.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPROPOSED working sequence:\\r\\nGate 0 — Don Intent\\r\\nGate 1 — Coda Governance Frame\\r\\nGate 2 — Kimi Methodology\\r\\nGate 3 — Chiave Architecture when materially required\\r\\nGate 4 — Principal Consultant Specification + Translation\\r\\nInput: accepted Don intent, Kimi methodology, Chiave architecture, governing canon/source state.\\r\\nOutput: traceability, discrepancy register, implementation contracts, no-coder-discretion register, routed questions, implementation-ready spec/package.\\r\\nRule: translation checkpoint only; no design or approval authority.\\r\\nGate 5 — Independent Design & Build [PROVISIONAL]\\r\\nInput: implementation-ready spec/package.\\r\\nOutput: concrete provider/model/runtime assignments, component/tool choices, detailed implementation design, build package, cost/value analysis, fallback/runtime manifest. May not change methodology or architecture.\\r\\nGate 6 — Talon Operational Routing / Deployment Control\\r\\nGate 7 — Keel Build / Deploy / Implementation Test / Evidence Return\\r\\nGate 8 — Luce Independent Verification / Ground Truth\\r\\nGate 9 — Coda Governance Reconciliation\\r\\nGate 10 — Don Decision\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent audition evidence for Gate 5: Grok 4.6 and GLM 5.1 have produced independent runtime-design candidates. No candidate design or seat runtime is canonical yet.\\r\\n.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2026-09-08 DON-APPROVED PROCESS ADDENDUM — CONVERSATION RECONCILIATION ANCHOR (CRA)\\r\\nThe Conversation Reconciliation Anchor (CRA) is now the standard long-chat reset and new-chat handoff control across EC⁸ work. Trigger it when conversation length creates drift risk, when labels/identities/authority begin to blur, when material corrections/retractions accumulate, or before moving into a new chat.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nA CRA is not merely a summary. It must: distill the conversation into topic-level bullets with one concise paragraph per topic; reconcile current truth against prior assumptions; preserve corrections/retractions/conflicts and provenance; identify open gaps/dependencies/ownership; and end with STATUS / CONFIDENCE / REASON / NEXT GATE / DON INPUT NEEDED.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCRA governing rules: IDENTITY != ROLE != LENS != PERSONALITY != AUTHORITY != MODEL; MODEL != SEAT; newer != canonical; corrections are additive rather than historical rewrites; conflicts remain preserved until resolved by correct authority; context breadth does not grant authority breadth; Edge Crew Quant != AI Convergence; UNKNOWN / NOT_AVAILABLE states may not be hidden for continuity convenience.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter Don approves a CRA, update/add the relevant artifacts without rewriting history, create a current handoff artifact, point the new chat to that handoff plus the relevant Google Drive knowledge base, preserve any local-vs-Drive source-of-truth distinction, and resume at the stated NEXT GATE.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPrimary protocol artifact: EC8_CONVERSATION_RECONCILIATION_ANCHOR_PROTOCOL_v1.0 (Drive ID 1i5qirCXzjoQIuOrIXWYalqC5BxAT0yduH6WY1aEfNGg).\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1MU0v_avYb8UpYpyHBID6AcnOaFHkQyc7KPMKfKuG--8/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"07_CURRENT_HANDOFF_2026-09-05\",\"id\":\"1MU0v_avYb8UpYpyHBID6AcnOaFHkQyc7KPMKfKuG--8\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"1903\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T03:23:59.874Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T03:24:12.637Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-06T03:24:12.637Z\",\"display_title\":\"07_CURRENT_HANDOFF_2026-09-05\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1MU0v_avYb8UpYpyHBID6AcnOaFHkQyc7KPMKfKuG--8/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1-2XT7kaaOIIu8aqjcGFIPF_ktPF0N9vQ\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿Current Handoff — 2026-09-05\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nWhy this project exists\\r\\nThe main GCE framework conversation accumulated filesystem/runtime architecture, Chiave onboarding, Talon execution, Luce verification, Kimi seat validation, Edge Crew history, and Command Center discussion. EC⁸ AI Convergence is being split into its own project to avoid cross-project contamination.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent decisions\\r\\n1. EC⁸ = parent intelligence platform.\\r\\n2. Edge Crew = quantitative / mathematical intelligence branch.\\r\\n3. AI Convergence = separate sibling branch; final branch name TBD.\\r\\n4. Kimi = Technical Stack Methodology / Design & Build.\\r\\n5. Larger structural decisions route to Chiave after methodology.\\r\\n6. Coda remains Strategic Governance and does not absorb specialist work.\\r\\n7. Edge Crew Quant is separate from AI Convergence.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent live input\\r\\nTalon / DeepSeek has returned an EC4 methodology recovery package. That recovery package is NOT yet incorporated into this knowledge base because it has not yet been supplied to Coda in this project setup turn.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nImmediate next gate\\r\\n1. Add the DeepSeek recovery package as a source artifact.\\r\\n2. Review it for Don intent, EC4 methodology of record, EC3 contamination, Quant contamination, contradictions, and unresolved questions.\\r\\n3. Produce the minimum clean Convergence methodology source package.\\r\\n4. Give that clean package to Kimi for the real-world methodology / Design & Build test.\\r\\n5. Route material architecture decisions to Chiave afterward.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDo not\\r\\n- start coding\\r\\n- call EC3 or EC4 implementation canonical\\r\\n- import Quant methodology\\r\\n- silently resolve DeepSeek-recovered conflicts\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ppRFYL9A0e2mnuLqTEocE9wbQOCuLkOGjHuSmoAdXtg/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"EC8_EDGE_CREW_QUANT_HANDOFF_2026-09-08_MLB_DAY2\",\"id\":\"1ppRFYL9A0e2mnuLqTEocE9wbQOCuLkOGjHuSmoAdXtg\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"9344\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-08T20:43:00.707Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-08T20:43:53.500Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-08T20:43:53.500Z\",\"display_title\":\"EC8_EDGE_CREW_QUANT_HANDOFF_2026-09-08_MLB_DAY2\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ppRFYL9A0e2mnuLqTEocE9wbQOCuLkOGjHuSmoAdXtg/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1pGZqmABuJf4t4fbw6ebaPIRFAqfC-az0\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿EC⁸ EdgeCrew Quant — Current Handoff\\r\\nDATE: 2026-09-08\\r\\nSESSION: MLB Day 2 / Conversation Reconciliation Anchor\\r\\nSEAT: Coda — Strategic Advisor / Governance\\r\\nCURRENT GATE: Corrado MLB 9/8 Quant Data-Floor Preflight\\r\\nSTATUS: CHECKPOINT\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPURPOSE\\r\\nThis is the primary handoff for the next project chat. Start here before interpreting older chat history. Ground in Google Drive for EC⁸ framework/governance history, but preserve the explicit distinction that current MLB operational truth is produced locally by Desktop\\\\mlb-data-system\\\\ unless/until that output is synchronized and verified in Drive.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nBRANCH / SOURCE DISCIPLINE\\r\\n- EC⁸ = parent intelligence platform.\\r\\n- Edge Crew = quantitative / mathematical intelligence.\\r\\n- AI Convergence = separate sibling branch.\\r\\n- Edge Crew Quant != AI Convergence.\\r\\n- Do not import AI Convergence seat labels into EdgeCrew Quant by convenience.\\r\\n- For the current MLB Quant lane, Corrado is the operating Quant owner/seat. Prior references to “Kimi” in this lane were model/runtime associations and must not replace the Corrado seat identity. This correction does not by itself rewrite the separate AI Convergence seat topology.\\r\\n- MODEL != SEAT.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDON-APPROVED CONVERSATION CONTROL\\r\\nConversation Reconciliation Anchor (CRA) is now the approved long-chat reset/handoff process. When a conversation becomes long, drift appears, identities/labels blur, or a new chat is needed, run a CRA: topic bullet + one paragraph per topic, preserve corrections/retractions/conflicts, state current truth/open gaps/ownership, and end with STATUS / CONFIDENCE / REASON / NEXT GATE / DON INPUT NEEDED. Primary protocol artifact: EC8_CONVERSATION_RECONCILIATION_ANCHOR_PROTOCOL_v1.0.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCHAT RECONCILIATION — MATERIAL TOPICS\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n1. Live Thesis Repricing / self-triggering system\\r\\nThe cross-sport live concept is a continuous edge-monitoring layer on top of the pregame thesis. Live game-state data and market prices refresh on a cadence; the system recomputes current edge and confidence and surfaces opportunities only when the market reprices more aggressively than the underlying state warrants. Governance line: self-triggering, not self-betting. A trigger requires human review and is never automatic execution.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2. MLB live-repricing example\\r\\nBaseball is a strong example: a heavy-hitting team can trail narrowly while still making quality contact; an opposing starter can be entering third-time-through exposure; a weak/taxed bullpen may be approaching; and the live price can expand materially. The trigger is not “team is losing.” The trigger is “original thesis remains intact or strengthens while price improves.”\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n3. Live probability\\r\\nGeneric in-game win probability is context, not authority. It can move violently on one baseball event. The framework should consider inning, outs, base state, lineup turn, pitcher fatigue, bullpen strength/availability, remaining lineup quality, and live price. Probability displays can inform but cannot decide.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n4. NFL live props / ticker\\r\\nDon connected the same primitive to the NFL live-props concept: a ticker-like system that updates live data every several minutes, recalculates edge/confidence, and surfaces threshold crossings. A placeholder threshold such as +10 is not canonical; replay/verification must determine useful bands.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n5. Historical replay requirement\\r\\nBefore live-trigger authority is trusted, replay historical live-game states, simulate threshold crossings, grade outcomes, identify durable signal bands, and then define trigger policy. Coda governs trigger authority; technical calculation methodology belongs to the appropriate Quant/technical owner; Luce verifies evidence/performance where applicable.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n6. VIP EdgeCrew product premise\\r\\nDon’s commercial vision is a private intelligence club, not a mass-market picks service: invite-only, roughly 10–50 members, tiered access, potentially ~$1,000/month at a premium tier, with some higher access earned through contribution of member picks/reads. No pooled betting, no custody, no auto-betting. The value is data, tracking, monitoring, time compression, and contribution-based intelligence.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n7. Give serious bettors time back\\r\\nA core product premise is that EdgeCrew should return hours to serious/professional bettors by absorbing data assembly, monitoring, reconciliation, and alerting. Humans should interact mainly at deliberate decision points rather than babysitting the system.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n8. Anti-gambling-volume doctrine\\r\\nDon wants no part of a mass-market microbetting/prediction-market engagement loop. EdgeCrew does not exist to create more bets; it exists to reduce bad ones. STAY AWAY is valid. No chasing. No pressure to manufacture picks. The system can tell the user to do nothing.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n9. Commercial boundary / acquisition\\r\\nThe system could theoretically attract strategic sportsbook interest if highly differentiated, but acquisition is not the design target. Don does not want mass exposure or college-age acquisition as the growth model. Preferred posture: private, selective, intelligence-first; acquisition remains optional future strategy.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n10. EC⁸ applied-AI strategic value\\r\\nDon connected EdgeCrew to prior enterprise AI work and observed that much of the market packages relatively narrow workflows as expensive “AI.” The strategic hypothesis captured here: EC⁸’s moat is not model access; it is the governed operating system around models — provenance, authority, source discipline, verification, failure handling, model substitution, data integrity, stopping conditions, and measured outcomes. Do not state “one or two years ahead” as a verified market fact without benchmarking.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n11. Enterprise PO-ingestion economics\\r\\nDon described vendor proposals for PO ingestion, Azure Document Intelligence, SQL/P21 integration, setup charges, per-transaction pricing, and expensive API access. The lesson is commercial/architectural judgment: decompose the workflow, understand true cloud/model/integration cost, avoid unnecessary vendor lock-in, and distinguish useful implementation/support value from inflated “AI” markup.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n12. MLB daily cadence\\r\\nMorning is baseline refresh only. Preferred full MLB primary run occurs around Don’s lunch break, then a targeted pregame delta roughly 60–90 minutes before the first meaningful game cluster. Do not rerun the whole model for every changed input; only revalidate material deltas such as starters, lineups, injuries, bullpen availability, weather, and market price.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n13. Cross-sport cadence families\\r\\nDaily Slate: MLB, NBA, WNBA, NHL. Weekly Football: NFL/NCAA football. Event-Based: UFC, Boxing, Golf. Soccer is separate. Live Repricing is a cross-sport overlay rather than a base cadence.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n14. Soccer as separate cadence family\\r\\nSoccer is not an ordinary two-touch slate because kickoff windows span time zones, confirmed lineups arrive near kickoff, rotation/fixture congestion can matter heavily, and halftime/live repricing is especially valuable. It can operate as a lighter always-on companion lane while Don is coding, surfacing only meaningful interaction points.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n15. Soccer persistent-state + competition context\\r\\nPersistent team/style/form variables can carry forward, but confirmed XI/formation, injuries/suspensions, fixture congestion, weather/venue, and price remain game-day deltas. Don’s prior methodology also treated league/club play differently from cup/tournament play because incentives and behavior differ. Future soccer data/methodology should treat competition class as first-class context; likely league/domestic, cup/knockout/continental, and international/national-team regimes.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMLB CLOSEOUT / 9-8 OPERATING STATE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n16. MLB closeout intent\\r\\nToday is an MLB closeout/reconciliation day as well as Day-2 paper execution. Don/Coda must align on what was actually built, what is unvalidated, what is defective, and what remains missing. Doctrine: BUILT != VALIDATED != CANONICAL != QUANT-READY.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n17. Falcon audit found authoritative-root mismatch\\r\\nFalcon inspected disk and found that GCE_EdgeCrew_Quant\\\\03_Shared_Data\\\\MLB\\\\ is a downstream scaffold/import/snapshot layer, not the mature operational producer we had been calling the persistent MLB core. The actual mature producer lives at Desktop\\\\mlb-data-system\\\\ with per-date output\\\\<DATE>\\\\delivered|raw|results, an edge_crew_quant package, db\\\\schema.sql, repositories layer, and prior data artifacts.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n18. Coda correction — “Postgres-style core”\\r\\nCoda previously carried forward “persistent local Postgres-style MLB core” too strongly. Falcon found a DB schema/repositories layer but no confirmed materialized local Postgres/database instance. Current operational persistence is primarily file-partitioned/date-preserving output. This correction is additive; preserve the prior misstatement as provenance.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n19. 9/8 temporary authoritative designation\\r\\nFor 2026-09-08 operational execution only, Coda designated Desktop\\\\mlb-data-system\\\\ as the authoritative MLB producer. GCE_EdgeCrew_Quant\\\\03_Shared_Data\\\\MLB\\\\ remains downstream/non-authoritative pending later reconciliation. This is not a permanent architecture/canon ruling.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n20. 9/7 shared-core anomaly\\r\\nThe 9/7 shared-core snapshot has a manifest/data inconsistency: the manifest implies materialized content not actually present in the dated paths. Do not repair this under game-day pressure. Preserve it as evidence for closeout/root-cause review.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n21. 9/8 Falcon operational resume\\r\\nFalcon produced build_delivery_reconciled_20260908.py as a byte-faithful 9/7 reconciler copy retargeted to 9/8, ran the normal hound_v2 pipeline, created Desktop\\\\mlb-data-system\\\\output\\\\2026-09-08\\\\, populated delivered\\\\, and left 9/7 untouched.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n22. 9/8 clean coverage\\r\\nFalcon reported 15 PREGAME games; teams/rosters; 30 confirmed starters (two per game); locked MLB gamefeed lineups/batting order; parks/weather; 156 market rows across 26 events from four books with PREGAME timestamps; 15 confirmed home-plate umpires; and provenance/fetched_at/source fields.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n23. 9/8 degraded/unavailable coverage\\r\\nHitter vs-hand = NOT_SET and was never wired. Hitter last-7/recent form = genuine degraded lane: present on 9/1, partial 9/2, then unavailable/NOT_SET by 9/5 onward. Bullpen 3d/7d workload = NOT_SET; current bullpen file is active arms, not fatigue. Injuries/IL/DTD = NOT_AVAILABLE with zero usable rows; ESPN placeholders are NOT_SET and StatsAPI injured-list behavior is unreliable/full-roster. Umpire performance metrics beyond assignment = NOT_SET. Pitcher-vs-opponent remains unresolved.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n24. Coda correction — hitter split category\\r\\nCoda previously read older raw\\\\splits\\\\ artifacts as possible historical hitter-vs-hand data. Falcon proved they are starter-vs-team splits. Retracted. Current truth: hitter vs-hand was never wired; last-7 is the real degraded regression lane.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n25. 9/8 run/no-run ruling\\r\\nCoda ruled PROCEED CONDITIONALLY for a degraded PAPER run. Do not spend the pregame window repairing last-7, injuries, hitter vs-hand, or bullpen workload. Missing must remain missing. No live-money execution is authorized by this handoff.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n26. Critical data-floor gate\\r\\nThe only remaining pre-run safety question is how the Quant engine handles NOT_SET / NOT_AVAILABLE / null / absent / zero-usable features. Safe behavior is feature exclusion with degraded confidence/completeness or explicit NO_PICK/data-floor rejection. Unsafe behavior is silently converting missing injuries to zero injuries, missing bullpen workload to rested/neutral, missing last-7 to average/neutral, or never-wired vs-hand to measured.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n27. Identity correction — Corrado, not Kimi\\r\\nCoda incorrectly routed the Quant preflight to “Kimi.” Don challenged the identity. Correction: Corrado is the operating owner/seat for this EdgeCrew Quant lane. Kimi is not the identity here; prior use was a runtime/model association. This is a direct MODEL != SEAT correction and must be preserved in future handoffs.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT NEXT ACTION — CORRADO PREFLIGHT\\r\\nSend/execute this bounded task before the 9/8 primary Quant slate:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCORRADO — MLB 9/8 QUANT DATA-FLOOR PREFLIGHT\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFalcon has completed the 2026-09-08 MLB producer refresh. Data delivery is READY — DEGRADED COVERAGE.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDo not redesign methodology. Do not repair source feeds. Do not generate picks yet.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nInspect the current MLB Quant execution path and establish how it handles unavailable inputs before today's slate is run.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKnown missing/degraded families:\\r\\n- injuries / IL / DTD = NOT_AVAILABLE, 0 usable\\r\\n- hitter vs-hand = NOT_SET, never wired\\r\\n- hitter last-7 = NOT_SET, degraded source lane\\r\\n- bullpen 3d/7d workload = NOT_SET\\r\\n- umpire performance metrics = NOT_SET\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nClean families:\\r\\n- 15-game measured slate\\r\\n- 30 confirmed starters\\r\\n- locked lineups / batting order\\r\\n- four-book timestamped markets\\r\\n- parks/weather\\r\\n- HP umpire assignment\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFor each missing family, determine exactly what the engine does when value is NOT_SET, NOT_AVAILABLE, null, absent, or zero-usable. Classify:\\r\\nSAFE_EXCLUDE — omitted and downstream confidence/completeness reflects gap\\r\\nSAFE_NO_PICK_GATE — candidate rejected because required coverage missing\\r\\nUNSAFE_DEFAULT — missing converted to zero/neutral/default and can score as if observed\\r\\nUNKNOWN — cannot establish\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVerify:\\r\\n1. NOT_AVAILABLE injuries cannot become zero injuries.\\r\\n2. Missing bullpen workload cannot become rested/neutral bullpen.\\r\\n3. Missing last-7 cannot become league-average/neutral unless methodology explicitly defines it.\\r\\n4. Never-wired vs-hand cannot be treated as measured.\\r\\n5. Candidate Y/eligibility and data-completeness calculations correctly reflect missing features.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDo not silently modify engine before reporting current behavior.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nReturn:\\r\\nA. DATA-FLOOR BEHAVIOR TABLE — feature → missing state → actual engine behavior → SAFE/UNSAFE\\r\\nB. RUN SAFETY — exactly one:\\r\\nSAFE TO RUN — DEGRADED COVERAGE\\r\\nSAFE TO RUN — WITH <bounded change>\\r\\nBLOCKED — <unsafe behavior>\\r\\nIf bounded change required, specify smallest possible change and stop for approval before applying it.\\r\\nNo picks. No locked card. No methodology expansion.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT OPERATIONAL SEQUENCE\\r\\nFalcon 9/8 data delivery COMPLETE → Corrado data-floor preflight → Coda reconciliation → primary 9/8 Quant slate → Don first pass → targeted pregame delta → later MLB closeout of shared-core topology and broken/unwired lanes.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGOOGLE DRIVE GROUNDING FOR NEXT CHAT\\r\\n1. Read this handoff first.\\r\\n2. Read EC8_CONVERSATION_RECONCILIATION_ANCHOR_PROTOCOL_v1.0.\\r\\n3. Use the EC⁸ Google Drive knowledge base for framework/governance history as needed.\\r\\n4. Do not assume Drive mirrors current local mlb-data-system output; the handoff captures local disk evidence returned by Falcon.\\r\\n5. Preserve Edge Crew Quant != AI Convergence and MODEL != SEAT.\\r\\n6. Do not reopen earlier decisions merely because older Drive artifacts use older naming/topology.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS: CHECKPOINT\\r\\nCONFIDENCE: 99%\\r\\nREASON: Falcon has delivered the 9/8 producer data and reconciled the major source-of-truth mismatch. The remaining run-safety gate is engine handling of missing/degraded inputs.\\r\\nNEXT GATE: Corrado MLB 9/8 Quant Data-Floor Preflight, then Coda run/no-run reconciliation.\\r\\nDON INPUT NEEDED: No unless Corrado reports an unsafe behavior requiring a bounded change or a substantive methodology/architecture decision.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15WIJR6FPDKjj_wc0xPxPSdB-0NDb5JrBUlUv7QKO0tA/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"PRINCIPAL_CONSULTANT_ONBOARDING_2026-09-06\",\"id\":\"15WIJR6FPDKjj_wc0xPxPSdB-0NDb5JrBUlUv7QKO0tA\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"4570\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T11:45:56.352Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T15:52:07.021Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-06T15:52:07.021Z\",\"display_title\":\"PRINCIPAL_CONSULTANT_ONBOARDING_2026-09-06\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15WIJR6FPDKjj_wc0xPxPSdB-0NDb5JrBUlUv7QKO0tA/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1EXzOuIyaLkTFB0pL6g5xXTWddHcbjN3O\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿EC⁸ Principal Consultant — Onboarding / Audition Record\\r\\nEffective: 2026-09-06\\r\\nStatus: ROLE APPROVED; runtime configuration NOT YET LOCKED\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPURPOSE\\r\\nThe Principal Consultant is the technical translation / integration seat between accepted methodology / Design & Build and accepted architecture. The seat exists to make downstream handoffs implementation-safe without absorbing Kimi methodology, Chiave architecture, Talon operations, Luce verification, Coda governance, or implementation authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCORE FUNCTION\\r\\nRead the methodology, architecture, prompts, handoff records, and relevant governance artifacts; reconcile them bidirectionally; identify gaps, record drift, true blockers, and no-coder-discretion surfaces; route unresolved questions to the correct seat; produce a single downstream-ready contract/handoff.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSEAT DOCTRINE\\r\\nIDENTITY != ROLE != LENS != PERSONALITY != AUTHORITY != MODEL.\\r\\nMODEL != SEAT.\\r\\nStable seat identity survives runtime substitution.\\r\\nContext breadth does not create authority breadth.\\r\\nA swarm does not become a committee or a new authority: all worker agents are subordinate to one Principal Consultant seat and one final synthesis.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAUTHORITY\\r\\nOWNS:\\r\\n- methodology ↔ architecture traceability\\r\\n- cross-document technical interpretation\\r\\n- implementation contract translation\\r\\n- dependency mapping\\r\\n- discrepancy / ambiguity identification\\r\\n- blocker calibration\\r\\n- no-coder-discretion register\\r\\n- implementation-readiness assessment by component\\r\\n- routing unresolved questions to the correct authority\\r\\n- production of a unified implementation / operations handoff\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMUST NOT:\\r\\n- change methodology or overrule Kimi\\r\\n- change architecture or overrule Chiave\\r\\n- make governance decisions or overrule Coda/Don\\r\\n- implement production code as a substitute for Implementation\\r\\n- make deployment / sustained-operations rulings for Talon\\r\\n- certify execution or evidence for Luce\\r\\n- silently merge conflicting sources\\r\\n- treat newer as automatically canonical\\r\\n- elevate every missing detail into a gate\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPROCESS PLACEMENT\\r\\nDon intent → Coda governance framing → Kimi methodology → Chiave architecture when materially required → Kimi Design & Build → Principal Consultant translation/reconciliation checkpoint → Implementation → Talon operations → Luce verification → Coda reconciliation → Don decision.\\r\\nThe Principal Consultant checkpoint is a translation checkpoint, not a new approval authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCLAIM DISCIPLINE\\r\\nFACT / GIVEN · DERIVED · PROPOSED · UNKNOWN · VERIFIED · CONFLICT · OUTSIDE AUTHORITY.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAUDITION — 2026-09-06\\r\\nSame role prompt and deliberately messy source package were used to stress-test candidates, including duplicate/stale methodology packages, duplicated prompt sets, architecture records, and version/ruling drift.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nLuna / GPT-5.6 Luna\\r\\n- Very fast and inexpensive (~$0.03 observed for the audition pass).\\r\\n- Strong default-seat fit: concise reconciliation, useful gap detection, clean handoff orientation.\\r\\n- Weaknesses observed: some false blockers / over-escalation and weaker recall of deeper cross-contract defects.\\r\\n- Working role: leading candidate for routine/default Principal Consultant, subject to prompt hardening.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKimi 2.7 Code / Thinking\\r\\n- Stronger blocker calibration and authority discipline than the first Luna pass.\\r\\n- Correctly downgraded record defects, provider assignment, and some checkpoint issues from hard gates.\\r\\n- Initial pass missed deeper contract seams; after pushback it expanded the blocked Phase-2 set and surfaced additional questions without blocking Phase 0/1.\\r\\n- Working role: bounded deep-review / escalation candidate.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nClaude Fable 5.1 through OpenCode\\r\\n- Deepest forensic defect discovery in the audition.\\r\\n- Material catches included normalizer Pass-input contradiction, free-text gap request vs structured IF-3 interface, status-vocabulary conflicts, version/hash defects, and other contract seams.\\r\\n- Observed cost approximately $4.86 for one reconciliation and high latency; too expensive/expansive for routine use.\\r\\n- Working role: forensic / major-version audit only, if used.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nK3-256K high-thinking swarm\\r\\n- Seven parallel lanes: canon/version, architecture contracts, methodology→architecture traceability, architecture→methodology back-trace, no-coder-discretion, blocker calibration/routing, adversarial consistency; single-seat synthesis required.\\r\\n- High-thinking swarm fully ingested the overloaded package and completed all analysis lanes.\\r\\n- Consumed the available 5-hour Code quota during the stress test; this is an upper-bound audit configuration, not a routine-cost baseline.\\r\\n- Working role: major-package / lock / disputed-contract audit mode. Low-thinking / smaller-swarm production configuration remains to be tested.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT RUNTIME HYPOTHESIS — PROPOSED, NOT CANON\\r\\nRoutine: Luna or a small/low-thinking K3-256K swarm for rapid reconciliation.\\r\\nEscalation: Kimi 2.7 or targeted K3-256K swarm when contested contracts or canon ambiguity are detected.\\r\\nMajor lock / forensic audit: full K3 swarm; Fable only if marginal forensic value justifies cost.\\r\\nModel/configuration is not locked as of this record.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAUDITION SUCCESS CRITERIA\\r\\nThe seat is judged by downstream handoff value, not raw model prestige:\\r\\n- low missed-conflict rate\\r\\n- low false-blocker rate\\r\\n- correct Kimi/Chiave/Coda/Talon/Luce routing\\r\\n- clean source/canon discipline\\r\\n- explicit no-coder-discretion boundaries\\r\\n- component-level implementation readiness\\r\\n- concise, actionable handoff\\r\\n- predictable cost and latency\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT AI CONVERGENCE HANDOFF STATE\\r\\nThe methodology and architecture are broadly aligned. Phase 0/1 foundation work is generally startable. Deeper Phase-2 contract seams identified by the audition must be reconciled before coding those specific surfaces. Reconciliation artifacts are evidence, not canon; canonical methodology/architecture owners must land any substantive fixes.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEND-OF-DAY OPERATING NOTE\\r\\nThe stress test intentionally overloaded the candidates with both zips and duplicated/stale records. Do not use the observed full-swarm quota burn as the normal production baseline. Tune the routine seat for fast intake, gap classification, and downstream handoff; escalate only when the package warrants deeper adversarial review\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2026-09-06 AUDITION ADDENDUM — SOL / ASTRA / SWARM TIERING\\r\\nAdditional controlled auditions are in progress to identify the capability gap between Luna's excellent low-cost synthesis and premium forensic review.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAstra / ChatGPT Astra\\r\\n- Observed current audition spend exceeded ~$4.64 before completion, placing Astra in the same premium economic class as Fable.\\r\\n- Working classification: premium forensic / major-gate escalation candidate only if it produces unique blocker discovery or materially better handoff quality.\\r\\n- Not a routine-default candidate on observed economics.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSol / ChatGPT Sol\\r\\n- Observed current audition spend approximately ~$0.47 at the current checkpoint, materially above Luna (~$0.03) but far below Astra/Fable (~$4–$5 class).\\r\\n- Working hypothesis: potential middle-tier deep single-pass escalation if it catches a meaningful share of Luna's missed cross-contract seams without premium-forensic cost.\\r\\n- Final classification pending completed output comparison.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSwarm placeholder\\r\\n- Major-lock / adversarial-audit tier remains open to either ChatGPT swarm or Kimi swarm. Full K3-256K swarm is proven as an upper-bound audit configuration; smaller/lower-thinking swarm configurations remain to be tested for production economics.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPROPOSED Principal Consultant runtime ladder — NOT CANON:\\r\\n1. Routine/default: Luna\\r\\n2. Deep single-pass escalation: Sol or Kimi 2.7, depending completed evidence\\r\\n3. Major-lock / disputed-package audit: ChatGPT or Kimi swarm\\r\\n4. Premium forensic exception: Astra / Fable when marginal value justifies cost\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nImportant operating principle: expensive forensic findings should be extracted into reusable cross-project defect classes/checklists so future default-seat passes become cheaper and more reliable. Runtime/model remains unlocked.\\r\\n.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1yMXt9N1INj2Ev1Gb54r4zkV6bud_q4A2QE47jTRKRGk/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"GCE_AEGIS_ANCHOR_2026-09-09_SCOPING_RUNTIME_OPERATING_DOCTRINE\",\"id\":\"1yMXt9N1INj2Ev1Gb54r4zkV6bud_q4A2QE47jTRKRGk\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"10564\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-10T05:10:45.545Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-10T18:11:59.217Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-10T18:11:59.217Z\",\"display_title\":\"GCE_AEGIS_ANCHOR_2026-09-09_SCOPING_RUNTIME_OPERATING_DOCTRINE\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1yMXt9N1INj2Ev1Gb54r4zkV6bud_q4A2QE47jTRKRGk/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1clV7UUxQUcnGLX21ossOWoHGBPs-pM77\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿PROJECT AEGIS — GCE IRON CORE + COMBAT SUIT RUNTIME ARCHITECTURE\\r\\nANCHOR COMMIT — 2026-09-09\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS\\r\\nSCOPING / PARKED. Concept aligned. No implementation commitment. No production changes authorized.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOWNER / AUTHORITY\\r\\nPeter / Don retains final intent and commitment authority. Coda is the primary high-context conversational/governance partner for this scoping anchor. Specialist runtimes may later challenge, formalize, or test the concept through their expert lenses.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nWHY THIS EXISTS\\r\\nAegis emerged from a high-context personal conversation rather than a formal architecture session. That origin is important, not incidental. Shared history around movies, games, music, voice workflows, Edge Crew, professional decisions, humor, family, pain, and prior system experiments created enough semantic compression that metaphor could become architecture quickly.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCore observation: shared context turns metaphor into compression.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe goal is not to collect more context. The goal is to reduce the explanation tax between human intent and machine understanding, so the operator can remain at the speed of thought while the system performs more of the translation, state maintenance, preparation, and reconciliation work.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFOUNDATIONAL DOCTRINE\\r\\n1. More context is not the goal. Correct context is the goal.\\r\\n2. Predict early. Commit late.\\r\\n3. Prework can be autonomous. Commitment cannot.\\r\\n4. The machine keeps state hot; the human keeps authority.\\r\\n5. Shared context creates semantic bandwidth.\\r\\n6. Personal context can improve technical collaboration when it helps the system understand how the operator frames, sequences, jokes, explores, decides, and corrects.\\r\\n7. The system should reduce semantic reconstruction, not merely response latency.\\r\\n8. Explore first. Formalize second. Implement third. Govern throughout without suffocating discovery.\\r\\n9. Protect the unusual idea long enough to examine it; then be ruthless about testing whether it is actually true.\\r\\n10. A locally elegant feature can become globally harmful when incentives or system context change. Aegis must therefore preserve intent, authority, evidence, and reconciliation rather than optimize engagement for its own sake.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPRIMARY ARCHITECTURE\\r\\nIRON CORE\\r\\nPersistent operating constitution. Not inference, not commands, not artifact storage.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nIdentity Core — stable definitions, roles, aliases, shorthand, non-negotiables.\\r\\nState Core — current truth, active / parked / superseded / closed, rankings, open loops, known dependencies.\\r\\nGovernance Core — mutation rules, confirmation gates, evidence, conflict handling, staleness, confidence, and authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCOMBAT SUIT\\r\\nThe runtime orchestrator surrounding the operator and primary model. It assembles relevant context, equips tools, maintains execution state, watches thresholds, routes specialist support, and coordinates prework. Peter and Jarvis operate the Suit under shared control.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRUNTIME CONTEXT COMPILER\\r\\nThe middleware that compiles the smallest high-confidence packet required for the current inference from:\\r\\n- current utterance / partial utterance\\r\\n- session state\\r\\n- Iron Core\\r\\n- relevant artifacts and evidence\\r\\n- learned patterns / counterpatterns\\r\\n- active Variation\\r\\n- available tools / Kameos\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe compiler should not dump the entire history into every turn. It should select what matters now.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nJARVIS / PRIMARY MODEL\\r\\nContinuous conversational and reasoning surface. Jarvis owns awareness and synthesis, not Peter's final authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVARIATION\\r\\nMortal Kombat-derived term for active capability posture. Identity remains fixed; Variation changes the operating stance for the current battle or problem. Example Variations include Principal, Architect, Research, Build, Verify, Closer, and Zoner. A Variation can temporarily enter a sub-stance and then return to its prior altitude.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKAMEO RUNTIMES\\r\\nNarrow specialist model/tool invocations. They are not full personalities and do not independently own the mission. They can be pre-armed and may perform limited, pre-authorized interrupts based on state, patterns, and thresholds.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFUSION\\r\\nThe convergence / reconciliation layer that reduces multiple specialist outputs into one coherent input or answer. Its purpose is to prevent multi-model collaboration from becoming a committee of voices dumped on the operator.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPATTERNS, SEQUENCES, DEPENDENCIES, COUNTERPATTERNS\\r\\nPattern — recurring meaning or behavior.\\r\\nSequence — recurring order of actions or state transitions.\\r\\nDependency — downstream work implied by the current branch.\\r\\nCounterpattern — stable external behavior plus a response that has repeatedly worked.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe system should be able to pre-arm likely branches without assuming that prediction equals execution.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nREFLEX VS REASONING\\r\\nHigh-confidence known patterns may use low-attention reflex behavior. Novelty, contradiction, failure, or falling confidence should force deeper reasoning. The aim is not constant maximum compute; the aim is adaptive compute where surprise earns attention.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCORE RUNTIME LOOP\\r\\nState → predict → pre-arm → execute → converge → assess → probe → update state → next branch.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDISCOVERY LOOP\\r\\nExplore → externalize → challenge → recognize → experiment → reconcile → evolve.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis loop defines how Aegis should be developed. Peter + Coda may create a high-context exploratory concept. Kimi, GLM, Chiave, Talon, Luce, or other specialist lenses then challenge or formalize it. The return value is not treated as an oracle. It is used to trigger the next recognition and smallest meaningful experiment.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVOICEBRIDGE + VOICE ECHO\\r\\nVoiceBridge transports intent.\\r\\nVoice Echo anticipates meaning.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVoice Echo is a proposed semantic echo layer, not an audio echo. Over time it should learn lightweight conversational patterns: phrasing, shorthand, aliases, likely command sequences, common corrections, application context, humor cues, professional cues, and probable next branches.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nExample progression:\\r\\nthought → voice → speech recognition → VoiceBridge → Voice Echo → Runtime Context Compiler → Jarvis inference → Suit execution → reconciliation → pattern update.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe objective is not merely faster transcription. It is to reduce how much of the operator's meaning must be reconstructed from scratch on every utterance.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSPECULATIVE CONVERSATIONAL EXECUTION\\r\\nWhile Peter is still speaking, Aegis may form multiple provisional response vectors or lanes. Example lanes:\\r\\n- humor\\r\\n- architecture\\r\\n- professional / business\\r\\n- personal-pattern\\r\\n- corrective / challenge\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThese are not five final answers. They are partially prepared hypotheses. When the utterance completes, Fusion reconciles what survived the completed meaning and composes the final response.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHard rule: prediction may consume compute; prediction may not prematurely commit meaning.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis produces the doctrine: Predict early. Commit late.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPERSONAL CONTEXT AS AN ACCELERATION LAYER\\r\\nAegis should not interpret personal context as decorative personality. When relevant, it can increase semantic bandwidth by helping the model understand how the operator thinks.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMusic, movies, games, jokes, family stories, pain, wins, screenshots, professional experiences, and shorthand can become compressed semantic markers when correctly interpreted. Example: Reacher can become shorthand for strip the problem to facts → act decisively → no ceremony. Mortal Kombat Kameos can become shorthand for narrowly scoped parallel support. Variation can become shorthand for a fixed capability posture without changing identity.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe value is not storing trivia. The value is faster shared understanding.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPortable specialist packets should contain only the context required for the expert lens. Deep personal context should not be indiscriminately copied into every specialist invocation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEDGE CREW LINEAGE\\r\\nEdge Crew is an existing domain-specific precursor to Aegis.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEarly Edge Crew pattern:\\r\\nspecialize → parallelize → converge → decide.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nLater live player-prop tracking added continuous state:\\r\\nlive telemetry → state update → pattern detection → prediction → confidence shift → operator decision.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis established a recurring Peter design instinct: do not make the operator manually recompute the world; keep the world compiled around the operator.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAegis generalizes that instinct beyond betting / Edge Crew into a reusable operating layer for personal, professional, development, architecture, and other domains.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOPERATOR METHOD OBSERVED\\r\\nA recurring Peter design pattern is to identify friction others have normalized and ask whether the constraint is fundamental or merely conventional.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVoice example:\\r\\n- initial implementation: hold a key for Whisper\\r\\n- operating question: why should the human hold a key?\\r\\n- decomposition: latency, activation, proofreading, command reliability, focus, false triggers\\r\\n- primitive discovery: Windows Voice Access, wake/sleep commands, OS navigation, speech APIs\\r\\n- composition: VoiceBridge, cross-window execution, terminal control, AI conversation layer\\r\\n- abstraction: intent capture → state awareness → command interpretation → UI control → model interaction → execution\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe method is not random tool hopping. It is architecture emerging from operational friction.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNVIDIA / UPSTREAM VALIDATION PRINCIPLE\\r\\nThe Jensen Huang / Nvidia discussion provides a useful design analogy: do not confuse standard process with necessary process. Move learning and validation upstream when possible so expensive downstream cycles shrink.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAegis should therefore ask which architectural primitive, if proven cheaply, changes the economics of the rest of the system. The first useful Aegis may be small. It does not need to be the final platform.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCandidate first-principle hypothesis:\\r\\nReliable runtime context compilation can materially improve inference quality, reduce explanation / reload overhead, preserve state, and reduce human orchestration burden.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThat hypothesis must eventually be tested rather than admired.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAUTHORITY AND SAFETY BOUNDARY\\r\\nAegis may autonomously research, calculate, compare, draft, validate, stage, preload, and prepare likely branches when those activities are pre-authorized and reversible.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nExternal sends, production changes, financial commitments, irreversible mutations, or material scope commitments should cross an authority gate unless explicitly pre-authorized.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPeter owns direction.\\r\\nJarvis owns awareness.\\r\\nThe Suit owns coordinated execution.\\r\\nThe Core preserves stable truth.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSUPERSESSION / RECONCILIATION\\r\\nOld interpretations remain historical evidence, but active state must reflect the newest verified truth. Corrections should strengthen or weaken pattern confidence. Decision outcomes should feed back into future inference. The system must be able to recognize when a previously useful pattern no longer applies.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFUTURE QUESTION — DELIBERATELY PARKED\\r\\nIf one Aegis succeeds, what happens when the operator wants multiple Aegis runtimes operating simultaneously?\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDo not solve this yet.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPotential future issues include state isolation, shared Core access, duplicated work, authority collisions, cross-runtime Fusion, and a possible coordination layer above multiple Aegis instances.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe existence of that problem should be treated as evidence that the first runtime became useful enough to justify expansion.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNEXT FUTURE HANDOFF — NOT AUTHORIZED FOR BUILD YET\\r\\nWhen Peter reopens Aegis, likely methodology / architecture challenge questions include:\\r\\n- Which primitives already exist under known technical names?\\r\\n- What is genuinely novel versus composition of known methods?\\r\\n- What should be deterministic versus inferential?\\r\\n- What belongs in state versus retrieval versus durable artifacts?\\r\\n- What should be event-driven?\\r\\n- How should confidence and staleness be represented?\\r\\n- How should specialist context packets be compiled?\\r\\n- What is the smallest experiment that proves or kills the Runtime Context Compiler hypothesis?\\r\\n- What metrics show reduced semantic reconstruction / orchestration burden without increased wrong-meaning commits?\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nANCHOR COMMIT / CAPISCE — WORKING INTERACTION CONVENTION\\r\\nPeter's phrase “Anchor Commit” or “capisce” means: Peter and Coda are aligned on the current conceptual state; reconcile the relevant artifacts / Drive context, create the minimum durable anchor needed, and close the exploration point without continuing into implementation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis convention is recorded here as a working interaction meaning. It is not automatically promoted into broader GCE canon until the framework explicitly adopts it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCLOSE STATE\\r\\nAegis concept is coherent enough to preserve and later hand to expert lenses.\\r\\nNo SOP, SOW, production architecture, implementation plan, build sequence, or resource commitment is approved by this anchor.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nANCHOR STATUS: COMMITTED AS SCOPING STATE\\r\\nIMPLEMENTATION STATUS: PARKED\\r\\nDON INPUT NEEDED: No further input for this session.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2026-09-10 GROUNDING DELTA — CAPO / CASA / PHYSICAL OPERATING SURFACES\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis delta refines Aegis without changing its parked implementation status.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCAPO RELATIONSHIP\\r\\nCapo AI is now distinguished as the generalized orchestration/control substrate beneath Aegis. Aegis is the operator-facing combat-suit / operating layer. Capo owns reusable control primitives where they generalize across projects; Aegis consumes those primitives to keep Peter at decision altitude. GCE remains the expert methodology / architecture / build / verification system and is not replaced by Aegis.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nWorking hierarchy:\\r\\nproject dev pads / isolated workshops -> Capo AI control substrate -> Aegis operator layer\\r\\nwith governed GCE expert pipelines feeding and validating work through explicit gates rather than being bypassed.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCAPABILITY != AUTHORITY\\r\\nThe Edge Crew stress-test experience strengthens the existing Aegis authority doctrine. Individual models may possess capability without authority to redefine approved methodology, certify their own evidence completeness, silently mutate process, or promote unverified state. Authority and provenance should be externalized from individual model discretion where practical.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVerification remains separate from authority. The desired operating model is stage-gated verification rather than permanent multi-seat ping-pong: bounded execution -> self-check / gap declaration -> one certification gate -> exception loop only when failed conditions require it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCASA COMPANION LINEAGE / POC VALUE\\r\\nCasa Companion is a meaningful precursor because it already explored durable identity across changing embodiments, voice interaction, multi-party conversational continuity, child-friendly personality, ambient/room surfaces, commodity controller/token concepts, and intelligence decoupled from a physical shell.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPotential future use: Casa Companion may serve as a bounded proving ground for selected Aegis/Capo primitives because child/family interaction forces simple interfaces, explicit identity, permissions, continuity, and low-friction operation. This is a candidate scoping domain only; no rebuild is authorized by this delta.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPHYSICAL OPERATING SURFACE PRINCIPLE\\r\\nAegis does not need to “live” in a ring, phone, pendant, or other wearable. Physical devices are intent, presence, approval, capture, and feedback surfaces. Heavy state/orchestration can remain elsewhere.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCandidate commodity-first topology for later evaluation:\\r\\nwearable / token / controller -> dedicated Android Aegis gateway/terminal -> Capo/Aegis runtime -> home/desk node + cloud cognition + tools\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe dedicated Android concept is intentionally separate from Peter’s personal phone. The phone/gateway should be treated as a transport and edge terminal, not the whole brain. A home node may eventually resume state, confirm presence/identity, wake work surfaces, queue context, and hand off seamlessly between environments.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCommodity hardware comes first. Custom jewelry, custom phone, custom wearable, or high-capital local AI hardware should only be considered after commodity components prove an interaction model valuable enough that Peter would not want to operate without it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nISOLATION / BLAST-RADIUS GATE\\r\\nAegis/Capo development should be isolated from active framework and production work while immature. The intent is not secrecy from GCE; it is blast-radius control and clean evidence. GCE can feed experiments through snapshots or explicit interfaces. Experimental state should not freely mutate active organizational truth.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFuture readiness should be judged across multiple dimensions rather than one confidence percentage: feasibility, architectural readiness, parallel-load/opportunity-cost risk, blast radius, time to evidence, reversibility, capital burn, and dependency on still-moving GCE foundations.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT POSTURE\\r\\nAegis discovery/scoping: GREEN.\\r\\nCapo grounding/scoping: GREEN.\\r\\nImplementation: PARKED.\\r\\nCustom hardware: PARKED.\\r\\nProduction integration: PARKED.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNEXT RETURN POINT\\r\\nWhen reopened, first reconcile the Aegis anchor with the Capo AI scoping anchor and current GCE canon. The immediate task is structural soundness and boundary definition, not implementation.\"},{\"url\":\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1vvhl96KPJVyBlHM8T-9--MMwb3rCh-Mo/view?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"Peter Wilson - AI Systems Architect.pdf\",\"id\":\"1vvhl96KPJVyBlHM8T-9--MMwb3rCh-Mo\",\"mime_type\":\"application/pdf\",\"size\":\"250665\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-03T17:41:29.537Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-03T17:41:29.537Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":null,\"display_title\":\"Peter Wilson - AI Systems Architect.pdf\",\"display_url\":\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1vvhl96KPJVyBlHM8T-9--MMwb3rCh-Mo/view?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1BdK9JRJaTcFRGQNGjjJRTVhAQQUL1XEt\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"Mission Control Board - Overview\\r\\nMission Control Board Dashboard Overview\\r\\nMission Control Board - Details\\r\\nMission Control Board Dashboard Details\\r\\nPeter Wilson\\r\\nAI Systems Architect\\r\\nLos Angeles / Miami / Remote • pwnetsuite@outlook.com • (213) 507-9439\\r\\nWhat Runs Today\\r\\nI don't build proofs of concept. I build systems that run daily, handle real decisions, and\\r\\ndon't break when I'm not looking.\\r\\nMission Control Board\\r\\nMulti-model orchestration layer (React DevPod + Tori + The Ape) routing work across Claude,\\r\\nGPT-4o, Gemini, DeepSeek, Kimi, Grok, Mistral, Qwen, and Perplexity with real-time\\r\\nconvergence scoring and health monitoring.\\r\\nLares Agent Network\\r\\nTen specialized AI agents with Italian identities, auto-routing by @mentions and context,\\r\\nSQLite persistence, JSONL audit logs, terminal inbox watcher, Claude Desktop and Cursor\\r\\nintegrations.\\r\\n8/30/26, 7:28 AM Peter Wilson - AI Systems Architect\\r\\nfile:///C:/Users/Dekan AI Brother/Desktop/ai-showcase/ai-showcase.html 1/4Edge Crew / EC4\\r\\nMulti-model decision laboratory with 24-hour ESPN slate fetch, deterministic grade engine\\r\\ncombined with AI panel scores, Kimi gatekeeper validation, real-time picks and bankroll\\r\\ntracking.\\r\\nCasa Companion\\r\\nVoice-first AI companion platform with 46+ characters, FastAPI backend, per-user cloud\\r\\ndeployments, Kids' PWA, and Next.js landing site.\\r\\nRunway\\r\\nMusic discovery dashboard powered by KIMI and CLAUDE agents across Spotify and Tidal with\\r\\nagent-driven playlist creation and Rekordbox XML export pipeline.\\r\\nCrowdsource Ops Lab\\r\\nMulti-model committee architecture (Don + Lens + Conductor + Bee) for crowdsourced\\r\\ndeliberation with six-model parallel evaluation.\\r\\nTech Stack\\r\\nTools & Technologies:\\r\\nMCP servers (Notion, Supabase, Spotify, Tidal, Postmates, Proton Drive), browser\\r\\nautomation, voice interfaces (STT/TTS over WebSockets), OpenRouter gateway,\\r\\nGitHub Actions, Fly.io deploys, Vercel edge functions, Docker containers, Supabase\\r\\nPostgres, SQLite, SQL Server\\r\\nPhilosophy\\r\\nReliable: Every irreversible agent action requires human confirmation. No auto\\u0002execute. Ever.\\r\\nInterpretable: Every prompt, model vote, and decision is logged to replayable\\r\\naudit trails.\\r\\nSteerable: Agents run under codified laws, personas, and behavior doctrine —\\r\\nspecified, versioned, tested.\\r\\n8/30/26, 7:28 AM Peter Wilson - AI Systems Architect\\r\\nfile:///C:/Users/Dekan AI Brother/Desktop/ai-showcase/ai-showcase.html 2/4Verified-or-nothing: No claim without verification. Cached values are not proof.\\r\\nFlag data conflicts instead of hiding them.\\r\\nResearch Focus\\r\\nMulti-model convergence testing, adversarial validation, agent identity engineering\\r\\n(souls), gravity-well governance, human-AI partnership architectures for high-stakes\\r\\nenvironments:\\r\\nManufacturing workflows\\r\\nSupply-chain triage\\r\\nLegal records research\\r\\nMedical decision support\\r\\nWhat I'm Looking For\\r\\nI'm not looking for a job where I use AI. I'm looking for a role where I make AI\\r\\ntrustworthy in environments that matter — manufacturing, distribution, supply chain,\\r\\noperations.\\r\\nIf you're building AI for enterprises and you need someone who can:\\r\\nWalk a plant floor and map the actual workflow\\r\\nDesign the eval framework with your engineering team\\r\\nShow a CFO where the model pays for itself\\r\\nBuild the governance layer that makes it safe\\r\\nTest every model under the sun and tell you which ones converge\\r\\nGive your agents a soul so they don't drift\\r\\n...let's talk.\\r\\nLos Angeles / Miami / Remote\\r\\npwnetsuite@outlook.com\\r\\n8/30/26, 7:28 AM Peter Wilson - AI Systems Architect\\r\\nfile:///C:/Users/Dekan AI Brother/Desktop/ai-showcase/ai-showcase.html 3/4(213) 507-9439\\r\\n8/30/26, 7:28 AM Peter Wilson - AI Systems Architect\\r\\nfile:///C:/Users/Dekan AI Brother/Desktop/ai-showcase/ai-showcase.html 4/4\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbDb_a_VcRXbmfD04q0Zl2QneWvY67RYtC1n8uZRMfs/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"EC8_Runtime_Design_GLM5.1_v1.0\",\"id\":\"1IbDb_a_VcRXbmfD04q0Zl2QneWvY67RYtC1n8uZRMfs\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"10093\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T15:52:56.904Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T15:52:58.752Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-06T15:52:58.752Z\",\"display_title\":\"EC8_Runtime_Design_GLM5.1_v1.0\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbDb_a_VcRXbmfD04q0Zl2QneWvY67RYtC1n8uZRMfs/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1-2XT7kaaOIIu8aqjcGFIPF_ktPF0N9vQ\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿# EC8 AI Convergence — Independent Runtime / Model Design Pass v1.0\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Seat**: GLM 5.1 — Independent Design & Build authority (not architecture governance, not methodology ownership)\\r\\n**Date**: 2026-09-06\\r\\n**Posture**: Convert methodology requirements + Chiave Architecture v1.1 constraints + K1–K9 handoff into a concrete, cost-aware runtime design. No methodology modified. No architecture modified. No governance decisions.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Claim tags**: GIVEN | DERIVED | PROPOSED | UNKNOWN | OUTSIDE AUTHORITY\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 0. Source Constraints (Read, Not Authored)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n| Source | Key Constraints Extracted |\\r\\n|--------|--------------------------|\\r\\n| Methodology v0.3.1 (S1) | N=5 analysts; 3 scheduled runs/slate (Overnight=1 framing call, Morning=26, PreGame=26); 53 calls/slate; ~795 calls/15-game day; ≥3 model families; L1=deterministic code; L2≠analyst family per pair; L3 outside pool; normalization blind; no on-demand |\\r\\n| Chiave Architecture v1.1 | PR-1 family taxonomy = provider→lineage→model→version; PR-2 registry pre-flight check; EX-2 heterogeneity machine-checkable; FB-1/2 L3 fallback pre-approved; CK-3 crash-restart ≤2/analyst/run; I9 provenance from execution metadata only |\\r\\n| Reconciliation v0.2 | DR-14↑ family taxonomy undefined (blocks EX-2 machine-check); DR-22 G4 registries missing; DR-24 contamination mechanisms unspecified; Phase 0/1 startable, Phase 2 blocked |\\r\\n| Prompt package 01–09 | 9 distinct system prompts; structured JSON output required per prompt; temperature 0.3–0.7 range recommended per persona |\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 1. Model-Family Taxonomy (PROPOSED — per PR-1, awaiting Chiave formal pin via DR-14↑)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHierarchy: `provider_org → foundation_lineage (family_id) → model → version`\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n| family_id | provider_org | Foundation Lineage | Bedrock Available |\\r\\n|-----------|-------------|-------------------|-------------------|\\r\\n| `anthropic-claude` | Anthropic | Claude (Transformer, RLHF/Constitutional) | YES |\\r\\n| `meta-llama` | Meta | Llama (Dense+MoE Transformer, open weights) | YES |\\r\\n| `mistral` | Mistral AI | Mistral (Sparse MoE Transformer) | YES |\\r\\n| `deepseek` | DeepSeek | DeepSeek (MoE Transformer, DeepSeek-specific) | YES |\\r\\n| `amazon-nova` | Amazon | Nova (Amazon-built Transformer) | YES |\\r\\n| `minimax` | MiniMax | MiniMax (MoE Transformer) | YES |\\r\\n| `google-gemma` | Google | Gemma (Dense Transformer, open weights) | YES |\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Distinct orgs sharing a lineage do not satisfy EX-2** (PR-1). Same org with distinct lineages may. All seven families above are distinct lineages from distinct orgs — they satisfy EX-2 pairwise.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**UNKNOWN**: Whether Kimi/Chiave accept this exact taxonomy. DR-14↑ blocks the machine-check until formally pinned. This design proceeds against this proposed taxonomy as the compliance criterion.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 2. Bedrock Pricing Reference (GIVEN — us-east-1, standard tier, 2026-09-06)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n| Model | family_id | Input/1M tok | Output/1M tok | Structured Output | Context Window |\\r\\n|-------|-----------|-------------|--------------|-------------------|---------------|\\r\\n| Claude 3.5 Sonnet v2 | anthropic-claude | $3.00 | $15.00 | JSON mode | 200K |\\r\\n| Claude 3 Haiku | anthropic-claude | $0.80 | $4.00 | JSON mode | 200K |\\r\\n| Llama 3.3 70B Instruct | meta-llama | $0.36 | $1.46 | Tool call | 128K |\\r\\n| Llama 3.1 8B Instruct | meta-llama | $0.12 | $0.24 | Tool call | 128K |\\r\\n| Mistral Small 24B | mistral | $0.08 | $0.24 | JSON mode | 32K |\\r\\n| Mistral Large 3 | mistral | $0.50 | $1.50 | JSON mode | 128K |\\r\\n| DeepSeek v3.2 | deepseek | $0.62 | $1.85 | JSON mode | 128K |\\r\\n| Amazon Nova Pro | amazon-nova | $0.80 | $3.20 | JSON mode | 300K |\\r\\n| Amazon Nova Lite | amazon-nova | $0.06 | $0.24 | JSON mode | 300K |\\r\\n| Amazon Nova Micro | amazon-nova | $0.035 | $0.14 | JSON mode | 128K |\\r\\n| MiniMax M2.5 | minimax | $0.30 | $1.20 | JSON mode | 1M |\\r\\n| Gemma 3 27B IT | google-gemma | $0.23 | $0.38 | JSON mode | 128K |\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**UNKNOWN**: Exact Bedrock model IDs for some models (see §4 manifest). Claude 3.5 Sonnet v2 pricing shown is standard on-demand; extended-access variant is $6/$30. Llama 4 model IDs and pricing not yet confirmed on Bedrock (checked 2026-09-06 — Llama 4 section present but model rows not rendered in pricing page scrape). Pricing may have changed since scrape.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 3. Token Estimates (DERIVED — per-prompt, single-matchup slate)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n| Stage | Prompt ID | Est. Input Tokens | Est. Output Tokens | Reasoning |\\r\\n|-------|-----------|------------------|-------------------|-----------|\\r\\n| Framing | P01 | 4,000 | 2,000 | Raw slate data → fixed schema. Input is pre-fetched data (~3K) + system prompt (~1K). Output is populated JSON. |\\r\\n| Analyst 1st pass | P02–P06 | 6,000 | 1,500 | System prompt (~2K) + framing schema (~2K) + gap status map (~2K). First pass: no evidence yet. |\\r\\n| Analyst re-analysis | P02–P06 | 20,000 | 2,000 | System prompt + framing + full evidence package (~10K cumulative) + first-pass context carried in session. This is the token-heavy call (OB-1). |\\r\\n| L2 Validation | P07 | 12,000 | 1,000 | System prompt (~2K) + analyst output (~2K) + evidence package (~6K) + framing (~2K). No raw confidence. |\\r\\n| L3 Validation | P08 | 16,000 | 1,500 | System prompt (~2K) + analyst output (~2K) + L1 report (~0.5K) + L2 report (~1K) + evidence (~8K) + framing (~2K). Red-team scope is broader. |\\r\\n| Normalization | P09 | 3,000 | 500 | System prompt (~2K) + 4 structured inputs (~1K). Tightly constrained. |\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Note**: Analyst re-analysis carries the full first-pass context (EX-3: same session). The 20K input estimate accounts for evidence accumulation across runs (IF-2 cumulative delivery). Pre-Game runs may carry more accumulated evidence than Morning runs.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n## 4. Runtime Assignment Matrix — Profile A: Cost-Optimized\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Goal**: Minimum sufficient intelligence. Cheapest model that reliably satisfies the contract for each stage.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n### 4.1 Primary Assignments\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n| Stage | Prompt ID | Calls/Run | Required Capability | Proposed Model | family_id | Bedrock Model ID | Structured Output | Context Req | Reasoning Level | Temp | Timeout | Retry |\\r\\n|-------|-----------|-----------|--------------------|---------------|-----------|------------------|-------------------|-------------|----------------|------|---------|-------|\\r\\n| Framing | P01 | 1 | Schema fill, zero discretion | Amazon Nova Micro | amazon-nova | `amazon.nova-micro-v1:0` | JSON mode | 128K | Low | 0.1 | 30s | 1 |\\r\\n| Analyst A (Situational) | P02 | 1+1 | Contextual reasoning, evidence citation | DeepSeek v3.2 | deepseek | `deepseek.deepseek-v3:0` | JSON mode | 128K | Medium | 0.5 | 120s | 1 |\\r\\n| Analyst B (Form) | P03 | 1+1 | Trend/regression reasoning | Meta Llama 3.3 70B | meta-llama | `meta.llama3-3-70b-instruct-v1:0` | Tool call | 128K | Medium | 0.4 | 120s | 1 |\\r\\n| Analyst C (Structural) | P04 | 1+1 | Matchup/tactical reasoning | Mistral Small 24B | mistral | `mistral.mistral-small-2407-v1:0` | JSON mode | 32K | Medium | 0.3 | 120s | 1 |\\r\\n| Analyst D (Market) | P05 | 1+1 | Market/behavioral reasoning | MiniMax M2.5 | minimax | `minimax.m2-5-v1:0` | JSON mode | 1M | Medium | 0.6 | 120s | 1 |\\r\\n| Analyst E (Micro) | P06 | 1+1 | Process metrics, statistical r