s.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT TASK\\r\\nWe are in the 2026-09-08 MLB Day-2 paper run. Falcon has completed the 9/8 local producer refresh from Desktop\\\\mlb-data-system\\\\. The producer is READY — DEGRADED COVERAGE. Coda has conditionally allowed the paper run, but only after Corrado verifies the Quant engine's data-floor behavior for missing inputs.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nImmediate next gate:\\r\\nCORRADO — MLB 9/8 QUANT DATA-FLOOR PREFLIGHT.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDo not generate picks before that preflight is reconciled.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKnown degraded/missing families:\\r\\n- injuries / IL / DTD = NOT_AVAILABLE\\r\\n- hitter vs-hand = NOT_SET, never wired\\r\\n- hitter last-7 = NOT_SET, degraded lane\\r\\n- bullpen 3d/7d workload = NOT_SET\\r\\n- umpire performance metrics beyond assignment = NOT_SET\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKnown clean families include the 15-game slate, confirmed starters, locked batting orders, timestamped four-book markets, parks/weather, HP umpire assignment, and provenance.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCritical safety rule:\\r\\nMissing/unavailable inputs may not silently become zero, neutral, rested, average, or measured values. They must be excluded with degraded completeness/confidence or force the appropriate NO_PICK/data-floor gate.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent operational sequence:\\r\\nFalcon delivery complete → Corrado data-floor preflight → Coda reconciliation → primary 9/8 Quant slate → Don first pass → targeted pregame delta → later MLB core/shared-data closeout.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nUse the approved Conversation Reconciliation Anchor process whenever this next chat becomes long or any naming/authority drift appears.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xmKy1byme2OfpdmMmJaKCqIVR0NNPH6UaedmHiarGN4/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"GCE_TO_EDGE_CREW_PROJECT_RECON_HANDOFF_2026-09-21\",\"id\":\"1xmKy1byme2OfpdmMmJaKCqIVR0NNPH6UaedmHiarGN4\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"5432\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-21T19:20:36.066Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-21T19:20:41.051Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-21T19:21:17.908Z\",\"display_title\":\"GCE_TO_EDGE_CREW_PROJECT_RECON_HANDOFF_2026-09-21\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xmKy1byme2OfpdmMmJaKCqIVR0NNPH6UaedmHiarGN4/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"19eSRsX4v67Y1aBiy62oIo5MEkTNJQUiO\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿GCE → EDGE CREW PROJECT RECON HANDOFF\\r\\nDate: 2026-09-21\\r\\nFrom: Coda — Strategic Advisor / Governance\\r\\nTo: Edge Crew project conversation / project-owned working lane\\r\\nStatus: RECON REQUEST — no project changes authorized by this handoff\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPURPOSE\\r\\nExplain what the framework-side recon found, how the main GCE framework chat is now operating, and what the Edge Crew project should review inside its own estate before any project documents are updated.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKEY BOUNDARY\\r\\nThe framework chat is now explicitly operating OUTSIDE Projects.\\r\\nProjects own project truth.\\r\\nFramework owns generalized doctrine, cross-project research, and governance reconciliation.\\r\\nFramework will not rewrite or reorganize Edge Crew implementation artifacts unless Don explicitly opens a project-specific task.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nWHAT FRAMEWORK RECON FOUND\\r\\n1. The canonical Drive split is sound:\\r\\n   GCE/\\r\\n   - GCE_ORG\\r\\n   - 03_Projects\\r\\n   - 06_Frozen_State_and_Archive\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2. Edge Crew correctly lives under:\\r\\n   GCE / 03_Projects / 01_Edge_Crew\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n3. The project already has a strong current Quant-oriented structure:\\r\\n   - 00_EC8_QUANT_CURRENT\\r\\n   - 01_CROSS_SPORT_METHOD\\r\\n   - 02_SPORTS\\r\\n   - 03_DATA_SUFFICIENCY\\r\\n   - 04_USER_PRODUCT_LOOP\\r\\n   - 90_PROVENANCE_ARCHIVE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n4. The project also contains older / legacy EC8 material, including:\\r\\n   - EC8\\r\\n   - 00_AI_Convergence_Project_Knowledge_Base\\r\\n   - older runtime designs, source-discipline docs, handoffs, and recovery material\\r\\n   These are valuable provenance but must not silently regain current authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n5. A few framework-oriented or cross-session documents are physically inside the Edge Crew project tree because they were created during project work. They should be reviewed by the project for correct ownership/disposition rather than automatically treated as Edge Crew methodology.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDOCUMENTS THE PROJECT SHOULD REVIEW\\r\\nAt minimum:\\r\\n- GCE_SESSION_HEADER_AND_PROMPT_DELIVERY_MEMORY_v1.0_2026-09-17\\r\\n  Current observed location: Edge Crew project root.\\r\\n  Framework assessment: cross-session GCE operating convention; likely framework-owned in substance.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- EC8_CONVERSATION_RECONCILIATION_ANCHOR_PROTOCOL_v1.0\\r\\n  Current observed location: Edge Crew project root.\\r\\n  Framework assessment: project-created reconciliation artifact; determine whether it remains project-specific, becomes generalized framework methodology, or both via separate owned artifacts.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- legacy EC8 / 00_AI_Convergence_Project_Knowledge_Base\\r\\n  Framework assessment: historical project provenance. Review for useful project lineage, but do not assume current AI Convergence authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- GCE_EDGE_CREW_* anchors / old session backups located outside the current Quant folders\\r\\n  Framework assessment: classify as project provenance vs generalized framework lesson. Do not duplicate current authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHOW FRAMEWORK IS OPERATING NOW\\r\\nFramework created non-project Technical Strategy lanes under:\\r\\nGCE_ORG / 01_Executive_Council / 02_Technical_Strategy_Systems_Intelligence\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n- 01_Model_Labor_Intelligence\\r\\n- 02_Runtime_Provider_Intelligence\\r\\n- 03_Proving_Grounds\\r\\n- 04_Cross_Project_Methodology_Research\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFramework has already extracted and preserved the cross-project lessons from the Black Pearl / model-lab work there.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nImportant: this does NOT change Edge Crew implementation truth.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nBLACK PEARL / MODEL LAB — FRAMEWORK VIEW\\r\\nBlack Pearl is being treated as a GCE proving-ground experiment, not an Edge Crew project branch.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFramework preserved these generalized findings:\\r\\n- model task-fit matters more than a simple model leaderboard\\r\\n- MODEL != SEAT\\r\\n- cognitive suitability != operational/provider suitability\\r\\n- independence must be evidenced, not assumed from different model names\\r\\n- POC / Discovery -> Design -> Architecture -> Validation -> Production\\r\\n- do not let an architect harden unfinished POC work prematurely\\r\\n- preserve provenance and disagreement\\r\\n- verification, adjudication, and final authority are separate\\r\\n- persistent architecture layers must be earned by repeated operating need\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe project should review any Black Pearl / AI Convergence / Matrix / Committee artifacts created from conversations and decide:\\r\\nA. project implementation truth\\r\\nB. project historical/provenance evidence\\r\\nC. cross-project/framework lesson already promoted outside Projects\\r\\nD. obsolete/superseded material\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDO NOT collapse those categories.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPROJECT RECON TASK\\r\\nPerform the same kind of recon inside Edge Crew that framework just performed outside it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nREAD FIRST. DO NOT UPDATE DOCUMENTS YET.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nReturn:\\r\\n1. CURRENT PROJECT AUTHORITY\\r\\n   - which folders/docs are actually current\\r\\n   - which artifact is the best project index / source-of-truth entry point\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2. PROJECT STRUCTURE\\r\\n   - current working lanes\\r\\n   - sport-specific lanes\\r\\n   - shared/cross-sport lanes\\r\\n   - AI Convergence / Matrix / Committee-related material if present\\r\\n   - archive/provenance\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n3. MISFILED OR CROSS-OWNED MATERIAL\\r\\n   - framework-owned docs inside Projects\\r\\n   - project docs outside Projects\\r\\n   - duplicate/superseded artifacts\\r\\n   - loose root artifacts\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n4. LINEAGE / SUPERSESSION\\r\\n   - EC3 / EC4 / EC8 / current Quant relationships\\r\\n   - which old AI Convergence materials are provenance only\\r\\n   - which newer artifacts supersede older project docs\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n5. BLACK PEARL / FOUR-LANE RECON\\r\\n   Review any documents from the recent Don+Coda discussion and classify:\\r\\n   - project-ready\\r\\n   - project research\\r\\n   - framework-only\\r\\n   - needs reconciliation\\r\\n   Do not promote anything merely because it is newer.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n6. RECOMMENDED PROJECT FILING PLAN\\r\\n   Propose the SMALLEST changes required.\\r\\n   Do not reorganize functioning Quant structure merely for aesthetics.\\r\\n   Prefer preserving current working paths and moving only clearly misfiled material.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n7. RETURN GAPS TO FRAMEWORK\\r\\n   Identify any project-derived lesson that appears genuinely cross-project and should be handed back to GCE for separate framework reconciliation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHARD RULES\\r\\n- Do not change project files during recon.\\r\\n- Do not rewrite frozen history.\\r\\n- Do not import framework research as project authority.\\r\\n- Do not let legacy AI Convergence material silently override newer project truth.\\r\\n- Do not create duplicate current artifacts.\\r\\n- Do not collapse project truth and framework doctrine into one document.\\r\\n- Preserve provenance and supersession explicitly.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPROJECT-TO-FRAMEWORK LOOP\\r\\nProject does work\\r\\n-> project owns current truth\\r\\n-> project produces handoff/evidence\\r\\n-> framework reconciles generalized lesson outside Projects\\r\\n-> Strategic Governance decides whether anything becomes standard/canon\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFramework does not become the project.\\r\\nProject does not become the framework.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEXPECTED STOP\\r\\nStop after the recon report and proposed filing plan.\\r\\nBring any ownership conflicts or material supersession questions back to Don before moving/updating artifacts.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS: CHECKPOINT\\r\\nCONFIDENCE: 97%\\r\\nREASON: framework-side ownership and research lanes are now separated; project-side truth still requires an internal Edge Crew recon before document updates.\\r\\nNEXT GATE: Edge Crew project performs read-only recon and returns classification / filing plan.\\r\\nDON INPUT NEEDED: only for disputed ownership, supersession, or material restructuring.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1i5qirCXzjoQIuOrIXWYalqC5BxAT0yduH6WY1aEfNGg/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"EC8_CONVERSATION_RECONCILIATION_ANCHOR_PROTOCOL_v1.0\",\"id\":\"1i5qirCXzjoQIuOrIXWYalqC5BxAT0yduH6WY1aEfNGg\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"3292\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-08T20:42:25.242Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-08T20:42:47.918Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-08T20:42:47.918Z\",\"display_title\":\"EC8_CONVERSATION_RECONCILIATION_ANCHOR_PROTOCOL_v1.0\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1i5qirCXzjoQIuOrIXWYalqC5BxAT0yduH6WY1aEfNGg/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"19eSRsX4v67Y1aBiy62oIo5MEkTNJQUiO\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿EC⁸ — Conversation Reconciliation Anchor (CRA) Protocol v1.0\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS: DON-APPROVED PROCESS STANDARD\\r\\nEFFECTIVE DATE: 2026-09-08\\r\\nOWNER: Coda — Strategic Governance\\r\\nSCOPE: EC⁸ project conversations and handoffs\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPURPOSE\\r\\nThe Conversation Reconciliation Anchor (CRA) is the standard long-chat reset and handoff control. It is used when a conversation becomes long, drift appears, labels/identities begin to blur, source assumptions accumulate, or a new chat is needed.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe CRA is not merely a summary. It must distill the conversation, reconcile corrections and supersessions, preserve unresolved conflicts, identify current truth, and create a clean continuation state.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nTRIGGERS\\r\\nRun a CRA when any of the following occur:\\r\\n- The conversation is long enough that context drift becomes plausible.\\r\\n- Don detects relabeling, identity/role confusion, authority drift, or source confusion.\\r\\n- The work is moving into a new chat/session.\\r\\n- Material corrections/retractions have accumulated.\\r\\n- A gate transition requires a clean state handoff.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nREQUIRED FORMAT\\r\\nDATE: YYYY-MM-DD\\r\\nSESSION: <current>\\r\\nSEAT: <current seat>\\r\\nCURRENT GATE: <gate>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThen provide topic-level bullets. Each bullet contains one concise paragraph that states:\\r\\n- what was discussed or decided;\\r\\n- current status and whether the statement is FACT / GIVEN / DERIVED / PROPOSED / UNKNOWN / VERIFIED / OUTSIDE AUTHORITY where material;\\r\\n- corrections or retractions that affect the topic;\\r\\n- unresolved gaps or dependencies;\\r\\n- authority/owner routing where material.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe CRA must end with:\\r\\nSTATUS: PROCEED / CHECKPOINT / STOP\\r\\nCONFIDENCE: X%\\r\\nREASON: ...\\r\\nNEXT GATE: ...\\r\\nDON INPUT NEEDED: Yes / No\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRECONCILIATION RULES\\r\\n1. IDENTITY != ROLE != LENS != PERSONALITY != AUTHORITY != MODEL.\\r\\n2. MODEL != SEAT. Runtime/model labels must not replace stable seat identity.\\r\\n3. Newer != canonical. A CRA must not silently promote the newest statement over prior canon.\\r\\n4. Corrections are additive. Preserve the prior error/provenance and state the correction explicitly.\\r\\n5. Conflicts are preserved until resolved by the correct authority.\\r\\n6. Context breadth does not grant authority breadth.\\r\\n7. A CRA does not create substantive authority. It records and reconciles the state already established.\\r\\n8. Do not silently merge Edge Crew Quant and AI Convergence. Branch/source boundaries remain in force.\\r\\n9. Do not hide UNKNOWN or NOT_AVAILABLE states for continuity convenience.\\r\\n10. The new chat must start from the CRA/current handoff before interpreting older history.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHANDOFF FUNCTION\\r\\nAfter Don approves a CRA:\\r\\n1. Update/add the relevant project artifacts without rewriting historical provenance.\\r\\n2. Create a current handoff artifact for the next chat.\\r\\n3. Point the new chat to the current handoff and relevant Google Drive knowledge-base artifacts.\\r\\n4. Preserve any local-vs-Drive source-of-truth distinction explicitly.\\r\\n5. Continue at the stated NEXT GATE rather than reopening earlier gates unless new evidence requires it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nQUALITY TEST\\r\\nA valid CRA should let a fresh project chat answer, without guessing:\\r\\n- What are we doing?\\r\\n- What is current truth?\\r\\n- What changed or was corrected?\\r\\n- Who owns the next action?\\r\\n- What is blocked, degraded, or unknown?\\r\\n- Which source is authoritative for the current task?\\r\\n- What is the exact next gate?\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAPPROVAL RECORD\\r\\nDon approved the Conversation Reconciliation Anchor framework on 2026-09-08 after using it to reconcile a long EdgeCrew Quant / MLB / product-strategy conversation. The process is approved as the default reset/handoff pattern when conversation length or drift warrants it.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sRa-hAVkK1Y2-t5qleexmwjUuB1_R_-7DtSSpSQ2_cg/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"EC8_Runtime_Design_Grok_ProfileV_Addendum_2026-09-06\",\"id\":\"1sRa-hAVkK1Y2-t5qleexmwjUuB1_R_-7DtSSpSQ2_cg\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"2482\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T15:52:20.006Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T15:53:44.627Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-06T15:53:44.627Z\",\"display_title\":\"EC8_Runtime_Design_Grok_ProfileV_Addendum_2026-09-06\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sRa-hAVkK1Y2-t5qleexmwjUuB1_R_-7DtSSpSQ2_cg/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1-2XT7kaaOIIu8aqjcGFIPF_ktPF0N9vQ\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿EC8 AI Convergence — Grok Profile V Value-Optimized Addendum\\r\\nDate: 2026-09-06\\r\\nSeat posture: Independent Design & Build candidate; runtime grok-4.6. Design evidence only; no methodology/architecture/governance change.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOptimization objective\\r\\nRe-optimized the original cost profile for VALUE, not minimum price: maximize expected quality, reliability, methodological fidelity, independence, and cost efficiency per dollar.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nProfile V assignments\\r\\n- Framing P01: Qwen3 32B — KEEP\\r\\n- Analyst A Situational P02: Qwen3 235B — CHANGE from MiniMax M2.5\\r\\n- Analyst B Form P03: Qwen3 235B — KEEP\\r\\n- Analyst C Structural P04: DeepSeek V3.2 — KEEP\\r\\n- Analyst D Market P05: Kimi K2.5 — KEEP\\r\\n- Analyst E Micro P06: GLM 5 — CHANGE from GLM 4.7\\r\\n- L2-A: DeepSeek V3.2 — CHANGE\\r\\n- L2-B: DeepSeek V3.2 — CHANGE\\r\\n- L2-C: Qwen3 235B — CHANGE\\r\\n- L2-D: DeepSeek V3.2 — KEEP\\r\\n- L2-E: Qwen3 235B — KEEP\\r\\n- L3 primary: Mistral Large 3 — KEEP\\r\\n- L3 fallback: Claude Haiku 4.5 — KEEP\\r\\n- Normalization P09: Qwen3 32B — KEEP\\r\\n- L1: deterministic code — KEEP\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nProfile V economics under Grok token assumptions\\r\\n- Morning: ~$0.217\\r\\n- Pre-Game: ~$0.217\\r\\n- 53-call slate: ~$0.436\\r\\n- 15-slate day: ~$6.54\\r\\n- 30 days at 15 slates/day: ~$196\\r\\n- Net increase over Profile A: ~8%\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nValue rationale\\r\\n- Pay more only where a named failure mode is being bought down: GLM 5 for Micro; stronger/legal L2 pairings.\\r\\n- Identified false economies: MiniMax as Situational/L2-C, GLM Flash analytical use, Gemma as L3, cheapening the Market lens, keeping GLM 4.7 on Micro.\\r\\n- Identified premium waste: premium Claude/GLM on framing/normalization, GLM 5 on Form, Grok on Situational, frontier premium models where the stage contract does not justify them.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nArchitecture posture\\r\\nAnalyst families after Profile V: {qwen, deepseek, kimi, glm} = 4 families, satisfying ≥3. L3 family mistral and fallback claude remain outside the analyst pool. Pairwise L2 family separation remains legal.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOpen concerns\\r\\n- Qwen/DeepSeek concentration may create correlated-reasoning risk despite formal family compliance; requires adversarial review/pilot evidence.\\r\\n- Several exact Mantle IDs were previously unverified; printed IDs must not be treated as VERIFIED until live catalog/invocation checks complete.\\r\\n- Nova is not permanently excluded. Prior current-path failure was execution evidence only; later GLM design independently recommends Nova and is now testing live access.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1REY4ZiC4qzII6mBzmDYjO5RqkGpiROrmhQpz7DwTCe8/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"02_EC8_BRAND_AND_BRANCH_MODEL\",\"id\":\"1REY4ZiC4qzII6mBzmDYjO5RqkGpiROrmhQpz7DwTCe8\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"1392\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T03:22:27.007Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T03:22:39.004Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-06T03:22:39.004Z\",\"display_title\":\"02_EC8_BRAND_AND_BRANCH_MODEL\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1REY4ZiC4qzII6mBzmDYjO5RqkGpiROrmhQpz7DwTCe8/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1-2XT7kaaOIIu8aqjcGFIPF_ktPF0N9vQ\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿EC⁸ Brand and Branch Model\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nParent\\r\\nEC⁸ is the umbrella intelligence platform. EC⁸ should not be interpreted as Edge Crew version 8; the exponent-eight identity is the parent brand.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nBranch model\\r\\nEC⁸\\r\\n├── Edge Crew — quantitative / mathematical intelligence: analytics, models, calculations, synthesis, measured edge\\r\\n├── AI Convergence branch — multi-model independent analysis, disagreement, reconciliation, confidence, committee intelligence\\r\\n└── future specialist branches\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNaming rule\\r\\nDo not use Edge Crew as the umbrella for non-quantitative methodologies. Keep Edge semantically tied to measurable / calculated / quantitative advantage.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nInternal mythology\\r\\nTerms such as Capo, seats, crews, council/table concepts may exist inside the operating system. The top-level public/system brand remains EC⁸.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bLQ0ZkL4I5r-wWviYgQPIwQPqpdvZySk7jYtVd8yDFw/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"GCE_EDGE_CREW_ANCHOR_2026-09-03_FRAMEWORK_METHODOLOGY_INTENT\",\"id\":\"1bLQ0ZkL4I5r-wWviYgQPIwQPqpdvZySk7jYtVd8yDFw\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"8360\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-03T17:54:48.334Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T11:49:33.494Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-06T11:49:33.494Z\",\"display_title\":\"GCE_EDGE_CREW_ANCHOR_2026-09-03_FRAMEWORK_METHODOLOGY_INTENT\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bLQ0ZkL4I5r-wWviYgQPIwQPqpdvZySk7jYtVd8yDFw/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1clV7UUxQUcnGLX21ossOWoHGBPs-pM77\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿GCE EDGE CREW ANCHOR — FRAMEWORK / METHODOLOGY / INTENT\\r\\nDate: 2026-09-03\\r\\nAuthority: Don + Coda\\r\\nStatus: WORKING CANONICAL ANCHOR / EDGE CREW\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPURPOSE\\r\\nPreserve the approved framework, methodology separations, Don intent, forensic findings, and current project checkpoints for Edge Crew so future sessions resume from this state rather than reconstructing from chat chronology.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n1. COMPANY / FRAMEWORK CONTEXT\\r\\nEdge Crew is a project environment, not a Council or methodology. It consumes Executive Council authority, Shared Enterprise Services, methodologies, managers, and implementation workers as needed.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nExecutive Council:\\r\\n- Coda — Strategic / Governance\\r\\n- Kimi — Technical Strategy / Systems Intelligence\\r\\n- Talon — Operations\\r\\n- Chiave — Architecture\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nShared Enterprise Services:\\r\\n- Data / Intelligence — Data Hound\\r\\n- Verification / Ground Truth — Big Pickle\\r\\n- QA / Validation\\r\\n- Prompt / Context Translation — placement approved 2026-09-03; final title/identity still open. Function translates and packages approved authority/context for model-specific execution. It does not invent methodology, architecture, or authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nImplementation seat:\\r\\n- Implementation Agent — replaceable coding/execution model. Implements approved architecture/spec, tests, fixes, and escalates. Model is runtime, not identity/authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCore rule: IDENTITY != ROLE != LENS != PERSONALITY != AUTHORITY != MODEL. Capability != authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2. EDGE CREW OVERALL INTENT\\r\\nEdge Crew is a sports decision-intelligence system, not fundamentally an edge-finding or tipster system.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOriginal Don intent:\\r\\n- Get Peter's analytical betting process out of his head and make it explicit, transparent, testable, and auditable.\\r\\n- Start from relevant data and structured evidence.\\r\\n- Preserve independent analytical lanes.\\r\\n- Detect compound signals and value signals.\\r\\n- Converge independent evidence into a recommendation.\\r\\n- Validate/challenge the recommendation without silently mutating it.\\r\\n- Show the reasoning and evidence.\\r\\n- Stop before wagering; Don makes the final human decision.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nTerminology correction approved 2026-09-03:\\r\\n- EDGE / EXPECTED VALUE are reserved for demonstrated quantitative pricing advantage.\\r\\n- COMPOUND SIGNAL / VALUE SIGNAL describe evidence that strengthens or weakens a play in the EC3/EC4 decision-intelligence lineage.\\r\\n- CONVERGENCE STRENGTH / DECISION CONFIDENCE describe agreement between independent analytical signals.\\r\\n- Quant is one methodology/analytical lane within the larger Edge Crew vision, not the definition of Edge Crew.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n3. ORIGINAL DESIGN EVIDENCE\\r\\nThe EC8 designer brief confirms the intended conceptual product:\\r\\n- decision-intelligence / sports analytics intelligence\\r\\n- transparency as the product\\r\\n- two processes, one convergence, one gatekeeper\\r\\n- deterministic 'Our Process' lane\\r\\n- independent AI Process lane\\r\\n- compound-signal detection\\r\\n- human-visible reasoning and final decision\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHistorical wording used 'edge' loosely. The corrected semantic interpretation is compound signal / value signal unless mathematically demonstrated EV is being discussed.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n4. METHODOLOGY SEPARATION\\r\\nMethodologies must remain isolated. No downstream model should know that multiple Edge Crew methodologies are compared at the Don level unless explicitly authorized.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent methodology branches:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nA. EDGE CREW QUANT\\r\\nPurpose: true quantitative edge / expected-value methodology.\\r\\nStatus: Methodology Checkpoint 01 preserved 2026-09-03.\\r\\nKey separation learned:\\r\\n- Kimi owns/recommends methodology, but recommendation does not prove source acquisition.\\r\\n- No source may participate operationally until acquisition is proven.\\r\\n- Data Hound proves source availability/reliability.\\r\\n- Chiave/GLM designs architecture from approved methodology + proven sources.\\r\\n- Implementation Agent executes approved architecture/spec.\\r\\n- Fixture/engine validation != live-ingestion validation != production validation.\\r\\n- Quant methodology is preserved; implementation is NOT frozen.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nB. EDGE CREW ORIGINAL CONVERGENCE — EC3 RECOVERED FOUNDATION\\r\\nPurpose: recover Peter's original working decision-intelligence process independent of implementation quality.\\r\\nFoundational rule: two independent signal lanes remain independent until Convergence.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSemantic flow:\\r\\n0. Slate assembly / ingestion\\r\\n1. Deterministic engine — 'our process'\\r\\n2. Independent AI judgment panel\\r\\n3. Convergence — single merge point\\r\\n4. Pick computation\\r\\n5. Value signals / hard rules\\r\\n6. Validation-only gatekeeper\\r\\n7. One terminal kill resolution\\r\\n8. Output\\r\\n9. Don outside the routine pipeline — lock/reject/discretionary action\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHard rules:\\r\\n- validation-only gatekeeper; no score/pick/confidence mutation\\r\\n- missing/insufficient data is a stop, never neutral evidence\\r\\n- deterministic and AI lanes remain independent until convergence\\r\\n- one terminal KILL state\\r\\n- resolved KILL cannot be resurrected by consensus\\r\\n- Don remains outside the normal pipeline\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nUnresolved methodology decisions:\\r\\n- exact convergence weights/thresholds\\r\\n- data-floor threshold and mandatory fields by sport\\r\\n- kill-evidence normalization\\r\\n- AI roster behavior by sport\\r\\n- enrichment boundaries\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nC. EC4-DERIVED CONVERGENCE / VALUE-DISCOVERY CANDIDATE\\r\\nPurpose: preserve the useful methodology that evolved in EC4 without allowing it to overwrite Original Convergence.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nClarified Don intent 2026-09-03:\\r\\nEC4 was intended to start from a blind slate and use structured data plus diverse AI reasoning to discover non-quantitative value signals and increase/decrease confidence.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nTwo concepts became blurred in implementation:\\r\\n1. AI VALUE DISCOVERY — different AI reasoning approaches inspect the same blind slate/evidence to surface contextual/situational/historical/market signals that are not purely mathematical.\\r\\n2. COMMITTEE CONVERGENCE — a bounded deliberative unit, originally envisioned as roughly three models within one call/process, hashes out a grade/confidence/rationale. A committee produces a signal; it does NOT replace the overall convergence process.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCritical semantic rules:\\r\\n- Committee != Convergence.\\r\\n- AI Value Discovery != Quant.\\r\\n- Gatekeeper != Fusion.\\r\\n- Quantitative EV/edge mechanisms are separate unless explicitly approved as part of this methodology.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEC4 forensic extraction identified candidate concepts such as committees, lenses, market verification, fusion/judging, Kelly sizing, and other later additions. These remain candidate extensions until Don + methodology review decides what belongs.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nD. EDGE CREW AI JUDGMENT\\r\\nPurpose: pure AI/model judgment lane, isolated from Quant, Original Convergence, and EC4-derived methodology.\\r\\nStatus: concept approved; methodology not yet formalized.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nE. GREENFIELD AI-BUILT CONVERGENCE\\r\\nPurpose: allow an AI team to design a fresh convergence methodology from first principles under explicit guardrails, blind to the other methodologies.\\r\\nStatus: concept approved for later design.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nF. EC8 DETERMINISTIC PIPELINE\\r\\nStatus: preserved as candidate evidence only. Do not promote to a methodology branch yet.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n5. DON-ONLY CONVERGENCE RULE\\r\\nThe independent Edge Crew systems do not know they are being run side by side.\\r\\nOnly the Don receives and compares their outputs.\\r\\nPurpose: preserve independence and avoid correlated reasoning / methodological contamination.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nWorking conceptual set:\\r\\n- Quant\\r\\n- Original Convergence\\r\\n- EC4-derived Value/Committee methodology\\r\\n- AI Judgment\\r\\n- Greenfield AI-built Convergence\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFinal comparison/convergence is Don-only.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n6. EC3 / EC4 FORENSIC FINDINGS\\r\\nTalon established:\\r\\n- EC4 is evidence, not authority.\\r\\n- 'Go back to EC3' means recover the working EC3 PROCESS/GATING MODEL, not blindly restore an old codebase.\\r\\n- EC3 code was already imperfect/monolithic; process and implementation quality must be separated.\\r\\n- 54d2ff5c is a strong code-era evidence candidate, not automatically canonical.\\r\\n- EC4 accumulated multiple stage systems, duplicate gatekeepers, EV calculators, orchestration surfaces, monoliths, and collisions.\\r\\n- EC4 contains useful methodology ideas that should be extracted into an independent lineage rather than discarded or merged back into EC3.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n7. ROLE / HANDOFF MODEL FOR EDGE CREW\\r\\nDon / Peter:\\r\\n- final intent and authority\\r\\n- rules on genuine ambiguity\\r\\n- receives final independent outputs\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCoda:\\r\\n- framework integrity\\r\\n- reconciliation\\r\\n- canonicalization / checkpoint preservation until Prompt/Context seat is staffed\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKimi:\\r\\n- methodology and technical strategy\\r\\n- aggressively recommends improvements\\r\\n- must separate recommendation from approved methodology and from operational proof\\r\\n- may not silently promote hypothetical sources or implementation assumptions into canonical state\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nData Hound:\\r\\n- source acquisition proof\\r\\n- availability, fields, reliability, freshness, coverage\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nBig Pickle:\\r\\n- evidence, provenance, falsification, verified state\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nChiave / GLM:\\r\\n- architecture from approved methodology + proven requirements/data\\r\\n- does not redefine methodology\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nTalon:\\r\\n- operations, routing, workflow, handoffs, state\\r\\n- forensic process reconstruction where assigned\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPrompt / Context Translation:\\r\\n- packages approved mission/methodology/evidence for each downstream model/seat\\r\\n- hard dependency on verified provenance where factual/evidentiary claims are included\\r\\n- does not invent authority or methodology\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nImplementation Agent:\\r\\n- executes approved architecture/spec\\r\\n- writes/runs code, tests, fixes bugs, escalates deviations\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n8. KEY FAILURE MODE LEARNED — EXPERTISE OVERREACH\\r\\nUseful expert behavior becomes dangerous when a model moves from recommendation into silent operational assumption.\\r\\nExample learned in Quant: adding books/weights that appear methodologically desirable without first proving that the data source can actually be acquired.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPolicy:\\r\\n- expertise recommendation is encouraged\\r\\n- recommendation must be explicitly labeled\\r\\n- methodology approval is separate\\r\\n- acquisition proof is separate\\r\\n- architecture is separate\\r\\n- implementation is separate\\r\\n- production validation is separate\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n9. EDGE CREW LIVING CHECKPOINT\\r\\nAs of 2026-09-03:\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nQuant:\\r\\n- Methodology Checkpoint 01 preserved.\\r\\n- Mathematical/engine and synthetic fixture validation exist.\\r\\n- Live ingestion and production validation remain unproven.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOriginal Convergence:\\r\\n- EC3 recovered foundation completed.\\r\\n- Ready for fresh Kimi methodology formalization with Don.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEC4-derived methodology:\\r\\n- forensic candidate extracted.\\r\\n- Don intent clarified: AI value discovery + committee signal generation, not Quant edge hunting.\\r\\n- Ready for separate Kimi formalization; do not expose Original Convergence/Quant unless specifically authorized.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAI Judgment:\\r\\n- concept approved; not formalized.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGreenfield AI-built Convergence:\\r\\n- concept approved; later blind design exercise.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCasa Companion:\\r\\n- planned final cross-domain framework test before broad migration/development.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n10. DEVELOPMENT / VALIDATION STRATEGY\\r\\nUse projects as staged framework tests:\\r\\n1. Edge Crew Quant — methodology boundaries, source authority, validation-state separation.\\r\\n2. Edge Crew Convergence family — full-team orchestration, forensic recovery, isolated methodology formalization, handoff fidelity.\\r\\n3. Casa Companion — final generalization test outside sports analytics before broad migration/development.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDo not rush implementation. First prove that the framework preserves intent, role boundaries, provenance, methodology isolation, and handoffs.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n11. NEXT GATES\\r\\n- Preserve this Edge Crew anchor as the return point.\\r\\n- Formalize Original Convergence with a fresh Kimi project.\\r\\n- Formalize EC4-derived Value/Committee methodology in a separate fresh Kimi project.\\r\\n- Keep the two blind to one another and blind to Quant unless Don explicitly changes that rule.\\r\\n- Later perform cross-method capability-gap analysis at the framework level.\\r\\n- Kimi may identify conceptual gaps; GLM translates approved methodologies into architecture/capability requirements.\\r\\n- Do not add a new methodology merely because a feature is missing; first determine whether the gap belongs to Shared Services, architecture, data, verification, operations, or implementation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS: PROCEED\\r\\nCONFIDENCE: 99%\\r\\nREASON: Edge Crew intent, framework, historical recovery, methodology boundaries, and current checkpoints are aligned and explicitly separated.\\r\\nNEXT GATE: Fresh methodology formalization passes, starting with Original Convergence and EC4-derived Value/Committee lineage.\\r\\nDON INPUT NEEDED: Only genuine methodology decisions surfaced by those independent passes.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2026-09-06 ADDENDUM — PRINCIPAL CONSULTANT CROSS-PROJECT USE\\r\\nPrincipal Consultant — Technical Translation / Integration is now an approved GCE cross-functional seat available to Edge Crew and EC⁸ sibling branches. It is not an Edge Crew methodology and does not change Edge Crew branch boundaries.\\r\\nFor Edge Crew use, the seat may reconcile approved Kimi methodology / Design & Build with approved Chiave architecture and package the result for Implementation/Talon. It may identify gaps, record drift, and no-coder-discretion surfaces, but may not rewrite methodology, redefine architecture, create governance authority, execute, or certify.\\r\\nThe older Prompt / Context Translation candidate function remains a separate historical record unless Don explicitly consolidates or supersedes it. Do not silently merge the two roles.\\r\\nRuntime/model for Principal Consultant is not locked; 2026-09-06 audition evidence is filed separately in Model Onboarding.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1cVD0XgrN5tOIUzPmUW9ZrgsidWmr1R0_3nf_BwgnyPQ/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"09_NEW_PROJECT_CHAT_BOOTSTRAP\",\"id\":\"1cVD0XgrN5tOIUzPmUW9ZrgsidWmr1R0_3nf_BwgnyPQ\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"3787\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T03:24:38.471Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T15:55:39.037Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-06T15:55:39.037Z\",\"display_title\":\"09_NEW_PROJECT_CHAT_BOOTSTRAP\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1cVD0XgrN5tOIUzPmUW9ZrgsidWmr1R0_3nf_BwgnyPQ/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1-2XT7kaaOIIu8aqjcGFIPF_ktPF0N9vQ\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿New Project Chat Bootstrap — EC⁸ AI Convergence\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGround yourself in the attached EC⁸ AI Convergence knowledge base.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nWe are building the AI Convergence branch of EC⁸ from scratch through the GCE framework.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEC⁸ is the parent.\\r\\nEdge Crew is the quantitative / mathematical branch.\\r\\nAI Convergence is a separate sibling branch.\\r\\nEdge Crew Quant != AI Convergence.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent seats:\\r\\n- Don — Vision / Final Authority / interim human orchestrator\\r\\n- Coda — Strategic Governance\\r\\n- Kimi — Technical Stack Methodology / Design & Build\\r\\n- Chiave — Architecture\\r\\n- Talon — Operations\\r\\n- Luce — Verification / Ground Truth\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent sequence:\\r\\nDon intent → Coda governance → Kimi methodology → Chiave architecture when materially required → Kimi Design & Build → implementation → Talon operations → Luce verification → Coda reconciliation → Don decision.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDeepSeek/Talon has already returned an EC4 methodology recovery package. Treat it as evidence, not automatic canon.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nImmediate next gate:\\r\\nreview the DeepSeek recovery, isolate the clean AI Convergence methodology, preserve conflicts/unknowns, and prepare the methodology package for Kimi.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDo not import EC3 or Edge Crew Quant by default.\\r\\nDo not silently merge conflicting historical material.\\r\\nDo not start coding before methodology is accepted.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2026-09-06 BOOTSTRAP ADDENDUM\\r\\nAdd current seat: Principal Consultant — Technical Translation / Integration.\\r\\nCurrent sequence: Don → Coda → Kimi methodology → Chiave architecture when required → Kimi Design & Build → Principal Consultant translation/reconciliation → Implementation → Talon → Luce → Coda → Don.\\r\\nCurrent state supersedes the old immediate-next-gate language above: methodology and Architecture Specification v1.0 now exist; the project is post-architecture-gate, pre-implementation. Phase 0/1 are generally startable; named Phase-2 contract seams require reconciliation before coding those surfaces.\\r\\nPrincipal Consultant runtime/model is not locked. Ground future chats in the Principal Consultant onboarding/audition record before making runtime assumptions\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2026-09-06 BOOTSTRAP ADDENDUM — RUNTIME DESIGN / NEW-CHAT STATE\\r\\nCurrent verified technical state:\\r\\n- Corrected handoff package has K1–K9 physically applied and verified.\\r\\n- Chiave Architecture v1.1 exists.\\r\\n- The project is post-methodology/post-architecture and is now in runtime/design selection before implementation.\\r\\n- Phase 0/1 foundation work remains generally startable; semantic/runtime surfaces still require the final design/constraint pass before implementation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent working organizational refinement — PROPOSED, not yet final canon:\\r\\nDon → Coda governance → Kimi methodology → Chiave architecture when required → Principal Consultant specification/translation → Independent Design & Build [provisional] → Talon operational routing → Keel build/deploy/implementation test/evidence return → Luce independent verification → Coda reconciliation → Don.\\r\\nDo not silently convert this proposal into canon; preserve the prior combined Kimi Design & Build record until Don explicitly locks the new seat topology.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRuntime Design audition state:\\r\\n- Grok 4.6 produced EC8 Runtime Design v1.0 and a Value-Optimized Profile V. Strong live-environment interrogation; tested Nova current-path behavior; current value profile approximately $0.436 per 53-call slate under its token assumptions.\\r\\n- GLM 5.1 produced Independent Runtime / Model Design Pass v1.0. Recommended Balanced Profile B at approximately $0.397 per 53-call slate; Nova-heavy and Bedrock-native on paper; direct Nova executability is being tested now.\\r\\n- No runtime roster is approved. Treat all model IDs, availability, structured-output support, pricing, and token assumptions as PROPOSED/UNKNOWN until live verified where required.\\r\\n- Important comparison issue: GLM Profile B's stated L3 fallback uses Llama while Llama is also in its analyst pool; this appears to violate the outside-pool L3 constraint and must be corrected before adoption.\\r\\n- Nova is NOT permanently excluded. Prior Grok/Talon current-path failure is execution evidence, not a governance decision. GLM is now testing whether a viable Nova invocation path exists.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPrincipal Consultant audition state:\\r\\n- Luna remains leading routine/default candidate (~$0.03 observed).\\r\\n- Sol is being tested as a possible low-cost deeper second-pass tier (~$0.47 observed at current point).\\r\\n- Kimi/ChatGPT swarm remains a major-lock audit placeholder.\\r\\n- Astra has moved into premium-forensic economics (~$4.64+ observed during current audition); Fable remains the earlier premium forensic benchmark (~$4.86 observed).\\r\\n- Runtime stack remains PROPOSED; no Principal Consultant model is locked.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nImmediate next work for a new project chat:\\r\\n1. Ground in the new current handoff document and the corrected K1–K9 package + Architecture v1.1.\\r\\n2. Receive/inspect GLM's Nova test and any final tangent findings.\\r\\n3. Reconcile Grok Profile V vs GLM Profile B slot-by-slot on VALUE, not cheapest price.\\r\\n4. Verify live model IDs / Nova path / family constraints before any runtime canon decision.\\r\\n5. Continue Principal Consultant Sol/Astra audition comparison only as needed; extract reusable defect classes into the GCE review checklist.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNEW-CHAT GROUNDING ANCHOR\\r\\nPrimary current handoff: 10_CURRENT_HANDOFF_2026-09-06_RUNTIME_DESIGN\\r\\nDrive ID: 1SLU50Xz-ujenM6hGHdweEhNIJTvAkNFhjzJuI66MDOU\\r\\nStart there before interpreting older bootstrap text.\\r\\n.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1SLU50Xz-ujenM6hGHdweEhNIJTvAkNFhjzJuI66MDOU/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"10_CURRENT_HANDOFF_2026-09-06_RUNTIME_DESIGN\",\"id\":\"1SLU50Xz-ujenM6hGHdweEhNIJTvAkNFhjzJuI66MDOU\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"9183\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T15:53:56.977Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T15:55:11.018Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-06T15:55:11.018Z\",\"display_title\":\"10_CURRENT_HANDOFF_2026-09-06_RUNTIME_DESIGN\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1SLU50Xz-ujenM6hGHdweEhNIJTvAkNFhjzJuI66MDOU/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1-2XT7kaaOIIu8aqjcGFIPF_ktPF0N9vQ\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿EC8 AI Convergence — Current Handoff\\r\\nDate: 2026-09-06\\r\\nSession focus: post-architecture runtime design, authority separation, Principal Consultant/runtime auditions\\r\\nSeat: Coda — Strategic Advisor / Governance\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n1. CURRENT PROJECT STATE\\r\\nEC8 AI Convergence is post-methodology, post-architecture, pre-implementation. Don approved the short canon decision establishing the current implementation baseline. Kimi's K1–K9 semantic corrections were ultimately physically applied and independently verified in the corrected handoff package. Chiave Architecture v1.1 exists. The immediate project question is no longer methodology invention; it is concrete runtime/model/provider design, live Bedrock executability, and the delivery-chain authority model that will carry the accepted spec into implementation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPhase posture:\\r\\n- Phase 0 Foundation: generally startable.\\r\\n- Phase 1 Provider/Ledger layer: generally startable.\\r\\n- Phase 2 semantic pipeline: do not treat as fully unblocked until the final runtime/contract checks and remaining architecture/operations constraints are closed.\\r\\n- Phase 3 pilot: not yet.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2. CANON / SOURCE STATE\\r\\nCurrent implementation baseline established by Don:\\r\\n- corrected handoff-zip methodology copy S1, content/hash controlled\\r\\n- Chiave architecture source, now supplemented by EC8_Architecture_v1.1.md\\r\\n- prompts 01–09, content controlled; K7–K9 prompt revisions applied\\r\\n- Reconciliation v0.2 + corrigendum remains the controlling reconciliation record until source corrections replace the need for its temporary interpretations; reconciliation is not methodology or architecture canon\\r\\n- older methodology copy is SUPERSEDED FOR IMPLEMENTATION / PROVENANCE-ONLY\\r\\n- ruling collisions bind by ruling substance/content + source hash until numbering is corrected\\r\\n- OnDemand excluded from pilot\\r\\n- one scheduled MLB game = one slate; multi-game days contain independent slates\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVerified Kimi correction state:\\r\\n- K1 Stage 4 deterministic behavior correction applied\\r\\n- K2 L1/L2 classification semantics applied\\r\\n- K3 machine-checkable G2 threshold/freshness behavior applied\\r\\n- K4 IF-3 gap-request contract applied\\r\\n- K5 cumulative request lifecycle applied\\r\\n- K6 sufficiency-score definitions applied\\r\\n- K7 baseline-lines vs restricted market evidence prompt boundary applied\\r\\n- K8 normalization-tier threshold authority clarified\\r\\n- K9 changed prompts version-bumped\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n3. AUTHORITY / ORGANIZATIONAL TOPOLOGY\\r\\nIMPORTANT: Don identified a governance conflict in the earlier combined Kimi “Technical Stack Methodology / Design & Build” ownership. The methodology author should not be the sole authority selecting the concrete implementation/runtime design that executes that methodology.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent working topology — PROPOSED / PROVISIONAL until Don explicitly locks the new seat:\\r\\nDON — Final Authority / Stakeholder / Decision Owner\\r\\nExecutive Council:\\r\\n- Coda — Strategic Governance: governance, authority, reconciliation, canon\\r\\n- Kimi — Technical Stack Methodology: methodology, technical process, design logic/requirements; not sole concrete runtime selector under the proposed refinement\\r\\n- Chiave — Architecture: system architecture, contracts, durable boundaries\\r\\n- Talon — Operations Authority: routing, operational control, execution flow\\r\\nShared Enterprise Services:\\r\\n- Data / Intelligence\\r\\n- Luce — Verification / Ground Truth\\r\\n- QA / Validation — vacant\\r\\nDelivery / Build Chain:\\r\\n- Principal Consultant — approved seat; Specification + Translation\\r\\n- Independent Design & Build — PROVISIONAL NEW SEAT; exact runtime/provider/model selection, implementation design, detailed build choices, cost/value optimization, runtime assignments\\r\\n- Talon — operational routing / deployment coordination\\r\\n- Keel — Build · Deploy · Implementation/Integration Test · Evidence Return\\r\\n- Soldiers / Contract Workers — bounded tasks (Falcon, Pigeon, Magpie, Raven, etc.)\\r\\n- Luce — independent verification / ground-truth certification\\r\\nReturn path: Luce → Coda reconciliation → Don decision\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMODEL != SEAT. Current Grok 4.6 audition is evidence for the provisional Independent Design & Build function, not a seat identity lock.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n4. PRINCIPAL CONSULTANT STATUS\\r\\nPrincipal Consultant role is APPROVED. Runtime/model is NOT locked.\\r\\nPurpose: consume accepted methodology + architecture + prompts + governing records and produce a downstream-safe Implementation Spec + Translation Pack without redesigning methodology/architecture or making governance decisions.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent audition evidence:\\r\\n- Luna / GPT-5.6 Luna: ~3-cent observed pass; extremely fast; strongest routine/default economics; good consolidation/handoff compression; weaker on deep cross-contract seam discovery and some blocker calibration.\\r\\n- Kimi 2.7 Code/Thinking: deeper bounded review; improved blocker calibration/authority routing after pushback; good escalation candidate.\\r\\n- K3-256K high-thinking swarm: seven-lane major-lock/adversarial audit; completed analysis lanes but consumed the 5-hour Code quota in stress configuration. Smaller/lower-thinking swarm remains a production option to test.\\r\\n- Claude Fable 5.1: strong forensic defect discovery; ~4.86-dollar observed pass; premium-forensic economics.\\r\\n- ChatGPT Astra: current audition spend exceeded ~4.64 dollars before completion; premium-forensic class; final unique-value comparison pending.\\r\\n- ChatGPT Sol: current audition approximately ~0.47 dollars at checkpoint; candidate for the missing middle tier if it catches a meaningful share of Luna's missed seams. Final return pending.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPROPOSED Principal Consultant runtime ladder, not canon:\\r\\n1. Routine/default — Luna\\r\\n2. Deeper single-pass escalation — Sol or Kimi 2.7, based on final evidence\\r\\n3. Major-lock / disputed-package audit — ChatGPT or Kimi swarm\\r\\n4. Premium forensic exception — Astra / Fable only when marginal value justifies cost\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOperating principle: extract premium-review findings into reusable GCE defect classes/checklists so future default-seat passes become cheaper and more reliable.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n5. INDEPENDENT DESIGN & BUILD / RUNTIME DESIGN AUDITIONS\\r\\nThe next concrete problem is to populate the 53-call MLB pilot with actual models/providers/runtime IDs without allowing the methodology author to select the implementation unchallenged.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nA. Grok 4.6 runtime design\\r\\nDrive artifact: EC8_Runtime_Design_Grok_v1.0\\r\\nProfile V addendum: EC8_Runtime_Design_Grok_ProfileV_Addendum_2026-09-06\\r\\nBehavioral strength: strong live-environment curiosity; it attempted Nova rather than only reasoning from documentation. It distinguished VERIFIED/PROPOSED/UNKNOWN reasonably well and re-optimized when Don changed the objective from CHEAPEST to VALUE.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGrok Profile V — current value proposal:\\r\\n- Framing P01: Qwen3 32B\\r\\n- Analyst A Situational: Qwen3 235B\\r\\n- Analyst B Form: Qwen3 235B\\r\\n- Analyst C Structural: DeepSeek V3.2\\r\\n- Analyst D Market: Kimi K2.5\\r\\n- Analyst E Micro: GLM 5\\r\\n- L2-A/B/D: DeepSeek V3.2\\r\\n- L2-C/E: Qwen3 235B\\r\\n- L3 primary: Mistral Large 3\\r\\n- L3 fallback: Claude Haiku 4.5\\r\\n- Normalization P09: Qwen3 32B\\r\\n- L1: deterministic code\\r\\nEstimated under its assumptions: ~0.217 dollars Morning, ~0.217 Pre-Game, ~0.436 per 53-call slate, ~6.54 dollars per 15-slate day, ~196 dollars / 30-day full-cadence month.\\r\\nOpen Grok question: Qwen/DeepSeek concentration may create correlated-reasoning risk despite formal family compliance. Several printed IDs remain to be live-pinned.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nB. GLM 5.1 runtime design\\r\\nDrive artifact: EC8_Runtime_Design_GLM5.1_v1.0\\r\\nGLM independently converged near the same value band but with a different model philosophy.\\r\\nRecommended Profile B — Balanced:\\r\\n- Framing: Amazon Nova Lite\\r\\n- Analyst A Situational: DeepSeek V3.2\\r\\n- Analyst B Form: Mistral Large 3\\r\\n- Analyst C Structural: Llama 3.3 70B\\r\\n- Analyst D Market: MiniMax M2.5\\r\\n- Analyst E Micro: Amazon Nova Pro\\r\\n- L2: mix of Llama / DeepSeek / Nova\\r\\n- L3 primary: Claude 3 Haiku\\r\\n- Normalization: Amazon Nova Lite\\r\\nEstimated: ~0.397 dollars per 53-call slate, ~5.95 dollars per 15-slate day, ~178 dollars/month at full 15-slate/day cadence.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nImportant GLM defect already identified by Coda: the stated Profile B L3 fallback is Llama 3.3 70B while Llama is also used as Analyst C. That appears to violate the architecture requirement that L3/fallback remain outside the analyst pool. Treat Profile B as a candidate, not approved.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGLM currently went on a useful tangent after Don explicitly asked it to test Nova. ACTIVE / NOT YET INGESTED: receive its live Nova invocation result and any corrected runtime observations before final comparison.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n6. NOVA / BEDROCK STATUS\\r\\nDo not confuse DESIGN FIT with CURRENT EXECUTABILITY.\\r\\n- Don specifically wants Amazon Bedrock partly to access Amazon models; Nova remains strategically relevant.\\r\\n- Grok/Talon current-path evidence indicated Nova was not callable through the tested Mantle/current configuration. Grok actually attempted the call; this is valuable execution evidence.\\r\\n- That failure is NOT a governance decision permanently excluding Nova.\\r\\n- GLM Profile B independently recommends Nova heavily on design/value grounds and is now explicitly testing whether it can obtain a live Nova path.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRequired next truth state for Nova:\\r\\nVERIFIED if an exact model + endpoint/API path + region + auth mode + model/inference-profile ID succeeds.\\r\\nPROPOSED if design-fit is strong but no live invocation is proven.\\r\\nUNAVAILABLE ON CURRENT PATH if a specific path fails. Never promote that wording to permanent architectural exclusion without broader evidence/Don decision.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n7. RUNTIME DESIGN DECISION CRITERION\\r\\nDon corrected an earlier Coda prompt bias: do NOT optimize for cheapest model.\\r\\nControlling design objective for comparisons:\\r\\nMAXIMIZE EXPECTED QUALITY + RELIABILITY + METHODOLOGICAL FIDELITY + INDEPENDENCE + COST EFFICIENCY PER DOLLAR.\\r\\nCost is a first-class design variable, not the sole objective and not a hard cap.\\r\\nA more expensive model is justified when it materially buys down a named failure mode. A cheaper model is preferred only when it is materially equivalent for the assigned stage.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nInteresting current convergence:\\r\\n- Grok Profile V ~0.436/slate\\r\\n- GLM Profile B ~0.397/slate\\r\\nThe few cents difference is not a meaningful decision driver. The real decision is stage fit, cognitive diversity, reliability, live availability, structured-output support, and failure/fallback legality.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHigh-interest disagreements for the next comparison:\\r\\n- Framing/Normalization: Qwen vs Nova\\r\\n- Situational: Qwen vs DeepSeek\\r\\n- Form: Qwen vs Mistral Large 3\\r\\n- Structural: DeepSeek vs Llama\\r\\n- Market: Kimi K2.5 vs MiniMax M2.5\\r\\n- Micro: GLM 5 vs Nova Pro\\r\\n- L2 concentration/topology\\r\\n- L3: Mistral Large 3 vs Claude Haiku\\r\\n- exact fallback legality\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n8. DATA-ACQUISITION NOTE\\r\\nDon already developed per-sport data-fetch work with Kimi through the Edge Crew Quant process. Do NOT import that wholesale into AI Convergence yet. Treat it as evidence/reusable-infrastructure candidate only. Later perform a bounded comparison: reusable shared acquisition infrastructure vs quant-specific methodology. Edge Crew Quant != AI Convergence remains controlling.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n9. VISUAL ARCHITECTURE\\r\\nA pipeline diagram was created during the session and materially improved Don's comprehension. It represents:\\r\\nexternal data/scraping → acquisition/store → Prompt 01 framing → five isolated Prompts 02–06 first pass → gap router/evidence acquisition → same-session Prompts 02–06 re-analysis → L1 deterministic + Prompt 07 L2 + Prompt 08 L3 → Prompt 09 normalization → nine-section SAP/artifact store, with provider abstraction/Bedrock, ledger, secrets, checkpoint/resume, observability underneath.\\r\\nTreat the diagram as explanatory, not canonical. Future version should populate the winning exact model/runtime assignments and stage costs after Don selects a roster.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n10. IMMEDIATE NEXT SESSION — DO THIS FIRST\\r\\n1. Ground in this handoff plus:\\r\\n   - corrected K1–K9 handoff package\\r\\n   - EC8 Architecture v1.1\\r\\n   - Reconciliation v0.2 + corrigendum\\r\\n   - EC8_Runtime_Design_Grok_v1.0\\r\\n   - EC8_Runtime_Design_Grok_ProfileV_Addendum_2026-09-06\\r\\n   - EC8_Runtime_Design_GLM5.1_v1.0\\r\\n   - Principal Consultant onboarding record\\r\\n2. Receive GLM 5.1's live Nova test/tangent output. Do not assume result before reading it.\\r\\n3. Receive Sol and Astra Principal Consultant audition outputs if completed. Score unique findings vs Luna/Fable/K2.7, not raw prestige.\\r\\n4. Reconcile Grok Profile V vs GLM Profile B slot-by-slot under VALUE criterion.\\r\\n5. Separate design recommendation from live runtime verification. Flag exact model IDs/support as VERIFIED/PROPOSED/UNKNOWN.\\r\\n6. Correct any L3/fallback family violations before a runtime can be considered compliant.\\r\\n7. Do not pick a canonical runtime roster until Don sees the side-by-side comparison and live Nova/model-ID evidence.\\r\\n8. If organizational topology is to be locked, Don must explicitly approve the provisional Independent Design & Build seat and the methodology/design separation. Until then preserve both the old combined-Kimi record and the proposed refinement as controlled provenance/conflict.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n11. ACTIVE OPEN QUESTIONS\\r\\n- Can GLM actually invoke Nova, and through what exact path?\\r\\n- Does Sol fill the Principal Consultant gap between Luna and premium forensic models?\\r\\n- Does Grok's Qwen/DeepSeek concentration reduce useful cognitive diversity despite formal EX-2 compliance?\\r\\n- Does GLM's Nova/Llama/MiniMax model mix survive live catalog and invocation tests?\\r\\n- Which runtime slots show enough value gain to justify premium spend?\\r\\n- Does Don canonize the Independent Design & Build seat, and if so what is the final seat name/authority language?\\r\\n- Principal Consultant runtime remains unlocked.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n12. SOURCE DISCIPLINE / HARD RULES\\r\\nEdge Crew Quant != AI Convergence.\\r\\nNewer != canonical.\\r\\nDo not silently merge conflicts.\\r\\nHistorical records remain provenance.\\r\\nSupersessions are additive.\\r\\nMODEL != SEAT.\\r\\nContext breadth does not grant authority breadth.\\r\\nImplementation may not invent missing methodology/architecture/governance.\\r\\nLive execution evidence is stronger than unsupported catalog assumptions, but a failed path is not automatically a permanent system-level prohibition.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS: PROCEED / CHECKPOINT\\r\\nReason: methodology and architecture corrections are mature enough to evaluate concrete runtime designs. Runtime roster, Nova path, Principal Consultant runtime tiering, and the proposed Independent Design & Build seat are not yet canonical.\\r\\nNext gate: ingest GLM Nova tangent + outstanding auditions → Coda side-by-side runtime reconciliation → Don decision framing.\\r\\nDon input needed: not until the comparison is ready, except explicit seat-topology canonization if Don chooses to lock it sooner.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/10LK7qH8X5iCGdDD00Wb2LjNfpi0R5q8OmL-x0My4NEw/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"07_CURRENT_HANDOFF_2026-09-06\",\"id\":\"10LK7qH8X5iCGdDD00Wb2LjNfpi0R5q8OmL-x0My4NEw\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"3217\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T11:50:06.081Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T15:55:23.287Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-06T15:55:23.287Z\",\"display_title\":\"07_CURRENT_HANDOFF_2026-09-06\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/10LK7qH8X5iCGdDD00Wb2LjNfpi0R5q8OmL-x0My4NEw/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1-2XT7kaaOIIu8aqjcGFIPF_ktPF0N9vQ\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿Current Handoff — 2026-09-06\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPROJECT STATE\\r\\nEC⁸ AI Convergence is post-architecture-gate, pre-implementation. Accepted methodology and Chiave Architecture Specification v1.0 are broadly aligned. Phase 0/1 foundation work is generally startable; named Phase-2 semantic/interface surfaces remain subject to owner reconciliation before coding those surfaces.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT SEATS\\r\\nDon — Vision / Final Authority / interim human orchestrator\\r\\nCoda — Strategic Governance\\r\\nKimi — Technical Stack Methodology / Design & Build\\r\\nChiave — Architecture\\r\\nPrincipal Consultant — Technical Translation / Integration\\r\\nTalon — Operations\\r\\nLuce — Verification / Ground Truth\\r\\nData / Intelligence — shared service\\r\\nQA / Validation — approved vacant shared service\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCURRENT PROCESS\\r\\nDon intent → Coda governance framing → Kimi methodology → Chiave architecture when materially required → Kimi Design & Build → Principal Consultant translation/reconciliation checkpoint → Implementation → Talon operations → Luce verification → Coda reconciliation → Don decision.\\r\\nPrincipal Consultant is a translation checkpoint, not a new approval authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPRINCIPAL CONSULTANT STATUS\\r\\nRole approved; runtime/model NOT locked.\\r\\nAudition evidence from 2026-09-06:\\r\\n- Luna: fastest/cheapest observed, strong routine/default fit, some deeper-defect misses/false blockers.\\r\\n- Kimi 2.7 Code/Thinking: stronger blocker calibration and authority routing; improved after pushback; good deep-review candidate.\\r\\n- Claude Fable 5.1: deepest forensic defect discovery but very high cost/latency; forensic-only profile if used.\\r\\n- K3-256K high-thinking swarm: seven parallel lanes, excellent deep-audit intake/decomposition, but consumed 5-hour Code quota in stress test; treat as audit-mode evidence.\\r\\nWorking hypothesis only: cheap/fast routine translation first, deeper Kimi/swarmer escalation when contested or at major locks.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPRINCIPAL CONSULTANT ARTIFACTS\\r\\nFiled under GCE onboarding → 03_Model_Onboarding → Principal_Consultant:\\r\\n- PRINCIPAL_CONSULTANT_ONBOARDING_2026-09-06\\r\\n- EC8_Handoff_Package_v0.3.1_FIXED.zip\\r\\n- EC8_Methodology_Architecture_Reconciliation_v0.1.md\\r\\n- EC8_Methodology_Architecture_Reconciliation_v0.2.md\\r\\n- EC8_Architecture_Specification_v1.0_Chiave_source.md\\r\\n- K3_256K_SWARM_AUDITION_OUTPUT_2026-09-06.txt\\r\\n- audition screenshots / quota evidence\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKNOWN RECONCILIATION POSTURE\\r\\nBroad alignment is established. Reconciliation evidence surfaced record/version/ruling drift plus deeper contract seams concentrated in Phase 2. Canonical remediation belongs to Kimi/Chiave/Coda according to ownership; reconciliation reports themselves are evidence, not canon.\\r\\nPhase 0/1 may proceed on unambiguous contracts. Do not let Implementation invent missing methodology/architecture decisions.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHOME ROOT CLEANUP CHECKPOINT\\r\\nBatch 2A = CLOSED / VERIFIED PASS.\\r\\nDevPonds = CLOSED / VERIFIED DELETE.\\r\\ntests = CLOSED / RETAIN IN PLACE.\\r\\nspeech-profile = OPEN / QUARANTINE-SECURITY HANDLING REQUIRED.\\r\\nNext speech-profile sequence: Chiave security/quarantine envelope → Talon exact plan → Luce pre-verification → authorized execution → Luce post-verification → close disposition.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNEXT SESSION\\r\\n1. Review completed K3-256K swarm synthesis/output.\\r\\n2. Compare downstream handoff quality against Luna/K2.7/Fable and decide runtime strategy only if evidence is sufficient.\\r\\n3. Continue speech-profile from Chiave quarantine ruling.\\r\\n4. Return to AI Convergence contract reconciliation / build handoff.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSOURCE DISCIPLINE\\r\\nNewer != automatically canonical. Historical records remain provenance. Do not silently merge conflicting sources. MODEL != SEAT\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2026-09-06 SUPERSESSION NOTE\\r\\nThis handoff remains provenance for the earlier 2026-09-06 state. The current continuation handoff is now:\\r\\n10_CURRENT_HANDOFF_2026-09-06_RUNTIME_DESIGN\\r\\nDrive ID: 1SLU50Xz-ujenM6hGHdweEhNIJTvAkNFhjzJuI66MDOU\\r\\nUse the newer handoff for runtime-design, provisional Independent Design & Build, Nova/Bedrock, and Principal Consultant audition state. Do not delete this earlier handoff.\\r\\n.\"},{\"url\":\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Jw5bgB1vgh7dLxjkug4nNVpD-WLVgCAp/view?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"EC8_Methodology_Architecture_Reconciliation_v0.2.md\",\"id\":\"1Jw5bgB1vgh7dLxjkug4nNVpD-WLVgCAp\",\"mime_type\":\"text/markdown\",\"size\":\"47675\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T11:47:23.645Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T11:47:23.645Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":null,\"display_title\":\"EC8_Methodology_Architecture_Reconciliation_v0.2.md\",\"display_url\":\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Jw5bgB1vgh7dLxjkug4nNVpD-WLVgCAp/view?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1EXzOuIyaLkTFB0pL6g5xXTWddHcbjN3O\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"# EC⁸ AI Convergence — Methodology ↔ Architecture Implementation Reconciliation v0.2\\n\\n**Seat**: Principal Consultant — Technical Translation / Integration\\n**Date**: 2026-09-06\\n**Status**: Reconciliation of supplied package; not a methodology or architecture amendment\\n**Supersedes**: `EC8_Methodology_Architecture_Reconciliation_v0.1.md` (prior consultant pass, same seat title, unattributed)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Sources Reconciled\\n\\n| ID | Artifact | Role in this reconciliation |\\n|----|----------|------------------------------|\\n| **S1** | `EC8_AI_Convergence_v0.3.1.md` — **handoff-zip copy** (from `EC8_Handoff_Package_v0.3.1_FIXED.zip`) | Methodology, content leader |\\n| **S2** | `EC8_AI_Convergence_v0.3.1.md` — **methodology-zip copy** (from `EC8_AI_Convergence_v0.3.1_Package.zip`) | Methodology, stale divergent copy |\\n| **S3** | `EC8_AI_Convergence_v0.3.md` (+ diff v0.3 → v0.3.1) | Provenance only |\\n| **S4** | `EC8_Architecure_Brief.txt` = **Architecture Specification v1.0** (Chiave, \\\"Post-gate, pre-build\\\") | Architecture, canonical |\\n| **S5** | `HANDOFF_v0.3.1.md` | Kimi's handoff note |\\n| **S6** | `prompts/01–09 + README` — both zip copies (handoff copies verified newer: G4 classification blocks added, `acquired_in_run` fields, `conflict_penalty` rename, framing ingestion split) | Prompt package; handoff copy is current |\\n\\nClaim discipline: FACT / DERIVED / PROPOSED / UNKNOWN / CONFLICT / VERIFIED / OUTSIDE AUTHORITY, per §6 of the consultant charter. No execution evidence was supplied; nothing here is VERIFIED.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Executive Reconciliation\\n\\n**FACT — The accepted methodology (S1) and accepted architecture (S4) are substantively aligned on every major contract.** Isolation (I2/EX-1/EX-6), request-gated evidence delivery (CR-1/DA-4/IF-2), the evidence-package invariant, G4 determinism (14 tests, retry-once for Correctable only), forward-only validation (I3/VL-7), normalization blindness (NO-1), effective-N accounting, terminal SAP-PreGame, and the 53-call/slate cost baseline all trace cleanly in both directions.\\n\\n**Resolved since v0.1** (the prior reconciliation left these open; the newer S1 copy answers them):\\n\\n- **Overnight behavior (brief §8.1)** — RESOLVED. Overnight = **1 model call** (framing, Stage 0) + deterministic evidence acquisition (APIs, no models). No analysts. Data acquisition and model execution are separated in both documents. \\\"Data-only\\\" means \\\"no analysts,\\\" not \\\"no model.\\\"\\n- **Framing-call count (§8.2)** — RESOLVED in S1. Framing executes **once per run × 3 runs = 3 calls/slate**, stated explicitly (S1 §9.1 note: \\\"Morning and Pre-Game each require a fresh framing snapshot\\\"). A fresh framing snapshot **does** require a new model invocation; this is now stated, not assumed.\\n- **53-call decomposition (§8.2)** — RESOLVED in S1: 26/run = 1 framing + 25 pipeline (5 first-pass + 5 re-analysis + 5 L2 + 5 L3 + 5 normalization); 53/slate = 3 + 10×5; ~795/day = 45 + 750. Arithmetic is now internally consistent **in S1 only** (see DR-03).\\n\\n**Still live (details in §5):**\\n\\n1. **Ruling-ID drift (§8.3)** — Chiave's CR-2/CR-4 carry different rulings than methodology's CR-2/CR-4; the on-demand removal is CR-2 in S4 but a Don decision (not a CR) in S1. Traceability defect; record fix.\\n2. **Two divergent copies both labeled v0.3.1** (§8.4) — S2 is stale (internal header still says v0.3, retains `OnDemand` enum, framing row arithmetically inconsistent, no Don attribution). Canonical identity unconfirmed.\\n3. **Architecture's \\\"pending v0.3.2\\\" list is partially stale** — three of the six items it lists are already fixed in S1.\\n4. **G2 gate threshold has no value** — blocks only G2 assertion tests.\\n5. **Artifact schema version never assigned** — IF-4 requires independent versioning; no version exists.\\n6. **Handoff status contradiction narrowed but not closed** — S5 says \\\"Ready for Coder / Coder unblocked\\\"; S4 says \\\"Post-gate, pre-build.\\\" The gap is now known to be record-fix-sized, not design-sized (DR-01).\\n\\n**Verdict (§10): PARTIALLY BLOCKED** — narrower than v0.1. Foundation phases (0–1) are READY WITH NON-BLOCKING FIXES. Named surfaces are blocked; nothing in the blocked set is a methodology/architecture redesign question.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. System Intent Summary\\n\\nImplementation-neutral statement of what the system is (all FACT from S1/S4 unless labeled):\\n\\n- **System objective**: Produce an independent \\\"analytical landscape\\\" of N=5 differentiated AI analysts on one MLB game — selections, confidence tiers, divergence, uncertainty — as a terminal artifact for downstream EC⁸ consumption. Explicitly not recommendations, consensus, or blended picks.\\n- **Unit of analysis**: A **slate = one scheduled MLB game**. Multi-game days = independent slates, each with its own full pipeline run (S1 §2.1 Slate Definition).\\n- **Scheduled cadence**: Three runs per slate in the final 24h: Overnight (T-24h→T-12h), Morning (T-12h→T-4h), Pre-Game (T-90min, adjustable [T-120, T-30]). Scheduled only; on-demand removed from pilot (Don decision #18 / S4 CR-2, revival conditions preserved in S4 §12).\\n- **Framing**: A dedicated form-filler model populates a fixed, versioned, enumerated schema (0.3-MLB). Zero discretion, `null`+reason-code for unavailable fields, no prose. Fresh snapshot per run; prior snapshots retained as record, never delivered to analysts.\\n- **Analyst topology**: 5 personas (Situational, Form/Trajectory, Structural/Matchup, Market/Behavioral, Micro/Process), each a distinct epistemic lens, ≥3 model families, unique prompts and sampling parameters.\\n- **Analyst independence**: Separate execution contexts; no peer outputs/reasoning/gap requests; no N, no peer personas, no knowledge that divergence is measured; canary tokens + output fingerprinting per analyst per run; results in the artifact's integrity report.\\n- **Evidence acquisition**: Analysts emit information gaps (Stage 1); the system semantically deduplicates, acquires (APIs, scraping, feeds), tags provenance (timestamp, source, reliability tier, run type, expiration), and stores in a shared append-only evidence store.\\n- **Personalized evidence delivery**: Each analyst receives exactly: current pass's framing snapshot + its own requested evidence (cumulatively, across runs, via the request-gated path) + request_status map. Nothing else, ever. Delivery is request-gated even though the store is shared (CR-1/DA-4).\\n- **Market-data isolation**: Market-class evidence deliverable to Persona D only, enforced role-keyed at the gap-request boundary. Baseline line fields in the framing snapshot ride the shared baseline to all analysts (S4 IF-2 explicit; see DR-18).\\n- **Validation stack**: L1 deterministic code (no model call); L2 different-architecture validator per pair (never sees raw confidence); L3 outside-the-pool red-team with pre-approved fallback provider. Forward-only: validation outputs never return to analyst context. No layer skippable; execution failure blocks.\\n- **G4 deterministic classification**: Every FAIL classified by observable tests into Critical Hallucination (CH-1..5) / Uncorrectable (UC-1..4) / Correctable (CO-1..5). CH/UC → immediate exclusion, no retry. CO → retry Stage 3 once in the same session with corrections as replacement evidence items; second FAIL (any class) → exclusion. L1 FAILs route to the same classification via an L1→L2 semantic router (S4 VL-2, flagged spec completion).\\n- **Retry/exclusion behavior**: Retries increment the cost ledger, not `ran_n` (S4 VL-8). Exclusions recorded with `{analyst, layer, class, test_id, detail, retry_number, action}` in effective-N.\\n- **Normalization**: Neutral model, four inputs exactly (self-assessment, evidence sufficiency score [deterministic code], validation state, validation flags), blind to reasoning/selection/peers. Five tiers: Conviction, Lean, Tentative, Pass, Contradicted. Pass is sacred; Contradicted is system-assignable.\\n- **Artifact creation**: Nine-section SAP per run. SAP-Morning retained for trajectory (non-terminal); **SAP-PreGame is the terminal artifact**. Artifacts immutable after G6.\\n- **Provenance**: Model/prompt/parameter versions captured from execution metadata, never configuration intent (I9). Full chain: analyst → claim → evidence ID → source → acquisition timestamp.\\n- **Cost measurement**: Unit = provider-billable request + token counts. Budget baseline 53/slate (reference only); the ledger is the only cost truth (I10/OB-3/OB-4). No cost ceiling (Don #8; measured, not capped).\\n- **Failure handling**: Blocks, never bypasses (I5). Partial-data mode for source outages; checkpoint/resume at gates (S4 completion); whole-store failure → abort and restore from backup, \\\"no artifact is ever preferable to a wrong artifact.\\\"\\n- **Replay**: Replay-as-record (I4) — stored artifact is canonical; re-execution verifies process, not results.\\n- **Pilot scope**: One MLB slate per run-day topology; scheduled cadence only; N=5; full validation; four seeded failure tests mandatory (S4 §11); acceptance is architectural (gates fired, isolation verified, ledger reconciles against provider invoices), not signal quality.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Methodology → Architecture Traceability Matrix\\n\\nStatus: **Exact** = architecture enforces the requirement as stated; **Partial** = enforced with a gap or an architecture completion filling it; **Missing** = no architectural enforcement found; **Conflict** = incompatible requirements.\\n\\n| Methodology Requirement | Source | Architecture Contract | Status | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Analyst isolation (P1, §5.2, §5.3) | S1 §1.4, §5 | I2, EX-1 (separate contexts, no shared memory/fs/netns/env), EX-6 (canaries, fingerprinting) | **Exact** | |\\n| Information self-determination (P2) | S1 §1.4, Stage 2 | IF-3 (gap-request interface), Stage 2 equivalents in S4 §2 | **Exact** | structured form is an architecture completion (DR-07) |\\n| Framing schema, enumerated, versioned (P6, §3.1, M1/M2) | S1 §3.1 | IF-1, CR-5 | **Exact** | S4's \\\"normative text @ v0.3.2\\\" pointer is stale (DR-04); schema content is identical |\\n| Evidence-package invariant | S1 §2.5 (two formulations) | I1 + IF-2 (incl. cumulative re-delivery clause) | **Exact via IF-2** | I1's \\\"requested evidence\\\" vs S1's \\\"all evidence ever acquired\\\" wording drift reconciled by IF-2; record fix DR-12 |\\n| Store vs. delivery separation | S1 §2.2/§2.5 (CR-1) | DA-4, I1, IF-2 choke point | **Exact** | |\\n| Gap-request lifecycle (filled/unfilled+reason/pending) | S1 Stage 2d, M23 | IF-2 request_status enum + IF-3 lifecycle `requested → filled \\\\| unfilled(reason) \\\\| pending` | **Exact** | IF-3 adds `malformed_request`/`access_denied` — completion |\\n| Market-persona exclusivity (§4.3, M20) | S1 §4.3 | IF-2 market policy, IF-3 access policy (role-keyed), SE-4 | **Exact** | baseline-lines exception explicit in IF-2; prompt wording tension DR-18 |\\n| Analyst session continuity (M19, C7, §2.6) | S1 §2.6, Stage 3 | EX-3 (\\\"Stage 1→3, two provider requests, one session\\\"), inter-run fresh context | **Exact** | prompts don't state session continuity explicitly; EX-3 governs |\\n| Model-family heterogeneity (M4) | S1 Stage 1 | EX-2 (≥3 families; L2 pairwise ≠; L3 outside pool; fallback pre-approved + exercised) | **Exact** | vendor registry/assignment algorithm absent — implementation detail under EX-2 (DR-14) |\\n| Validation layers mandatory (P4, M21) | S1 Stage 4 | VL-1..8, I5 | **Exact** | VL-2 L1→L2 router is a flagged completion under CR-4 |\\n| G4 classification (§7.1, M30) | S1 §7.1 (14 tests, 3 classes) | VL-5 (deterministic action table; classification reliability measured) | **Exact** | ruling **IDs** conflict (DR-02), content does not |\\n| Retry semantics (§7.1 retry protocol) | S1 §7.1 | VL-6 (sealed report, replacement evidence items, same-session Stage 3 re-run, second FAIL → exclusion), VL-8 | **Exact** | handoff-copy prompts 07/08 implement `failure_class`/`test_id`; methodology-zip prompts lack them (DR-03/DR-09) |\\n| Forward-only validation | S1 Stage 4 | I3, VL-7 (topology constraint) | **Exact** | |\\n| Normalization inputs & blindness (Stage 5, M8) | S1 Stage 5 | NO-1..6 (4 inputs exactly; stateless; non-collapsing; sufficiency score deterministic) | **Exact** | `conflict_penalty` name consistent in S1 + handoff prompts |\\n| Confidence tiers | S1 Stage 5 | NO-6 (enum versioned independently; Contradicted system-assignable) | **Exact** | numeric thresholds live in prompt 09 only — DR-17 |\\n| Effective-N (M24, §7.1) | S1 §7.1, Stage 6 §3 | IF-4 fields (`configured_n/ran_n/included_n/excluded_n/exclusions[]`), VL-8, I7 | **Exact** | |\\n| Integrity report (M25) | S1 Stage 6 §9 | IF-4 §9 (contamination, gate outcomes, anomalies, session-continuity verification) | **Exact** | |\\n| Terminal SAP (Stage 6, C8) | S1 Stage 6 | IF-4 (SAP-PreGame canonical terminal; immutability at store level) | **Exact** | artifact schema **version number** missing (DR-08) |\\n| Morning vs. Pre-Game artifacts | S1 §2.3/§2.4 | IF-4 (SAP-Morning retained, non-terminal) | **Exact** | |\\n| Cost ledger (§9.1, CR-3) | S1 §9.1 | OB-1..4 (unit, granularity, execution-point metering, 53/slate budget reference), I10 | **Exact** | \\\"645-vs-795\\\" cited as the failure mode OB-3 prevents |\\n| Failure handling (gate table §7) | S1 §7 gates G0–G6 | S4 §7 failure domains (superset; adds checkpoint/resume, L3 fallback, store-restore) | **Exact + completions** | checkpoint/resume flagged, not ruled silently |\\n| Replay/provenance (Stage 6 §8) | S1 Stage 6 | I4, I9, DA-1..3, EX-5 | **Exact** | hashing/append-only is architecture completion of methodology's immutability intent |\\n\\n**Net: zero Missing, zero substantive Conflicts in content.** All conflicts are in *records* (IDs, versions, status claims), not in requirements.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Architecture → Methodology Back-Trace\\n\\nFor each major S4 contract, the authorizing methodology/governance requirement:\\n\\n| Architecture Contract | Authorization | Classification |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| I1–I10 invariants | Directly required by P1–P7, M18–M30, Don guardrails | **Directly required** |\\n| IF-1 framing schema interface | P6, §3.1, M1/M2, CR-5 | **Directly required** |\\n| IF-2 evidence package | §2.5 invariant, M18/M23/M28/M29/M30, CR-1 | **Directly required** |\\n| IF-3 gap request (structured form, access policy, malformed/access_denied) | §4.3 policy, Stage 2; structure/access machine-checkability from G4 determinism (CR-2/S4) | **Reasonably derived + completion** (free-text→structured mapping contract still needed: DR-07) |\\n| IF-4 terminal artifact | Stage 6, M10/M24/M25, C8 | **Directly required** (versioning regime stated, version number never assigned: DR-08) |\\n| EX-1 isolation mechanics | §5.2 | **Directly required** |\\n| EX-2 heterogeneity + L3 fallback | M4, Stage 1/4 (fallback = Talon coordination in S1) | **Directly required** |\\n| EX-3 continuity (\\\"two provider requests, one session\\\") | M19, C7, §2.6 | **Directly required** |\\n| EX-4 concurrency, EX-5 version pinning, EX-6 contamination | Stage 1 controls, §5.4, I9 | **Directly required** |\\n| DA-1 SHA-256 append-only store | \\\"Shared EC⁸ data layer,\\\" provenance tags, evidence-never-mutates identity rule | **Reasonably derived** (hashing is the enforcement mechanism) |\\n| DA-2 evidence identity (entity, attribute, snapshot-time) | S1 §2.6 evidence accumulation + immutability | **Directly required** (S1 states \\\"never mutates a record; creates a new one\\\" via S4) |\\n| DA-3 provenance tags | S1 §2.2/§2.6 (timestamp, source, reliability tier, run type, expiration) | **Directly required** |\\n| DA-4 store-vs-delivery | CR-1, §2.5 | **Directly required** |\\n| DA-5 backup set | Not in methodology | **Architecture-owned completion** (governance value; consistent with I4) |\\n| VL-1 L1 deterministic | Stage 4 (\\\"Automated — No Model Call\\\") | **Directly required** |\\n| VL-2 L1 semantic router | S1 §7.1: \\\"L1 FAILs are routed through the same classification\\\"; G4 determinism | **Flagged spec completion** (authorized by standing ruling; S4 declares it) |\\n| VL-3/VL-4 L2/L3 | Stage 4 | **Directly required** |\\n| VL-5 G4 action table | S1 §7.1, M30 | **Directly required** |\\n| VL-6 retry protocol | S1 §7.1 Retry Protocol | **Directly required** |\\n| VL-7 forward-only | Stage 4 | **Directly required** |\\n| VL-8 retry ledger accounting (not ran_n) | S1 §9.1 (token truthfulness), M24 semantics | **Reasonably derived** |\\n| NO-1..6 normalization | Stage 5, M8 | **Directly required** |\\n| §7 failure domains | S1 §7 gate actions; S1 §8 (L3 fallback) | **Directly required + completions** (checkpoint/resume flagged) |\\n| SE-1..7 security boundaries | S1 §8 boundary crossing (Chiave owns security) | **Architecture-owned domain** (seat-authorized) |\\n| OB-1..5 observability | S1 §9.1, §4.3 measurement, M14 | **Directly required + completion** (emit-points) |\\n| §10 build plan, §11 pilot + seeded failures | Not in methodology — pilot design is architecture's | **Architecture-owned completion** (consistent with S1 §9 measurement intent) |\\n| §12 gate register (CR-1..5) | v0.3.1 gate rulings | **Directly required — but IDs drifted from S1's register (DR-02)** |\\n| §13 ownership map, §14 traceability | Governance | **Architecture-owned completion** |\\n\\n**Nothing in S4 is unsupported by supplied methodology/governance, and nothing conflicts with methodology in substance.** Two completions (VL-2 router, checkpoint/resume) are properly flagged as such in S4 — this is the correct pattern.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Discrepancy Register\\n\\nGate classes: **NBRF** = NON-BLOCKING RECORD FIX · **ICR** = IMPLEMENTATION CLARIFICATION REQUIRED · **AG** = ARCHITECTURE GATE · **MG** = METHODOLOGY GATE · **GDD** = GOVERNANCE / DON DECISION.\\n\\n| ID | Classification | Source A | Source B | Conflict | Implementation Impact | Owner | Gate |\\n|----|---------------|----------|----------|----------|----------------------|-------|------|\\n| **DR-01** (was D-01, narrowed) | authority ambiguity | S5: \\\"Methodology Complete, Architecture Approved, Ready for Coder / Coder UNBLOCKED\\\" | S4: \\\"Status: Post-gate, pre-build\\\", companion \\\"methodology v0.3.1 pending v0.3.2 record fixes\\\" | Same project, two readiness states | Coder could start full build against records another authority calls pre-final | Coda (with Don confirming intent) | **GDD** — but record-fix-sized, not design-sized |\\n| **DR-02** (D-03) | ruling-ID drift | S4 §12: CR-2 = on-demand removal; CR-3 = cost; CR-4 = G4; CR-5 = framing | S1 §10.2: CR-2 = G4; CR-3 = cost; CR-4 = framing; on-demand = Don decision #18 (no CR) | Identical IDs, different rulings; identical ruling (on-demand), different IDs | Tests/docs keying on bare \\\"CR-2/CR-4\\\" bind to the wrong ruling depending on source | Coda (crosswalk); Kimi+Chiave (source corrections) | **NBRF** — bind traceability to ruling *content*, not ID, until fixed |\\n| **DR-03** | version drift | S2 (labeled v0.3.1; internal header \\\"v0.3\\\"; `OnDemand` enum present; framing row = 2/slate making totals 52≠53, 780≠795; rulings labeled \\\"Ruling 1–5\\\" without Don attribution; §2.5 delta-style older text) | S1 (same version label; enum fixed; framing 3/slate consistent; Don attribution present; cumulative delivery rule) | Two artifacts, one version label, different content | Implementation cannot know which v0.3.1 is canonical; binding to S2 breaks the OnDemand enum and 53-math | Kimi (stamp v0.3.2 or declare S1 canonical; retire S2 to provenance) + Coda (canon confirm) | **NBRF for code** (bind to S1 content by hash) · **MG/record** for the stamp |\\n| **DR-04** (D-05/D-12, narrowed) | stale reference | S4 §0/§14: six fixes \\\"pending on methodology v0.3.2\\\" (enum removal, Stage 6 terminal line, on-demand attribution among them) | S1: those three fixes already landed | Architecture's pending list is partially stale | None for code; record confusion about what v0.3.2 still owes | Chiave (refresh §14 after Kimi's stamp) | **NBRF** |\\n| **DR-05** (D-06/D-07) — **RESOLVED** | — | S1 §9.1 note | S1 §2 cadence table | Framing = 3/slate explicitly; 26 = 1+25; 53 = 3+50 | None. Budget assertions become testable | — | Closed |\\n| **DR-06** (D-08) | missing contract | S1 Stage 2 Gate 2: \\\">threshold% of requested gaps\\\" | S4: I6 (machine-checkable gates) — no threshold value anywhere | G2 criteria not machine-checkable | G2 assertion tests cannot be written; gate must either be parameterized or pinned | Kimi (pin value, denominator, unmet action; Don if business-threshold) | **MG** — blocks G2 tests only |\\n| **DR-07** (D-09, narrowed) | implementation ambiguity | Prompts: gap requests are free-text `requested` strings in `information_gaps[]` | S4 IF-3: structured form (entity, attribute, timeframe, granularity, data class) + `malformed_request`/`access_denied` | No stated mapping from free-text output to structured request; semantic dedup semantics (S1 Stage 2a) unspecified | Gap-request router coder must invent the parser/dedup contract | Kimi + Chiave jointly | **ICR** — blocks gap-router semantics |\\n| **DR-08** (D-11) | missing contract | S4 IF-4: \\\"artifact schema versioned independently; downstream binds to artifact schema version\\\" | No artifact schema version number exists in any artifact | Versioning regime declared, version absent | Artifact validation and downstream binding have no pin | Chiave | **AG** — blocks artifact-schema binding |\\n| **DR-09** | version drift | Prompt headers: all \\\"System Prompt v0.3\\\" (01: \\\"v0.3-MLB\\\") | Handoff-copy prompt content changed (G4 blocks in 07/08, `acquired_in_run` in 02–06, `conflict_penalty` in 09, framing ingestion split in 01) | Content changed under unchanged version labels | Pinning by version string binds stale content | Kimi (re-version prompts, e.g. v0.3.1) | **NBRF** — pin by content hash meanwhile |\\n| **DR-10** (D-02) | stale handoff | S5 §9: \\\"Chiave_Architecture_Brief_v0.3.1.md is not yet produced… do not create it independently\\\" | S4 exists (Architecture Specification v1.0, supplied as EC8_Architecure_Brief.txt) | Handoff predates the architecture doc | Coder following S5 §9 would think no architecture exists | Kimi (correct S5 §9 at next touch) | **NBRF** |\\n| **DR-11** | textual drift | S5 §2 council table: architecture seat named \\\"GLM\\\" (\\\"APPROVED — Phase 0 design begins\\\") | S5 §4 and all other artifacts: seat = Chiave | Same seat, two names in one document | Identity confusion in routing | Kimi (record fix in S5) | **NBRF** |\\n| **DR-12** | textual drift | S4 I1: package = \\\"requested evidence\\\" | S1 §2.5: \\\"all evidence ever acquired for this analyst across all runs\\\" | Wording implies delta vs. cumulative | IF-2's cumulative clause resolves it; I1 wording should align to prevent coder misreading | Chiave (wording fix at next revision) | **NBRF** — contract follows IF-2 |\\n| **DR-13** (D-13) — **RESOLVED** | — | S1 §2.1 Slate Definition | S5 pilot scope | Slate = one scheduled MLB game; multi-game days = independent slates | None | — | Closed |\\n| **DR-14** (D-10, downgraded) | implementation ambiguity | \\\"Different architecture family\\\" (S1) / provider registry check (S4 EX-2) | No vendor registry or assignment algorithm supplied | Who fills which slot is unspecified | None — this is an ordinary implementation choice *constrained* by EX-2 (≥3 families, pairwise L2, L3 outside pool) | Implementation + Talon within EX-2; Luce verifies | **Not a gate** |\\n| **DR-15** (D-14, downgraded) | implementation ambiguity | S4 §7: checkpoint/resume at gates; L3 fallback coordination | S1 §8: Talon owns scheduling/fallback coordination | Operational contract not yet written | Blocks Phase 2/3 ops readiness, not code | Talon + Chiave | **ICR** — schedule before Phase 2 |\\n| **DR-16** | textual drift | README version line: \\\"effective-N accounting\\\" | No prompt body defines effective-N (it is system-side artifact accounting) | Dangling version claim | None; prompts don't need it | Kimi (README wording) | **NBRF** |\\n| **DR-17** | implementation ambiguity | S1 Stage 5 tier conditions marked \\\"Typical\\\" | Prompt 09 encodes numeric thresholds (composite >0.75 etc.) | Which is normative? | Normalizer coder must know whether prompt numbers are the contract | Kimi | **ICR** — small; likely \\\"prompt is normative\\\" |\\n| **DR-18** | semantic conflict (mild) | Prompts 02/03/04/06: \\\"The system will not deliver lines… to you\\\" | Framing schema `lines` block (spread/total/moneyline) rides the shared baseline to ALL analysts (S1 §2.3; S4 IF-2 explicit) | Literal prompt wording contradicts baseline delivery | Package assembler must not strip baseline lines for non-D personas; prompts must be read as scoped to market-class *evidence* | Kimi (confirm intended scope; adjust prompt sentence if needed) | **ICR** — blocks package-assembler market-filter semantics only |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Version / Ruling Crosswalk\\n\\n### 6.1 Ruling crosswalk (bind to content, not ID, until DR-02 is fixed)\\n\\n| Ruling content | S4 §12 (Chiave) | S1 §10.2 (methodology) | S5 §4 (handoff) |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Evidence delivery request-gated | CR-1 | CR-1 | CR-1 |\\n| On-demand removed from pilot (Don scope ruling) | **CR-2** | Don decision #18 (not a CR) | Don guardrail (listed) |\\n| Cost ledger unit + figures (26/53/~795) | CR-3 | CR-3 | CR-3 |\\n| G4 deterministic | CR-4 | **CR-2** | **CR-2** |\\n| Framing schema approved | CR-5 | CR-4 | CR-4 |\\n\\n**Collision set: CR-2 and CR-4.** Identical IDs, different rulings across registers. Identical ruling (on-demand) attached to an ID in S4 and to no ID in S1. Traceability defect per brief §8.3 — record it; do not rewrite history.\\n\\n### 6.2 Safe bindings for implementation (PROPOSED — consultant recommendation, authoritative only once owners confirm)\\n\\n| Surface | Safe bind now | Do NOT bind to |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Methodology content | S1 (handoff-zip v0.3.1), identified by SHA-256 | S2; any \\\"v0.3.2\\\" until it exists |\\n| Framing schema | `0.3-MLB` exactly as printed in S1 §3.1; `run_context ∈ {Overnight, Morning, PreGame}` | the `OnDemand` enum (S2/S3 provenance only) |\\n| Prompts | handoff-zip copies 01–09, pinned by content hash (headers still say v0.3 — DR-09) | methodology-zip prompt copies |\\n| G4 protocol | S1 §7.1 table (14 tests; retry once, Correctable only) | the old \\\"isolated and correctable\\\" runtime-judgment language (dead) |\\n| Cost baseline | 53/slate budget reference; ledger = truth (S4 OB-4) | any cost cap (none exists) |\\n| Artifact schema | nine sections per S1 Stage 6 + IF-4 fields | a version number (none exists — DR-08) |\\n| Cadence | Overnight(1 call)/Morning(26)/PreGame(26); framing ×3 | S2's framing-2 row (arithmetically inconsistent) |\\n| Ruling references | ruling **content** strings | bare CR numbers (DR-02) |\\n\\n### 6.3 \\\"Build-ready\\\" translation (brief §8.5)\\n\\n| Phrase | Where | Precise gate state |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| \\\"Methodology Complete / Ready for Coder / Coder UNBLOCKED\\\" | S5 header, §2 | Overclaim relative to S4 (DR-01) |\\n| \\\"Post-gate, pre-build\\\" | S4 header | Accurate for the full build; gate = architecture gate passed, build phases 0–3 not started |\\n| \\\"All contracts pinned. No deferred blockers for pilot design.\\\" | S1 §Exec 10 | Mostly true; G2 threshold and artifact schema version are unpinned (DR-06/DR-08) |\\n| Phase 0 design | S5 §2 (GLM/Chiave), S4 §10 | Design-owned by Chiave; build-owned by Implementation |\\n\\n**Translation (DERIVED):** the system is *post-architecture-gate, pre-implementation*, with Phase 0–1 unblocked, and a short list of record fixes that must land before the coder handoff is re-issued as \\\"unblocked\\\" for semantic surfaces.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Implementation Contract by Pipeline Stage\\n\\nDerived from S1 + S4 + handoff-copy prompts. \\\"Gate\\\" = machine-checkable condition to progress. Claims are FACT where both S1/S4 agree, DERIVED where assembled.\\n\\n### 7.1 Acquisition (overnight pre-fetch + Stage 2c)\\n- **Inputs**: slate schedule; gap requests (Stage 2c); proactive list (pitcher profiles, batter splits, form, weather, injuries, market lines — S1 §2.2).\\n- **Outputs**: evidence items in the shared store, tagged (timestamp, source, reliability tier, run type, expiration).\\n- **Must never receive**: analyst outputs; anything destined for a specific analyst's package (acquisition is analyst-blind; delivery is a separate contract).\\n- **State**: persistent, append-only, SHA-256 content-addressed (DA-1). Identity = (entity, attribute, snapshot-time); time-variant data creates new items, never mutates (DA-2).\\n- **Session**: none (no model).\\n- **Access**: acquisition engine = trust boundary (SE-1); untrusted text marked/sanitized (SE-3); market-class items tagged `market` (IF-3).\\n- **Failure**: source outage → partial-data mode; requesting analysts get `unfilled(reason)`; severe gaps flagged (S4 §7). No analyst impact beyond unfilled statuses.\\n- **Provenance**: DA-3 tags mandatory per item.\\n- **Metering**: every acquisition logged (count + source); not provider-billable (OB-2 granularity by source).\\n- **Gate**: item passes schema + provenance completeness before store commit.\\n\\n### 7.2 Framing\\n- **Inputs**: pre-fetched raw slate data from the ingestion layer (prompt 01-B: \\\"You do NOT fetch data, verify sources, query APIs, or make external calls\\\").\\n- **Outputs**: populated Framing Schema `0.3-MLB` instance; `null`+reason-code for unavailable fields (enum: `not_yet_released|source_unreliable|not_applicable|timeout|error`).\\n- **Must never receive**: analyst outputs; evidence items; prior run's framing snapshot.\\n- **State**: ephemeral per invocation; snapshot persisted as record; **prior snapshots never delivered to analysts** (M28).\\n- **Session**: stateless; one invocation per run (3/slate).\\n- **Access**: architecturally isolated from analysts (S1 Stage 0 controls).\\n- **Failure**: malformed output → anomaly-tracked re-run (S1 §9.1 note); structural errors → G0 reject slate.\\n- **Provenance**: `schema_version`, `generated_at`, per-field sources; run captured in execution metadata (I9).\\n- **Metering**: 1 provider-billable request per run; tokens counted (OB-1).\\n- **Gate (G0)**: matchups resolvable; temporal window valid; schema validates structurally.\\n\\n### 7.3 Analyst first pass (Stage 1)\\n- **Inputs**: current pass's framing snapshot only (+ training knowledge). No evidence yet; Stage 1 gap statuses are `null` (prompts 02–06-B).\\n- **Outputs**: preliminary conviction per matchup; `information_gaps[]` (free-text `requested` today — DR-07); meta-cognitive calibration; self-critique; first-pass selection/confidence.\\n- **Must never receive**: peer outputs/reasoning/gap requests; evidence; N; peer personas; divergence knowledge; market-class evidence (non-D; D has exclusive market access).\\n- **State**: none persistent from the analyst's side; canary token injected per analyst per run (EX-6).\\n- **Session**: opens the run's single analyst session (EX-3: two provider requests, one session).\\n- **Access**: separate execution context per analyst; unique prompt + sampling parameters (EX-1).\\n- **Failure**: execution error → re-run or exclude; contamination indicator → G1 investigation (never proceed silently).\\n- **Provenance**: model version, prompt hash, parameters captured from execution metadata (I9/EX-5).\\n- **Metering**: 5 requests/run; tokens per analyst (OB-2).\\n- **Gate (G1)**: all 5 complete; coherent gap requests; canary/fingerprint clean.\\n\\n### 7.4 Gap-request router (Stage 2a/2b + IF-3)\\n- **Inputs**: 5 analysts' `information_gaps[]`.\\n- **Outputs**: structured requests {entity, attribute, timeframe, granularity, data class}; semantic dedup; feasibility flags (`unacquirable|too_expensive`).\\n- **Must never receive**: analyst reasoning/selections (gap items only — otherwise bias channel).\\n- **State**: persistent request log per analyst per slate (feeds cumulative request_status map).\\n- **Session**: n/a (deterministic code + parsing; DR-07 mapping contract required before coding semantics).\\n- **Access**: market-class request from non-D persona → `access_denied` + `market_data_request_rate` event (expected 0% non-D) (IF-3).\\n- **Failure**: malformed → `unfilled(malformed_request)`; no blocking.\\n- **Provenance**: requester → request → outcome mapping retained for status replay.\\n- **Metering**: router is code, not model (DERIVED from L1-analogous determinism; confirm with Chiave — no model call is budgeted for it in the 53).\\n- **Gate**: every gap item classified (structured class or malformed) before acquisition dispatch.\\n\\n### 7.5 Evidence acquisition (Stage 2c)\\nSame contract as 7.1, scoped to requested items; additionally:\\n- **Gate (G2 — DR-06)**: threshold % filled — **value UNKNOWN; gate cannot be made machine-checkable until Kimi pins it**. Interim behavior per S1: proceed with partial data, flag severe gaps.\\n\\n### 7.6 Package assembler (IF-2 choke point — the single most security-sensitive component)\\n- **Inputs**: current framing snapshot; store items matching the analyst's request history; request_status map (cumulative, with `acquired_in_run`).\\n- **Outputs**: per-analyst package = framing snapshot + own requested evidence (cumulative) + request_status map. **Nothing else, ever (I1).**\\n- **Must never receive into a package**: peer-requested evidence; market-class evidence for non-D personas (except framing-schema baseline lines — DR-18); prior framing snapshots; validation outputs; system commentary about the analyst.\\n- **State**: ephemeral assembly; every assembly logged and reconstructable post-hoc (IF-2).\\n- **Session**: n/a.\\n- **Access**: single choke-point function; role-keyed market filter enforced here AND at IF-3 (defense in depth).\\n- **Failure**: any package item not reconstructable as {schema field | fulfilled request | status entry} = G6 failure (IF-2 Verify).\\n- **Provenance**: disclosure line included (M29); assembly logged.\\n- **Metering**: n/a (code).\\n- **Gate**: package audit passes before delivery.\\n\\n### 7.7 Analyst re-analysis (Stage 3)\\n- **Inputs**: same session continues; package from 7.6; replacement evidence items only if G4 retry (VL-6 — corrections arrive as evidence, never as commentary).\\n- **Outputs**: final selection (or Pass), raw confidence, reasoning with citations, key evidence, residual uncertainty, self-critique; gap items with system-populated `status/reason_if_unfilled/acquired_in_run`.\\n- **Must never receive**: everything in 7.3's forbidden list, plus validation reports (sealed).\\n- **State**: session transcript sealed into provenance at run end (EX-3).\\n- **Session**: **same session as Stage 1** — continuation, not fresh context (M19/EX-3).\\n- **Access**: same as 7.3.\\n- **Failure**: incomplete → G3 re-run.\\n- **Provenance**: as 7.3.\\n- **Metering**: 5 requests/run (full first-pass context carried — token-heavy; OB-1).\\n- **Gate (G3)**: structured outputs; reasoning traceable to evidence; residual uncertainties flagged.\\n\\n### 7.8 Validation L1\\n- **Inputs**: analyst final outputs; evidence package; framing schema.\\n- **Outputs**: PASS|FLAG|FAIL + mechanical findings; FAILs needing semantic classification (CO-3/5, UC-1..4) routed to L2 (VL-2); mechanical classes (CH-1/2/4/5, CO-1/2/4) decided here (VL-1).\\n- **Must never receive**: nothing forbidden — L1 sees what the analyst saw.\\n- **State**: deterministic code; replay-consistent.\\n- **Session**: n/a. **No model call** (S1 Stage 4; DERIVED that no ledger entry accrues).\\n- **Access**: read-only.\\n- **Failure**: L1 execution failure blocks the entry; never skipped (I5).\\n- **Provenance**: findings + routed classifications logged per analysis (VL-2).\\n- **Metering**: none (code).\\n- **Gate**: every FAIL carries a class or a routed classification before G4.\\n\\n### 7.9 Validation L2\\n- **Inputs**: analyst output (minus raw confidence), evidence package, framing schema; L1-routed semantic FAILs.\\n- **Outputs**: PASS|FLAG|FAIL + `failure_class` (`critical_hallucination|uncorrectable|correctable|null`), `test_id` (CH/UC/CO-n), `classification_reason` (prompts 07/08-B).\\n- **Must never receive**: analyst raw confidence; peer outputs; normalized tier.\\n- **State**: report sealed on FAIL (VL-6).\\n- **Session**: one invocation per analyst per layer.\\n- **Access**: model family ≠ analyst family, per pair (EX-2/VL-3).\\n- **Failure**: execution failure blocks that entry; retry; never skipped.\\n- **Provenance**: validator model/version captured.\\n- **Metering**: 5/run baseline + retries in ledger.\\n- **Gate**: every FAIL classified (no runtime judgment — CR-2).\\n\\n### 7.10 Validation L3\\n- **Inputs**: analyst output + L1 + L2 reports; framing schema.\\n- **Outputs**: as L2 + red-team opinion (quality score, calibration, missed evidence, alternatives).\\n- **Must never receive**: peer outputs; normalized tier.\\n- **State**: sealed reports.\\n- **Session**: one per analyst.\\n- **Access**: model outside analyst pool; **pre-approved fallback provider configured and exercised before pilot** (EX-2/VL-4).\\n- **Failure**: primary outage → fallback activates; fallback outage → entries blocked, never bypassed (S4 §7).\\n- **Provenance**: as L2.\\n- **Metering**: 5/run + retries.\\n- **Gate**: as L2; then G4 action table executes deterministically.\\n\\n### 7.11 Normalizer\\n- **Inputs**: exactly {analyst self-assessment, evidence sufficiency score (deterministic code: `fill_rate × weighted_reliability × conflict_penalty × recency_decay` — NO-5), validation state (L1/L2/L3), validation flags}.\\n- **Outputs**: tier ∈ {Conviction, Lean, Tentative, Pass, Contradicted} + justification + all four inputs preserved (NO-4).\\n- **Must never receive**: reasoning; selection; peers; matchup context (\\\"blind to the conclusion\\\").\\n- **State**: stateless, per-analyst, no batching (NO-2).\\n- **Session**: one invocation per included analyst.\\n- **Access**: neutral model; any capable family (README).\\n- **Failure**: failure blocks the whole artifact; retry; never bypassed (S4 §7).\\n- **Provenance**: input-set version recorded (NO-3 — version-gated changes).\\n- **Metering**: 5/run.\\n- **Gate (G5)**: every included analysis tiered + justified; FAIL analysts never receive Conviction/Lean.\\n\\n### 7.12 SAP assembler\\n- **Inputs**: all stage outputs; effective-N accounting; integrity report data (canaries, fingerprints, gate outcomes, anomalies, session-continuity verification).\\n- **Outputs**: nine-section SAP (S1 Stage 6); exclusions with `{analyst, layer, class, test_id, detail, retry_number, action}`.\\n- **Must never receive**: nothing beyond stage outputs; must not synthesize a system pick or blended score (Don #17).\\n- **State**: artifact immutable after G6 (IF-4).\\n- **Session**: n/a.\\n- **Access**: assembler is code; divergence matrix computed here.\\n- **Failure**: assembly failure → re-assemble (G6); structural incompleteness blocks.\\n- **Provenance**: full §8 chain; model/prompt versions from execution metadata only (I9).\\n- **Metering**: n/a.\\n- **Gate (G6)**: nine sections complete; effective-N present; provenance intact; integrity report present; no contamination evidence.\\n\\n### 7.13 Artifact store\\n- **Inputs**: G6-passed artifacts.\\n- **Outputs**: retrievable immutable artifacts; SAP-PreGame flagged terminal per slate.\\n- **Must never receive**: mutated artifacts (store enforces immutability — IF-4).\\n- **State**: persistent; store snapshots join the §0 backup set post-build.\\n- **Session/Access**: n/a; store-level immutability enforcement.\\n- **Failure**: whole-store failure → abort; restore from DA-5; no artifact preferable to a wrong artifact.\\n- **Provenance**: artifact-level chain complete.\\n- **Metering**: n/a.\\n- **Gate**: G6 pass is the only write path.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Decisions the Implementation Engineer Is Not Permitted to Make\\n\\n1. **N** (configured analysts) — pinned at 5 (M11/Don #11).\\n2. **Persona definitions, lenses, or count** — M3, S1 §4.\\n3. **Framing schema fields, enums, or versions** — M2/IF-1; changes are versioned methodology decisions.\\n4. **Package contents** — I1/IF-2: snapshot + requested evidence + request_status map, nothing else, ever. No \\\"helpful\\\" additions.\\n5. **Evidence push** — nothing enters a package unrequested (CR-1/DA-4), including overnight pre-fetch.\\n6. **Market-class scope decisions** — which classes are `market` and who receives them (Persona D only) — §4.3/IF-3. Baseline framing lines are NOT market-class evidence (IF-2); do not strip them (DR-18 pending Kimi confirmation).\\n7. **Validation layer count, order, skippability, or blindness rules** — P4/VL-1..8. L2 never sees raw confidence; L3 outside pool.\\n8. **G4 classes, tests, actions, or retry counts** — S1 §7.1/M30. No new failure classes; no second retry; no runtime-judgment escapes (CR-2).\\n9. **Forward-only topology** — no path from validation outputs to analyst context (I3/VL-7). Corrections only as replacement evidence items.\\n10. **Normalization inputs, blindness, or tier enum** — NO-1..6/M8. Contradicted is system-assignable only.\\n11. **Artifact sections, terminal semantics, or immutability** — M10/IF-4. SAP-PreGame is terminal; no system pick, no blended score (Don #17).\\n12. **Effective-N definitions** — configured/ran/included/excluded semantics; retries count in ledger, not ran_n (VL-8).\\n13. **Cadence, timing windows, or new run types** — S1 §2; on-demand is out of pilot scope (Don #18) — do not build the surface, stubs, or \\\"temporary\\\" triggers.\\n14. **Session semantics** — intra-run continuation, inter-run fresh context (M19/EX-3). Do not implement Stage 3 as a fresh call.\\n15. **request_status reason enum or gap lifecycle states** — M23/IF-2/IF-3.\\n16. **Cost caps or budget enforcement** — none exist; measure only (Don #8/D5). Budget 53 is reference, ledger is truth (OB-4).\\n17. **Contamination methodology** — canary injection, fingerprinting, pairwise sampling (EX-6/M7).\\n18. **Slate definition** — one MLB game per slate (S1 §2.1).\\n19. **Isolation mechanisms** — separate contexts, no shared memory/fs/netns/env (EX-1).\\n20. **Kill-switch-equivalents** — G4 exclusions are final; there is no promote/revive path (analogous to standing workspace doctrine; here explicit in §7.1).\\n\\n**Unresolved choices embedded in the package (route before coding that surface):** G2 threshold (DR-06); free-text→structured gap mapping (DR-07); artifact schema version (DR-08); prompt isolation sentence scope (DR-18); normalization numeric-threshold normativity (DR-17).\\n\\nOrdinary implementation discretion (allowed): vendor/provider selection within EX-2 constraints; language/framework; infrastructure; parser internals once DR-07 contract lands; test harness design; monitoring dashboards.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Routed Questions\\n\\n| # | Question | Seat | Why that seat |\\n|---|----------|------|---------------|\\n| Q1 | Confirm canonical methodology: stamp S1 content as v0.3.2 (or declare it canonical v0.3.1) and retire S2 to provenance (DR-03) | **Kimi** (record), **Coda** (canon confirm) | Methodology owner + supersession control |\\n| Q2 | Adjudicate ruling-ID crosswalk; declare content-keyed binding interim (DR-02) | **Coda** | Canon/supersession; cross-seat conflict |\\n| Q3 | Pin G2 threshold: value, denominator, action when unmet (DR-06) | **Kimi** (methodology gate); **Don** only if it's a business threshold | Gate criteria are methodology-owned |\\n| Q4 | Assign artifact schema version; publish versioned artifact contract (DR-08) | **Chiave** | Artifact interface owner |\\n| Q5 | Specify free-text gap → IF-3 structured form mapping + semantic dedup contract (DR-07) | **Kimi + Chiave** jointly | Splits methodology semantics / interface form |\\n| Q6 | Confirm scope of prompt sentence \\\"system will not deliver lines to you\\\" vs baseline framing lines delivered to all (DR-18) | **Kimi** (prompt wording) | Prompts are methodology-owned |\\n| Q7 | Confirm prompt 09 numeric thresholds are the normative tier contract vs S1's \\\"Typical\\\" (DR-17) | **Kimi** | Same |\\n| Q8 | Refresh S4 §14 pending list (3 of 6 landed); align I1 wording with IF-2 (DR-04/DR-12); rename artifact file (typo \\\"Architecure\\\"; S4 itself instructs `EC8_Architecture_v1.0.md`) | **Chiave** (own document) | Architecture records |\\n| Q9 | On-demand revival policy lines (who may trigger; quota) — needed only when the surface is revived, post-pilot (S4 CR-2) | **Don** | Policy lines; deliberately deferred |\\n| Q10 | Checkpoint/resume operational contract + L3 fallback coordination before Phase 2/3 (DR-15) | **Talon + Chiave** | Operations + failure semantics |\\n| Q11 | Provider/vendor slot assignments | **No ruling needed** — Implementation + Talon within EX-2; Luce verifies | Ordinary constrained choice (DR-14) |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Implementation Readiness Verdict\\n\\n### PARTIALLY BLOCKED\\n\\n**READY WITH NON-BLOCKING FIXES (can start immediately):**\\n- **Phase 0 — Foundation**: evidence store (DA-1..5: append-only, SHA-256, identity, provenance, backup), secrets (SE-5), data-layer schema. No blocked surface touches this.\\n- **Phase 1 — Orchestration**: provider abstraction with ledger hooks (OB-3) and observability emit-points (OB-5). The 53/26/1 budget is now decomposable and testable (DR-05 closed).\\n- Non-semantic scaffolding: run IDs, scheduling skeletons, store round-trips.\\n\\n**BLOCKED SURFACES (named):**\\n1. **G2 gate assertions** — threshold value absent (DR-06, Q3 → Kimi).\\n2. **Artifact schema binding** — no version exists for downstream/test pinning (DR-08, Q4 → Chiave).\\n3. **Gap-request router semantics** — free-text→structured mapping and dedup contract unspecified (DR-07, Q5 → Kimi+Chiave).\\n4. **Package-assembler market-filter semantics** — prompt wording vs baseline-lines delivery (DR-18, Q6 → Kimi).\\n5. **Ruling-keyed traceability in tests/docs** — bind to ruling content, not CR IDs, until DR-02 is adjudicated (Q2 → Coda).\\n\\n**NOT BLOCKED (downgraded from v0.1):** framing scheduler + call-budget assertions (now specified: 3 framing/slate); overnight model-call question (closed: 1 framing call); multi-game slate topology (closed: independent slates); on-demand (settled: excluded); evidence delivery model (aligned: request-gated store-only).\\n\\n**Note on evidence:** no execution evidence was supplied; every claim above is FACT/DERIVED/CONFLICT from records, not VERIFIED. This is a translation document, not a correctness certification (Luce's seat).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Recommended Next Handoff\\n\\n1. **To Coda** (single session): adjudicate DR-01/DR-02/DR-03 — readiness-state contradiction, ruling-ID crosswalk, canonical methodology stamp. This unblocks the \\\"unblocked\\\" claim in S5.\\n2. **To Kimi**: issue the v0.3.2 record stamp (or canonical declaration) over S1 content; pin G2 (Q3); specify the gap-mapping contract (Q5); fix prompt wording (Q6, Q18) and re-version prompts (DR-09); correct S5 §9/§11 (DR-10/DR-11).\\n3. **To Chiave**: assign artifact schema version (Q4); refresh §14; align I1 wording; rename the spec file per its own closing instruction.\\n4. **To Implementation (parallel, now)**: begin Phase 0 + Phase 1 against §7 contracts of this document; bind records by content hash.\\n5. **To Luce**: define the verification evidence matrix for the four seeded pilot failures (S4 §11) so Phase 3 acceptance is checkable on arrival.\\n6. **To Talon**: draft the scheduling + L3-fallback operational contract (Q10) in parallel; needed by Phase 2, not Phase 0.\\n\\n*Prior-handoff continuity: this document supersedes `EC8_Methodology_Architecture_Reconciliation_v0.1.md` — it resolves D-05/D-06/D-07/D-13, narrows D-01, retains D-08 (as DR-06) and D-11 (as DR-08), and adds the ruling-ID crosswalk (DR-02), the dual-v0.3.1 finding (DR-03), and the prompt/baseline market wording conflict (DR-18).*\\n\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O9Lca5zqZ7tyf8XcYWGXwBtlGb9LnIhXn4tmSKZK75A/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"05_GCE_PROCESS_AND_GATES\",\"id\":\"1O9Lca5zqZ7tyf8XcYWGXwBtlGb9LnIhXn4tmSKZK75A\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"3225\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T03:23:24.205Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-08T20:44:36.993Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-08T20:44:36.993Z\",\"display_title\":\"05_GCE_PROCESS_AND_GATES\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O9Lca5zqZ7tyf8XcYWGXwBtlGb9LnIhXn4tmSKZK75A/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1-2XT7kaaOIIu8aqjcGFIPF_ktPF0N9vQ\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿EC⁸ AI Convergence — GCE Process and Gates\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGate 0 — Don Intent\\r\\nDefine problem, purpose, success criteria, exclusions, and Don sign-off boundaries.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGate 1 — Coda Governance Frame\\r\\nDefine authority, seat ownership, source-of-truth rules, canon/supersession rules, and routing boundaries.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGate 2 — Kimi Methodology\\r\\nDeliver convergence methodology, technical-stack methodology, independent-analysis method, reconciliation method, confidence method, stopping conditions, and methodology test plan. No implementation lock before methodology acceptance.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGate 3 — Chiave Architecture\\r\\nInvoke for material structural concerns: topology, interfaces, durable state, security architecture, runtime boundaries, failure domains, scaling/concurrency, canonical infrastructure.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGate 4 — Kimi Design & Build\\r\\nInput approved methodology + architecture where required. Deliver component plan, build sequence, implementation package, prototype sequence, assumption register, and technical tests.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGate 5 — Implementation\\r\\nBuild only approved scope and surface assumptions.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGate 6 — Talon Operations\\r\\nDeliver deployment sequence, runtime procedures, handoffs, observability, recovery, operational ownership.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGate 7 — Luce Verification\\r\\nVerify evidence lineage, claims, reproducibility, constraints, contradiction preservation, and execution.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGate 8 — Coda Governance Reconciliation\\r\\nConfirm authority compliance, canon state, unresolved Don decisions, and that no seat exceeded authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nGate 9 — Don Decision\\r\\nAccept / reject / modify / return to prior gate.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRule\\r\\nCompetence does not replace authority separation. Do not skip gates because a model appears capable.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2026-09-06 ADDENDUM — TRANSLATION CHECKPOINT\\r\\nInsert between Gate 4 (Kimi Design & Build) and Gate 5 (Implementation):\\r\\nGate 4A — Principal Consultant Technical Translation / Integration\\r\\nInput: accepted methodology, accepted architecture where materially required, Kimi Design & Build package, governing source/canon state.\\r\\nOutput: methodology↔architecture traceability, discrepancy register, version/ruling crosswalk, implementation contract by component, no-coder-discretion register, routed questions, and component-level readiness verdict.\\r\\nRule: this is a translation checkpoint, not an approval gate. It may identify and route unresolved methodology/architecture/governance questions but may not resolve them by authority. Implementation proceeds only on surfaces whose contracts are unambiguous.\\r\\nOperational success test: Implementation/Talon can act from the handoff without inventing requirements or reinterpreting upstream methodology/architecture\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2026-09-06 PROPOSED PROCESS REVISION — TRANSLATION BEFORE INDEPENDENT DESIGN\\r\\nDon clarified that methodology authorship and concrete Design & Build selection should be separated. The earlier Gate 4 / Gate 4A ordering is therefore under controlled revision. Do not erase the earlier gate record; preserve it as provenance until Don canonizes the replacement.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPROPOSED working sequence:\\r\\nGate 0 — Don Intent\\r\\nGate 1 — Coda Governance Frame\\r\\nGate 2 — Kimi Methodology\\r\\nGate 3 — Chiave Architecture when materially required\\r\\nGate 4 — Principal Consultant Specification + Translation\\r\\nInput: accepted Don intent, Kimi methodology, Chiave architecture, governing canon/source state.\\r\\nOutput: traceability, discrepancy register, implementation contracts, no-coder-discretion register, routed questions, implementation-ready spec/package.\\r\\nRule: translation checkpoint only; no design or approval authority.\\r\\nGate 5 — Independent Design & Build [PROVISIONAL]\\r\\nInput: implementation-ready spec/package.\\r\\nOutput: concrete provider/model/runtime assignments, component/tool choices, detailed implementation design, build package, cost/value analysis, fallback/runtime manifest. May not change methodology or architecture.\\r\\nGate 6 — Talon Operational Routing / Deployment Control\\r\\nGate 7 — Keel Build / Deploy / Implementation Test / Evidence Return\\r\\nGate 8 — Luce Independent Verification / Ground Truth\\r\\nGate 9 — Coda Governance Reconciliation\\r\\nGate 10 — Don Decision\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent audition evidence for Gate 5: Grok 4.6 and GLM 5.1 have produced independent runtime-design candidates. No candidate design or seat runtime is canonical yet.\\r\\n.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2026-09-08 DON-APPROVED PROCESS ADDENDUM — CONVERSATION RECONCILIATION ANCHOR (CRA)\\r\\nThe Conversation Reconciliation Anchor (CRA) is now the standard long-chat reset and new-chat handoff control across EC⁸ work. Trigger it when conversation length creates drift risk, when labels/identities/authority begin to blur, when material corrections/retractions accumulate, or before moving into a new chat.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nA CRA is not merely a summary. It must: distill the conversation into topic-level bullets with one concise paragraph per topic; reconcile current truth against prior assumptions; preserve corrections/retractions/conflicts and provenance; identify open gaps/dependencies/ownership; and end with STATUS / CONFIDENCE / REASON / NEXT GATE / DON INPUT NEEDED.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCRA governing rules: IDENTITY != ROLE != LENS != PERSONALITY != AUTHORITY != MODEL; MODEL != SEAT; newer != canonical; corrections are additive rather than historical rewrites; conflicts remain preserved until resolved by correct authority; context breadth does not grant authority breadth; Edge Crew Quant != AI Convergence; UNKNOWN / NOT_AVAILABLE states may not be hidden for continuity convenience.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter Don approves a CRA, update/add the relevant artifacts without rewriting history, create a current handoff artifact, point the new chat to that handoff plus the relevant Google Drive knowledge base, preserve any local-vs-Drive source-of-truth distinction, and resume at the stated NEXT GATE.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPrimary protocol artifact: EC8_CONVERSATION_RECONCILIATION_ANCHOR_PROTOCOL_v1.0 (Drive ID 1i5qirCXzjoQIuOrIXWYalqC5BxAT0yduH6WY1aEfNGg).\"},{\"url\":\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1oprgQ1DkAfDeg-AS3njg_YBcmCLOYoaI/view?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"EC8_Methodology_Architecture_Reconciliation_v0.1.md\",\"id\":\"1oprgQ1DkAfDeg-AS3njg_YBcmCLOYoaI\",\"mime_type\":\"text/markdown\",\"size\":\"22033\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T11:47:12.335Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T11:47:12.335Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":null,\"display_title\":\"EC8_Methodology_Architecture_Reconciliation_v0.1.md\",\"display_url\":\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1oprgQ1DkAfDeg-AS3njg_YBcmCLOYoaI/view?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1EXzOuIyaLkTFB0pL6g5xXTWddHcbjN3O\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"# EC8 Methodology <-> Architecture Implementation Reconciliation\\n\\n**Prepared by:** Principal Consultant — Technical Translation / Integration  \\n**Status:** Reconciliation of supplied package; not a methodology or architecture amendment  \\n**Sources:** Kimi methodology `v0.3.1` in both archives; fixed `HANDOFF_v0.3.1`; Chiave `Architecture Specification v1.0` / `EC8_Architecure_Brief.txt`; production prompts 01-09.\\n\\nClaim labels used below: **FACT**, **DERIVED**, **PROPOSED**, **UNKNOWN**, **CONFLICT**, **OUTSIDE AUTHORITY**.\\n\\n## 1. Executive Reconciliation\\n\\n**FACT:** The intended system is a scheduled MLB Sovereign Analysis Pipeline. It creates five independent analyst landscapes, not a consensus pick, validates each analysis through L1/L2/L3, normalizes confidence, and emits immutable SAP artifacts.\\n\\n**FACT:** The accepted architecture is structurally aligned with the accepted methodology on isolation, request-gated evidence delivery, market-persona exclusivity, forward-only validation, deterministic G4, effective-N, provenance, metering, and terminal `SAP-PreGame`.\\n\\n**CONFLICT / record defect:** The fixed handoff declares “Ready for Coder,” while Chiave v1.0 declares “Post-gate, pre-build,” companion methodology pending six v0.3.2 record fixes, and Phase 0 still has exit criteria. This is a status contradiction, not permission to choose a side.\\n\\n**CONFLICT:** The package's older architecture brief and v0.3 source retain OnDemand and an `OnDemand` framing enum; the accepted v0.3.1 methodology and Chiave v1.0 remove OnDemand from pilot scope and bind the build to the corrected enum. The old artifacts are provenance only.\\n\\n**CONFLICT:** Ruling IDs drift. In the handoff, CR-1..CR-4 are evidence gating, deterministic G4, cost, and framing. In Chiave v1.0, CR-1 is evidence gating, CR-2 is OnDemand scope/revival conditions, CR-3 is cost, CR-4 is G4, and CR-5 is framing. The fixed methodology text also assigns differing names to CR-2/CR-4 in places.\\n\\n**IMPLEMENTATION CLARIFICATION REQUIRED:** “53 calls/slate” is a budget fact, but the supplied documents do not provide a machine-checkable call decomposition. Fresh framing is required for Overnight, Morning, and Pre-Game, yet Overnight is described as one call and full runs as 26. The ledger must count actual calls; Kimi/Chiave must document the intended baseline decomposition before budget assertions become tests.\\n\\n**VERDICT:** **PARTIALLY BLOCKED.** Phase 0 store/secrets design and non-semantic orchestration scaffolding can proceed. Framing scheduler, call-budget assertions, ruling-keyed traceability, terminal artifact binding, and any OnDemand surface are blocked until the named record/contract questions are resolved.\\n\\n## 2. System Intent Summary\\n\\n**FACT:** Within the final 24-hour window for each scheduled MLB slate, ingest the slate and create a schema-enumerated framing snapshot; acquire evidence into an append-only provenance store; run five isolated, heterogeneous, persona-specific analysts; let each request and receive only its own evidence; continue each analyst in-session for re-analysis; validate forward-only through deterministic L1, pairwise different-family L2, and outside-pool L3; normalize from four preserved inputs; and seal an immutable nine-section SAP landscape.\\n\\nCadence is Overnight (framing/store population only), Morning (full analyst run), and Pre-Game (full analyst run; terminal). Prior snapshots remain records and are never delivered. Market-class evidence is exclusive to Persona D. Missing data remains explicit. Retries, exclusions, effective-N, integrity, provenance, and provider/token cost are recorded. Pilot scope is one scheduled MLB slate, N=5, full validation, and four seeded failures. No consensus, EV engine, human arbitration, trigger reruns, or pilot OnDemand.\\n\\n## 3. Methodology -> Architecture Traceability\\n\\n| Methodology requirement | Source | Architecture contract | Status | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Five independent personas; no peer context | Methodology §§1, 3.2, 5; prompts 02-06 | I2, EX-1, EX-6 | Exact | Architecture adds process/container/network/env isolation and canaries. |\\n| Analysts self-determine gaps | §§1.4 P2, Stage 2 | IF-3, DA-4 | Exact | Store may be broad; delivery is request-gated. |\\n| Package invariant | §§2.5, Stage 2 | I1, IF-2 | Exact | Single choke point and audit are machine-enforced. |\\n| Evidence identity and cumulative delivery | §2.5 | IF-2, DA-1/2/3 | Partial | `acquired_in_run` and complete status-map shape need schema binding. |\\n| Market evidence only Persona D | §4.3; prompt 05 | IF-2/3, SE-4 | Exact | Boundary and re-check are explicit. |\\n| Intra-run continuity; inter-run freshness | §2.6, Stage 3 | EX-3 | Exact | Retry also stays in same session per VL-6. |\\n| Heterogeneity | §3 Stage 1 | EX-2 | Partial | Architecture gives >=3 families and pairwise L2 rule; provider assignment/registry is not supplied. |\\n| Three validation layers; no skip | §4 | VL-1..7, I3/I5 | Exact | L1 semantic router is architecture completion under standing rulings. |\\n| G4 deterministic classification/retry | §7.1 | VL-2, VL-5, VL-6 | Exact | Observable classification tests are methodology-owned. |\\n| Forward-only validation | §4 | I3, VL-7 | Exact | Corrections are replacement evidence only. |\\n| Normalizer four inputs, neutral/stateless | §5, prompt 09 | NO-1..6 | Exact | Selection/reasoning/peers forbidden. |\\n| Confidence tiers and effective-N | §§5-6 | IF-4, NO-4/6 | Partial | Tier enum is methodology-owned; artifact schema version is architecture-owned and not yet pinned. |\\n| Integrity report | §3/Stage 6 | IF-4, I7 | Exact | Includes contamination, gates, anomalies, continuity. |\\n| Terminal SAP-PreGame; Morning retained | §2.3-2.4, §6 | IF-4 | Exact | Older source's SAP-OnDemand is stale for pilot. |\\n| Append-only evidence/provenance/replay | §§2, 6, 9 | DA-1..5, I4/I9 | Exact | Re-execution verifies process, not historical result. |\\n| Cost measurement at execution point | §9 | I10, OB-1..4 | Partial | Unit is fixed; 53-call decomposition and provider pricing binding are unresolved. |\\n| Failure behavior | §§7, 7.1 | §7 Failure Domains, checkpoints | Partial | Checkpoint/resume is architecture completion; acquisition threshold semantics remain underspecified. |\\n\\n## 4. Architecture -> Methodology Back-Trace\\n\\n| Architecture contract | Authorizing source | Classification | Trace / issue |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| I1/IF-2 package choke point | Methodology package invariant; CR-1 | DIRECTLY REQUIRED | Exact. |\\n| I2/EX-1 isolation and canaries | P1 and §5 controls | DIRECTLY REQUIRED | Container/process granularity is architecture-owned completion. |\\n| I3/VL-7 forward-only | Stage 4 forward-only rule | DIRECTLY REQUIRED | Exact. |\\n| I4 replay-as-record | Provenance/artifact requirements | REASONABLY DERIVED | Canonical replay semantics are architecture-owned completion; no methodology conflict found. |\\n| I6 machine-checkable gates | §7.1 G4 ruling | DIRECTLY REQUIRED | Exact. |\\n| IF-1 fixed `0.3-MLB`; no OnDemand | schema §3.1 plus accepted v0.3.1 scope | DIRECTLY REQUIRED | The `OnDemand` enum in older artifacts is stale. |\\n| IF-4 independent artifact schema and immutability | Stage 6 plus architecture ownership | ARCHITECTURE-OWNED COMPLETION | Binding version and store immutability require implementation contract. |\\n| VL-2 L1 semantic router | G4 determinism and gates-as-checkpoints standing rulings | ARCHITECTURE-OWNED COMPLETION | Explicitly flagged by Chiave; not a new methodology ruling. |\\n| Checkpoint/resume at each gate | gates-as-checkpoints standing ruling | ARCHITECTURE-OWNED COMPLETION | Requires persistence semantics and idempotency contract. |\\n| L3 fallback pre-approved/configured/exercised | methodology L3 fallback requirement | DIRECTLY REQUIRED | Operations coordination belongs to Talon; implementation must expose the hook. |\\n| SE-1..7 security boundaries | prompt/data isolation and trust requirements | REASONABLY DERIVED | Security implementation is Chiave-owned; OnDemand trust boundary is deferred. |\\n| OB-3 provider abstraction metering | methodology cost ledger | DIRECTLY REQUIRED | Exact provider/invoice integration is not specified. |\\n\\nNo supplied architecture contract was found to authorize a consensus engine, EV engine, trigger-based rerun, human arbitration, market access for non-D, or pilot OnDemand.\\n\\n## 5. Discrepancy Register\\n\\n| ID | Classification | Source A | Source B | Conflict / impact | Owner | Gate |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| D-01 | status drift | HANDOFF §1-2, §9 | Chiave v1.0 header/§10 | “Coder unblocked/ready” vs post-gate/pre-build and pending v0.3.2 fixes. | Coda | GOVERNANCE / DON DECISION |\\n| D-02 | stale handoff | HANDOFF §9 | Chiave v1.0 §0/§14 | Handoff says architecture brief does not exist; supplied canonical architecture does. | Coda | NON-BLOCKING RECORD FIX |\\n| D-03 | ruling-ID drift | methodology changelog; HANDOFF §4 | Chiave §12 | Same CR IDs carry different ruling names; traceability tests cannot bind safely. | Coda + Kimi + Chiave | GOVERNANCE / DON DECISION |\\n| D-04 | semantic conflict | old v0.3 / old architecture brief | accepted v0.3.1 + Chiave v1.0 | OnDemand and enum retained in old records but removed from pilot. | Coda | NON-BLOCKING RECORD FIX; pilot surface blocked |\\n| D-05 | version drift | Chiave §0/§14 | handoff title/status | Architecture v1.0 references methodology v0.3.1 pending v0.3.2 record fixes; handoff calls v0.3.1 complete. | Kimi + Coda | IMPLEMENTATION CLARIFICATION REQUIRED |\\n| D-06 | implementation ambiguity | methodology §2, §9 | Chiave OB-4 | 53 total / 26 full-run calls is not decomposed against three framing snapshots and all stages. | Kimi + Chiave | ARCHITECTURE GATE |\\n| D-07 | implementation ambiguity | methodology §2.1/§2.6 | Chiave IF-1/§7 | “Fresh framing snapshot” may imply a model invocation, but only Overnight=1 and full-run=26 are budgeted. | Kimi | METHODOLOGY GATE |\\n| D-08 | missing contract | Stage 2 G2 | Chiave §7 | `>threshold%` has no value, denominator, or action when unmet; partial mode is described but not parameterized. | Kimi | METHODOLOGY GATE |\\n| D-09 | missing contract | Stage 2/IF-3 | Chiave IF-3 | Semantic deduplication, requester-to-item mapping, and cumulative status-map schema are not specified enough for deterministic replay. | Kimi + Chiave | IMPLEMENTATION CLARIFICATION REQUIRED |\\n| D-10 | missing contract | prompts/README | EX-2 | “Different architecture family” registry and assignment algorithm are absent; normalization family constraints are absent. | Chiave | ARCHITECTURE GATE |\\n| D-11 | missing contract | Stage 6 | IF-4 | Artifact schema version and exact nine-section JSON contract are not supplied. | Chiave | ARCHITECTURE GATE |\\n| D-12 | textual drift | methodology versions | Chiave §14 | Pending six fixes include Stage 6 terminal line, ruling numbering, attribution, H1 version; source package does not include accepted v0.3.2. | Kimi | METHODOLOGY GATE |\\n| D-13 | scope ambiguity | methodology handoff | Chiave §11 | “one MLB slate” versus handoff definition of slate as one scheduled game; multi-game execution topology is unclear. | Don + Kimi | GOVERNANCE / DON DECISION |\\n| D-14 | operational boundary | Chiave §7/§13 | pilot/handoff | Checkpoint/resume and L3 fallback require deployment, persistence, and recovery behavior not owned by coder alone. | Talon + Chiave | IMPLEMENTATION CLARIFICATION REQUIRED |\\n\\n## 6. Version / Ruling Crosswalk\\n\\n| Subject | Safe binding now | Unsafe/stale reference |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Methodology | Accepted `EC8_AI_Convergence_v0.3.1.md` content as supplied, with v0.3.2 record fixes unresolved | `EC8_AI_Convergence_v0.3.md` as normative source |\\n| Architecture | `Architecture Specification v1.0` / `EC8_Architecure_Brief.txt` | Older `Chiave_Architecture_Brief.md` that still exposes OnDemand |\\n| Framing schema | `0.3-MLB`, `run_context ∈ {Overnight, Morning, PreGame}` | Any schema containing `OnDemand`; old schema text with divergent enum |\\n| Prompts | Fixed handoff prompts 01-09, prompt package v0.3 | Prompt copies without manifest/hash binding |\\n| Artifact | Nine sections; terminal `SAP-PreGame`; schema version must be assigned by Chiave | `SAP-OnDemand` for pilot; unversioned artifact JSON |\\n| Rulings | Content can be implemented only after a canonical ID map is issued | Binding tests to CR number alone |\\n\\n## 7. Implementation Contract By Pipeline Stage\\n\\nThe following is a translation of accepted contracts, not production code.\\n\\n| Stage | Inputs / outputs | Must never receive | State / session | Access / failure | Provenance / metering | Gate |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Acquisition | Raw slate/source requests -> immutable evidence items/status | Peer outputs, analyst reasoning; secrets in payloads | Persistent append-only store; acquisition execution ephemeral | Source failure => `unfilled(reason)`; no silent substitution | SHA-256 identity, source, time, reliability, run type, expiration; meter acquisition at execution | Source item valid and stored or explicit status |\\n| Framing | Raw slate + trusted structured inputs -> `0.3-MLB` snapshot | Analyst outputs, prose judgment, prior snapshot delivery | Snapshot persistent; framing call isolated | Invalid schema blocks G0; no OnDemand pilot context | model/prompt/params/runtime metadata; one ledger entry per actual call | G0 |\\n| Analyst first pass | Current framing snapshot + training knowledge -> structured preliminary analysis and gap requests | Peers, N, peer personas, divergence, prior runs, unrequested evidence, market data unless D | Fresh context per run; continuous into Stage 3 | Execution failure retry/exclude per slot; contamination recorded | analyst canary, model family, prompt/params, session ID; provider ledger | G1 |\\n| Gap-request router | Analyst-owned structured requests -> authorized acquisition work/status | Peer request content for delivery; market requests from non-D | Ephemeral routing plus persistent request lifecycle | Malformed => `unfilled(malformed_request)`; non-D market => `access_denied` + event | requester persona, request ID, policy decision, timestamps | Every request authorized and traceable |\\n| Evidence acquisition | Authorized requests/store -> immutable items | Analyst outputs and peer context | Persistent store; no analyst session | Partial mode; `unfilled` reason; never mutate item | Per-item lineage and acquisition ledger | G2 inputs available; unresolved threshold contract D-08 |\\n| Package assembler | Current snapshot + that analyst's requested/cumulative items + status map -> package | Peer items/reasoning/gaps, prior snapshots, non-D market | Single choke point; package ephemeral, audit persistent | Any invariant breach => G6-style failure/block | package hash, item IDs, disclosure line, audit record | I1/IF-2 audit passes |\\n| Analyst re-analysis | Same session + package -> final analysis | Validation reports, peer data, sealed corrections as commentary | Same session as first pass; retry same session; fresh next run | Incomplete/hallucination => G3 action; correction only as replacement evidence | session transcript sealed; all evidence IDs | G3 |\\n| L1 | Analysis + package + registries -> mechanical report / semantic classification event | Peer outputs; analyst raw confidence is not needed | Stateless per analysis; persisted report | Failure routes through L2 classification; never skip | test IDs, registry versions, timestamps; ledger only if model router invoked (L1 itself no model call) | VL-1/VL-2 |\\n| L2 | Analysis + evidence/package + L1 report -> pairwise validation | Raw analyst confidence; peer analysts; wrong-family validator | Independent validator context; report sealed | FAIL classified; correctable retry once, second FAIL exclude; execution failure blocks/retries | validator model family, report hash, class/test IDs, ledger | VL-3/VL-6 |\\n| L3 | Analysis + L1/L2 reports -> red-team report | Analyst pool identity/context beyond allowed input; no bypass | Outside-pool context; fallback preconfigured | Primary outage -> fallback; both unavailable blocks, never skip | provider/fallback identity, report lineage, ledger | VL-4/VL-6 |\\n| Normalizer | Exactly self-assessment, sufficiency score, validation state, flags -> tier + justification | Reasoning, selection, peer outputs, raw package | Stateless per analyst; no batching | Failure blocks artifact and retries; `Contradicted` system-assigned only | formula/version, model metadata, four inputs preserved; meter model call | NO-1..6 / G5 |\\n| SAP assembler | Framing, included analyses, validation, divergence, sufficiency, provenance, integrity -> nine-section artifact | Mutable post-G6 inputs; hidden smoothing; unrecorded exclusions | Persistent immutable artifact; checkpointed orchestration | Missing section/gate/provenance blocks; no artifact preferred to wrong artifact | full chain, effective-N, integrity, cost ledger reconciliation | G6 |\\n| Artifact store | Validated artifact + manifest -> immutable retrievable terminal | Mutation, overwrite, unbound schema | Write-once persistent store; backup snapshots | Store failure aborts/recovery from DA-5 | artifact hash, schema/method/prompt versions, run ID | Immutability and restore test |\\n\\n## 8. Decisions the Implementation Engineer Is Not Permitted to Make\\n\\n- Choose between conflicting methodology or architecture versions.\\n- Treat the handoff's “coder unblocked” wording as authority to bypass the architecture gate.\\n- Reintroduce OnDemand, trigger reruns, consensus, EV scoring, or human arbitration.\\n- Decide whether fresh framing means a model call, or alter the 53/26 budget decomposition.\\n- Define a slate as one game or a multi-game slate.\\n- Alter the framing schema, enum, null/reason-code behavior, or artifact section semantics.\\n- Deliver prior snapshots, peer outputs, peer requests, peer personas, or non-D market evidence.\\n- Share analyst filesystem, network namespace, memory, environment, prompt template, or secrets.\\n- Select model families, L2 pairings, L3 provider/fallback, or normalization visibility in a way that changes heterogeneity/isolation.\\n- Convert a validation report into analyst-visible instructions or feed validation backward.\\n- Replace evidence items in place, hide missing evidence, or invent a fallback source/status.\\n- Change G4 tests, classes, retry count, retry session, exclusion behavior, or effective-N accounting.\\n- Define the G2 threshold, reliability formula, sufficiency formula, tier conditions, or `Contradicted` semantics.\\n- Assign artifact schema version, terminal pointer behavior, or post-G6 mutability without Chiave.\\n- Claim cost truth from configured intent, call counts alone, or a reconstructed ledger.\\n- Decide security boundaries, credential placement, retention, replay semantics, or checkpoint idempotency.\\n\\nOrdinary choices such as language, library, queue implementation, serialization library, and non-semantic naming are permitted only if all above contracts remain unchanged and tests expose the contract.\\n\\n## 9. Routed Questions\\n\\n1. **Kimi:** Is the normative implementation source v0.3.1 pending v0.3.2, and what exact six record fixes comprise v0.3.2? Provide canonical ruling IDs and the H1/version crosswalk.\\n2. **Kimi:** Does “fresh framing snapshot” require a new framing model invocation for Morning and Pre-Game? Publish the exact 53-call decomposition, including framing, analyst, validation, normalization, and retry exclusions.\\n3. **Kimi:** What is the numeric G2 threshold, denominator, freshness window, and action when the threshold is not met?\\n4. **Kimi + Chiave:** Define deterministic request deduplication, cumulative `request_status` schema, `acquired_in_run`, and requester-to-evidence authorization mapping.\\n5. **Chiave:** Issue a canonical ruling-ID map and artifact schema version/JSON contract, including exact nine sections and schema compatibility rules.\\n6. **Chiave:** Publish the provider-family registry, analyst-to-family assignment, pairwise L2 constraint, L3 outside-pool constraint, and normalization provider rule.\\n7. **Don + Kimi:** Resolve whether “slate” means one scheduled MLB game or a multi-game unit; specify run and artifact identity for a multi-game day.\\n8. **Chiave + Talon:** Define checkpoint persistence, resume idempotency, L3 fallback activation, operator ownership, and recovery evidence for the pilot.\\n9. **Coda:** Rule which older package artifacts are provenance-only and issue the status wording that replaces “ready for coder/unblocked.”\\n10. **Luce:** Confirm the machine-checkable verification evidence required for isolation, invoice reconciliation, classification reliability, and checkpoint/replay claims.\\n\\n## 10. Implementation Readiness Verdict\\n\\n### PARTIALLY BLOCKED\\n\\n**Can proceed:** Phase 0 append-only evidence store foundation, secret isolation skeleton, provider abstraction interfaces, execution-point ledger hooks, test harnesses, and non-semantic orchestration scaffolding.\\n\\n**Blocked:** framing scheduler and call-budget assertions; canonical ruling-keyed traceability; artifact schema binding and terminal pointer; G2 threshold behavior; semantic request deduplication/status replay; provider-family assignments; checkpoint/resume behavior; any OnDemand surface; multi-game slate topology.\\n\\nThis is not a correctness certification. No execution evidence was supplied, so all claims remain FACT/DERIVED/CONFLICT rather than VERIFIED.\\n\\n## 11. Recommended Next Handoff\\n\\nRoute this reconciliation to **Coda** for the status/ruling provenance decision, then to **Kimi and Chiave jointly** for the call-budget, G2, request lifecycle, provider registry, artifact schema, and slate-identity contracts. After those answers are recorded in the owned sources and the stale package is marked provenance-only, hand **Phase 0** to Implementation with Luce's acceptance evidence matrix and Talon's checkpoint/fallback operational contract.\\n\"},{\"url\":\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1FHXcC5DKiLLIQROsHo5_0t9faw0GlVv5/view?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"EC8_Architecture_Specification_v1.0_Chiave_source.md\",\"id\":\"1FHXcC5DKiLLIQROsHo5_0t9faw0GlVv5\",\"mime_type\":\"text/markdown\",\"size\":\"20212\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-06T11:47:30.362Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-06T11:47:30.362Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":null,\"display_title\":\"EC8_Architecture_Specification_v1.0_Chiave_source.md\",\"display_url\":\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1FHXcC5DKiLLIQROsHo5_0t9faw0GlVv5/view?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1EXzOuIyaLkTFB0pL6g5xXTWddHcbjN3O\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"**Chiave — architecture documentation, hardened.**\\r\\n\\r\\nHere is the durable document. One design choice up front, made deliberately: **this spec references the methodology by version and pin rather than duplicating its content.** The framing schema JSON, the G4 test tables, the tier definitions — those live in Kimi's document, versioned. Duplicating them here would create exactly the two-write-path problem P7 exists to kill (and the stale-brief failure we just caught). What this document owns: the invariants, the interface contracts in checkable form, failure domains, security boundaries, instrumentation, the build plan, and the ruling register — including content the methodology has *not yet preserved*, which is the real backup value.\\r\\n\\r\\nTwo specifications in here are completions rather than consolidations — the L1 semantic-classification router and checkpoint/resume semantics — both flowing from standing rulings (G4 determinism, gates-as-checkpoints), exercised under normal design authority, flagged as such in the register. No new rulings were issued.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n# EC⁸ AI Convergence — Architecture Specification v1.0\\r\\n\\r\\n**Owner**: Chiave (Architecture) · **Status**: Post-gate, pre-build · **Companion**: Methodology v0.3.1 (Kimi, pending v0.3.2 record fixes)\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §0 — Document Authority\\r\\n\\r\\nThis is the canonical record of the architecture layer: structure, interfaces, failure behavior, instrumentation, and invariants. Methodology v0.3.1 governs process; this governs structure. Where this document's interface contracts and the methodology describe the same surface, they are the same ruling recorded twice — any divergence is a record error to be corrected at source, not adjudicated.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Governance**: versioned independently of the methodology; changes land here at adoption; every version diffs against the ruling register (§12). Build commits record actuals (chosen providers, infrastructure) in v1.1+ — this document is design-of-record until then.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Reference discipline**: methodology content is referenced by section and version, never copied. The normative framing schema text is methodology §3.1 @ v0.3.2 (enum fix pending); the G4 classification protocol is methodology §7.1 @ v0.3.1.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Backup set** (version-locked): `{this spec, methodology v0.3.x, prompts/01–09, governance changelog}` + manifest with SHA-256 per file. Post-build, evidence-store snapshots join the set. With these artifacts, the system is re-derivable.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §1 — System Invariants\\r\\n\\r\\nThe constitution. Violation of any invariant means the system is no longer what it claims to be, regardless of output quality.\\r\\n\\r\\n| ID | Invariant | Enforcement |\\r\\n|---|---|---|\\r\\n| **I1** | Analyst evidence package = current framing snapshot + requested evidence + request_status map. **Nothing else, ever.** | Single choke-point assembly function (IF-2); post-hoc package audit every run |\\r\\n| **I2** | No analyst context contains peer outputs, peer reasoning, peer gap requests, N, peer personas, or divergence measurement | Canaries, fingerprinting, package audit, isolation checks (EX-6) |\\r\\n| **I3** | Validation flow is forward-only: validation outputs feed normalizer and artifact; no path to analyst context exists | Topology constraint (VL-7); corrections reach analysts only as replacement evidence items |\\r\\n| **I4** | Replay-as-record: complete state capture; the stored artifact is canonical, re-execution verifies process, not results | Provenance chain (DA-3), evidence hashes, execution metadata (EX-5) |\\r\\n| **I5** | No validation layer is skipped; execution failure blocks, never bypasses | Layer scheduler (VL-4); G4 |\\r\\n| **I6** | Gates evaluate machine-checkable criteria only; no runtime judgment | G4 deterministic action table (VL-5); semantic classification is recorded and measured, never judged |\\r\\n| **I7** | Fail-transparent: partials, exclusions, and unfilled gaps are recorded, never smoothed | request_status, effective-N, integrity report are mandatory artifact sections |\\r\\n| **I8** | Every input shared by all analysts is a versioned constant, never per-run curation | Framing schema (IF-1) + disclosure set; store-vs-delivery separation (DA-4) |\\r\\n| **I9** | Provenance records model/prompt/parameter versions from execution metadata — never from configuration intent or org charts | Runtime capture at provider abstraction (EX-5) |\\r\\n| **I10** | Every model call and acquisition is metered at its execution point; the ledger is the only source of cost truth | Instrumentation at provider/acquisition layers (OB-3) |\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §2 — Interface Contracts\\r\\n\\r\\nThe four cross-seat interfaces. These are what other seats build against and what downstream binds to.\\r\\n\\r\\n### IF-1 — Framing Schema Interface\\r\\n- Output is a populated instance of framing schema **0.3-MLB** (methodology §3.1; v0.3.2 removes `OnDemand` from `run_context` — build commits to the fixed enum). Enumerated fields only; `null`-with-reason-code; no free-text fields; form-filler regime; **prior snapshots retained as record, never delivered** (M29).\\r\\n- **Verify**: schema validator rejects non-conforming output at G0; delivery log shows no analyst receiving more than one snapshot per run.\\r\\n\\r\\n### IF-2 — Evidence Package Interface\\r\\n- Contents per I1. `request_status`: `filled` | `unfilled` + reason (`unacquirable` | `source_unreliable` | `too_expensive` | `timeout` | `not_applicable`) | `pending`.\\r\\n- **Evidence identity**: (entity, attribute, snapshot-time) — each a distinct immutable store item. Time-variant data (lines, weather, injuries) never mutates a record; it creates a new one.\\r\\n- **Cumulative re-delivery** per run (M18/M30), with the disclosure line present in packaging.\\r\\n- **Market policy enforcement**: market-class evidence (movements, current lines at non-baseline times, public %, sharp indicators, volume) deliverable to Persona D only. Baseline line fields from the framing schema ride the shared baseline to all. Enforced role-keyed at the gap-request boundary (IF-3) and re-verified at the choke point.\\r\\n- **Assembly via a single choke-point function**; every package assembly logged and reconstructable post-hoc.\\r\\n- **Verify**: package audit reconstructs every delivered item as {schema field | fulfilled request | status entry}; any exception is a G6 failure.\\r\\n\\r\\n### IF-3 — Gap Request Interface\\r\\n- Structured form: entity, attribute, timeframe, granularity, data class. Lifecycle: `requested → filled | unfilled(reason) | pending`.\\r\\n- Access policy: data class `market` → Persona D only; all other classes → any persona.\\r\\n- **Verify**: malformed requests return `unfilled(malformed_request)`; market-class request from a non-D persona returns `access_denied` and emits a `market_data_request_rate` event (expected: 0% non-D).\\r\\n\\r\\n### IF-4 — Terminal Artifact Interface\\r\\n- Nine sections per methodology Stage 6. Effective-N fields: `configured_n, ran_n, included_n, excluded_n, exclusions[{analyst, reason, layer, class, test_id, detail}]`. Integrity report houses contamination results, gate outcomes, anomalies, session-continuity verification.\\r\\n- **Canonical terminal: SAP-PreGame** (scheduled scope only). SAP-Morning retained for trajectory, non-terminal. Artifacts immutable after G6. **Artifact schema versioned independently of methodology version; downstream binds to artifact schema version.**\\r\\n- **Verify**: G6 structural validation; immutability enforced at store level.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §3 — Execution Contracts\\r\\n\\r\\n| ID | Contract | Verify |\\r\\n|---|---|---|\\r\\n| **EX-1** | Separate execution context per analyst (process/container): no shared memory, filesystem, network namespace, or env vars. Per-persona prompts; unique sampling parameters per analyst per run | Isolation check per run; canary uniqueness |\\r\\n| **EX-2** | Heterogeneity: ≥3 model families across 5 analysts; L2 validator family ≠ analyst family **per pair**; L3 outside the analyst pool; L3 fallback pre-approved, configured, and exercised before pilot | Provider registry check at orchestration; fallback test (§11) |\\r\\n| **EX-3** | Continuity: intra-run = same session (Stage 1→3, two provider requests, one session); inter-run = fresh context; session transcript sealed into provenance at run end | Session-continuity verification in integrity report |\\r\\n| **EX-4** | Concurrency: analysts sequential or parallel, no ordering-dependent state; run IDs globally unique | Orchestration test |\\r\\n| **EX-5** | Version pinning: model versions, prompts, parameters pinned per run, captured from execution metadata (I9) | Provenance audit |\\r\\n| **EX-6** | Contamination detection: canary tokens unique per analyst per run; output fingerprinting; post-hoc pairwise sampling; all results → integrity report | Canary cross-appearance scan; fingerprint pass |\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §4 — Data Contracts\\r\\n\\r\\n| ID | Contract |\\r\\n|---|---|\\r\\n| **DA-1** | Evidence store: append-only, write-once, SHA-256 content-addressed; items immutable |\\r\\n| **DA-2** | Evidence identity per IF-2 — distinct immutable items, never mutation |\\r\\n| **DA-3** | Provenance tags: acquisition timestamp, source, reliability tier, run type, expiration. Artifact-level chain: analyst → claim → evidence ID → source → acquisition timestamp |\\r\\n| **DA-4** | **Store-vs-delivery separation**: acquisition — including all overnight pre-fetch — populates the store. Nothing enters a package except through IF-2. The store was always shared; the package never was (CR-1) |\\r\\n| **DA-5** | Store backup: store snapshots + the §0 backup set are the whole-store failure recovery mechanism |\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §5 — Validation Stack Contracts\\r\\n\\r\\n| ID | Contract |\\r\\n|---|---|\\r\\n| **VL-1** | Layer 1 is deterministic code: traceability, statistical verification, temporal, logical, entity checks. Machine-checks the mechanical G4 classes (CH-1/2/4/5, CO-1/2/4) |\\r\\n| **VL-2** | **L1 semantic-classification router** *(spec completion under CR-4)*: L1 FAILs requiring semantic classification (CO-3/5, UC-1–4) route to the L2 validator assigned to that analyst. Classification events logged per-analysis |\\r\\n| **VL-3** | Layer 2: pairwise family-difference vs. the analyst it validates; checks factual accuracy and reasoning soundness; never receives the analyst's raw confidence expression |\\r\\n| **VL-4** | Layer 3: outside the analyst pool; receives the analysis plus L1/L2 reports; red-team stance; pre-approved fallback provider (EX-2) |\\r\\n| **VL-5** | G4 action table is deterministic per methodology §7.1. Class assignment is recorded per-analysis; **classification reliability is a measured quantity** (Luce audit surface) |\\r\\n| **VL-6** | Retry protocol: validation report sealed; corrections delivered only as replacement evidence items with new provenance; re-run of Stage 3 in the same session; full re-validation; second FAIL (any class) → exclusion |\\r\\n| **VL-7** | Forward-only (I3): no data path from validation outputs to analyst context exists in the topology |\\r\\n| **VL-8** | Accounting: `ran_n` counts analyst slots; retries increment the cost ledger, not `ran_n` |\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §6 — Normalization Contracts\\r\\n\\r\\n| ID | Contract |\\r\\n|---|---|\\r\\n| **NO-1** | Neutral model; inputs exactly {self-assessment, evidence sufficiency score, validation state, validation flags}; never receives reasoning, selection, or peer outputs |\\r\\n| **NO-2** | Stateless, per-analyst invocation. No cross-analyst context, no batching |\\r\\n| **NO-3** | Input set is a versioned contract; changes shift tier comparability downstream → version-gated |\\r\\n| **NO-4** | Non-collapsing: final tier + justification + all four input components preserved separately in the artifact |\\r\\n| **NO-5** | Sufficiency score: deterministic code (formula owned by methodology); never a model call; replay-consistent |\\r\\n| **NO-6** | `Contradicted` is system-assignable only — it depends on validation state analysts cannot see. Tier enum versioned independently |\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §7 — Failure Domains\\r\\n\\r\\n| Domain | Blast radius | Behavior |\\r\\n|---|---|---|\\r\\n| Single analyst execution failure | One slot | Re-run or exclude; artifact continues; effective-N records it |\\r\\n| Correctable validation failure | One slot | Retry once (VL-6); second FAIL → exclude |\\r\\n| Critical hallucination / uncorrectable | One slot | Immediate exclusion, per-exclusion reason recorded |\\r\\n| L2 execution failure | That analyst's entry | Blocks entry; retry; never skipped (I5) |\\r\\n| L3 primary outage | Whole slate (if unmitigated) | Pre-approved fallback activates; fallback outage → entries blocked, never bypassed |\\r\\n| Normalizer failure | Whole artifact | Blocks artifact; retry; never bypassed |\\r\\n| Acquisition / source outage | Requesting analysts | Partial-data mode; `unfilled(reason)`; severe gaps flagged |\\r\\n| Orchestrator failure mid-run | The run | **Checkpoint at each gate; resume from last persisted gate state** *(spec completion under the standing gates-as-checkpoints ruling)* |\\r\\n| Overnight failure | Overnight only | Cheap redo at Morning (data-only run; no analyst state lost) |\\r\\n| Whole-store failure | The system | Run aborts; recovery = DA-5 backup/restore; **no artifact is ever preferable to a wrong artifact** |\\r\\n| Full pipeline failure | The slate | Reject; alert operators; honest absence recorded |\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §8 — Security & Trust Boundaries\\r\\n\\r\\n- **SE-1** The acquisition engine is the trust boundary. All external data enters here; scraped/social/news sources are untrusted text.\\r\\n- **SE-2** Structured-first: canonical structured evidence format; free-text passthrough minimized to genuinely unstructured classes.\\r\\n- **SE-3** Untrusted text is marked and sanitized at the boundary — containment over prevention.\\r\\n- **SE-4** Blast radius: poisoned evidence reaches only requesting analysts (per-analyst delivery is containment by construction); market data further scoped to Persona D.\\r\\n- **SE-5** Secrets managed from the first API call; per-component credential isolation; no credentials in prompts, logs, or artifacts.\\r\\n- **SE-6** Injection defense-in-depth: evidence packaged as data, not instructions (IF-2 format discipline); provenance and reliability tiers; validation stack as backstop.\\r\\n- **SE-7** On-demand trust boundary: deferred; revival conditions in §12/CR-2.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §9 — Observability & Cost Instrumentation\\r\\n\\r\\n- **OB-1** Ledger unit: provider-billable request + token counts (re-analysis requests carry full first-pass context — call counts alone understate; the ledger carries both).\\r\\n- **OB-2** Granularity: per component, run, analyst slot, layer, source.\\r\\n- **OB-3** Metered at execution point inside the provider abstraction; **retrofitting is forbidden** — that is how 645-vs-795 happens.\\r\\n- **OB-4** Happy-path scheduled budget: **53/slate** (1 + 26 + 26), ~795/day at 15 slates. Retries excluded from budget, included in ledger. **Budget is reference; ledger is truth.**\\r\\n- **OB-5** Metric emit-points: contamination rate, hallucination by layer, gate outcomes, framing completeness per snapshot, market request rate by persona, effective-N vs. configured, classification reliability.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §10 — Build Plan\\r\\n\\r\\n| Phase | Scope | Exit criteria |\\r\\n|---|---|---|\\r\\n| **0 — Foundation** | Evidence store (DA-1..5), secrets (SE-5), data-layer schema | Store round-trips evidence with identity + provenance; secrets isolated |\\r\\n| **1 — Orchestration** | Provider abstraction with ledger hooks and observability emit-points, same layer | Mocked end-to-end call path meters correctly (OB-3) |\\r\\n| **2 — Isolation & wiring** | EX-1..6, IF-2 choke point, VL stack, NO stack, L3 fallback | All contract Verify lines pass in integration |\\r\\n| **3 — Pilot** | §11 | Pilot acceptance criteria |\\r\\n\\r\\nScalability and failure-domain *testing* at scale are post-pilot — with the §11 seeded failures as the mandatory exception.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §11 — Pilot Design\\r\\n\\r\\n**Scope**: one MLB slate; scheduled cadence only (Overnight → Morning → Pre-Game); N=5; full validation; full measurement.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Seeded failure tests — mandatory, one per class:**\\r\\n(a) G4 correctable retry (VL-6 full protocol); (b) L3 primary→fallback switchover; (c) one source outage in partial-data mode; (d) one analyst exclusion, visible in effective-N.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Acceptance criteria — architectural, not signal:**\\r\\n1. Terminal artifact complete, nine sections, provenance chain **reconciles against provider invoices**.\\r\\n2. Every gate fired deterministically; outcomes in the integrity report.\\r\\n3. All four seeded failures behaved per the §7 table.\\r\\n4. Isolation verified: canaries unique per analyst per run; package audit clean (IF-2).\\r\\n5. Ledger measured vs. budget: variance reported with component breakdown.\\r\\n\\r\\n**The pilot is not**: a signal-quality test, a calibration test, or a scale test. Metrics accumulate from run one; conclusions come later, through Luce and methodology §9.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §12 — Gate Register\\r\\n\\r\\n| ID | Ruling | Provenance |\\r\\n|---|---|---|\\r\\n| **CR-1** | Evidence delivery is request-gated; pre-fetch populates the store only; package invariant per I1 | Chiave gate ruling, v0.3.1 |\\r\\n| **CR-2** | On-demand removed from pilot scope | Chiave recommendation → **Don scope ruling**. **Revival conditions preserved here**: G0 window bound (pre-first-pitch only); single canonical terminal per slate (most-recently-completed terminal, pointer semantics, all artifacts immutable); failure-domain independence from scheduled runs; trust boundary with authn/authz + quota enforcement + requester attribution in provenance; **plus two Don policy lines — who may trigger, and quota — required before build** |\\r\\n| **CR-3** | Cost ledger unit = provider-billable request + tokens; true figures 26/run, 53/slate, ~795/day | Chiave gate ruling, v0.3.1 |\\r\\n| **CR-4** | G4 deterministic; Kimi's §7.1 protocol accepted with recorded conditions (VL-2, VL-5, VL-8) | Chiave gate ruling + Kimi methodology decision |\\r\\n| **CR-5** | Framing schema 0.3-MLB approved; field content owned by methodology | Chiave gate ruling, v0.3.1 |\\r\\n\\r\\n**Gate reopen triggers**: framing schema major revision · artifact schema change · on-demand surface build · pilot contract violation · new cross-system dependency · store architecture change.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §13 — Ownership Boundary Map\\r\\n\\r\\n| Seat | Owns |\\r\\n|---|---|\\r\\n| **Don** | Strategy, scope, policy lines (on-demand trigger/quota when revived), thresholds, cost ceiling posture |\\r\\n| **Kimi** | Methodology, prompts, personas, G4 class semantics, tolerance refinements, sufficiency formula |\\r\\n| **Chiave** | This document: structure, interfaces, failure domains, instrumentation design, invariants |\\r\\n| **Talon** | Scheduling, monitoring cadence and response, source maintenance, L3 fallback coordination, cost reporting |\\r\\n| **Luce** | Verification: layer effectiveness, classification reliability, contamination-audit accuracy, calibration audit, post-pilot go/no-go |\\r\\n| **Governance** | Data usage policy, ToS compliance, regulatory |\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## §14 — Traceability & Pending\\r\\n\\r\\n**Rulings → contracts**: CR-1 → IF-2/DA-4 · CR-2 → §12/SE-7 · CR-3 → OB-1..4 · CR-4 → VL-1..8 · CR-5 → IF-1.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Pending on methodology v0.3.2 (Kimi's six fixes)**: brief regeneration as a derived artifact · `OnDemand` enum removal · Stage 6 terminal line · ruling numbering + CR-2 content preservation · attribution of the on-demand removal · H1 version. **This document preserves CR-2's content independently, so the backup set is safe regardless of v0.3.2 timing.**\\r\\n\\r\\n**Spec completions issued under standing authority** (flagged, not new rulings): VL-2 (L1 router) · §7 checkpoint/resume semantics.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n**Boundary check**: I consolidated the architecture layer into its durable document — no new rulings beyond two flagged completions of standing ones. The backup set is defined and version-lockable. Still owed by others: Kimi's six record fixes (this document makes the backup safe without them, but the Coder handoff still needs the regenerated brief). My next move is Phase 0 design against §10. Save this as `EC8_Architecture_v1.0.md` alongside the methodology — the manifest binds them.\"},{\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NDhIIIK1xL6YaLEjs4lgF0eP9fdjpJwMl2bvWTw2ko4/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"title\":\"GCE_SESSION2_CLOSE_CANONICAL_ORG_2026-09-02\",\"id\":\"1NDhIIIK1xL6YaLEjs4lgF0eP9fdjpJwMl2bvWTw2ko4\",\"mime_type\":\"application/vnd.google-apps.document\",\"size\":\"12270\",\"file_or_folder\":\"file\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-02T23:59:48.400Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-08T15:30:12.562Z\",\"viewedByMeTime\":\"2026-09-08T15:30:12.562Z\",\"display_title\":\"GCE_SESSION2_CLOSE_CANONICAL_ORG_2026-09-02\",\"display_url\":\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NDhIIIK1xL6YaLEjs4lgF0eP9fdjpJwMl2bvWTw2ko4/edit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1clV7UUxQUcnGLX21ossOWoHGBPs-pM77\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿GCE SESSION 2 CLOSE — CANONICAL ORGANIZATIONAL MODEL\\r\\nDate: 2026-09-02\\r\\nAuthority: Don + Coda\\r\\nStatus: CANONICAL / SESSION CLOSE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPURPOSE\\r\\nPersist the refined organizational source of truth reached at Session 2 close and supersede the earlier interpretation of seven equal Councils.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCANONICAL ORGANIZATIONAL MODEL\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDON\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEXECUTIVE COUNCIL — 4 seats with Don's ear\\r\\n1. Coda — Strategic / Governance\\r\\n2. Kimi — Technical Strategy / Systems Intelligence\\r\\n3. Talon — Operations\\r\\n4. Chiave — Architecture\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThese four are the executive/advisory authority seats. They interpret, challenge, recommend, and route material decisions to Don.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nExecutive hierarchy:\\r\\nDon -> Executive Council seat / Lieutenant -> optional Manager / Capo only where workload creates a distinct management responsibility -> Contract Workers / Soldiers / Specialists.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nManagers are not manufactured for symmetry.\\r\\n- Operations currently justifies Talon -> Keel -> bounded contract workers.\\r\\n- Architecture Manager remains vacant unless workload proves the need.\\r\\n- Strategic/Governance and Technical Strategy do not require permanent Managers merely to satisfy a template.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSHARED ENTERPRISE SERVICES — 3\\r\\n1. Data / Intelligence\\r\\n2. Verification / Ground Truth — Big Pickle\\r\\n3. QA / Validation\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nShared Services are enterprise-wide neutral functions. They do not have Don's standing ear and are not peer Executive Council seats.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nShared Service structure:\\r\\nService Lead / Director-Manager -> bounded Contract Workers / Specialists as needed.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nShared Service rules:\\r\\n- one accountable permanent lead seat\\r\\n- no separate permanent Manager layer unless explicitly redesigned later\\r\\n- identity + narrow functional lens + explicit authority + contracts + provenance/evidence rules + stop/escalation conditions\\r\\n- minimal or no personality by default\\r\\n- personality must never bias data, verification, falsification, or QA outcomes\\r\\n- workers are added only when workload requires them\\r\\n- Shared Services serve all four Executive Council seats and approved projects/workflows\\r\\n- the requesting seat cannot dictate the service result\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVERIFICATION / GROUND TRUTH\\r\\nBig Pickle is a locked identity in the Verification / Ground Truth Shared Service.\\r\\nNarrow lens: evidence -> provenance -> falsification -> verified state.\\r\\nNo rich personality layer is required.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDATA / INTELLIGENCE\\r\\nData Hound is a locked bounded identity used for data/intelligence work. Project assignment does not imply enterprise leadership or redefine organizational reporting.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nLAYER DISTINCTIONS\\r\\nExecutive Council != Shared Enterprise Services != Methodologies != Projects.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMethodologies:\\r\\n- EC_QUANT\\r\\n- EC_CONVERGENCE\\r\\nThese are reusable methods, not departments.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nProjects:\\r\\n- Edge Crew and other project environments\\r\\nProjects consume Executive Council authority, Shared Services, methodologies, managers, and contract workers as needed. Edge Crew is not a Council.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPHYSICAL FILESYSTEM STATE\\r\\nAt Session 2 close, Talon verified seven domain folders existed under GCE_ORG\\\\02_COUNCILS with the standard internal template:\\r\\n- Strategic_Governance\\r\\n- Technical_Strategy_Systems_Intelligence\\r\\n- Operations\\r\\n- Architecture\\r\\n- Data_Intelligence\\r\\n- Verification_Ground_Truth\\r\\n- QA_Validation\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe earlier R34-DIS Architecture-lanes discrepancy was resolved as an incomplete-read false alarm. All seven domain folders exist.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSEMANTIC REFINEMENT\\r\\nThose seven domains are no longer interpreted as seven equal Councils. The current semantic source of truth is:\\r\\n4 Executive Council domains + 3 Shared Enterprise Services.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPhysical placement should be reconciled through the least-destructive approved change. Preserve provenance and historical references.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nIDENTITY / BOOTSTRAP STATE\\r\\n- Coda: locked Strategic / Governance identity; computer/API bootstrap still needs forensic review before local onboarding.\\r\\n- Kimi: locked Technical Strategy / Systems Intelligence seat/function; methodology and technical classification authority.\\r\\n- Talon: locked Operations identity; DeepSeek V4 Flash runtime; operational load root exists.\\r\\n- Keel: locked Operations Manager identity; separate load root exists; fresh isolation rerun remains unproven.\\r\\n- Chiave: locked Architecture identity; GLM 5.1 onboarding runtime of record; Stage 6 qualification administration pending; Stage 7 materialization not authorized.\\r\\n- Big Pickle: locked Verification / Ground Truth Shared Service identity; minimal/no personality by design.\\r\\n- Data Hound: locked bounded data/intelligence identity.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCHIAVE O1 STATE\\r\\nStage 1 COMPLETE\\r\\nStage 2 COMPLETE\\r\\nStage 3 COMPLETE\\r\\nStage 4 COMPLETE / PASS\\r\\nStage 5 COMPLETE / PASS WITH AMENDMENTS\\r\\nStage 6 DESIGN APPROVED / ADMINISTRATION PENDING — NOT STARTED\\r\\nStage 7 CLOSED / NOT AUTHORIZED\\r\\nChiave / GLM is on HOLD.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOPERATIONS CLOSE\\r\\nTalon final reconciliation completed.\\r\\nR34-DIS resolved as false alarm.\\r\\nO-OPS-4 Keel isolation rerun remains OPEN / NOT PROVEN.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSOURCE-OF-TRUTH RULE\\r\\nThis document is the Session 2 organizational close anchor. Where earlier Session 2 framework documents describe seven equal Councils, this document supersedes that interpretation while preserving the earlier material as provenance.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCORE PRINCIPLES PRESERVED\\r\\nIDENTITY != ROLE != LENS != PERSONALITY != AUTHORITY != MODEL.\\r\\nCapability != authority.\\r\\nContext breadth != authority breadth.\\r\\nOne owner per responsibility.\\r\\nOne context per role.\\r\\nMethodology remains separate from sessions and projects.\\r\\nEvidence before destructive change.\\r\\nExplicit handoffs and stop conditions.\\r\\nPersonality/lens never expand authority.\\r\\nRuntime is replaceable; stable seat survives.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS: HOLD\\r\\nCONFIDENCE: 100%\\r\\nREASON: Session 2 organizational model is now defined as 4 Executive Council seats plus 3 Shared Enterprise Services, with remaining validation gates explicitly open rather than implied complete.\\r\\nNEXT GATE: Resume from this anchor; do not reconstruct the organization from prior chat chronology.\\r\\nDON INPUT NEEDED: NONE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSUPERSEDING ORGANIZATIONAL BOARD UPDATE — 2026-09-06\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPRINCIPAL CONSULTANT — APPROVED VACANT SEAT\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe 4 Executive Council + 3 Shared Enterprise Services model remains intact. This update adds one cross-functional solution-definition / delivery-interface seat; it does not create a fifth Executive Council seat or fourth Shared Enterprise Service.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent delivery chain for complex builds:\\r\\nDon / Stakeholder\\r\\n-> relevant Executive Council outputs (Kimi methodology; Chiave architecture; Coda governance as required)\\r\\n-> Principal Consultant\\r\\n-> Talon / Operations\\r\\n-> Keel / build-deploy-test-evidence-return resources\\r\\n-> Luce / Verification-Ground Truth adjudication\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPrincipal Consultant owns one integrated middle-layer function with two internal capabilities:\\r\\n1. Specification / Solution Definition\\r\\n2. Translation / Alignment\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nRole purpose: turn frozen upstream intent/methodology/architecture/governance into an implementation-ready specification and translation pack without contaminating or silently rewriting upstream authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOwned output: IMPLEMENTATION SPEC + TRANSLATION PACK.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAuthority boundary: may clarify requirements, expose gaps, define interfaces/schemas/outputs/acceptance criteria, recommend model/function assignments, and translate approved specification into bounded work packages/prompts. May not redefine methodology, architecture, governance, scope, Verification truth state, or execute builds/deployments.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSeat state: APPROVED VACANT / ONBOARDING-READY. Model/runtime/name/animal/personality remain TBD pending controlled audition and standard onboarding gates.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSource-of-truth rule: where the earlier organizational flow jumps directly from Council outputs to Operations for complex solution work, this 2026-09-06 update inserts Principal Consultant as the implementation-readiness interface. Operations authority and the 4+3 organizational model otherwise remain unchanged.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSUPERSEDING ORGANIZATIONAL HARDENING UPDATE — 2026-09-06\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAUTHORITY: Don + Coda\\r\\nSTATUS: CURRENT WORKING CANON — supersedes earlier 4 Executive Council + 3 Shared Enterprise Services interpretation where inconsistent. Historical text remains provenance.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCORE DOCTRINE\\r\\nIDENTITY != ROLE != LENS != PERSONALITY != AUTHORITY != MODEL\\r\\nMODEL != SEAT\\r\\nCLASS != OPERATIONAL ROUTING AUTHORITY\\r\\nOne owner per responsibility. Capability and personality do not expand authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nEXECUTIVE COUNCIL — 4\\r\\n1. Coda — Strategic Governance. Current occupant/runtime: ChatGPT 5.6 Sol. Made-person: Coda. Animal: Volpe / Fox. Mafia rank: Consigliere.\\r\\n2. Kimi — Technical Stack Methodology. Current occupant/runtime: Kimi / Moonshot. Seat/function is locked. Made-person name and animal are intentionally NOT assigned yet; do not manufacture them.\\r\\n3. Chiave — Architecture. Current occupant/runtime: GLM / Z.AI. Current working model: GLM 5.3. Made-person: Chiave. Animal: Aquila / Eagle. Mafia rank: Counsel / Lieutenant. Deep/formal architecture remains Chiave.\\r\\n4. Talon — Operations. Current occupant/runtime: DeepSeek. Made-person: Talon. Animal: Tasso / Badger. Mafia rank: Counsel-Lieutenant / Head of Operations. Talon owns routing, sequencing, operational control, work assignment, and bounded low-level implementation directing; Talon does not absorb Chiave architecture.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCoda governs framework integrity across the entire stack and is not another delivery-chain step.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDELIVERY CHAIN — CURRENT\\r\\nDon / stakeholder intent\\r\\n-> Kimi methodology\\r\\n-> Chiave architecture\\r\\n-> Principal Consultant\\r\\n-> Calibro / Implementation Design & Engineer\\r\\n-> Talon / Operations\\r\\n-> Keel / Build-Deploy-Test-Evidence Return\\r\\n-> Coder / implementation workers / contract specialists\\r\\n-> Luce / Verification-Ground Truth\\r\\n-> QA / Validation\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPRINCIPAL CONSULTANT\\r\\nCurrent occupant: ChatGPT 5.6 Luna.\\r\\nState: functionally slotted for routine use; NOT currently being onboarded as a made-person.\\r\\nPurpose: reconciliation, specification, translation, implementation-readiness, blocker/gap exposure, acceptance conditions, and traceable handoff.\\r\\nOwned output remains implementation-ready specification / translation package.\\r\\nAuthority does not include methodology re-authoring, architecture redefinition, governance expansion, build execution, or Verification adjudication.\\r\\nCurrent hardening objective: improve the reusable Principal Consultant prompt for lower verbosity, stronger claim discipline, mechanical blocker routing, and Talon/Keel-ready outputs without invention.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCALIBRO\\r\\nMade-person: Calibro.\\r\\nAnimal: Picchio / Woodpecker.\\r\\nSeat: Implementation Design & Engineer.\\r\\nClass / mafia rank: Capo.\\r\\nCurrent occupant/model: Grok 4.6; occupant is not the seat.\\r\\nPurpose: take accepted methodology + architecture + Principal Consultant package and decide the bounded implementation design: runtime/provider/model assignment, family assignment, gateway/API choice, configuration/parameters, retry/timeout/fallback strategy, cost-quality-reliability tradeoffs, implementation manifests, and implementation-level sequencing.\\r\\nBoundary: Calibro does not rewrite Kimi methodology, amend Chiave architecture, override Coda governance, route Operations as Talon, execute as Keel/Coder, or verify as Luce.\\r\\nOperating identity: exact pins, evidence over brochure, slot-local change over system redesign, reversible PROPOSED choices when evidence is incomplete, and no silent CONFLICT repair.\\r\\nBootstrap state: identity locked; bootstrap substance authored by Calibro; materialization/fresh-session testing is the current gate.\\r\\nRouter doctrine: explicit active seat binding controls. Do not encode model-family = seat. Unknown/ambiguous mapping must STOP / ASK; never default to Luce and never assume every Grok runtime is Calibro.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOPERATIONS EXECUTION FAMILY\\r\\nTalon — Head of Operations / Counsel-Lieutenant.\\r\\nKeel — Operations Manager / Capo; build, deploy, test, evidence return. Keel authority does not include methodology or architecture redesign. Live execution vetting remains a current proof gate.\\r\\nCoder / Implementation Engineer — OPEN permanent seat; actual code production within approved package.\\r\\nBounded contract workers / specialists may execute under approved Operations routing.\\r\\nOperations soldiers remain bounded identities/functions including Falcon Data Hound, Pigeon Transport, Magpie Secretary/Register, and Raven Documentation.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nVERIFICATION AND QA\\r\\nLuce — made-person Verification / Ground Truth lead; current runtime Big Pickle; animal Lince / Lynx. Luce independently determines supportable truth from evidence and does not build or rewrite upstream design.\\r\\nQA / Validation is a VACANT downstream assurance function positioned AFTER delivery and Verification. It is no longer modeled as a peer Shared Enterprise Service in the current flow.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDATA / INTELLIGENCE RETIREMENT\\r\\nData / Intelligence is RETIRED as a standalone enterprise service. Its useful capabilities may be reallocated later to concrete seats/services when functionally justified.\\r\\nFalcon / Data Hound remains a bounded Operations soldier/function; this does not recreate an enterprise Data / Intelligence 