gy -> Coda governance as needed -> Chiave architecture -> Luce pre-PC certification -> Ragno packaging -> Calibro implementation design -> Talon routing -> Keel build/deploy/test/evidence -> Luce execution verification -> QA when staffed.\\r\\n- Coda governs framework integrity across the stack rather than acting as a sequential delivery hop.\\r\\n- Ragno/Principal Consultant is now actively demonstrated as a seat occupied by K3/Kimi Swarm for scraper packaging; MODEL != SEAT was preserved.\\r\\n- Calibro identity is locked as Implementation Design & Engineer / Picchio-Woodpecker / Capo; Grok 4.6 current occupant.\\r\\n- Talon remains Operations owner; Keel owns build/deploy/test/evidence return; Luce independently verifies and does not repair or redesign.\\r\\n- Falcon/Data Hound remains a bounded Operations soldier used for evidence hunts and reconciliation, not a restored enterprise Data/Intelligence service.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHANDOFF / MATERIALIZATION DOCTRINE — CONFIRMED\\r\\n- Singular live handoff bus is Operations\\\\06_HANDOFFS\\\\<RECEIVING_SEAT>\\\\.\\r\\n- Legacy GCE_DON\\\\03_HANDOFFS is frozen for new writes; no bulk migration.\\r\\n- Complete downstream handoff artifact must be materialized; terminal/session output alone is not a handoff.\\r\\n- Artifact ownership != transport routing: authoritative artifact stays with owner; transport copy goes to receiving seat lane.\\r\\n- New operational lesson confirmed overnight: DELIVERED != DISCOVERED != VERIFIED. Consumer-side reconciliation/adjudication state is required; a file existing in a receiving lane does not prove the receiving seat has consumed it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKIMI LOAD-SURFACE CLEANUP — CLOSED\\r\\n- Luce audit identified dead/contaminated Kimi load-surface residue including Notion MCP residue, stale plugin duplicates, secret-bearing backups, orphan kimi-chat-cleanup, fabricated SWARM/AgentSwarm behavior mappings, and emoji transcript contamination.\\r\\n- Don approved bounded D1-D4 cleanup; Ke