it that ledger and continue forward without reconstructing the prior week.\n\n---\n\n[L61] # 3. ACCOMPLISHMENTS BY DATE\n\n[L63] ## DATE: September 16, 2026\n\n[L65] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:**  \n[L66] Confirmed that the prior Luxor **$50 authorization released overnight** after a clean, zero-balance checkout/folio.\n\n[L68] **DECISION / RESULT:**  \n[L69] Clean-folio release behavior became a supported planning observation, while older/adjusted holds remained subject to conservative timing.\n\n[L71] **WHO / WHICH SEAT OWNED IT:**  \n[L72] Don observed and supplied bank evidence; Coda reconciled the operating implication.\n\n[L74] **STATUS:** verified\n\n---\n\n[L78] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:**  \n[L79] Confirmed that the old Excalibur **$55.55 authorization remained pending** despite the Luxor release.\n\n[L81] **DECISION / RESULT:**  \n[L82] The $55.55 was separated from normal hold-recycling assumptions and treated as a problem case rather than expected liquidity.\n\n[L84] **WHO / WHICH SEAT OWNED IT:**  \n[L85] Don / Coda\n\n[L87] **STATUS:** accepted\n\n---\n\n[L91] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:**  \n[L92] Don obtained Excalibur paperwork showing a closed **$0.00 folio** and authorization history connected to the unresolved hold.\n\n[L94] **DECISION / RESULT:**  \n[L95] If the $55.55 did not clear, the next step was in-person escalation using the paperwork rather than continued passive waiting.\n\n[L97] **WHO / WHICH SEAT OWNED IT:**  \nDon\n\n[L100] **STATUS:** implemented\n\n---\n\n[L104] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:**  \n[L105] The hotel bridge was restructured so the Luxor stay began **Friday, September 18**, for three nights in the **Silver Tower**.\n\n[L107] **DECISION / RESULT:**  \n[L108] Friday funding was modeled around approximately:\n\n[L110] - ~$32 projected hard cash after Thursday check-in mechanics;\n[L111] - ~$160 NY-NY expected release;\n[L112] - ~$22 Amazon expected refund;\n[L113] - total approximately **$214**;\n[L114] - grounded Luxor planning autho