superseded structures, historical backups, frozen artifacts, legacy estates\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNEW 2026-09-21 TECHNICAL STRATEGY LANES\\r\\n01_Model_Labor_Intelligence\\r\\n- cross-project evidence about model task-fit and failure signatures\\r\\n- not permanent seat assignment by itself\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n02_Runtime_Provider_Intelligence\\r\\n- route, host, provider, latency, state-continuity, and operational reliability evidence\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n03_Proving_Grounds\\r\\n- bounded experiments such as Black Pearl\\r\\n- evidence only; no automatic authority promotion\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n04_Cross_Project_Methodology_Research\\r\\n- reusable methodology candidates extracted from projects / experiments\\r\\n- must be reconciled before becoming framework standard\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPROJECT BOUNDARY\\r\\nThis framework lane does not modify Projects.\\r\\nProject-specific artifacts remain owned by their project even when the framework learns from them.\\r\\nIf a project lesson generalizes, create/reconcile the generalized framework artifact outside Projects; do not rewrite project history.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPROMOTION PATH\\r\\nProject / POC / chat evidence\\r\\n-> Technical Strategy / Proving Ground\\r\\n-> cross-project reconciliation\\r\\n-> Strategic Governance review\\r\\n-> Framework Standard / Canon when approved\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDO NOT\\r\\n- create model-named top-level organizational folders\\r\\n- create a GCE project merely because a framework experiment used project data\\r\\n- move or rewrite project artifacts from framework reconciliation\\r\\n- treat research evidence as canon\\r\\n- duplicate current authoritative documents\\r\\n- silently supersede historical artifacts\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS: PROCEED\\r\\nCONFIDENCE: 99%\\r\\nNEXT GATE: maintain framework artifacts outside Projects; reconcile project handoffs into generalized standards only when needed.\"}]},\"error\":null,\"error_data\":null,\"error_code\":null,\"classification_id\":null,\"json_rpc_error_code\":nu