51\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿GCE MODEL LABOR INTELLIGENCE — CURRENT\\r\\nDate: 2026-09-21\\r\\nOwner: Technical Strategy / Systems Intelligence\\r\\nStatus: RESEARCH CURRENT — not seat canon by itself\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPURPOSE\\r\\nPreserve cross-project evidence about model task-fit, failure signatures, and useful cognitive labor patterns without turning any one project result into organizational authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCORE RULES\\r\\n- MODEL != SEAT.\\r\\n- A model name does not grant authority.\\r\\n- Different providers do not guarantee independent reasoning.\\r\\n- Task-fit must be demonstrated against bounded work.\\r\\n- Model labor evidence is advisory until promoted through GCE governance.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nBLACK PEARL / TRIAL 01 OBSERVED LABOR MAP\\r\\n- GPT-5.6 Sol: bounded senior analyst / disciplined first read.\\r\\n- Nex N2.5 Pro: grounded skeptic; price-vs-evidence tension.\\r\\n- Muse Spark 1.3: pattern analyst.\\r\\n- Dots3 Note Preview: anomaly hunter; aggressive, requires audit.\\r\\n- Grok 4.6: cross-examiner / contradiction auditor; best when narrowly boxed.\\r\\n- Kimi K3 High: methodology challenger; attacks hidden assumptions and reasoning machinery.\\r\\n- Big Pickle: verifier / truth-teller; evidence bookkeeping, arithmetic, unknowns.\\r\\n- GLM 5.1 / 5.3-class: architecture / integration / normalization, with stage discipline required.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNEGATIVE / NARROW-FIT LESSONS\\r\\nSeveral models were useful only in narrow lanes or showed contamination, gap filling, math errors, generic reasoning, or route problems. Do not promote a model because it is generally strong; evaluate the specific job.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFRAMEWORK IMPLICATION\\r\\nSeat assignment should be based on demonstrated task-fit, authority boundaries, and known failure signature. Occupants remain replaceable. Research evidence should be periodically re-tested because model versions change.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPROMOTION PATH\\r\\nProving Ground evidence -> Model Labor Intelligence -> cross-project reconciliation -> Strategic Governance -> seat/standard change only if explicitly approved.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPROJECT BOUNDARY\\r\\nProject-specific rosters, prompts, scores, or betting logic remain project-owned and are not canonized here.\"}]},\"error\":null,\"error_data\":null,\"error_code\":null,\"classification_id\":null,\"json_rpc_error_code\":null,\"error_http_status_code\":null,\"error_http_headers\":null,\"internal\":{\"external_call_time_ms\":1371},\"clamp_errors\":null,\"clamp_rewrites\":null,\"connector_id\":\"connector_5f3c8c41a1e54ad7a76272c89e2554fa\",\"connector_name\":\"Google Drive\",\"action_name\":\"search\",\"is_sync\":false}"}, "create_time": 1790199310.421975, "end_turn": null, "id": "fa16352c-7c47-4fd9-b505-0d70c9e94b6e", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "chime_version": 1, "classifier_response": "default", "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab43fca21d0819183966405a724bf5d", "invoked_plugin": {}, "invoked_resource": {"api_tool_version": "v2", "app_name": "Google Drive", "contains_mcp_source": false, "description": "Search Google Drive and return file or folder metadata. Calls without `item_type` and `page_token` retain the legacy search and optional best-effort text hydration. An explicit `image`, `document`, or `folder` item type searches exactly one metadata-only provider page; it never fetches file contents, even with `best_effort_fetch=True`. Return the opaque, provider-owned `next_page_token` unchanged as the next request's `page_token`, including when a page has no allowed results. Use short, specific keywords, or omit the query to browse accessible files. Broaden an empty-result search with related terms, abbreviations, or synonyms. `special_filter_query_str` is a raw Google Drive v3 `q` filter for MIME type, modification time, ownership, sharing, or folder selection. Set `require_viewed_by_user=True` to restrict results to viewed files. Search covers a