dit?usp=drivesdk\",\"parent_ids\":[\"1HWN3CKJrtZExf9IcCmlKakv_HcDFtFqn\"],\"shared\":false,\"content\":\"﻿PERSONAL TECH / OPERATIONS HANDOFF\\r\\nDate: 2026-09-21\\r\\nOwner: Don\\r\\nScope: personal technology, phone/carrier, workstation, voice, network, and small operational loose ends\\r\\nStatus: CURRENT HANDOFF / RECON BASELINE\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPURPOSE\\r\\nSeparate personal-tech and household/consumer-operations work from GCE framework, Edge Crew projects, job-search work, travel/relocation planning, and health.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThis is a personal operations handoff, not a GCE project artifact.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n1. PHONE / CARRIER — SPECTRUM EXIT\\r\\nCurrent known state:\\r\\n- Don has two Spectrum mobile lines but only one active/needed line should remain.\\r\\n- Goal: leave Spectrum and eliminate the unused second line before another large monthly bill.\\r\\n- Target ongoing U.S. mobile cost is roughly $40/month if practical.\\r\\n- Heavy/usable hotspot capability matters.\\r\\n- Current Spectrum-financed iPhone balance was recently around $458; earlier shorthand was roughly $400.\\r\\n- Don prefers Android over the current iPhone and is particularly interested in OnePlus.\\r\\n- Do not buy a OnePlus until exact T-Mobile compatibility / IMEI and promotion path are confirmed.\\r\\n- Don is new to T-Mobile; wife's prior T-Mobile history should not be treated as Don's account history.\\r\\n- Don prefers a T-Mobile store to quarterback the carrier switch rather than engineering the whole transition alone.\\r\\n- Primary constraint: avoid an unnecessary large upfront Spectrum-device payoff if a legitimate reimbursement / carrier-switch path applies.\\r\\n- T-Mobile cannot unlock a Spectrum-financed phone itself; the exact switch mechanism must match the device/account state.\\r\\n- Prior research discussed Keep & Switch vs Carrier Freedom. Treat program eligibility, accepted carriers, balance reimbursement, unlock requirements, and current terms as items to verify at the time of execution rather than permanent facts.\\r\\n- For Mexico, Don intends to use separate local-data service while retaining a low-cost U.S. number/line. Telcel Amigo and AT&T México were prior candidates; this is a future execution decision, not a locked carrier choice.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNEXT PHONE/CARRIER RECON\\r\\nBefore acting:\\r\\n1. confirm current Spectrum lines and exact device balance;\\r\\n2. identify which line/number is being preserved;\\r\\n3. confirm current phone lock/unlock state;\\r\\n4. confirm current T-Mobile switch program that applies to Spectrum and the financed device;\\r\\n5. confirm OnePlus device/IMEI compatibility and any promotion path;\\r\\n6. establish total day-one cash requirement before porting;\\r\\n7. close the unused Spectrum line only when number/device dependencies are clear.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n2. IPHONE USABILITY\\r\\nKnown issue:\\r\\n- Don is frustrated that text selection inside the iPhone ChatGPT app does not reliably expose a simple Select All / Copy workflow.\\r\\n- Don specifically asked whether this could be fixed through preferences/settings.\\r\\n- Treat this as a UI/usability issue, not a GCE framework issue.\\r\\n- If revisited, check current iOS / ChatGPT app behavior before giving steps because the UI changes frequently.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n3. PHONE COMMAND CENTER / PERSONAL EXECUTOR\\r\\nActive design concept:\\r\\nVOICE -> UNDERSTAND -> ROUTE -> EXECUTE -> CONFIRM\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nTarget use cases include:\\r\\n- reminders\\r\\n- notes\\r\\n- tasks\\r\\n- calendar changes\\r\\n- capture\\r\\n- travel/family scheduling\\r\\n- interview/work blocks\\r\\n- recurring routines\\r\\n- multi-step replanning\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nArchitecture boundary:\\r\\n- LLM interprets intent.\\r\\n- Deterministic execution layer performs mutations/actions.\\r\\n- The assistant should not equate language-model interpretation with execution authority.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrent design questions:\\r\\n- iOS vs Android capabilities\\r\\n- app intents / shortcuts\\r\\n- background execution\\r\\n- widgets / notifications\\r\\n- messaging restrictions\\r\\n- calendar / contacts\\r\\n- file / Drive operations\\r\\n- voice activation and confirmation\\r\\n- which actions can happen on-device vs require a desktop/gateway\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n4. PROTON-FIRST PERSONAL DATA MODEL\\r\\nWorking concept:\\r\\n- Proton = vault / personal truth\\r\\n- Phone assistant = command surface\\r\\n- Execution gateway = controlled writer\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNeed to prove:\\r\\n- what Proton / Proton Bridge actually expose;\\r\\n- what requires desktop presence;\\r\\n- what can run directly from mobile;\\r\\n- what needs an intermediary or execution gateway.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDo not code the final personal executor until those constraints are truth-tested.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n5. VOICEBRIDGE / VOICE OPERATIONS\\r\\nPersonal-use thread:\\r\\n- VoiceBridge moved from Whisper -> Deepgram -> AssemblyAI during experimentation.\\r\\n- Intended capabilities included automatic proofreading, intent audit, terminal jump, and future voice profile / audio ducking.\\r\\n- VoiceBridge is also present in GCE engineering context, so avoid duplicating framework/project ownership.\\r\\n- Personal handoff should track the user-experience requirement; implementation ownership can remain in the appropriate technical lane.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCore personal objective:\\r\\nDon should be able to speak naturally, preserve intent, and move work across phone/desktop without manually rebuilding context or fighting UI friction.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n6. RAZER BLADE 15 / WI-FI / BLUETOOTH\\r\\nMachine:\\r\\n- Razer Blade 15 Base 2019\\r\\n- model/board: RZ09-03006E92\\r\\n- i7-9750H / RTX 2060 / HM370\\r\\n- factory wireless: Intel Wireless-AC 9560, CNVio gen-1\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nKnown physical/network issues:\\r\\n- antenna wire damage existed;\\r\\n- webcam cable was replaced;\\r\\n- RJ45 port is broken;\\r\\n- battery was previously replaced;\\r\\n- Bluetooth headset reliability has been poor;\\r\\n- hotspot became the primary network path while the internal Wi-Fi situation was unresolved.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nReplacement attempt:\\r\\n- AX210 laptop kit was purchased.\\r\\n- Card physically fit the socket.\\r\\n- Main difficulty was seating the tiny u.FL/IPEX antenna leads safely.\\r\\n- Don paused rather than damage the connectors.\\r\\n- Practical plan was to have a local technician seat the antenna leads for roughly $10-$20 if possible.\\r\\n- External USB Wi-Fi remained a fallback.\\r\\n- Direct slot-routing compatibility was treated with caveats because the original AC-9560 is CNVio while AX210 uses PCIe/USB.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDo not assume the internal-card repair is complete until current machine state is rechecked.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n7. WINDOWS / WORKSTATION CLEANUP\\r\\nKnown completed/important work:\\r\\n- redirected Windows shell folders were repaired back toward standard profile locations;\\r\\n- collisions were staged rather than blindly overwritten;\\r\\n- OneDrive paths were intentionally not adopted as the long-term operating model;\\r\\n- user prefers Proton Drive for backup/sync strategy;\\r\\n- Kimi/GLM banners and older Claude/Notion-MCP remnants were cleaned up;\\r\\n- dead scheduled tasks were removed;\\r\\n- Intel telemetry was disabled;\\r\\n- Windows Widgets respawn remained an annoyance at last known state.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nOperational preference:\\r\\nClean up first, then use the computer normally. Fix real regressions surgically as they appear instead of pre-hardening every theoretical failure.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n8. NETWORK / SPECTRUM / GAMING LESSON\\r\\nImportant historical correction:\\r\\n- The Mortal Kombat problem was Spectrum/network packet loss, not a thermal/FPS problem.\\r\\n- For gaming/network diagnosis, prioritize packet loss, jitter, and latency consistency before chasing maximum FPS or thermals.\\r\\n- Do not conflate CPU spikes observed from boot with OpenCode activity unless evidence supports it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nHistorical networking lesson from an earlier setup:\\r\\n- a wired Mac-to-gateway test was stable at 0% packet loss and roughly 1.3 ms local average latency;\\r\\n- Wi-Fi placement / walls / mesh placement materially affected performance;\\r\\n- this is useful background, not necessarily the current Las Vegas network topology.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n9. PERSONAL TECH BOUNDARIES\\r\\nThis handoff intentionally excludes:\\r\\n- GCE framework doctrine\\r\\n- Edge Crew project implementation\\r\\n- job-search/interview artifacts\\r\\n- Vegas hotel cash-flow ledger\\r\\n- Playa del Karma relocation plan\\r\\n- health / wellness\\r\\n- fantasy / sports entertainment unless it directly affects device/network troubleshooting\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n10. RE-ENTRY METHOD\\r\\nWhen this personal-tech lane is reopened:\\r\\n- truth current device/carrier/network state first;\\r\\n- separate solved items from open items;\\r\\n- avoid reconstructing old problems as if still active;\\r\\n- identify the one immediate friction in Don's hands;\\r\\n- solve it without turning personal ops into another giant framework project.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nSTATUS: CHECKPOINT\\r\\nCONFIDENCE: 94%\\r\\nREASON: personal-tech context has been separated from framework/project work, but several device/carrier facts are time-sensitive and must be re-verified before execution.\\r\\nNEXT GATE: recon current Spectrum/T-Mobile/phone state or current workstation/network state, depending on which personal issue Don opens next.\"}]},\"error\":null,\"error_data\":null,\"error_code\":null,\"classification_id\":null,\"json_rpc_error_code\":null,\"error_http_status_code\":null,\"error_http_headers\":null,\"internal\":{\"external_call_time_ms\":1378},\"clamp_errors\":null,\"clamp_rewrites\":null,\"connector_id\":\"connector_5f3c8c41a1e54ad7a76272c89e2554fa\",\"connector_name\":\"Google Drive\",\"action_name\":\"search\",\"is_sync\":false}"}, "create_time": 1790199319.0964253, "end_turn": null, "id": "29a1