DRIVE MODIFIED:** **NO**\n\nThis fits Wave 3 perfectly. It is **not a new top-level GCE project**. It is a **GCE Stack subproject/component** with a very clean current state. fileciteturn49file0L3-L13\n\n## What actually survived\n\nThe build converged on a deliberately tiny capture primitive:\n\n**Action Button → Record Audio → Save File → playable local `.m4a`**\n\nThat path was successfully proven on the actual iPhone. The key doctrine is:\n\n> **Raw audio is the authoritative evidence. Transcription is a derived projection.**\n\nThe earlier Dictate Text → Scriptable → JSON path was superseded by a better primitive; it was **not** proven universally broken. fileciteturn49file0L21-L53\n\nThat distinction is excellent and should stay intact.\n\n## Current project truth\n\nThese are the project-canonical decisions:\n\n- audio-first capture;\n- `Record Audio → Save File`;\n- raw audio = source evidence;\n- transcription = derived/rebuildable;\n- Scriptable exits the capture critical path;\n- one immutable recording per thought;\n- flat folder + timestamp-derived filenames is the preferred next direction, but still provisional until tested. fileciteturn49file0L213-L283\n\nThe current implementation artifact is the **`Capture Thought`** iPhone Shortcut, with a successful `WalkingCapture.m4a` bench artifact. The old `GCE_Capture` Scriptable code survives only as build-history/supporting evidence. fileciteturn49file0L405-L463\n\n---\n\n# Reconciliation against Wave 1 / Wave 2\n\n### GCE Stack\n**MATCH.**\n\nThis is exactly the kind of thing the GCE Stack parent is supposed to own:\n\n- capture;\n- local device primitive;\n- later transport/sync;\n- VoiceBridge-adjacent integration eventually;\n- local-to-desktop pipeline later.\n\nSo this strengthens the case for the parent structure:\n\n**GCE Stack**  \n→ Walking Capture / Mobile Capture  \n→ Web Bridge / scraper  \n→ VoiceBridge  \n→ transport/sync  \n→ runtime plumbing / local services  \n→ adapters/utilities\n\nNo separate parent project needed.\n\n### Framework\n**No current Framework change.**\n\nThere are several potentially reusable lessons, especially:\n\n- evidence before interpretation;\n- preserve source vs derived projection;\n- distinguish **superseded** from **failed**;\n- prove the smallest native primitive before adding orchestration.\n\nBut the source itself correctly says these are **reconciliation candidates**, not automatic canon. fileciteturn49file0L475-L517\n\nThat is the right classification.\n\n---\n\n# What is dead and should stay dead\n\nDo **not** resurrect:\n\n- Dictate Text → Scriptable → JSON as the capture architecture;\n- dictated text as “raw” evidence;\n- Scriptable as required for safe capture;\n- sequential `capture_001` counters;\n- dynamic daily folders;\n- sidecar JSON in the capture transaction;\n- transcription in the critical path;\n- Siri invocation as the v0.1 trigger;\n- Tailscale, VoiceBridge, desktop, network, Drive, or AI dependencies in v0.1. fileciteturn49file0L638-L655\n\nThis is important because the whole success of this POC came from **shrinking the critical path**.\n\n---\n\n# Open work — still valid\n\nThe remaining work is implementation hardening, not architecture:\n\n1. unique timestamp/random-suffix filenames;\n2. fixed flat `WalkingCapture` folder;\n3. Action Button binding;\n4. locked-screen test;\n5. rapid-fire collision test;\n6. long-ramble test;\n7. 20-thought walking field test;\n8. transcription layer only **after** raw capture proves stable. fileciteturn49file0L548-L634\n\nThat means this is actually a very healthy project state:\n\n**No conceptual blocker. Only bench hardening and field validation remain.** fileciteturn49file0L661-L679\n\n---\n\n# Wave 3 registry entry\n\n**W3-01 — Walking Capture / Mobile Thought Capture**\n\n**Classification:** `GCE STACK SUBPROJECT — ACTIVE POC`  \n**Authority:** Don  \n**Current stage:** verified primitive → hardening / field test  \n**Current truth:** audio-first native iPhone capture  \n**Framework impact:** candidates only  \n**Drive state:** no governing artifact yet  \n**Next route:** dedicated **Walking Capture / GCE Stack implementation chat**  \n**Do not create separate parent project:** correct\n\n## One useful addition to our master action ledger\n\nWhen we materialize the GCE Stack parent, **Walking Capture should be explicitly listed as a subproject/component**, with the current boundary:\n\n> **Capture first. Interpretation and transport later.**\n\nThat will prevent future chats from re-attaching VoiceBridge, AI, transcription, or network plumbing to the critical capture path prematurely.\n\n**Wave 3 is now open, and W3-01 is cleanly registered.**"]}, "create_time": 1790202538.422042, "end_turn": true, "id": "1a77a467-da51-484f-abd5-fdc76a151fe2", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [{"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 503, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "files/context_stuff", "authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "df8d6e6a-796b-4c58-97a0-7e41234f9e6a", "cited_message_idx": 553, "cloud_doc_url": null, "doi": null, "effective_time": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_65cdde5e58448191a52ff391cb46a2e0", "line_range": [3, 13], "publication_year": null, "retrieval_file_index": 0, "retrieval_turn": 49, "run_id": null, "search_result_idx": null, "set_id": null, "source_icon_url": null, "source_label": null, "source_url": null, "spl_version": null, "title": null}, "id": "file_00000000a84081fda5376aa86be3793c", "name": "Pasted text.txt", "source": "my_files", "text": "**CHAT / WORKSTREAM:** GCE Peter Throwing Shit at the Wall — Walking Capture / iPhone Thought-Capture POC  \n**PRIMARY DOMAIN:** GCE Stack / Project  \n**DATE RANGE COVERED:** 2026-09-22 to 2026-09-23  ", "type": "file"}, "start_ix": 474}, {"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 990, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source":