rn_exchange_id": "c444c346-9e7d-46cb-86bb-8def86995380", "working_turn_id": "c444c346-9e7d-46cb-86bb-8def86995380"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790202565.752381, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": "api_tool", "role": "tool"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content_type": "multimodal_text", "parts": ["Make sure to include fileciteturn49file0L5-L8 in your response to cite this file, or to surface it as a link. Replace the placeholder line range with the actual line range from the result that best fits the snippet you want to surface with the citation. If you cite multiple files, use a separate complete `filecite` marker for each file. Never put multiple `turnNfileM` targets inside a single `filecite` marker.\nUse ref_id \"turn49file0\" to reference this file. For broad questions or unknown locations, retrieve relevant chunks with `files.search` scoped to this file. Use `files.find` only for exact text, and use `files.read` for a known range or to expand relevant results. Full file size: 700 file lines.", "[L1] # 1. SESSION HEADER\n\n[L3] **CHAT / WORKSTREAM:** GCE Peter Throwing Shit at the Wall — Walking Capture / iPhone Thought-Capture POC  \n[L4] **PRIMARY DOMAIN:** GCE Stack / Project  \n[L5] **DATE RANGE COVERED:** 2026-09-22 to 2026-09-23  \n[L6] **FIRST MATERIAL DATE:** 2026-09-22  \n[L7] **LAST MATERIAL DATE:** 2026-09-23  \n\n[L9] **PRIMARY AUTHORITY:** Don  \n[L10] **PRIMARY SEATS INVOLVED:** Don; Coda. GLM was identified as a downstream architecture/reconciliation recipient, but no GLM execution occurred in this chat.  \n[L11] **CURRENT STATUS:** HANDOFF REQUIRED  \n\n[L13] **CONFIDENCE:** 98%\n\n---\n\n[L17] # 2. WHAT THIS CHAT WAS ACTUALLY ABOUT\n\n[L19] ## Original objective\n\n[L21] The chat began as a broader GCE Stack brainstorming / architecture sandbox, then narrowed into a concrete iPhone **Walking Capture v0.1** proof of concept.\n\n[L23] The practical goal became:\n\n[L25] > Allow Don to press the iPhone Action Button while walking, capture a thought with minimal interruption, preserve it locally, and review/process it later rather than immediately sending every thought to AI.\n\n[L27] The original implementation candidate was:\n\n[L29] **Action Button → Dictate Text → Scriptable → immutable JSON**\n\n[L31] ## Major pivots\n\n[L33] The Dictate Text path created repeated Shortcuts / Scriptable wiring problems and exposed an architectural issue: dictated text was being treated as “raw” evidence even though Apple dictation is already an interpretation layer.\n\n[L35] The chat pivoted to:\n\n[L37] **Action Button → Record Audio → Save File**\n\n[L39] This was successfully bench-tested on the actual phone.\n\n[L41] The key conceptual correction was then ratified:\n\n[L43] > **Audio is the authority. Transcription is a derived projection.**\n\n[L45] The earlier Dictate Text design was **not proven broken overall**. It was superseded before its non-Siri execution path was fully tested because audio-first was judged a better primitive on doctrine and implementation simplicity.\n\n[L47] ## Final scope\n\n[L49] The surviving v0.1 scope is deliberately small:\n\n[L51] **Action Button → Record Audio → unique local audio file → confirmation**\n\n[L53] Transcription, JSON, daily summaries, AI classification, desktop transport, VoiceBridge, Tailscale, network synchronization, and downstream reconciliation remain outside the capture critical path.\n\n---\n\n[L57] # 3. ACCOMPLISHMENTS BY DATE\n\n[L59] ## DATE: 2026-09-22\n\n[L61] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:**  \n[L62] Walking Capture v0.1 was scoped as a phone-only POC. Initial architecture used iPhone Shortcuts with Dictate Text feeding Scriptable, intended to create immutable JSON captures.\n\n[L64] **DECISION / RESULT:**  \n[L65] Phone-only scope was locked. Network, desktop, VoiceBridge, Tailscale, Drive, AI classification, and background processing were explicitly excluded from v0.1.\n\n[L67] **WHO / WHICH SEAT OWNED IT:** Don authority; Coda design/support.\n\n[L69] **STATUS:** accepted\n\n---\n\n[L73] ## DATE: 2026-09-22\n\n[L75] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:**  \n[L76] A Scriptable capture implementation named `GCE_Capture` was developed to receive shortcut text and write immutable JSON under a WalkingCapture directory.\n\n[L78] **DECISION / RESULT:**  \n[L79] The implementation included UUID capture IDs, local timestamps, source/capture metadata, overwrite protection, and terminal statuses such as `ok`, `cancelled`, and `fail`.\n\n[L81] **WHO / WHICH SEAT OWNED IT:** Coda implementation support under Don direction.\n\n[L83] **STATUS:** implemented, later superseded from the capture critical path\n\n---\n\n[L87] ## DATE: 2026-09-22\n\n[L89] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:**  \n[L90] Actual iPhone Shortcuts behavior was pressure-tested through screenshots and live interaction.\n\n[L92] **DECISION / RESULT:**  \n[L93] Several assumed Shortcuts / Scriptable input behaviors were disproven by the actual UI:\n[L94] - Scriptable’s visible `Parameter` field opened a file picker.\n[L95] - Scriptable’s `Texts` editor did not behave like a normal persistent literal-text field.\n[L96] - The intended Dictate Text → composed Text → Scriptable parameter path was not successfully proven.\n\n[L98] A Siri-context banner explicitly showed:\n\n[L100] **“Dictation is not supported in Siri.”**\n\n[L102] **WHO / WHICH SEAT OWNED IT:** Don performed ground test; Coda reconciled findings.\n\n[L104] **STATUS:** verified\n\n---\n\n[L108] ## DATE: 2026-09-22\n\n[L110] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:**  \n[L111] Don identified that `Dictate Text` itself was the wrong primitive for the desired capture behavior.\n\n[L113] **DECISION / RESULT:**  \n[L114] The design pivoted from text-first capture to **Record Audio**.\n\n[L116] **WHO / WHICH SEAT OWNED IT:** Don identified the break; Coda formulated the architectural pivot.\n\n[L118] **STATUS:** accepted\n\n---\n\n[L122] ## DATE: 2026-09-22\n\n[L124] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPL