: null, "id": "4838c4d7-cb19-4320-a2af-69cfa744ee0d", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "chime_version": 1, "classifier_response": "default", "command": "spinner", "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab43fca21d0819183966405a724bf5d", "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "parent_id": "6b209af2-cfc4-40d3-b552-ae580cebb3cd", "reasoning_start_time": 1790197729.6128519, "request_id": "649ac7c7-c6e0-4221-a84e-b40c0d3c588f", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "status": "running", "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "9ba6c645-1412-47eb-8843-70640a416df0", "working_turn_id": "9ba6c645-1412-47eb-8843-70640a416df0"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": null, "weight": 0}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": "api_tool", "role": "tool"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content_type": "multimodal_text", "parts": ["Make sure to include fileciteturn0file0L5-L8 in your response to cite this file, or to surface it as a link. Replace the placeholder line range with the actual line range from the result that best fits the snippet you want to surface with the citation. If you cite multiple files, use a separate complete `filecite` marker for each file. Never put multiple `turnNfileM` targets inside a single `filecite` marker.\nUse ref_id \"turn0file0\" to reference this file. For broad questions or unknown locations, retrieve relevant chunks with `files.search` scoped to this file. Use `files.find` only for exact text, and use `files.read` for a known range or to expand relevant results. Full file size: 576 file lines.", "[L1] GCE FRAMEWORK RECONCILIATION PROJECT\n[L2] STALE CHAT INTAKE / ORGANIZATION / DRIVE RECON\n\n[L4] Authority: Don\n[L5] Mode: READ-FIRST / RECONCILIATION\n[L6] Purpose: Create one project-level workspace for ingesting stale or closed ChatGPT conversations, reconstructing what actually happened in them, organizing their durable content by lane, and reconciling those findings against current GCE authority.\n\n[L8] This is NOT the live Framework governance conversation.\n\n[L10] This project exists to clean up historical conversational state so the live Framework can be validated against a much cleaner body of evidence.\n\n[L12] ────────────────────────────────────\n[L13] 1. PROJECT MISSION\n[L14] ────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L16] The project receives stale chats, old handoffs, recap dumps, mixed-domain conversations, and historical framework/project discussions.\n\n[L18] Its job is to determine:\n\n[L20] - what each chat was actually about;\n[L21] - what happened and on what dates;\n[L22] - what decisions survived;\n[L23] - what was superseded;\n[L24] - what became canonical;\n[L25] - what remained project-local;\n[L26] - what artifacts were created;\n[L27] - where those artifacts live;\n[L28] - what is in Google Drive;\n[L29] - what exists only locally;\n[L30] - what is chat-only;\n[L31] - what should be preserved as provenance;\n[L32] - what should NOT be carried forward.\n\n[L34] The project then organizes that recovered state into clearly separated lanes.\n\n[L36] It does NOT automatically update Framework canon.\n\n[L38] ────────────────────────────────────\n[L39] 2. PRIMARY LANES\n[L40] ────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L42] Every chat or extracted item should be classified into one or more of these lanes:\n\n[L44] A. GCE FRAMEWORK\n[L45] - authority\n[L46] - seat doctrine\n[L47] - governance\n[L48] - routing\n[L49] - canon\n[L50] - lifecycle\n[L51] - Command Center\n[L52] - framework infrastructure\n[L53] - framework-wide operating rules\n\n[L55] B. GCE STACK\n[L56] - scraper / Web Bridge\n[L57] - transport\n[L58] - state synchronization\n[L59] - capture/recovery\n[L60] - runtime plumbing\n[L61] - local services\n[L62] - APIs/adapters\n[L63] - developer utilities\n[L64] - VoiceBridge technical components\n[L65] - Command Center supporting technology\n[L66] - archival/recovery tooling\n[L67] - framework-support automation\n\n[L69] C. PROJECTS\n[L70] Examples:\n[L71] - Edge Crew / EC8\n[L72] - Parent Quant\n- ECQ\n- EC4\n[L75] - other active technical projects\n\n[L77] Projects own their own implementation truth.\n\n[L79] D. JOB SEARCH\n[L80] - companies\n[L81] - interviews\n[L82] - benefits\n[L83] - offer analysis\n[L84] - interview preparation\n[L85] - job pipeline\n\n[L87] E. PERSONAL\n[L88] - devices\n[L89] - financial logistics\n[L90] - phone\n[L91] - hotels\n[L92] - general personal operations\n\n[L94] F. HEALTH / WELLNESS\n\n[L96] G. TRAVEL / RELOCATION\n\n[L98] H. OTHER / UNKNOWN\n\n[L100] If a chat crosses lanes, split the extracted findings by lane rather than forcing the entire chat into one bucket.\n\n[L102] ────────────────────────────────────\n[L103] 3. SOURCE OF TRUTH RULES\n[L104] ────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L106] Use the following precedence:\n\n[L108] 1. Current explicitly accepted authority\n[L109] 2. Current Google Drive canonical/current artifact\n[L110] 3. Current local authoritative artifact\n[L111] 4. Project-current implementation truth\n[L112] 5. Accepted dated handoff\n[L113] 6. Historical provenance\n[L114] 7. Chat discussion\n[L115] 8. Memory/inference\n\n[L117] A chat is NEVER canonical merely because it contains a strong conclusion.\n\n[L119] Canonical status must be established from evidence.\n\n[L121] If uncertain:\n[L122] MARK UNKNOWN / NEEDS RECONCILIATION.\n\n[L124] ────────────────────────────────────\n[L125] 4. GOOGLE DRIVE RULE\n[L126] ────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L128] FIRST PHASE IS RECON ONLY.\n\n[L130] Google Drive is initially READ-ONLY.\n\n[L132] Do NOT:\n[L133] - edit\n[L134] - create\n[L135] - rename\n[L136] - move\n[L137] - delete\n[L138] - normalize\n[L139] - reorganize\n\n[L141] Google Drive content during intake.\n\n[L143] The first job is to compare recovered chat state against what is already in Drive.\n\n[L145] For every relevant Drive artifact determine:\n\n[L147] - artifact name;\n[L148] - location;\n[L149] - date;\n[L150] - authority;\n[L151] - current/superseded status;\n[L152] - what chat state it supports;\n[L153] - what chat state it contradicts;\n[L154] - whether the chat contains anything newer than Drive;\n[L155] - whether Drive contains anything newer than the chat.\n\n[L157] Do not assume the chat is newer or better.\n\n[L159] Do not assume Drive is canonical simply because it is in Drive.\n\n[L161] Reconcile authority explicitly.\n\n[L163] ────────────────────────────────────\n[L164] 5. UNIVERSAL CHAT INTAKE PROCEDURE\n[L165] ────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L167] For every stale chat Don provides:\n\n[L169] STEP 1 — CLOSEOUT RECON\n\n[L171] Reconstruct:\n\n[L173] - workstream;\n[L174] - domain;\n[L175] - date range;\n[L176] - primary seats;\n[L177] - objective;\n[L178] - pivots;\n[L179] - accomplishments;\n[L180] - accepted decisions;\n[L181] - rejected decisions;\n[L182] - superseded state;\n[L183] - artifacts;\n[L184] - open items.\n\n[L186] STEP 2 — LANE EXTRACTION\n\n[L188] Separate findings into:\n[L189] - Framework\n[L190] - GCE Stack\n[L191] - Projects\n[L192] - Personal\n[L193] - Job Search\n[L194] - Health\n[L195] - Travel\n[L196] - Other\n\n[L198] STEP 3 — AUTHORITY CLASSIFICATION\n\n[L200] Classify each durable finding:\n\n[L202] - FRAMEWORK CANON\n[L203] - PROJECT CANON\n[L204] - CURRENT SUPPORTING\n[L205] - EXPERIMENTAL\n[L206] - HISTORICAL PROVENANCE\n[L207] - SUPERSEDED\n[L208] - CHAT-ONLY\n[L209] - UNKNOWN / NEEDS RECONCILIATION\n\n[L211] STEP 4 — ARTIFACT LOCATION\n\n[L213] For each material artifact record:\n\nNAME:\nTYPE:\n[L217] KNOWN PATH / LOCATION:\n[L218] LOCAL / DRIVE / CHAT:\n[L219] AUTHORITY:\n[L220] CURRENT STATUS:\nDATE:\n[L222] RELATED LANE:\n\n[L224] Never invent a path.\n\n[L226] STEP 5 — DRIVE RECON\n\n[L228] Compare the extracted durable state against current Google Drive artifacts.\n\n[L230] Record:\n\nMATCH\n[L233] CHAT NEWER\n[L234] DRIVE NEWER\n[L235] CONFLICT\n[L236] MISSING FROM DRIVE\n[L237] MISSING FROM CHAT\n[L238] UNKNOWN\n\n[L240] No Drive mutation during this step.\n\n[L242] STEP 6 — DISPOSITION\n\n[L244] For each material item:\n\n[L246] KEEP CURRENT\n[L247] PRESERVE AS HISTORY\n[L248] ROUTE TO PROJECT\n[L249] ROUTE TO FRAMEWORK RECONCILIATION\n[L250] SUPERSEDE\n[L251] DROP / DO NOT CARRY\n[L252] NEEDS DON DECISION\n\n[L254] ────────────────────────────────────\n[L255] 6. PROJECT / FRAMEWORK BOUNDARY\n[L256] ────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L258] Binding rule:\n\n[L260] Projects do the work and own current implementation truth.\n\n[L262] Framework:\n[L263] - governs authority;\n[L264] - governs canon;\n[L265] - governs seat doctrine;\n[L266] - consumes reusable lessons through reconciliation.\n\n[L268] Do NOT promote project implementation detail directly into Framework.\n\n[L270] When a project produced a reusable lesson:\n\n[L272] OBSERVE\n[L273] → EXTRACT\n[L274] → RECONCILE\n[L275] → PROPOSE\n[L276] → FORMAL FRAMEWORK ADOPTION IF ACCEPTED\n\n[L278] ────────────────────────────────────\n[L279] 7. CURRENT FROZEN FRAMEWORK ROSTER\n[L280] ────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L282] Do not reinterpret or rename these during stale-chat reconciliation.\n\nDon\n[L285] Final authority / orchestrator.\n\nCoda\n[L288] Strategic advisor / governance / canon / reconciliation.\n\n[L290] Vittorio\n[L291] Technical advisor / warboard / challenge.\n\n[L293] Chiave\n[L294] Architecture.\n\nNico\n[L297] Implementation hammer / builder / design-to-build.\n\n[L299] Corrado\n[L300] Quant engine only.\n\n[L302] Falcon\n[L303] Data acquisition / retrieval.\n\nTalon\n[L306] Operations / routing / coordination / maintenance.\n\nKeel\n[L309] Operational build support / deployment / stability.\n\nLuce\n[L312] Verification / ground truth.\n\nRagno\n[L315] Principal Consultant / integration / translation when actually needed.\n\n[L317] Magpie\n[L318] Registry / secretary.\n\n[L320] Pigeon\n[L321] Transport.\n\nRaven\n[L324] Documentation / durable record.\n\n[L326] Core separation:\n\n[L328] Vittorio advises.\n[L329] Chiave architects.\n[L330] Nico builds.\n[L331] Corrado computes.\n\n[L333] Historical Kimi / Calibro / prior Corrado identities may appear in old chats and artifacts.\n\n[L335] Preserve those names where historically true.\n\n[L337] Do not rewrite history to match current naming.\n\n[L339] ────────────────────────────────────\n[L340] 8. MODEL / SEAT DOCTRINE\n[L341] ────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L343] Binding:\n\n[L345] IDENTITY != ROLE != LENS != PERSONALITY != AUTHORITY != MODEL\n\n[L347] MODEL != SEAT\n\n[L349] Current operating practice is identity-first and seat-first.\n\n[L351] Historical references to Kimi, GLM, Big Pickle, Kimi_Plumb, etc. may describe:\n[L352] - old seat names;\n[L353] - model/provider occupants;\n[L354] - runtime references;\n[L355] - historical project labels.\n\n[L357] Classify them from context.\n\n[L359] Do not automatically convert every historical model reference into a current seat.\n\n[L361] ────────────────────────────────────\n[L362] 9. STALE CHAT OUTPUT FORMAT\n[L363] ────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L365] For each chat, produce:\n\n[L367] A. CHAT IDENTITY\n[L368] - title/workstream\n[L369] - domain\n[L370] - date range\n[L371] - status\n[L372] - confidence\n\n[L374] B. WHAT IT ACTUALLY ACCOMPLISHED\n\n[L376] C. MATERIAL EVENTS BY DATE\n\n[L378] D. FINAL ACCEPTED DECISIONS\n\n[L380] E. CANON / AUTHORITY CLASSIFICATION\n\n[L382] F. ARTIFACT LOCATION MAP\n\n[L384] G. GOOGLE DRIVE RECON STATUS\n\n[L386] H. FRAMEWORK IMPACT\n\n[L388] I. PROJECT IMPACT\n\n[L390] J. PERSONAL / OTHER LANE EXTRACTIONS\n\n[L392] K. OPEN ITEMS THAT STILL MATTER\n\n[L394] L. SUPERSEDED / DO-NOT-CARRY-FORWARD\n\n[L396] M. HANDOFF / DISPOSITION\n\n[L398] ────────────────────────────────────\n[L399] 10. MASTER PROJECT REGISTRY\n[L400] ────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L402] Maintain a cumulative project-level registry of everything processed.\n\n[L404] Conceptually track:\n\n[L406] CHAT / SOURCE\n[L407] DATE RANGE\nLANE\n[L409] SUBJECT\n[L410] KEY DECISIONS\n[L411] CANON STATUS\n[L412] PROJECT\n[L413] ARTIFACTS\n[L414] LOCAL PATH\n[L415] DRIVE LOCATION\n[L416] CURRENT / SUPERSEDED\n[L417] OPEN ITEM\n[L418] NEXT ROUTE\n[L419] CONFIDENCE\n\n[L421] Do not let individual chat recaps become isolated islands.\n\n[L423] The purpose is to build one reconciled historical map.\n\n[L425] ────────────────────────────────────\n[L426] 11. DUPLICATE / CONFLICT HANDLING\n[L427] ────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L429] When multiple chats discuss the same thing:\n\n[L431] Do not simply keep the newest chat.\n\n[L433] Compare:\n[L434] - dates;\n[L435] - authority;\n[L436] - accepted decisions;\n[L437] - artifact evidence;\n[L438] - project implementation truth;\n[L439] - later supersession.\n\n[L441] Return:\n\n[L443] EARLIER STATE:\n[L444] LATER STATE:\n[L445] CURRENT WINNER:\nWHY:\n[L447] PROVENANCE TO PRESERVE:\n\n[L449] If evidence does not establish a winner:\n[L450] ESCALATE TO DON/CODA.\n\n[L452] ────────────────────────────────────\n[L453] 12. WHAT NOT TO DO\n[L454] ────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L456] Do not:\n\n[L458] - redesign Framework;\n[L459] - invent new architecture;\n[L460] - create new seats;\n[L461] - rename seats;\n[L462] - rewrite historical provenance;\n[L463] - modify Google Drive during initial recon;\n[L464] - promote project-specific conclusions into Framework automatically;\n[L465] - treat chat summaries as authority;\n[L466] - resurrect abandoned ideas;\n[L467] - fill unknown paths from memory;\n[L468] - collapse personal/project/framework lanes together.\n\n[L470] ────────────────────────────────────\n[L471] 13. PROJECT PHASES\n[L472] ────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L474] PHASE 1 — INGEST / CLASSIFY\n[L475] Process stale chats and extract durable state.\n\n[L477] PHASE 2 — ORGANIZE\n[L478] Group findings by lane, project, date, authority, and artifact.\n\n[L480] PHASE 3 — GO