h. fileciteturn2file0L90-L108\n\n### SUPERSEDED\nThe following did **not survive**:\n- ATEX/Apex as merely relationship maintenance;\n- MHI as unquestioned first priority;\n- the September 21 ranking of MHI → Oasis → R-Smart → ATEX/Apex.\n\nThe later A-Tex-specific record materially changes that state.\n\n## F. Artifact map\n\nThe record identifies:\n- **Job Search Status & Interview Prep** — Google Drive, exact path not verified;\n- MHI Principal Consultant reference table — chat-only;\n- Oasis / James Delaney handoff — chat-only;\n- claim-ready outreach list — historical;\n- ATEX notes — supporting. fileciteturn2file0L124-L135\n\n## G–J. Impact\n\n**Framework canon:** none.\n\nThe “reference-table” communication method is at most a reconciliation candidate; the job-specific compensation/travel/authority criteria remain domain-local rather than Framework doctrine. fileciteturn2file0L137-L147\n\n**Project impact:** Job Search only.\n\n## K–M. Disposition\n\nThe source still listed MHI outcome, Oasis economics, R-Smart status and ATEX disposition as open. fileciteturn2file0L158-L165\n\nThose open items must now be reconciled against later job-search evidence rather than carried forward wholesale.\n\n**FINAL DISPOSITION:**  \n**PRESERVE MHI positioning framework + Oasis provenance; SUPERSEDE the September 21 opportunity ordering; queue Drive artifact verification later.**\n\n---\n\n# INTAKE 004 — A-Tex Benefits / Compensation / Friday CFO Positioning\n\n## A. Chat identity\n**Workstream:** Job Search — A-Tex Benefits / Compensation Reconciliation and Friday CFO Positioning  \n**Domain:** Job Search  \n**Date:** September 22, 2026, with closeout September 23  \n**Status:** HANDOFF REQUIRED  \n**Confidence:** 96% fileciteturn2file1L3-L13\n\n## B–D. What it actually accomplished\n\nThis record materially updates Intake 003.\n\nThe key analytical correction was that A-Tex should not be judged through a generic “benefits good/bad” framework. The accepted question became:\n\n**What incremental economic and operating value does A-Tex add versus the competing jobs?**\n\nThat led to a more precise compensation picture:\n- employer 401(k) match exists after eligibility;\n- match percentage is unknown;\n- a 15% Senior NetSuite Admin bonus is evidence of meaningful variable comp, but **not** proof of the Director bonus;\n- hypothetical total-comp scenarios were explicitly kept separate from offer terms;\n- A-Tex’s stronger guaranteed-base structure was distinguished from utilization-dependent MHI economics. fileciteturn2file1L105-L145 fileciteturn2file1L149-L199\n\nThe Friday session was also reclassified as a **working conversation**, not a presentation exercise, after Kaylnne positively validated the outline and said no further formal preparation was necessary. fileciteturn2file1L244-L264\n\n---\n\n# Major supersession against Intake 003\n\nThis is the important reconciliation result.\n\n### EARLIER STATE — Intake 003\nAs of September 21:\n- MHI was primary.\n- Oasis was strongest parallel.\n- ATEX/Apex was relationship-only due to onsite/relocation concerns. fileciteturn2file0L71-L76\n\n### LATER STATE — Intake 004\nAs of September 22:\n- **A-Tex had moved into the lead** and strengthened after benefits/compensation review.\n- The immediate priority became the Friday CFO session.\n- The working ordering was recorded as **A-Tex / Apex → RF-SMART → MHI → Oasis**. fileciteturn2file1L51-L67\n\n### CURRENT WINNER\n**Later A-Tex-led state.**\n\nThis is a clean supersession based on later explicit Don authority, not inference.\n\nThe earlier “no full Orlando relocation for ATEX/Apex” position should therefore be retained as **historical provenance**, not current job-search truth. It had already been overtaken by subsequent A-Tex negotiations and transition planning.\n\n---\n\n# E. Authority classification\n\n## PROJECT-CURRENT / STRONG SUPPORTING\nWithin the Job Search workstream, the later chat established:\n\n- A-Tex is the current lead at that point.\n- Employer 401(k) match exists after eligibility.\n- Match formula remains unknown.\n- Unknown match percentage must not be modeled as zero.\n- 15% Senior Admin bonus is reference evidence only.\n- Friday is a working session rather than a presentation exercise. fileciteturn2file1L268-L337\n\nI am retaining the source’s “project-canonical” labels **within the Job Search project context**, not elevating any of these to GCE Framework canon.\n\n## SUPPORTING / PROVISIONAL\n- $237.6K / $261.2K A-Tex modeled scenarios.\n- $1,600 travel/hotel value.\n- MHI ~$260K model at 35 billable hours.\n- Oasis 3% non-elective contribution benchmark. fileciteturn2file1L371-L383\n\n## SUPERSEDED / DO NOT CARRY\n- MHI has a documented 401(k).\n- MHI has a documented 3% match.\n- MHI full-utilization comp ≈ $320K.\n- A-Tex has a confirmed 3% match.\n- A-Tex Director bonus is confirmed at 15%.\n- $237.6K or $261.2K is the actual A-Tex offer.\n- Generic PTO criticism as a major decision factor. fileciteturn2file1L660-L692\n\n---\n\n# F. Artifact map\n\nThis intake identifies four especially important sources:\n\n| Artifact | Location status | Reconciliation status |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Job Search Status & Interview Prep** | Google Drive; exact path unknown | CURRENT SOURCE — verify read-only later |\n| **A-Tex / Clavis — Director ERP & Enterprise Systems — Friday CFO Interview Prep — 2026-09-20** | Google Drive; exact path unknown | CURRENT SOURCE — verify |\n| **A-Tex / Clavis — Friday CFO Interview — Waves 2 & 3 Working Artifact — 2026-09-21** | Google Drive; exact path unknown | CURRENT SOURCE — verify |\n| **2025 Atex Distributing Benefit Guide (3).pdf** | Uploaded source; persistent external location unknown | CURRENT SUPPORTING EVIDENCE |\n\nfileciteturn2file1L419-L468\n\nThere is also an Oasis benefits source and Kaylnne correspondence, but their exact locations remain unresolved. fileciteturn2file1L451-L489\n\n---\n\n# G. Google Drive reconciliation status\n\n**QUEUED — READ-ONLY, NOT YET EXECUTED.**\n\nThis is a higher-priority Drive recon candidate than Intake 003 because it explicitly names the job-board source plus two A-Tex working artifacts and states that they remain authoritative. fileciteturn2file1L698-L720\n\nNo Drive mutation occurred in the source chat. fileciteturn2file1L725-L741\n\n---\n\n# H. Framework impact\n\nThree candidate lessons emerged:\n\n- **UNKNOWN ≠ ZERO.**\n- Artifact-backed claims outrank unsupported assumptions.\n- Analysis must honor the actual decision objective rather than substitute a generic evaluation framework.\n\nThe first two align strongly with existing GCE evidence discipline, but this chat did **not** itself create Framework canon. fileciteturn2file1L493-L535\n\n**Disposition:** `ROUTE TO FRAMEWORK RECONCILIATION`, not promote automatically.\n\n---\n\n# I–J. Project / lane impact\n\n### Job Search / A-Tex\nMaterially advanced.\n\n### Job Search / MHI\nCorrected unsupported retirement assumptions; retains comparison value.\n\n### Job Search / Oasis\nRetains known retirement benchmark; profit-share economics remain unresolved.\n\n### RF-SMART\nNo substantive new state in this intake. fileciteturn2file1L539-L614\n\nNo separate Personal or Framework state should be extracted beyond job-transition implications.\n\n---\n\n# K. Open items that survived this intake\n\nAs of this source:\n- A-Tex Director bonus/incentive structure;\n- A-Tex 401(k) match formula;\n- final A-Tex compensation;\n- artifact-grounded MHI comparison numbers. fileciteturn2file1L618-L656\n\nThese are **historical open items from September 22/23** and must be reconciled against later job-search chats before being treated as currently open.\n\n---\n\n# CUMULATIVE REGISTRY — NEW ENTRIES\n\n| Intake | Lane | Core subject | Current disposition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 003 | Job Search | MHI Principal Consultant positioning / Oasis parallel lane | **PARTLY CURRENT SUPPORTING; priority ordering superseded** |\n| 004 | Job Search | A-Tex benefits, comp, Friday CFO prep | **LATER / higher-authority job-search state; Drive recon queued** |\n\n## Conflict / supersession map\n\n**Conflict 1 — Job priority**  \nEarlier: MHI first, ATEX relationship-only.  \nLater: A-Tex first.  \n**Winner:** Later A-Tex state.\n\n**Conflict 2 — relocation posture**  \nEarlier: no full Orlando relocation for ATEX/Apex.  \nLater: A-Tex remained active and moved into the lead despite onsite implications.  \n**Disposition:** Earlier posture = historical, not current.\n\n**Conflict 3 — MHI retirement assumptions**  \nEarlier evidence was incomplete; later record explicitly rejects undocumented MHI 401(k) claims.  \n**Winner:** Do not attribute a documented MHI 401(k) without artifact verification.\n\n**Conflict 4 — A-Tex compensation certainty**  \nScenario math existed, but 3% match and 15% Director bonus were hypothetical.  \n**Winner:** Match exists but percentage unknown; Director bonus unknown.\n\n---\n\n# SESSION FOOTER\n\n**STATUS:** COMPLETE FOR THESE 2 INTAKES  \n**CONFIDENCE:** 97%  \n**INPUTS PROCESSED:** 2  \n**DATE RANGE COVERED:** September 6–23, 2026  \n**LANES UPDATED:** Job Search  \n**CANONICAL ITEMS FOUND:** 0 GCE Framework items  \n**PROJECT-CANONICAL ITEMS FOUND:** Later A-Tex job-search state and compensation interpretations, subject to Drive recon  \n**HISTORICAL ITEMS FOUND:** MHI-first ranking; ATEX relationship-only posture; old outreach state  \n**SUPERSEDED ITEMS FOUND:** Yes — job priority, relocation stance, MHI 401(k)/$320K assertions, A-Tex 3%/15% assumptions as facts  \n**ARTIFACTS / LOCATIONS:** Job Search Status & Interview Prep; two dedicated A-Tex Drive artifacts; A-Tex benefits guide; Oasis source; several chat-only artifacts  \n**GOOGLE DRIVE REFERENCES:** 3 priority job-search artifacts  \n**GOOGLE DRIVE MODIFIED:** **NO**  \n**CONFLICTS FOUND:** 4 meaningful supersession/reconciliation items  \n**OPEN ITEMS:** Exact Drive paths; latest A-Tex/MHI/Oasis/RF-SMART state to be reconciled from later evidence  \n**NEXT INTAKE:** Ready  \n**NEXT ROUTE:** Continue accumulation; do not perform full job-search Drive reconciliation prematurely  \n**DON INPUT NEEDED:** **NO**  \n**ANCHOR STATUS:** ACTIVE / REGISTRY ACCUMULATING CLEANLY"]}, "create_time": 1790198028.563639, "end_turn": true, "id": "410f9a30-6f9d-4081-85d3-6b70b961eae0", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [{"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 887, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "files/context_stuff", "authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "5441c93a-257b-4156-82e5-df8525c9791a", "cited_message_idx": 51, "cloud_doc_url": null, "doi": null, "effective_time": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_cf6260d00bd08191acbd91262c2df55b", "line_range": [3, 11], "publication_year": null, "retrieval_file_index": 0, "retrieval_turn": 2, "run_id": null, "search_result_idx": null, "set_id": null, "source_icon_url": null, "source_label": null, "source_url": null, "spl_version": null, "title": null}, "id": "file_0000000029d481fda049d82c011d17bb", "name": "Pasted text.txt", "source": "my_files", "text": "**CHAT / WORKSTREAM:** Director-Level ERP + AI Job Search / Principal Consultant Positioning  \n**PRIMARY DOMAIN:** Job Search  \n**DATE RANGE COVERED:** September 6–21, 2026  ", "type": "file"}, "start_ix": 859}, {"citation_format_type": "berry_file_search", "end_ix": 1333, "metadata": {"extra": {"api_tool_source": "files/context_stuff", "authors_display": null, "cited_message_id": "5441c93a-257b-4156-82e5-df8525c9791a", "cited_message_idx": 51, "cloud_doc_url": null, "doi": null, "effective_time": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_cf6260d00bd08191acbd91262c2df55b", "line_range": [50, 62], "publication_year": null, "retrieval_file_index": 0, "retrieval_turn": 2, "run_id": null, "search_