ved methodology?\n- Can she turn that methodology into a practical Design & Build direction?\n- Can she distinguish:\n  - facts\n  - derived conclusions\n  - proposals\n  - unknowns\n  - architecture routes\n  - operations routes\n- Can she avoid silently filling gaps?\n- Can she know when a structural issue belongs to Chiave instead of solving it herself?\n\n### PROJECT SPLIT THAT RESULTED FROM THIS TEST\n\nDuring this discussion, Don and Coda clarified that **Edge Crew should not be the umbrella brand**.\n\nThe accepted branch structure became:\n```\nEC⁸\n├── Edge Crew\n│   Quantitative / mathematical intelligence\n│\n└── AI Convergence\n    Multi-model AI analysis / reconciliation / committee intelligence\n```\n\nSo:\n\n`EC⁸` = parent platform.\n\n`Edge Crew` = quantitative / mathematical / analytics branch.\n\n`AI Convergence` = separate sibling methodology/project.\n\nThis matters because future chats must **not** treat AI Convergence as “Edge Crew v4” or as part of Edge Crew Quant by default.\n\n### DEEPSEEK / TALON RECOVERY USE CASE\n\nBefore handing the real project to Kimi, Don wanted Talon/DeepSeek to recover what had actually existed as the prior EC4 convergence methodology.\n\nThe recovery assignment was explicitly evidence-only.\n\nDeepSeek was instructed to recover:\n\n- original Don intent\n- methodology of record\n- process flow\n- model/role responsibilities\n- evidence handling\n- independent analysis\n- disagreement handling\n- convergence / reconciliation\n- grading\n- confidence\n- Don intervention\n- stopping conditions\n- final output\n- conflicts\n- EC3 contamination\n- Quant contamination\n- unresolved questions\n\nDeepSeek was told:\n\n- do not redesign the methodology\n- do not silently merge versions\n- do not import EC3 unless explicitly carried forward\n- do not import Quant merely because both are Edge Crew-related\n- preserve conflicts\n- classify recovered material as canonical / active working / experimental / superseded / conflicting / unknown\n\nThe intended output was a **minimum clean methodology package** that could be handed to Kimi as if she were starting the Design & Build phase fresh.\n\n### CURRENT STATUS OF THIS USE CASE\n\nAt the end of this chat:\n\n- DeepSeek/Talon had already returned the EC4 methodology recovery package to Don.\n- That recovery had **not yet been reconciled inside the new EC⁸ AI Convergence project**.\n- A new dedicated EC⁸ AI Convergence project knowledge base had been created.\n- The project was intentionally split out of this overloaded framework chat.\n- The next project action was:\n  1. bring the DeepSeek recovery into the new EC⁸ project;\n  2. review it as evidence;\n  3. isolate the clean methodology;\n  4. then give that to Kimi for the real-world Design & Build test.\n\n### WHY THIS USE CASE MATTERS TO GCE\n\nThis is not just an Edge Crew project.\n\nIt is also the first real-world pressure test of the new GCE division of labor:\n```\nDon\n→ Coda governance framing\n→ Kimi methodology\n→ Chiave architecture when materially required\n→ Kimi Design & Build\n→ implementation\n→ Talon operations\n→ Luce verification\n→ Coda reconciliation\n→ Don decision\n```\n\nThe use case is specifically testing whether Kimi can own **methodology + Design & Build** while preserving the handoff boundaries to Chiave, Talon, Luce, and Coda.\n\nThat is the detail I would absolutely add to the handoff for the next chat.\n\nIf you want, I can also give you the **entire handoff again with this section already integrated in the right place**, so you can paste one clean block into the next chat."]}, "create_time": 1790198255.075, "end_turn": null, "id": "3c80e5cf-5fd1-4833-9169-048175af24d8", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "message_source": null, "request_id": "a310457e-ede4-43dd-a361-4248153e2e11", "serialization_metadata": {"render_format": "markdown"}, "turn_exchange_id": "5a02e502-a7fd-4b95-8b59-88ae7b99388a", "working_turn_id": "5a02e502-a7fd-4b95-8b59-88ae7b99388a"}, "r