arantee independent reasoning.\\r\\n- Task-fit must be demonstrated against bounded work.\\r\\n- Model labor evidence is advisory until promoted through GCE governance.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nBLACK PEARL / TRIAL 01 OBSERVED LABOR MAP\\r\\n- GPT-5.6 Sol: bounded senior analyst / disciplined first read.\\r\\n- Nex N2.5 Pro: grounded skeptic; price-vs-evidence tension.\\r\\n- Muse Spark 1.3: pattern analyst.\\r\\n- Dots3 Note Preview: anomaly hunter; aggressive, requires audit.\\r\\n- Grok 4.6: cross-examiner / contradiction auditor; best when narrowly boxed.\\r\\n- Kimi K3 High: methodology challenger; attacks hidden assumptions and reasoning machinery.\\r\\n- Big Pickle: verifier / truth-teller; evidence bookkeeping, arithmetic, unknowns.\\r\\n- GLM 5.1 / 5.3-class: architecture / integration / normalization, with stage discipline required.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNEGATIVE / NARROW-FIT LESSONS\\r\\nSeveral models were useful only in narrow lanes or showed contamination, gap filling, math errors, generic reasoning, or route problems. Do not promote a model because it is generally strong; evaluate the specific job.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFRAMEWORK IMPLICATION\\r\\nSeat assignment should be based on demonstrated task-fit, authority boundaries, and known failure signature. Occupants remain replaceable. Research evidence should be periodically re-tested because model versions change.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPROMOTION PATH\\r\\nProving Ground evidence -> Model Labor Intelligence -> cross-project reconciliation -> Strategic Governance -> seat/standard change only if explicitly approved.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nPROJECT BOUNDARY\\r\\nProject-specific rosters, prompts, scores, or betting logic remain project-owned and are not canonized here.\"}]},\"error\":null,\"error_data\":null,\"error_code\":null,\"classification_id\":null,\"json_rpc_error_code\":null,\"error_http_status_code\":null,\"error_http_headers\":null,\"internal\":{\"external_call_time_ms\":1371},\"clamp_errors\":null,\"clamp_rewrites\":null,\"co