separation is consistent.**\n2. **Job Search is actually very well reconciled by the latest Drive updates.**\n3. **The model-testing / proving-ground work exists, but its lineage is more fragmented than its substance.**\n\nThe largest real variance is **Framework seat doctrine**: Wave 1 contains a later frozen organizational roster than the September 21 Drive framework handoff.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Framework governance — **MATCH with one important supersession**\n\n### What matches\n\nThe September 21 Drive manifest and framework handoff strongly agree with Wave 1 on the core doctrine:\n\n- `MODEL != SEAT`\n- Don = final authority.\n- capability does not grant authority.\n- Projects own implementation truth.\n- Framework consumes project evidence through reconciliation.\n- Black Pearl is proving-ground research, **not** an Edge Crew project branch.\n- research does not automatically become canon.\n- provenance is preserved rather than rewritten.\n\nThat is exactly the core state reconstructed in Intake 005. The stale-chat record explicitly closes on the same boundary: Projects own implementation truth; Black Pearl sits in research/proving-ground lineage; later seat doctrine overrides older model-bound maps. fileciteturn3file0L893-L914\n\n### **VARIANCE 1 — HIGH: latest roster is newer than the Drive Framework handoff**\n\nThe September 21 Drive handoff predates the September 22 frozen roster.\n\nWave 1 explicitly says later seat doctrine supersedes older documents that bound organizational roles too tightly to Kimi/model occupants. fileciteturn3file0L330-L340\n\nIt also explicitly says **do not carry forward earlier seat maps that bind seat identity to Kimi, Big Pickle, GLM or other runtimes**. fileciteturn3file0L870-L889\n\nSo the Drive artifact:\n\n**`GCE_FRAMEWORK_HANDOFF_2026-09-21_MAIN_CHAT_RECONCILIATION`**\n\nis still an excellent framework handoff, **but its organizational/seat state is one generation behind Wave 1**.\n\n### Don ruling needed later\nI do **not** need you to resolve the doctrine—we already have the later roster. What needs deciding eventually is whether:\n\n- the September 21 handoff is simply marked **historical/supporting**, or\n- a newer Framework anchor should supersede it in Drive.\n\n**My reconciliation classification:**  \n`DRIVE OLDER / WAVE 1 NEWER — winner = Wave 1 later frozen roster.`\n\n---\n\n## 2. Drive filing taxonomy — **probably valid, but needs a semantic check**\n\nThe September 21 manifest is internally disciplined:\n\n- `GCE_ORG`\n- `03_Projects`\n- `06_Frozen_State_and_Archive`\n- research outside Projects\n- project truth remains project-owned\n- no duplicate current authority.\n\nThat all matches Wave 1.\n\n### **VARIANCE 2 — MEDIUM: folder names may reflect an older organizational model**\n\nThe manifest still physically contains:\n\n`01_Executive_Council/02_Technical_Strategy_Systems_Intelligence`\n\nand the older Shared Enterprise Services topology.\n\nThat may be perfectly acceptable as a **filing taxonomy** even though the seat roster later changed. I do **not** have evidence that the folders themselves must be renamed.\n\nSo I am **not calling this a conflict**.\n\nI am flagging it as:\n\n> **Does organizational folder taxonomy describe stable functional estates, or is it intended to mirror the live seat board exactly?**\n\nIf the first: **no problem**.  \nIf the second: **Drive taxonomy is stale.**\n\nThis is a genuine Don/Coda semantic ruling for the later Framework phase.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Model research / Black Pearl — **strong match**\n\nThis is one of the cleanest areas.\n\nDrive contains:\n\n- `GCE_MODEL_LABOR_INTELLIGENCE_CURRENT_2026-09-21`\n- `GCE_RUNTIME_PROVIDER_INTELLIGENCE_CURRENT_2026-09-21`\n- `GCE_BLACK_PEARL_MODEL_LAB_RESEARCH_ANCHOR_2026-09-21`\n- `GCE_CROSS_PROJECT_METHODOLOGY_RESEARCH_CURRENT_2026-09-21`\n\nTheir content matches the chat reconstruction exceptionally well.\n\nThe Black Pearl record explicitly says the experiment is research, not project authority, and the Wave-1 closeout independently classifies it the same way. fileciteturn3file0L473-L501\n\nThe project/framework promotion path also matches.\n\n**Disposition:** **MATCH / KEEP.**\n\n---\n\n## 4. Model test cases — **content is strong; registry is the gap**\n\nThis is where your Disney point mattered.\n\nThe **Disney Test Case absolutely exists** in Drive as a proper suite:\n\n- source case;\n- blind package;\n- blind reconstruction prompt;\n- role/lens independent judgment;\n- Don reveal/reconciliation;\n- protocol README.\n\nSo we were right **not** to recreate it.\n\n### **VARIANCE 3 — MEDIUM-HIGH: no obvious unified model-test-case registry**\n\nWhat I do see is several related proving mechanisms:\n\n**Disney**\n→ reconstruction of intent/objective function, role/lens discipline and independent judgment.\n\n**Monitor harness**\n→ identical-prompt comparative model testing.\n\n**Kimi / EC⁸ real-world validation**\n→ can a runtime perform methodology + Design & Build while respecting architecture/ops/verifier/governance boundaries?\n\n**Black Pearl**\n→ cognitive labor fit, failure signatures, independence, contamination control, provider/runtime behavior.\n\nThese belong to one **model evaluation lineage**, but the September 21 Model Labor Intelligence document primarily memorializes Black Pearl.\n\nSo the **substance exists; the catalog/index layer is incomplete**.\n\nThis is not a missing methodology. It is a **discoverability / registry gap**.\n\n### Later recommendation\nEventually the Framework should probably have one model-test registry pointing to these cases rather than creating another testing architecture.\n\nNo write now.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Edge Crew / EC8 — **boundary is good; current project truth intentionally outside Framework**\n\nWave 1 repeatedly gets this right:\n\n- framework does not own current EC8 implementation;\n- current project truth belongs in the dedicated project estate;\n- Black Pearl does not overwrite it;\n- old AI Convergence and EC3/EC4 material remain provenance.\n\nThe September 21 Drive handoff to Edge Crew says the same thing.\n\nThe Sept 16–17 source also captured a concrete authority map at that time:\n\n- `GCE_DON\\GCE_EC8` operative/current;\n- `Projects\\EC8` supporting;\n- Desktop EC8 stale;\n- Falcon live feed separately bounded. fileciteturn12file1L179-L202\n\n### **VARIANCE 4 — LOW / expected: historical EC8 authority snapshots differ**\n\nThere are multiple EC8 generations in Wave 1. That is expected, not corruption.\n\nThe important rule is:\n\n> A Framework recon must **not choose the current Parent Quant implementation from old Drive/chat evidence**.\n\nWave 1 already tells us to defer to the dedicated current project.\n\n**Disposition:** **NO DON DECISION NEEDED. Preserve lineage.**\n\n---\n\n## 6. Root routing / bootstrap / Falcon — **strong historical implementation evidence**\n\nThe Sept 16–17 record is strong and internally verified:\n\n- neutral `GCE_SEAT_ROUTER.md`;\n- root `opencode.json`;\n- live bootstrap acceptance;\n- Falcon fail-closed search boundary;\n- identity routing separated from data-authority routing. fileciteturn12file1L87-L143 fileciteturn12file1L361-L409\n\n### **GAP 1 — current local state not Drive-verifiable**\n\nThese are local-machine artifacts, so Drive cannot establish whether every file remains exactly as it was on September 17.\n\nThis is not a contradiction.\n\nClassification:\n\n**`CURRENT-AS-OF-LOCAL-EVIDENCE / CURRENT LOCAL RECHECK REQUIRED ONLY IF WE REOPEN THAT SYSTEM.`**\n\nDo not rediscover them now.\n\n---\n\n# 7. Personal Tech — **real stale Drive handoff found**\n\nThis is one of the clearest discrepancies.\n\nThe Drive document:\n\n**`PERSONAL_TECH_OPERATIONS_HANDOFF_2026-09-21`**\n\nstill says, in substance:\n\n- AX210 had been purchased/fitted;\n- antenna seating was unresolved;\n- card compatibility remained caveated;\n- technician install was still the practical plan;\n- do not assume internal repair is complete.\n\nBut Intake 001 contains later machine ground truth:\n\n- AX210 physically installed and operating;\n- Bluetooth operational;\n- electrical compatibility closed;\n- network stack normalized;\n- broader machine cleanup completed;\n- Defender clean;\n- System Protection repaired;\n- final post-reboot baseline captured. fileciteturn1file0L90-L99 fileciteturn1file0L230-L254\n\n### **VARIANCE 5 — HIGH: Personal Tech Drive handoff is stale**\n\nThis is a legitimate Drive-vs-Wave-1 mismatch.\n\n**Winner:** later Luce/local-machine evidence from September 19.\n\nThe Drive file should eventually be treated as:\n\n**historical handoff / superseded machine subsection**, not current machine truth.\n\nThat does **not** mean the whole document is bad—its phone/carrier and personal-executor sections may still be useful. The **Razer subsection is stale**.\n\n---\n\n# 8. Personal Operating Context index — **structurally good, operationally stale**\n\nThe Drive index is actually well designed. It explicitly separates:\n\n- Vegas;\n- Mexico/family;\n- contacts;\n- personal systems;\n- Job Search cross-reference rather than duplication.\n\nGood.\n\nBut it still says things such as:\n\n- latest session anchor = September 7;\n- primary live Vegas source = the older Vegas Budget anchor;\n- current chronology largely framed from early September.\n\n### **VARIANCE 6 — MEDIUM-HIGH: index has not caught up to later Personal Ops state**\n\nWave 1 contains later:\n\n- Vegas liquidity and hotel-calendar revisions;\n- MGM promotional-rule reconciliation;\n- later Playa timing;\n- Daphne contact;\n- current Personal Tech machine state;\n- health lane split. fileciteturn4file0L417-L429\n\nSo the Personal Context **structure remains useful**, but its “latest/current” pointers are stale.\n\nThis is exactly the kind of thing that can make a new AI confidently resurrect an old hotel calendar.\n\n---\n\n# 9. Vegas / liquidity — **historical artifacts are preserved correctly, but “live source” pointers lag**\n\nThe earlier Vegas Budget anchor exists in Drive and was correctly identified in Intake 008. fileciteturn12file0L419-L440\n\nWave 1 establishes a clean supersession chain:\n\nSept 16–17 bridge  \n→ Sept 20 frozen calendar  \n→ later Sep 22/23 operational changes.\n\nThe old numeric states should remain history.\n\n### **VARIANCE 7 — MEDIUM: Drive has older live anchors but Wave 1 has later chat authority**\n\nThis is not a factual disagreement. It is an **artifact freshness gap**.\n\nIf later Personal Ops work is going to rely on Drive as first-load truth, it eventually needs a refreshed anchor or an explicit pointer saying:\n\n> “Do not use the Sep 14/early Sep living plan for current balances/calendar; load the newer state.”\n\nNo action now.\n\n---\n\n# 10. Job Search — **very good reconciliation**\n\nThis is the strongest operational area.\n\nThe Drive **Job Search Status & Interview Prep** contains a long append-only history, but the **September 22 current-status block** substantially agrees with Intake 011:\n\n1. **A-Tex / Apex** lead.\n2. **RF-SMART** potential challenger.\n3. **MHI** alive but secondary.\n4. **Oasis** economically weaker pending hard economics.\n\nThat agrees with the latest stale-chat closeout. fileciteturn13file0L17-L32\n\nThe Drive artifact also correctly records:\n- $220K target / $200K floor;\n- A-Tex not yet a written offer;\n- internal ownership thesis;\n- MHI structural consulting concern;\n- Oasis profit share treated as unpriced;\n- RF-SMART needing comp/authority validation.\n\n### **VARIANCE 8 — MEDIUM: append-only Job Search doc contains stale calculations above current sections**\n\nThe same document still contains earlier text such as:\n- MHI potentially ~$319K under one interpretation;\n- older rankings;\n- older job opportunities;\n- earlier RF-SMART/A-Tex classifications.\n\nThe latest appended block corrects them, but a model retrieving a middle chunk could still mistake historical state for current state.\n\nThis is a **retrieval hazard**, not a Don-decision conflict.\n\nA future cleanup could mark dated sections clearly as historical or place a short current-state header at the top.\n\n---\n\n# 11. A-Tex compensation — **no material conflict**\n\nThe latest Wave-1 position is disciplined:\n\n- $200K = budget floor assumption, not offer.\n- $220K = target/upside.\n- bonus structure = not known.\n- 401(k) match exists but exact formula unknown.\n- Senior Admin 15% = reference signal only, not Director bonus.\n\nThe closeout explicitly warns against converting any of those modeled assumptions into facts. fileciteturn2file1L660-L692\n\nThe current Drive A-Tex artifacts are consistent with the broad picture.\n\n### Minor variance\nThe Job Search Drive artifact allows a **10–20% bonus planning range** pending actual terms.\n\nThat is acceptable as scenario planning, but it should never be retrieved as a known A-Tex Director bonus.\n\n**Classification:** `NO CONFLICT / PROVISIONAL MODEL ONLY.`\n\n---\n\n# 12. MHI — **methodology strong; economics still messy**\n\nThe MHI Principal Consultant methodology is consistent across:\n- chat;\n- Job Search Drive;\n- hardened artifacts;\n- later interview anchor.\n\nThat survived well.\n\nThe role altitude is clear:\n- validate sold solution;\n- own lifecycle coherence;\n- preserve requirements/scope;\n- delegate specialist work;\n- descend into technical detail only when material.\n\n### **VARIANCE 9 — MEDIUM-HIGH: compensation history remains inconsistent**\n\nAcross Wave 1 we have several historical models:\n- ~$175K target;\n- 48% / quarterly invoicing interpretation;\n- ~$319K theoretical calculation;\n- later ~$260K working comparison;\n- warnings that the basis does not reconcile cleanly;\n- retirement assumptions later rejected as unverified.\n\nThe latest closeouts correctly classify those numbers as **not fully source-verified**. fileciteturn13file0L489-L503\n\nSo:\n\n**MHI methodology = strong/current supporting.**  \n**MHI exact economics = unresolved unless a formal compensation source exists.**\n\nThat is a real remaining gap.\n\n---\n\n# 13. MHI FLOW v2 — **correctly remains provisional**\n\nThe four FLOW v2 artifacts were generated but not formally ratified.\n\nThe stale chat explicitly says they do **not** supersede HARDENED merely by existing. fileciteturn12file2L463-L497\n\nNo Drive artifact claims otherwise.\n\n**Disposition:** **MATCH / leave provisional.**\n\nNo reason to make Don review them now unless MHI becomes active again.\n\n---\n\n# 14. Disney test case — **excellent condition**\n\nThis was a pleasant confirmation.\n\nThe suite exists, has blind/non-blind phases, a protocol, and separate role/lens and reveal/reconciliation prompts.\n\n**No artifact creation required.**\n\nThe only gap is the **higher-level registry** connecting it to the rest of the model-evaluation estate.\n\n---\n\n# 15. Items I would put directly in front of Don\n\nThese are the items where your answer materially helps the later cleanup:\n\n| # | Variance / gap | My current classification | Don input? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **1** | Sep-21 Framework handoff predates Sep-22 frozen roster | **Wave 1 newer / Drive older** | Later, only for artifact disposition |\n| **2** | Technical Strategy/Shared-Service folder taxonomy vs latest seat roster | **Possible semantic mismatch** | **Yes** — does taxonomy track functions or live seats? |\n| **3** | No unified index for Disney + Monitor + Kimi real-world validation + Black Pearl | **Registry/discoverability gap** | Later |\n| **4** | Personal Tech Drive handoff says AX210 unresolved, while later Luce evidence says repaired/verified | **Drive stale** | No factual ruling needed |\n| **5** | Personal Context index points at older Vegas/personal anchors as current | **Drive stale** | No factual ruling needed |\n| **6** | Job Search master doc contains historical states mixed with latest current append | **Retrieval hazard** | No |\n| **7** | MHI exact comp/retirement economics remain internally inconsistent | **Needs source evidence** | Only if MHI matters again |\n| **8** | Current local router/VoiceBridge/Falcon implementations cannot be verified from Drive | **Expected local-only gap** | No |\n\n---\n\n# What I do **not** see\n\nI do **not** see evidence that:\n\n- GCE Framework needs redesign.\n- Projects were improperly absorbed into Framework.\n- Black Pearl became accidental canon.\n- Disney needs to be recreated.\n- Edge Crew project truth needs to be rewritten from this recon.\n- Job Search needs wholesale reconstruction.\n- Personal historical artifacts should be deleted.\n- older Wave-1 sources should be rewritten to use the current roster.\n\nThat is important. **The reconciliation problem is mostly state labeling and supersession—not bad underlying work.**\n\n---\n\n# Don-facing reconciliation verdict\n\n### **PROCEED — 97%**\n\n**Wave 1 is a strong current-era baseline.**\n\nThe current authority picture I would carry forward is:\n\n> **Use Wave 1's later explicit decisions over older Drive state where they conflict. Preserve Drive history. Do not rewrite historical documents. Correct stale “CURRENT” signaling later through supersession/indexing, not destructive cleanup.**\n\nThe two items I would actually want your instinct on are:\n\n**A.** Does the **GCE Drive organizational taxonomy** intentionally represent durable *functional estates* even when seats change? If yes, I will stop treating names such as Technical Strategy / Shared Enterprise Services as possible roster drift.\n\n**B.** For the later cleanup, should the **model-test estate** become one explicit registry containing **Disney, Monitor, Kimi/EC⁸ validation, and Black Pearl**, while leaving each underlying test artifact exactly where it lives?\n\nEverything else I can reconcile mechanically from the evidence without asking you to re-decide settled history."]}, "create_time": 1790199334.43