eze, Technical-Lifecycle Rework, and Project-Handoff Preparation\n\n[L5] **PRIMARY DOMAIN:** GCE Framework  \n[L6] **SECONDARY DOMAINS:** GCE Stack; Project\n\n[L8] **DATE RANGE COVERED:** 2026-09-20 through 2026-09-23  \n[L9] **FIRST MATERIAL DATE:** 2026-09-20  \n[L10] **LAST MATERIAL DATE:** 2026-09-23\n\n[L12] **PRIMARY AUTHORITY:** Don\n\n[L14] **PRIMARY SEATS INVOLVED:** Coda, Luce, Talon, Keel, Vittorio, Chiave, Nico, Corrado; supporting references to Falcon, Ragno, Magpie, Pigeon, Raven.\n\n[L16] **CURRENT STATUS:** **HANDOFF REQUIRED**\n\n[L18] **CONFIDENCE:** **98%**\n\n[L20] The chat contains strong direct evidence for the major decisions, including the original Framework reset handoff, Luce’s filesystem/seat audit, Don’s explicit frozen-seat rulings, and the subsequent migration-planning outputs.\n\n---\n\n[L24] # 2. WHAT THIS CHAT WAS ACTUALLY ABOUT\n\n[L26] ## Original objective\n\n[L28] The chat began as the **restart of the main GCE Framework conversation** from a clean 2026-09-20 handoff. That handoff explicitly separated Framework from Edge Crew, re-established **MODEL != SEAT**, preserved stable authority, and instructed the new conversation to reconstruct current truth before redesigning anything. :chatgpt-content-reference{index=\"0\"}\n\n[L30] ## Major pivots\n\n[L32] The work then moved through four major pivots:\n\n[L34] 1. **Machine / framework filesystem hygiene**\n[L35]    - Luce performed a whole-machine deep truthing pass.\n[L36]    - Keel executed a bounded cleanup wave.\n[L37]    - Luce independently verified the cleanup.\n\n[L39] 2. **Framework authority and seat re-evaluation**\n[L40]    - Existing Corrado / Calibro / Kimi coupling was challenged.\n[L41]    - The technical lifecycle was simplified conceptually.\n[L42]    - Don froze a new identity-first roster.\n\n[L44] 3. **Seat migration planning**\n[L45]    - Luce performed a dedicated Corrado / Calibro blast-radius audit.\n[L46]    - The audit showed that seat names were fused into router paths, identity folders, Command Center config, VoiceBridge, mailroom, and ECQ routing. :chatgpt-content-reference{index=\"1\"}\n[L47]    - Talon/Keel planning then reconciled the new frozen roster against those active surfaces.\n\n[L49] 4. **Project and stale-chat reconciliation structure**\n[L50]    - A new **GCE Stack parent-project handoff** was drafted.\n[L51]    - A **Universal Chat Closeout / Recap** prompt was created.\n[L52]    - A **GCE Framework Reconciliation Project** handoff was drafted for stale-chat ingestion, lane classification, and later read-only Google Drive reconciliation.\n\n[L54] ## Final scope\n\n[L56] The final purpose of this chat became:\n\n[L58] **freeze current Framework identity/seat doctrine, reconcile the resulting migration impact, preserve machine/framework hygiene, define GCE Stack as a separate supporting project, and prepare a new Framework Reconciliation Project to ingest stale chats and reconstruct historical/current truth without contaminating the live Framework conversation.**\n\n---\n\n[L62] # 3. ACCOMPLISHMENTS BY DATE\n\n[L64] ## 2026-09-20\n\n[L66] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:** Main Framework reset handoff established.\n\n[L68] **DECISION / RESULT:** Framework was separated from Edge Crew implementation. Stable seat identity, authority, runtime occupancy, shared-state direction, Command Center lessons, single Users-based home, verification discipline, and minimal-redesign doctrine were re-anchored. :chatgpt-content-reference{index=\"2\"}\n\n[L70] **OWNER:** Don / Coda\n\n[L72] **STATUS:** accepted\n\n---\n\n[L76] ## 2026-09-21\n\n[L78] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:** Full-machine / GCE deep cleanup recon.\n\n[L80] **DECISION / RESULT:** Luce found the Framework estate itself generally healthy and identified cleanup candidates, duplicate media/Proton state, stale shells, and ambiguous structures.\n\n[L82] **OWNER:** Luce\n\n[L84] **STATUS:** verified\n\n[L86] ### Keel cleanup\n\n[L88] Keel executed the broad cleanup wave:\n\n[L90] - obsolete/duplicate installers removed;\n[L91] - PDF extraction residue removed;\n[L92] - duplicate Downloads artifacts collapsed;\n[L93] - stranded media relocated/deduped;\n[L94] - duplicate Framework handoff on Desktop removed;\n[L95] - protected surfaces left untouched.\n\n[L97] **OWNER:** Keel\n\n[L99] **STATUS:** implemented\n\n[L101] ### Luce post-cleanup verification\n\n[L103] Luce verified:\n\n[L105] - no routing regression;\n[L106] - core GCE surfaces remained intact;\n[L107] - stale elevated-delete candidates remained;\n[L108] - one prior archive classification was corrected;\n[L109] - no material anomaly was introduced.\n\n[L111] **OWNER:** Luce\n\n[L113] **STATUS:** verified\n\n[L115] ### Framework research-lane reconciliation\n\n[L117] The conversation established that current Framework work had been organized into Technical Strategy research lanes and that current artifacts included:\n\n[L119] - `GCE_MODEL_LABOR_INTELLIGENCE_CURRENT_2026-09-21`\n[L120] - `GCE_RUNTIME_PROVIDER_INTELLIGENCE_CURRENT_2026-09-21`\n[L121] - `GCE_BLACK_PEARL_MODEL_LAB_RESEARCH_ANCHOR_2026-09-21`\n[L122] - `GCE_CROSS_PROJECT_METHODOLOGY_RESEARCH_CURRENT_2026-09-21`\n[L123] - `GCE_GOOGLE_DRIVE_STRUCTURE_MANIFEST_CURRENT_2026-09-21`\n[L124] - `GCE_FRAMEWORK_HANDOFF_2026-09-21_MAIN_CHAT_RECONCILIATION`\n\n[L126] The current project/framework boundary was explicitly restated:\n\n[L128] **Projects own implementation truth; Framework consumes reusable lessons only through reconciliation.**\n\n[L130] **OWNER:** Don / Coda\n\n[L132] **STATUS:** accepted, but exact Drive state remains to be re-truthed in the new reconciliation project.\n\n---\n\n[L136] ## 2026-09-22\n\n[L138] ### Gate 7 technical stage clarified\n\n[L140] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:** The ECQ Gate 7 package was inspected conceptually and the current stage was clarified as **Design & Build**, with methodology already completed and Chiave architecture already completed.\n\n[L142] **DECISION / RESULT:** Avoid reopening methodology or architecture during the terminal build lane.\n\n[L144] **OWNER:** Don / Coda / Chiave upstream; builder lane downstream\n\n[L146] **STATUS:** accepted for ECQ project scope\n\n[L148] ### Technical seat naming collision identified\n\n[L150] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:** Don recognized that Corrado / Chiave / Calibro created unnecessary cognitive collision.\n\n[L152] **DECISION / RESULT:** Names and responsibilities were revisited before lifecycle compression.\n\n[L154] **OWNER:** Don\n\n[L156] **STATUS:** accepted\n\n[L158] ### Vittorio established\n\n[L160] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:** Corrado’s old technical-advisor role was conceptually replaced by **Vittorio**.\n\n[L162] **DECISION / RESULT:** Vittorio became the technical-advisor / warboard / challenge identity.\n\n[L164] **OWNER:** Don\n\n[L166] **STATUS:** accepted\n\n[L168] ### Nico established\n\n[L170] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:** **Nico** was created as the implementation hammer / builder identity.\n\n[L172] **DECISION / RESULT:** Nico owns design-to-build translation and primary system creation.\n\n[L174] **OWNER:** Don\n\n[L176] **STATUS:** accepted\n\n[L178] ### Corrado preserved as quant engine\n\n[L180] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:** Instead of deleting Corrado, Don preserved the identity as a distinct specialist seat.\n\n[L182] **DECISION / RESULT:** Corrado became **quant engine only**: calculation, quantitative modeling, simulation, scoring, statistical/mathematical execution.\n\n[L184] **OWNER:** Don\n\n[L186] **STATUS:** accepted\n\n[L188] ### Frozen seat doctrine established\n\n[L190] The central technical separation became:\n\n[L192] **Vittorio advises.**  \n[L193] **Chiave architects.**  \n[L194] **Nico builds.**  \n[L195] **Corrado computes.**\n\n[L197] Underlying model/provider/runtime naming was deliberately demoted from day-to-day operating identity.\n\n[L199] **OWNER:** Don\n\n[L201] **STATUS:** CANONICAL / frozen in chat\n\n[L203] ### Luce rename blast-radius audit\n\n[L205] Luce found the migration was **moderate-to-high risk** because live dispatch surfaces were fused to exact seat names and paths. Approximately 12 must-change surfaces, six should-change surfaces, and 50+ historical references were identified. :chatgpt-content-reference{index=\"3\"}\n\n[L207] The audit established that:\n\n[L209] - current Corrado authority was methodology/advisor;\n[L210] - current Calibro authority was implementation design;\n[L211] - project-scoped Corrado had already crept into Design & Build;\n[L212] - Command Center, VoiceBridge, mailroom, router, and identity folders were name/path coupled. :chatgpt-content-reference{index=\"4\"}\n\n[L214] **OWNER:** Luce\n\n[L216] **STATUS:** verified\n\n[L218] ### Phase 0 migration governance resolved\n\n[L220] Don/Coda rulings included:\n\n[L222] - temporary **Calibro → Nico** alias allowed;\n[L223] - **no Corrado → Vittorio alias**;\n[L224] - **no Kimi → Vittorio alias**;\n[L225] - Vittorio created as a new canonical identity;\n[L226] - Nico absorbs active Calibro implementation-design authority;\n[L227] - Corrado survives as quant engine;\n[L228] - Kimi retires from the operating-seat namespace;\n[L229] - Chiave remains unchanged;\n[L230] - Ragno remains Principal Consultant/integration/translation but is not an automatic lifecycle gate;\n[L231] - Magpie and Pigeon remain named seats without unnecessary operational machinery;\n[L232] - Command Center freeze receives a one-time scoped migration override;\n[L233] - historical artifacts remain untouched.\n\n[L235] **OWNER:** Don / Coda\n\n[L237] **STATUS:** accepted\n\n[L239] ### Talon/Keel migration planning\n\n[L241] A migration plan and Phase 0 delta package were produced, but **execution had not yet occurred in this chat**.\n\n[L243] **STATUS:** proposed / execution-ready preparation, not implementation\n\n---\n\n[L247] ## 2026-09-23\n\n[L249] ### GCE Stack project defined\n\n[L251] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:** A parent handoff was drafted for **GCE Stack**.\n\n[L253] **DECISION / RESULT:** GCE Stack was defined as the technical support layer beneath/around Framework, including scraper/recovery, transport, synchronization, runtime plumbing, local services, APIs/adapters, utilities, supporting Command Center technology, VoiceBridge technical components, archival/recovery, and framework-support automation.\n\n[L255] The existing Kimi Web Bridge / scraper became a **subproject/component**, not the identity of the whole project.\n\n[L257] **OWNER:** Don / Coda\n\n[L259] **STATUS:** project handoff prepared\n\n[L261] ### Universal stale-chat closeout prompt created\n\n[L263] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:** A reusable prompt was created to close old chats by extracting:\n\n[L265] - what happened;\n[L266] - dates;\n[L267] - canonical vs project-local state;\n[L268] - artifacts and locations;\n[L269] - superseded decisions;\n[L270] - Google Drive references;\n[L271] - next-chat handoff.\n\n[L273] **OWNER:** Coda under Don authority\n\n[L275] **STATUS:** supporting / reusable prompt\n\n[L277] ### Framework Reconciliation Project designed\n\n[L279] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:** A parent handoff was drafted for a new project that will ingest stale chats, classify them by lane, map artifacts, reconcile them read-only against Google Drive, and build a cumulative historical registry.\n\n[L281] **OWNER:** Don / Coda\n\n[L283] **STATUS:** handoff prepared\n\n---\n\n[L287] # 4. FINAL ACCEPTED DECISIONS\n\n[L289] ## Decision: identity-first / seat-first Framework\n\n[L291] **DATE ACCEPTED:** 2026-09-22  \n[L292] **AUTHORITY:** Don  \n[L293] **SCOPE:** Framework-wide  \n[L294] **STATUS:** **CANONICAL**\n\n[L296] Underlying model/provider/runtime does not define operating identity.\n\n---\n\n[L300] ## Decision: frozen technical separation\n\n[L302] **DATE ACCEPTED:** 2026-09-22  \n[L303] **AUTHORITY:** Don  \n[L304] **SCOPE:** Framework-wide\n\n[L306] **Vittorio advises.  \n[L307] Chiave architects.  \n[L308] Nico builds.  \n[L309] Corrado computes.**\n\n[L311] **STATUS:** **CANONICAL**\n\n---\n\n[L315] ## Decision: Vittorio\n\n[L317] **DATE ACCEPTED:** 2026-09-22  \n[L318] **AUTHORITY:** Don  \n[L319] **SCOPE:** Framework-wide  \n[L320] **STATUS:** **CANONICAL**\n\n[L322] Technical advisor / warboard / challenge.\n\n---\n\n[L326] ## Decision: Nico\n\n[L328] **DATE ACCEPTED:** 2026-09-22  \n[L329] **AUTHORITY:** Don  \n[L330] **SCOPE:** Framework-wide  \n[L331] **STATUS:** **CANONICAL**\n\n[L333] Implementation hammer / builder / design-to-build.\n\n---\n\n[L337] ## Decision: Corrado survives\n\n[L339] **DATE ACCEPTED:** 2026-09-22  \n[L340] **AUTHORITY:** Don  \n[L341] **SCOPE:** Framework-wide  \n[L342] **STATUS:** **CANONICAL**\n\n[L344] Corrado is a specialist **quant engine**, not general methodology/advisory/build authority.\n\n---\n\n[L348] ## Decision: Chiave remains unchanged\n\n[L350] **DATE ACCEPTED:** 2026-09-22  \n[L351] **AUTHORITY:** Don  \n[L352] **SCOPE:** Framework-wide  \n[L353] **STATUS:** **CANONICAL**\n\n[L355] Architecture remains an independent seat/gate.\n\n---\n\n[L359] ## Decision: Kimi no longer defines operating seat identity\n\n[L361] **DATE ACCEPTED:** 2026-09-22  \n[L362] **AUTHORITY:** Don  \n[L363] **SCOPE:** Framework operating doctrine  \n[L364] **STATUS:** **CANONICAL**, implementation migration not yet verified complete\n\n[L366] Historical Kimi references remain provenance.\n\n---\n\n[L370] ## Decision: no Corrado→Vittorio alias\n\n[L372] **DATE ACCEPTED:** 2026-09-22  \n[L373] **AUTHORITY:** Don / Coda  \n[L374] **SCOPE:** migration/routing  \n[L375] **STATUS:** **CANONICAL**\n\n[L377] Because Corrado remains an active current seat.\n\n---\n\n[L381] ## Decision: no Kimi→Vittorio alias\n\n[L383] **DATE ACCEPTED:** 2026-09-22  \n[L384] **AUTHORITY:** Don / Coda  \n[L385] **SCOPE:** migration/routing  \n[L386] **STATUS:** **CANONICAL**\n\n[L388] Avoids preserving model/seat conflation.\n\n---\n\n[L392] ## Decision: Calibro→Nico temporary migration alias permitted\n\n[L