mplemented, later superseded from the capture critical path\n\n---\n\n[L87] ## DATE: 2026-09-22\n\n[L89] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:**  \n[L90] Actual iPhone Shortcuts behavior was pressure-tested through screenshots and live interaction.\n\n[L92] **DECISION / RESULT:**  \n[L93] Several assumed Shortcuts / Scriptable input behaviors were disproven by the actual UI:\n[L94] - Scriptable’s visible `Parameter` field opened a file picker.\n[L95] - Scriptable’s `Texts` editor did not behave like a normal persistent literal-text field.\n[L96] - The intended Dictate Text → composed Text → Scriptable parameter path was not successfully proven.\n\n[L98] A Siri-context banner explicitly showed:\n\n[L100] **“Dictation is not supported in Siri.”**\n\n[L102] **WHO / WHICH SEAT OWNED IT:** Don performed ground test; Coda reconciled findings.\n\n[L104] **STATUS:** verified\n\n---\n\n[L108] ## DATE: 2026-09-22\n\n[L110] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:**  \n[L111] Don identified that `Dictate Text` itself was the wrong primitive for the desired capture behavior.\n\n[L113] **DECISION / RESULT:**  \n[L114] The design pivoted from text-first capture to **Record Audio**.\n\n[L116] **WHO / WHICH SEAT OWNED IT:** Don identified the break; Coda formulated the architectural pivot.\n\n[L118] **STATUS:** accepted\n\n---\n\n[L122] ## DATE: 2026-09-22\n\n[L124] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:**  \n[L125] Native Shortcuts `Record Audio` was added and executed successfully.\n\n[L127] **DECISION / RESULT:**  \n[L128] The phone successfully produced a real `Recorded Audio` object.\n\n[L130] **WHO / WHICH SEAT OWNED IT:** Don ground test.\n\n[L132] **STATUS:** verified\n\n---\n\n[L136] ## DATE: 2026-09-22\n\n[L138] **WHAT WAS ACCOMPLISHED:**  \n[L139] `Recorded Audio` was connected directly into native `Save File`.\n\n[L141] **DECISION / RESULT:**  \n[L142] A playable local `.m4a` was successfully saved. This was the first capture primitive to survive contact with the actual phone.\n\n[L144] Observed saved evidence:\